window.ACTS = [{"id":"aiko_shimokita","host":"isle.aiko","cat":"go","t":{"zh":"东京下北泽一日","en":"A day in Shimokitazawa"},"pic":"aiko/street","days":1,"starts":["2026-11-22","2026-12-20"],"n":134,"why":["Shimokitazawa is my neighbourhood. Every Sunday I walk it slowly — records, old clothes, curry. Come walk with me, just one day.","下北泽是我住的地方。每个周日我都慢慢逛一圈——唱片、旧衣服、咖喱。来跟我走一天吧，就一天。"],"D":[{"k":"排你在下北泽的一天","say":["Locals just say Shimokita. Vintage shops, tiny theatres, curry on every corner. Maybe you dig for records first, like my customers — then you eat.","本地人就叫它「下北」。古着店、小剧场，每个街角都有咖喱。也许你先像我的客人那样翻唱片——然后去吃饭。"],"line":"I'd go [digging] for ___, then have ___.","z":"我会先去淘 ___，然后吃 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.mei","I'd go digging for city pop, then have curry. Then the live house — ticket plus one drink, right?","我会先去淘 city pop，然后吃咖喱。再去 live house——门票加一杯饮料，对吧？"],["new_york.xiaoyu","I'd go digging for a vintage coat, then have soup curry. New York winter is coming.","我会先去淘一件古着大衣，然后吃汤咖喱。纽约的冬天要来了。"],["isle.kenji","I'd go digging for old game music on vinyl, then have curry. Two plates, maybe.","我会先去淘黑胶的老游戏音乐，然后吃咖喱。可能吃两盘。"]],"shout":["Mei, yes — one drink rule! You are ready for live house. Our shop live sells out fast, so come early.","Mei，对——要买一杯饮料！你已经可以去 live house 了。我们店里的小演出票卖得很快，要早点来。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"SHIMOKITA","next":"aiko_live"}},{"id":"amara_jetlag","host":"isle.amara","cat":"move","t":{"zh":"落地不睡，3 天倒时差","en":"Beat jet lag in 3 days"},"pic":"amara/hotel","days":3,"starts":["2026-11-20","2026-12-18"],"n":120,"why":["Five cities in one week, my dear — I live in jet lag. This is what we do in the crew room: no nap, sunlight, eat on local time. I land in Manchester on Friday. Come and do it with me, wherever you just landed.","一周五座城，亲爱的——我就住在时差里。机组休息室里大家都这么做：不补觉、晒太阳、按当地时间吃饭。我周五落地曼彻斯特。不管你刚落在哪儿，跟我一起。"],"D":[{"k":"落地先别睡","say":["We land at seven in the morning and every bone says ‘bed’. Abeg, don't. Shower, go outside, get daylight. Bed at night, local time.","早上七点落地，浑身每根骨头都在喊「睡觉」。拜托，别睡。洗个澡，出门，晒晒太阳。按当地时间晚上再睡。"],"line":"I'm [staying up] till ten, local time.","z":"我要撑到当地时间十点再睡。","from":"跟同伴说","crowd":[["stars.emma","I'm staying up till ten, local time. Lisbon sun helps — trust me, a coffee by the river too.","我要撑到当地时间十点。里斯本的太阳有用——相信我，河边一杯咖啡也有用。"],["isle.linhao","Flew back to Lyon from Shanghai. Stayed up till ten. Fell asleep at 9:40 on the sofa. Almost.","从上海飞回里昂。撑到十点。九点四十在沙发上睡着了。差一点。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Not travelling, but I stayed up for the 2 a.m. pizza. Does that count?","我没出门，可我为了凌晨两点的披萨熬夜了。算吗？"]],"shout":["Linhao, 9:40 is a win, my dear. Xiaoyu — no, but I respect it.","林浩，九点四十也算赢，亲爱的。小雨——不算，但我尊重你。"]},{"k":"按当地时间吃","say":["Manchester, 7 degrees, raining. My body thinks it's lunchtime in Dubai. But here it's breakfast, so I'm eating breakfast. Ask someone local what's good.","曼彻斯特，7 度，下雨。我的身体以为现在是迪拜的午饭时间。可这儿是早上，那我就吃早饭。问问当地人吃什么好。"],"line":"What's [good for breakfast] around here?","z":"这附近早饭吃什么好？","from":"问当地人","crowd":[["isle.tom","Round here? A bacon butty and a cup of tea, mate. That's Bristol advice, mind.","我们这儿？培根三明治配一杯茶。不过这是布里斯托的说法啊。"],["isle.mei","Asked a tourist in my shop what's good for breakfast in his city. He said ‘coffee’. Just coffee 😂","我在店里问一个游客，他那边早饭吃什么好。他说「咖啡」。就咖啡 😂"]],"shout":["Tom, I took your advice. A bacon butty in the rain is a full-body hug.","Tom，我听你的了。雨里一个培根三明治，像被整个人抱住。"]},{"k":"说你自己的办法","say":["Day three, I feel human again. Honestly, everyone has their own trick. Tell me yours — the first thing you do when you land.","第三天，我又像个人了。说真的，每个人都有自己的办法。告诉我你的——你一落地做的第一件事。"],"line":"When I land, the first thing I [do] is ___.","z":"我一落地，第一件事是 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.emma","When I land, the first thing I do is buy a local SIM and get lost on purpose.","我一落地，第一件事是买张当地电话卡，然后故意迷路。"],["isle.kenji","When I land, the first thing I do is find a convenience store. Any country. It's my church.","我一落地，第一件事是找便利店。哪个国家都一样。那是我的教堂。"],["isle.bea","When I land, the first thing I do is text my mum. Then street food. In that order, always.","我一落地，第一件事是给我妈发消息。然后吃路边摊。永远是这个顺序。"]],"shout":["Bea, text mum first — my grandma would love you. Three days done. No wahala.","Bea，先给妈妈发消息——我外婆会喜欢你的。三天完成。没问题。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"LOCAL TIME","next":"amara_cities"}},{"id":"arun_know","host":"more.friends_a.arun","cat":"world","t":{"zh":"5 天 5 个「我们怎么知道的」","en":"How do we know?"},"pic":"arun/students","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-21","2026-12-19"],"n":145,"why":["A 12-year-old asked me why the sky is blue, and my first answer was terrible. So this week, five things everyone 'knows' — and how we actually found out. Slow is allowed.","一个 12 岁的孩子问我天为什么是蓝的，我第一次回答得一塌糊涂。所以这周我们看五件「大家都知道」的事——人到底是怎么知道的。慢一点没关系。"],"D":[{"k":"地球是圆的，怎么知道","say":["More than 2,000 years ago, Eratosthenes heard that at noon on one day of the year, the sun shone straight down a well in Syene. In Alexandria, on the same day, a stick still had a shadow. From the angle of the shadow, he worked out the size of the Earth. Sticks and shadows!","两千多年前，埃拉托色尼听说：一年里有一天正午，太阳能直直照到赛伊尼一口井的井底；同一天在亚历山大城，竖着的木棍还有影子。他用影子的角度算出了地球有多大。就靠木棍和影子！"],"line":"How do we [know] that?","z":"我们怎么知道的？","from":"聊看法","crowd":[["isle.kenji","How do we know that? Asked my coworker about a 'fact' in our docs. Nobody knew. We fixed the docs.","我们怎么知道的？我拿这句问同事文档里的一个「事实」。没人知道。我们把文档改了。"],["isle.xiaoyu","How do we know that? My mum says cold water makes you sick. I asked. Now we're both googling.","我们怎么知道的？我妈说喝凉水会生病。我问了这句。现在我们俩都在搜。"],["isle.mei","How do we no — know that. Okay. Sticks and shadows, I love this guy.","我们怎么知……知道的。好。木棍和影子，我喜欢这个人。"]],"shout":["Kenji's team fixed their documents because of one question. That is science, in an office.","Kenji 的团队因为一个问题改了文档。这就是科学，在办公室里。"]},{"k":"天为什么是蓝的","say":["Sunlight is every colour mixed. Air scatters blue light much more than red, so blue comes at you from every direction. My granddaughter asked why not violet — sunlight has less violet, and our eyes like blue more.","阳光是各种颜色混在一起的。空气散射蓝光比红光多得多，所以蓝光从四面八方朝你来。我孙女问为什么不是紫色——阳光里紫光本来就少，我们的眼睛也对蓝色更敏感。"],"line":"That's a really [good question].","z":"这个问题问得真好。","from":"接话","crowd":[["isle.bea","That's a really good question — I say this on my videos when I don't know the answer yet 😅","这个问题问得真好——我拍视频的时候，还不知道答案就先说这句 😅"],["isle.tom","That's a really good question. Said it to a seven-year-old at lunch. She looked so proud.","这个问题问得真好。午饭时我对一个七岁的孩子说了。她可得意了。"],["isle.linhao","That's a really good question. And the answer is… Rayleigh! I remembered the name.","这个问题问得真好。答案是……瑞利！我记住名字了。"]],"shout":["Tom, that child will ask ten more questions now. Good. That's how it starts.","Tom，那孩子现在会再问你十个问题。很好，就是这么开始的。"]},{"k":"太阳的光走了多久","say":["The light you see from the Sun left it about eight minutes ago. In 1676, Ole Rømer noticed one of Jupiter's moons appeared late when Earth was far from Jupiter — light needs time to travel.","你看到的太阳光，大约是八分钟前从太阳出发的。1676 年，罗默发现：地球离木星远的时候，木星的一颗卫星总是「晚到」——光走路是要时间的。"],"line":"It takes [about] eight minutes.","z":"大概要八分钟。","from":"说要多久","crowd":[["isle.amara","It takes about eight minutes. Same as boarding at a small airport — if you're lucky.","大概要八分钟。跟小机场登机差不多——运气好的话。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","It takes about eight minutes — to the Sun? From the Sun. Okay my brain needs eight minutes too.","大概要八分钟——到太阳？从太阳来。好吧我的脑子也要八分钟。"],["isle.kenji","It takes about eight minutes. So the sunset I watched was already gone. That's a bit sad.","大概要八分钟。所以我看的日落其实已经没了。有点伤感。"]],"shout":["Kenji, sad but true — you always see the past. Every time you look up.","Kenji，伤感，但是真的——你每次抬头，看到的都是过去。"]},{"k":"说一句「我可能错了」","say":["Today I teach the class! Last night I checked my slides twice and still found a mistake. Count the seconds between lightning and thunder, divide by three: that's roughly how many kilometres away the storm is. Sound is slow — about one kilometre in three seconds.","今天我去给孩子们上课！昨晚幻灯片我检查了两遍，还是找出一个错。看到闪电后数秒，等雷声来，秒数除以三，差不多就是雷暴离你几公里。声音走得慢——三秒左右一公里。"],"line":"I [might be wrong], but I think it's far.","z":"我可能说错了，但我觉得挺远的。","from":"说看法","crowd":[["isle.bea","I might be wrong, but I think it's far. Counted twelve seconds in Manila tonight — four kilometres!","我可能说错了，但我觉得挺远的。今晚在马尼拉数了十二秒——四公里！"],["isle.eleni","I might be wrong, but… Socrates would love this sentence. So do I.","我可能说错了，但是……苏格拉底会爱死这句。我也爱。"],["isle.linhao","I might be wrong, but I think my professor is wrong. I didn't say it to him. Yet.","我可能说错了，但我觉得我导师错了。我还没跟他说。暂时。"]],"shout":["Bea measured a real storm — twelve seconds, four kilometres. And the lesson went well! A child asked about the sky on Mars. I said, 'Let's find out together.'","Bea 测了一场真的雷暴：十二秒，四公里。课也讲得很好！一个孩子问火星上的天是什么颜色。我说：「我们一起去查吧。」"]},{"k":"说你改变的一个想法","say":["Last day. The best scientists change their minds. Tell me one thing you used to believe — and what you know now.","最后一天。最厉害的科学家都会改主意。说一件你以前相信的事，和你现在知道的。"],"line":"I [used to think] ___, but now I know ___.","z":"我以前以为 ___，现在知道 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.mei","I used to think the sky was blue because of the sea. Now I know it's the air.","我以前以为天是蓝的是因为大海。现在知道是因为空气。"],["isle.kenji","I used to think slow meant stupid. Now I know slow is allowed.","我以前以为慢就是笨。现在知道，慢一点没关系。"],["isle.xiaoyu","I used to think Greenland was huge. Now I know Jordi was right — it's the map.","我以前以为格陵兰很大。现在知道 Jordi 说得对——是地图的问题。"]],"shout":["Kenji, you quoted my old teacher back to me. I'm seventy and I nearly cried. Thank you, all of you.","Kenji，你把我老师当年的话还给了我。我七十岁了，差点哭出来。谢谢你们每一个人。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"HOW DO WE KNOW","next":"arun_light"},"_sources":{"埃拉托色尼用赛伊尼和亚历山大城正午的影子算地球周长（约公元前 240 年）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eratosthenes","瑞利散射、天为什么是蓝的":"https://spaceplace.nasa.gov/blue-sky/","天为什么不是紫的":"https://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/physics/General/BlueSky/blue_sky.html","太阳光到地球约 8 分 20 秒":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speed_of_light","罗默 1676 年用木卫一的时间推出光速有限":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%B8mer%27s_determination_of_the_speed_of_light","闪电到雷声：声速约 343 m/s，约 3 秒一公里":"https://www.weather.gov/safety/lightning-science-thunder","火星上的蓝色日落（11-24 那堂课）":"https://photojournal.jpl.nasa.gov/catalog/PIA19400"}},{"id":"bea_taglish","host":"isle.bea","cat":"go","t":{"zh":"一周听懂 Taglish","en":"A week of Taglish"},"pic":"bea/family","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-21","2026-12-19"],"n":87,"why":["I'm filming in Thailand, and my mum sends me a voice note every single day — in Taglish. Guys, decode them with me, and learn what the rest of the world says instead.","我在泰国拍片，我妈每天都给我发一条语音——用 Taglish。大家跟我一起解码，顺便学学世界上别的地方是怎么说的。"],"D":[{"k":"CR 是哪儿","say":["Today's voice note: ‘Anak, is the CR in your hotel clean?’ CR is comfort room — the toilet. For real, only Filipinos say it. Outside, use this.","今天的语音：「孩子，你酒店的 CR 干净吗？」CR 就是 comfort room，厕所。说真的，只有菲律宾人这么说。出了国，用这句。"],"line":"Excuse me, where's the [restroom]?","z":"请问，洗手间在哪儿？","from":"练习册 · 问路","crowd":[["isle.amara","Excuse me, where's the restroom? On the plane we say ‘lavatory’, my dear. Even fancier than CR.","请问，洗手间在哪儿？飞机上我们说 lavatory，亲爱的。比 CR 还讲究。"],["isle.kenji","Excuse me, where's the restroom? I always said ‘toilet’. Is that also okay?","请问，洗手间在哪儿？我一直说 toilet。那样也行吗？"]],"shout":["Kenji — ‘toilet’ is totally fine in the UK. In the US, ‘restroom’ just sounds softer.","Kenji——在英国说 toilet 完全没问题。在美国，说 restroom 听着更柔和一点。"]},{"k":"把灯「关上」","say":["Mum again: ‘Close the light before you sleep, ha!’ We say open and close the light. Everyone else turns it on and off.","又是我妈：「睡觉前把灯关上，听到没！」我们说 open、close the light。别的地方都说 turn on、turn off。"],"line":"Could you [turn off] the light?","z":"能把灯关一下吗？","from":"合租、住酒店","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Could you turn off the light? In Chinese we also ‘close’ the light — 关灯. Same as Bea's mum!","能把灯关一下吗？中文也是「关」灯。跟 Bea 的妈妈一样！"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Could you turn off the light — said it to my roommate at 1 a.m. It worked.","能把灯关一下吗——凌晨一点对室友说的。管用了。"]],"shout":["Linhao, Chinese and Tagalog both ‘close’ the light? Okay, Asia is one family.","林浩，中文和他加禄语都是「关」灯？好吧，亚洲是一家人。"]},{"k":"电话里的「for a while」","say":["When a Filipino picks up the phone and says ‘For a while po’, it means ‘hold on’. Mum did it to me today, then forgot me for five minutes.","菲律宾人接电话说 For a while po，意思是「等一下」。我妈今天就这么对我说的，然后把我忘了五分钟。"],"line":"Hold on a [sec], let me check.","z":"等一下，我看看。","from":"打电话、开会","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Hold on a sec, let me check. I say this in every stand-up now. It buys me ten seconds.","等一下，我看看。我现在每次站会都说这句。能给我多争取十秒。"],["isle.amara","Hold on a sec, let me check — that's half my job, my dear.","等一下，我看看——这就是我一半的工作，亲爱的。"]],"shout":["Kenji, ten free seconds in a stand-up. That's the hook, guys.","Kenji，站会里白赚十秒。这就是重点，大家。"]},{"k":"听不懂就说「太深了」","say":["My little brother read my script and said ‘Nosebleed!’ — Taglish for English that's too deep. When someone talks over your head, ask like this.","我弟看了我的脚本，说「流鼻血了！」——Taglish 里就是英语太深、听不懂。别人说得太难的时候，这样问。"],"line":"Sorry, could you say that more [simply]?","z":"不好意思，能说得简单一点吗？","from":"练习册 · 听不懂的时候","crowd":[["new_york.xiaoyu","Could you say that more simply? My visa agent talks so fast. I asked — and she slowed down!","能说得简单一点吗？帮我办签证的中介说话太快了。我问了——她真的放慢了！"],["isle.linhao","Sorry, could you say that more simply? My professor laughed, then drew a picture.","不好意思，能说得简单一点吗？我教授笑了，然后画了张图。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu asked a real person and it worked. No nosebleed needed.","小雨问了真人，而且管用了。不用流鼻血了。"]},{"k":"说你们那儿的说法","say":["Last day. Every country has its own Taglish. Give me one thing you say back home, and the English everyone else uses.","最后一天。每个国家都有自己的 Taglish。告诉我一个你们那儿的说法，再说一下别人都怎么说。"],"line":"Back home we [say] ___, but in English it's ___.","z":"在我们那儿说 ___，英语里是 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Back home we say ‘mansion’ for a flat, but in English a mansion is a huge house. Big surprise.","在我们那儿，公寓叫「mansion」，可英语里 mansion 是豪宅。吓我一跳。"],["isle.mei","Back home we say ‘QQ’ for chewy, but in English it's just ‘chewy’. Less cute.","在我们那儿，有嚼劲叫「QQ」，英语里就是 chewy。没那么可爱。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Back home we say ‘add oil’, but in English it's ‘you've got this’.","在我们那儿说「加油」，英语里是 you've got this。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu, fun fact: ‘add oil’ is in the Oxford English Dictionary now. So — both! Streak still alive 🔥","小雨，冷知识：add oil 现在已经收进《牛津英语词典》了。所以——两个都对！打卡还没断 🔥"]}],"end":{"stamp":"GETS IT","next":"bea_seasia"}},{"id":"daniel_praise","host":"isle.daniel","cat":"say","t":{"zh":"一周学会接住夸奖","en":"Learn to take a compliment"},"pic":"daniel/teach","days":6,"starts":["2026-11-18","2026-12-16"],"n":133,"why":["Last week I told Haruka her project was great, and she said “No, no, it was nothing.” Honestly? Half my students do that. Six days: five compliments, then your own way — let's learn to just say thanks.","上周我夸 Haruka 的项目做得好，她说「没有没有，没什么」。说实话，我一半的学生都这样。六天：五句夸奖，最后说说你那边的接法。我们一起学会说一声谢谢就好。"],"D":[{"k":"别说没有没有","say":["When someone praises your work, don't push it away. Say thanks, then one true thing.","别人夸你做的事，别往外推。先说谢谢，再说一句实话。"],"line":"Thanks — I'm really [proud of] that one.","z":"谢谢，那个我挺骄傲的。","from":"工作上被夸","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Thanks — I'm really proud of that one. It feels like lying, but okay.","谢谢，那个我挺骄傲的。感觉像在说谎，不过好吧。"],["isle.xiaoyu","My boss said my report was good. I said this. She looked surprised, in a good way!","领导说我报告写得好，我就这么回了。她有点意外，是好的那种意外！"],["isle.linhao","Thanks — I'm really proud of… that one. I stopped in the middle.","谢谢，那个我挺……骄傲的。说到一半停住了。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu tried it on her boss on day one. That's brave. And Kenji — it's not lying if it's true.","小雨第一天就对领导用上了，胆子真大。还有 Kenji——是真的，就不算说谎。"]},{"k":"夸你衣服的时候","say":["In the US, people praise your jacket all the time. Say thanks and add a tiny story — y'know, where you got it.","在美国，别人老是夸你外套好看。说声谢谢，再加一句小事，比如在哪儿买的。"],"line":"Thanks! I [got it] in a sale.","z":"谢谢！打折的时候买的。","from":"闲聊","crowd":[["isle.mei","Thanks! I got it in a sale. Actually it was my sister's, but that's a longer story.","谢谢！打折买的。其实是我姐的，不过说来话长。"],["isle.aiko","Thanks! I got it in a secondhand shop. Same street as my record shop.","谢谢！在二手店买的，跟我们唱片店在同一条街。"],["more.friends_e.jade","Thanks! I got it in a sale — three years ago. I run in it every week.","谢谢！打折买的——三年前了。每周都穿着它跑步。"]],"shout":["Aiko changed the line to fit her life. Perfect — that's what I want.","Aiko 把这句改成了她自己的事。完美，我要的就是这个。"]},{"k":"夸你英语说得好","say":["“Your English is so good!” Most of my students say “No, it's terrible.” Try this instead. It's true, and it's kind to yourself.","「你英语真好！」我的学生大多会说「不不，很烂」。换成这句吧。是实话，也对自己好一点。"],"line":"Thanks — I've [been working on it].","z":"谢谢，我一直在练。","from":"被夸语言","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Thanks — I've been working on it. My Bangalore teammate said it yesterday. I used this!","谢谢，我一直在练。昨天班加罗尔的同事这么夸我，我就用上了！"],["isle.bea","Thanks — I've been working on it. Said it to a café owner in Hanoi. In English, about my Vietnamese.","谢谢，我一直在练。在河内对一家咖啡店的老板说的。用英语说，说的是我的越南语。"],["stars.yuriko","My Spanish teacher said this to me. I said “No, no.” Then I remembered Daniel. Thanks — I've been working on it!","我西语老师这么夸我，我先说了「没有没有」。然后想起了 Daniel。谢谢，我一直在练！"]],"shout":["Kenji used it with a real teammate. Bea used it in Hanoi. This is how it sticks.","Kenji 对真同事用了，Bea 在河内用了。就是这样才记得住。"]},{"k":"夸你的人分量重","say":["When your boss or your teacher praises you, you can show it matters. Short and warm.","夸你的是老板、老师，你可以让对方知道这句话对你有分量。短一点，暖一点。"],"line":"Thanks — that [means a lot] coming from you.","z":"谢谢，你这么说，对我意义很大。","from":"被前辈夸","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Thanks — that means a lot coming from you. I said it to my professor. He smiled!","谢谢，你这么说对我意义很大。我对教授说了，他笑了！"],["isle.mei","I said it to my manager. Then she asked me to work on Sunday. Hmm.","我对店长说了这句。然后她让我周日来上班。嗯……"],["isle.amara","My captain said I handled a tricky passenger well. I said this one. Felt grown-up.","机长说我那个难缠的乘客处理得好。我回了这句，感觉自己很成熟。"]],"shout":["Mei — ha! That's a different lesson: how to say no to Sunday. Next time, I promise.","Mei——哈！那是另一课了：怎么拒绝周日上班。下次教，我保证。"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last day. Think of one thing you did this week that went well. Someone praises it — what do you say?","最后一天。想一件你这周做得不错的事。有人夸你，你怎么回？"],"line":"Thanks — I'm really [happy with] how ___ turned out.","z":"谢谢，___ 最后弄成这样，我挺满意的。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Thanks — I'm really happy with how the bug fix turned out. Nice catch, me.","谢谢，那个 bug 修成这样我挺满意的。干得好，我自己。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Thanks — I'm really happy with how my visa interview turned out. Very happy!!","谢谢，签证面试的结果我挺满意的。非常满意！！"],["isle.rosa","Thanks — I'm really happy with how my daughter's English sign turned out. She did the spelling.","谢谢，女儿给摊子做的英文牌子我挺满意的。拼写是她弄的。"]],"shout":["Five compliments, no more “no, no”. Haruka's interview is tomorrow — and she's ready to say thanks. Otsukare, everyone.","五句夸奖，不再说「没有没有」。Haruka 明天面试，她已经会说谢谢了。大家辛苦啦（お疲れ）。"]},{"k":"说说你那边怎么接","say":["One more day. Back home, when someone praises you, what do people usually say? Tell us in English — I'd love to hear your way.","再加一天。在你那边，被人夸了，一般怎么接？用英语说说——我想听听你们的接法。"],"line":"Back home, when someone praises us, we usually [say] ___.","z":"在我们那儿，被人夸了，一般会说___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","Back home, we usually say ‘哪里哪里’ — literally ‘where, where?’ My mum still says it every time.","在我们那儿，一般说「哪里哪里」。我妈到现在每次都这么说。"],["isle.kenji","Back home, we usually say ‘No, no, not at all.’ This week I tried ‘Thanks’ — it felt strange, but nice.","在我们那儿，一般说「没有没有」。这周我试着说了 thanks——有点不习惯，但感觉不错。"],["isle.rosa","Back home, we say thank you and give one back: ‘Ay, you too!’","在我们那儿，先说谢谢，再夸回去：「哎呀，你也是！」"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu's mum says 哪里哪里, Kenji says ‘no, no’, Rosa says ‘you too!’. Every place has its own way — and now we all know a few.","小雨妈妈说「哪里哪里」，Kenji 说「没有没有」，Rosa 说「你也是！」。每个地方都有自己的接法，现在我们都多会了几种。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"THANKS","next":"daniel_no"}},{"id":"demo_parts","hidden":true,"host":"isle.nadia","cat":"eat","t":{"zh":"零件试一遍（不上架）","en":"Parts test (hidden)"},"pic":"nadia/label","days":12,"starts":[],"n":0,"why":["Twelve kinds of steps, one a day.","十二种玩法，一天一种。只用来检查零件。"],"D":[{"k":"说三遍","type":"say","say":["Today, just one line.","今天就一句。"],"line":"I'll have the [oat milk], please.","z":"我要燕麦奶，谢谢。","from":"at a café"},{"k":"跟着做","type":"follow","say":["Stand up. Three moves, I'll call them.","站起来，三个动作，我喊。"],"moves":[["Roll your shoulders","转转肩膀",5],["Reach up high","往上够",5],["Touch your toes","摸脚尖",5]],"line":"I [stretched] for a minute this morning.","z":"我今天早上拉伸了一分钟。","from":"telling a friend"},{"k":"拍照","type":"photo","say":["Find a label in your kitchen.","在厨房找一个包装。"],"prompt":["Take a photo of one food label.","拍一张食品包装上的标签。"],"own":true,"line":"This one has [___ grams of sugar] per serving.","z":"这个每份有 ___ 克糖。","from":"reading a label"},{"k":"排一排","type":"plan","say":["Plan three dinners.","排三顿晚饭。"],"slots":[{"lab":["Monday","周一"],"opts":["pasta","rice and beans","soup"]},{"lab":["Wednesday","周三"],"opts":["stir-fry","tacos","salad"]},{"lab":["Friday","周五"],"opts":["curry","pizza","fish"]}],"tpl":"This week I'm making {0}, {1} and {2}.","own":true,"line":"This week I'm making [___], [___] and [___].","z":"这周我做……","from":"planning the week"},{"k":"走一遍","type":"walk","say":["Walk the market with me.","跟我逛一圈市场。"],"stops":[{"at":["Fruit stall","水果摊"],"img":"rosa/market","q":["You want half a kilo of apples.","你想要半公斤苹果。"],"opts":[["Half a kilo of apples, please.",true,"自然、清楚。"],["Give me apples half.",false,"顺序不对，换一个。"]]},{"at":["Bakery","面包店"],"img":"jordi/corner","q":["Ask if the bread is from today.","问面包是不是今天的。"],"opts":[["Is this bread new?",false,"new 容易听成「新出的」；问是不是今天烤的，说 baked today 对方更容易懂。"],["Is this baked today?",true,"对，就这么问。"]]}],"line":"Is this [baked today]?","z":"这是今天烤的吗？","from":"at the bakery"},{"k":"站一边","type":"vote","say":["Breakfast — yes or no?","早饭吃不吃？"],"q":["Is breakfast the most important meal?","早饭是最重要的一顿吗？"],"sides":[["Yes, always","是，一定要吃",58],["Not really","不一定",42]],"own":true,"line":"I'd say [___], because ___.","z":"我觉得……因为……","from":"giving your opinion"},{"k":"听","type":"listen","say":["Listen to my shopping list.","听我的购物单。"],"text":"I need some eggs, a loaf of bread, two lemons and a bag of spinach.","chips":[["eggs",true],["milk",false],["lemons",true],["spinach",true],["cheese",false]],"line":"I need [a loaf of bread].","z":"我要一条面包。","from":"shopping list"},{"k":"看一分钟","type":"look","say":["Look at this stall for a bit.","看这个摊子一会儿。"],"img":"rosa/stall","secs":10,"q":["What's on the table? What's the person doing?","桌上有什么？人在干嘛？"],"own":true,"line":"I noticed [___].","z":"我注意到……","from":"describing a photo"},{"k":"猜一猜","type":"guess","say":["Guess this one.","猜一个。"],"img":"hana/market","q":["Which has more fibre per 100g?","每 100 克哪个纤维多？"],"opts":[["White rice",false],["Lentils",true],["Chicken",false]],"reveal":["Lentils — about 8g, rice under 1g.","扁豆约 8 克，白米不到 1 克。"],"line":"[Lentils] have way more fibre.","z":"扁豆的纤维多得多。","from":"sharing a fact"},{"k":"一起做","type":"together","say":["Let's write a cookbook — one line each.","一起写一本菜谱，每人一句。"],"title":["Our 10-minute dinners","我们的十分钟晚饭"],"wall":[["isle.mei","Noodles, an egg and spring onion.","面、一个蛋、葱花。"],["isle.rosa","Tortilla, beans, cheese — done.","饼、豆子、奶酪，搞定。"],["more.friends_e.hana","Rice, natto and kimchi.","米饭、纳豆、泡菜。"]],"own":true,"line":"My 10-minute dinner: [___].","z":"我的十分钟晚饭：……","from":"the cookbook"},{"k":"60 秒说","type":"timed","say":["One minute. Don't stop.","一分钟，别停。"],"secs":20,"prompt":["Tell me what you ate yesterday.","说说你昨天吃了什么。"],"hints":["For breakfast I had…","Then for lunch…","In the evening…"]},{"k":"日记","type":"diary","say":["Last day. One line about this week.","最后一天，写一句这一周。"],"q":["What's one thing you'll keep doing?","有什么你会一直做下去？"],"own":true,"line":"I'm going to keep [___].","z":"我会一直……","from":"your diary"}],"end":{"stamp":"PARTS","next":""}},{"id":"eleni_lines","host":"isle.eleni","cat":"world","t":{"zh":"7 天 7 句古人的话","en":"Seven old lines for now"},"pic":"eleni/agora","days":7,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":167,"why":["On Friday my class goes to the Agora, where Socrates talked with anyone who would listen. Before that, one old line a day — the kind you can still use on a Tuesday.","周五我要带学生去古市集，就是苏格拉底当年找人聊天的地方。去之前，每天一句古人的话——今天随便哪个周二都还用得上的那种。"],"D":[{"k":"有的事不由你","say":["Epictetus was born a slave and became a teacher. His big idea: some things are up to us, some are not. The weather, other people's moods — not up to you.","爱比克泰德生来是奴隶，后来当了老师。他最重要的一句：有的事由我们，有的事不由我们。天气、别人的心情，都不由你。"],"line":"That's [not up to me].","z":"那不由我决定。","from":"放下一件事","crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","That's not up to me. The visa office decides. I just check my email 40 times a day.","那不由我决定。签证处说了算。我只能一天看 40 遍邮箱。"],["isle.kenji","That's not up to me — I said this about my boss's mood. Felt better, honestly.","那不由我决定——我拿这句说了老板的心情。说真的，舒服多了。"],["isle.mei","That's not up to me! The rain, the customers, the bubble machine breaking 🙃","那不由我决定！下雨、客人、珍珠机又坏了 🙃"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu — checking 40 times is also… up to you. Ah, interesting, no?","小雨——一天看 40 遍邮箱，这件事倒是由你的。有意思吧？"]},{"k":"问一句「你是说……」","say":["Socrates didn't give answers. He asked questions. The oldest one still works best when someone says 'everyone knows that'.","苏格拉底不给答案，他只提问。有人说「谁都知道」的时候，最老的那个问题还是最好用。"],"line":"What do you [mean by] 'normal'?","z":"你说的「正常」是指什么？","from":"聊看法","crowd":[["isle.linhao","What do you mean by 'normal'? My French flatmate said dinner at 8 is normal. Jordi would say 10.","你说的「正常」是指什么？我的法国室友说八点吃晚饭才正常。Jordi 会说十点。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","What do you mean by 'normal'? Used it on a guy who said my accent isn't normal. He had no answer.","你说的「正常」是指什么？有个人说我口音不正常，我就这么问他。他答不上来。"],["isle.bea","What do you mean by 'normal'? Asked my mum. Conversation lasted two hours 😅","你说的「正常」是指什么？我问了我妈。聊了两个小时 😅"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu asked a real question to a real person, and he had no answer. Socrates would buy you a coffee.","小雨对一个真人问了一个真问题，他答不上来。苏格拉底会请你喝咖啡的。"]},{"k":"同一条河，踩不了两次","say":["Heraclitus said you can't step into the same river twice. The water is new, and so are you. I think of it every time I visit my old school.","赫拉克利特说，人不能两次踏进同一条河。水是新的，你也是新的。每次回我的母校，我都会想起这句。"],"line":"It's [not the same] anymore.","z":"已经不一样了。","from":"回到一个老地方","crowd":[["isle.linhao","It's not the same anymore. Went back to my hometown noodle shop on video call — new owner, new bowls.","已经不一样了。视频里看了老家那家面馆——换了老板，换了碗。"],["isle.aiko","It's not the same anymore… Shimokitazawa, I mean. But I'm not the same either. Heraclitus wins.","已经不一样了……我说的是下北泽。不过我也不一样了。赫拉克利特赢了。"]],"shout":["Aiko finished the thought by herself: 'I'm not the same either.' That's the second half nobody remembers.","Aiko 自己把后半句说出来了：「我也不一样了」。这后半句，大多数人都忘了。"]},{"k":"说一句「我不确定」","say":["Today we're at the Agora. Socrates said he was wiser than one man only because he didn't think he knew what he didn't know. Not knowing is allowed.","今天我们在古市集。苏格拉底说，他比一个人聪明，只是因为他不会把自己不知道的东西当成知道。不知道是可以的。"],"line":"I'm [not sure], actually.","z":"其实我也不太确定。","from":"接话","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I'm not sure, actually. — Said it in a meeting instead of guessing. Nobody died.","其实我也不太确定。——开会时我没瞎猜，说了这句。谁也没怎么样。"],["more.friends_a.arun","I'm not sure, actually. Fifty years in a lab, and it's still my most useful sentence.","其实我也不太确定。在实验室五十年了，这还是我最有用的一句。"],["isle.mei","I'm not shure — not SURE, actually. Okay that one I'm sure.","其实我也不太……确定。好吧，这个词我确定了。"]],"shout":["Kenji said it in a real meeting. Arun said it after fifty years. You're in good company, Kenji.","Kenji 在真的会上说了。Arun 干了五十年还在说。Kenji，你跟对人了。"]},{"k":"我们是要聊天的动物","say":["After the Agora, my students didn't go home — they sat in a café in Plaka and kept arguing. Aristotle said we are 'political animals': made to live together, talking.","去完古市集，我的学生没回家，在普拉卡的一家咖啡馆坐着接着吵。亚里士多德说人是「城邦的动物」：生来就要住在一起、说话。"],"line":"Let's [talk it over] with a coffee.","z":"我们边喝咖啡边聊吧。","from":"约朋友","crowd":[["isle.bea","Let's talk it over with a coffee — sent to my sister. We haven't really talked in a month.","我们边喝咖啡边聊吧——发给我姐了。我们一个月没好好说话了。"],["stars.emma","Let's talk it over with a coffee. Every fight I've had on a trip ended this way, trust me.","我们边喝咖啡边聊吧。我旅行时吵过的每一架都是这么收场的，相信我。"],["isle.linhao","Let's talk it over with a coffee. Or tea? Can I say tea?","我们边喝咖啡边聊吧。或者喝茶？可以说茶吗？"]],"shout":["Linhao, yes — Aristotle doesn't mind tea. Bea, tell us what your sister said.","林浩，可以——亚里士多德不介意喝茶。Bea，告诉我们你姐姐怎么回的。"]},{"k":"没想的那么糟","say":["Seneca wrote to a friend: we suffer more often in imagination than in reality. I tell myself this at 3 a.m., when everything looks bigger.","塞涅卡给朋友写信说：我们在想象里受的苦，比真的多。凌晨三点什么都显得很大的时候，我就这么跟自己说。"],"line":"It's probably [not as bad as] I think.","z":"可能没我想的那么糟。","from":"安慰自己","crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","It's probably not as bad as I think. The visa interview, I mean. Saying it three times did help a bit.","可能没我想的那么糟。我说的是签证面试。说了三遍，确实好一点。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","It's probably not as bad as I think — my set bombed last night. Okay, it was a little bad.","可能没我想的那么糟——昨晚我的段子冷场了。好吧，是有一点糟。"],["isle.kenji","It's probably not as bad as I think. My code review had 31 comments. 30 were 'nit'.","可能没我想的那么糟。我的代码有 31 条评论，30 条是「小问题」。"]],"shout":["Kenji counted. 30 of 31 were small. That's Seneca with a spreadsheet.","Kenji 数了：31 条里 30 条是小事。这是拿表格做的塞涅卡。"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last day. Take Epictetus home: one thing in your life that's up to you, and one that isn't.","最后一天。把爱比克泰德带回家：说一件由你的事，一件不由你的事。"],"line":"___ [is up to me]. ___ [isn't].","z":"___ 由我。___ 不由我。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","How hard I practise is up to me. The visa isn't.","我练得多认真，由我。签证不由我。"],["isle.mei","Being kind to rude customers is up to me. The customers aren't.","对没礼貌的客人客不客气，由我。客人不由我。"],["isle.aiko","What I play in the shop is up to me. Who walks in isn't.","店里放什么歌，由我。谁走进来，不由我。"]],"shout":["Seven days, seven old lines. Aiko's is my favourite — I'll read it to my class on Monday. Thank you, my porch people.","七天，七句古人的话。我最喜欢 Aiko 那句——周一我要念给学生听。谢谢你们，我的「柱廊派」。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"STOIC","next":"eleni_questions"},"_sources":{"爱比克泰德生来是奴隶；《手册》开头：有的事由我们，有的不由":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enchiridion_of_Epictetus","苏格拉底式提问":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socratic_method","赫拉克利特：不能两次踏进同一条河（柏拉图《克拉底鲁篇》转述）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heraclitus","苏格拉底：我比他聪明，因为我不把不知道的当成知道（柏拉图《申辩篇》21d）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_know_that_I_know_nothing","亚里士多德：人是城邦的动物（《政治学》）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politics_(Aristotle)","塞涅卡《致卢基里乌斯书》第 13 封：我们在想象里受的苦比现实多":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Moral_letters_to_Lucilius/Letter_13","斯多葛派名字来自画廊（柱廊）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stoa_Poikile"}},{"id":"emma_toronto","host":"stars.emma","cat":"go","t":{"zh":"这周跟我在多伦多问路","en":"Ask for directions with me in Toronto"},"pic":"emma/hostel","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-20","2026-12-18"],"n":156,"why":["New city, new cold. Every day this week I'll get lost on purpose in Toronto — you tell me what to ask.","新城市，新的冷。这周我每天在多伦多故意迷路一次，你来告诉我该怎么问。"],"D":[{"k":"问路的第一句","say":["Start soft. Nobody likes a question shot at them. In Toronto, ‘sorry’ opens every door.","开口要软。没人喜欢一句话直接怼过来。在多伦多，一句 sorry 什么门都能打开。"],"line":"Sorry, which [way] is Union Station?","z":"不好意思，联合车站往哪边走？","from":"练习册 · 问路","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Sorry, which way is Union Station? I said it to my mirror. The mirror didn't know.","不好意思，联合车站往哪边走？我对着镜子问的。镜子不知道。"],["isle.mei","Sorry, which way is the MRT? Same sentence, works in Taipei too!","不好意思，捷运往哪边走？同一句，台北也能用！"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Which way is… sorry! Sorry first. Okay, again.","往哪边走……对不起！先说 sorry。好，重来。"]],"shout":["Mei took it home to Taipei on day one. That's exactly how you keep a sentence.","Mei 第一天就把这句带回台北用了。一句话就是这么留下来的。"]},{"k":"上车前先问一句","say":["Toronto has red streetcars. The 510 goes up Spadina towards Kensington Market — but I wasn't sure, so I asked the driver.","多伦多有红色的有轨电车。510 路沿着 Spadina 往北，去肯辛顿市场那边——我不太确定，就问了司机。"],"line":"Does this [go to] Kensington Market?","z":"这车到肯辛顿市场吗？","from":"练习册 · 坐车","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Does this go to Namba? I asked a real driver in Osaka. He said yes in English!","这车到难波吗？我在大阪真去问了司机。他用英语说了 yes！"],["isle.amara","Does this go to Terminal 3? My dear, I ask this every single week.","这车到 3 号航站楼吗？亲爱的，我每个礼拜都要问一遍。"]],"shout":["Kenji asked a real driver. That's the step — sentence in the mouth, not in the notebook.","Kenji 真去问了司机。要的就是这一步——句子在嘴里，不在本子里。"]},{"k":"没听清，再问一遍","say":["A man told me, ‘Walk up to Young.’ I looked for ‘Young’ for ten minutes. It's spelled Y-O-N-G-E. Trust me, just ask again.","一个大叔跟我说：走到 Young 街。我找了十分钟 Young。结果它写作 Y-O-N-G-E。相信我，没听清就再问一遍。"],"line":"Sorry, I didn't [catch] that. Could you say it again?","z":"不好意思，我没听清。能再说一遍吗？","from":"练习册 · 问路","crowd":[["isle.bea","Sorry, I didn't catch that! Filming this in Bangkok traffic, so… very real.","不好意思，我没听清！我在曼谷的车流里拍的，所以……非常真实。"],["isle.linhao","I didn't catch that. Ha — I use this in every class in Lyon now.","我没听清。哈——我现在在里昂每节课都用这句。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Could you say it again? Better than saying ‘yes’ to everything, I learned that the hard way.","能再说一遍吗？总比什么都说 yes 强，我是吃过亏才学会的。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu — I saw your open mic in New York. ‘Say it again’ is the cure for the yes-to-everything thing.","小雨——我在纽约看过你的开放麦。Say it again 正好治「什么都说 yes」。"]},{"k":"外面太冷了","say":["It's freezing today. Downtown has a whole city underground — the PATH. You can walk between stations and shops without going outside.","今天冷得要命。市中心地下有一整座城——PATH 地下通道。车站和商场之间能一路走过去，不用出门。"],"line":"Can I get there [without going outside]?","z":"能不能不出门走过去？","from":"练习册 · 问路","crowd":[["isle.aiko","Can I get there without going outside? Shinjuku station is also like this. Maybe more lost.","能不能不出门走过去？新宿站也是这样。可能更容易迷路。"],["isle.amara","Can I get there without going outside — I asked this in Dubai, but for the heat.","能不能不出门走过去——我在迪拜也问过，不过是因为太热。"]],"shout":["Amara, same question, opposite weather. I love that.","Amara，同一个问题，天气正好反过来。太喜欢了。"]},{"k":"问你自己城市的路","say":["Last day. Pretend a lost tourist is you, in your own city. Where would you go?","最后一天。假装你自己是个迷路的游客，就在你住的城市。你想去哪儿？"],"line":"Excuse me, how do I [get to] ___ from here?","z":"请问，从这儿去 ___ 怎么走？","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Excuse me, how do I get to Dotonbori from here? I live here and I still get lost.","请问，从这儿去道顿堀怎么走？我住在这儿，还是会迷路。"],["isle.mei","Excuse me, how do I get to Shilin Night Market from here? Take the red line, I'll tell you!","请问，从这儿去士林夜市怎么走？坐红线，我告诉你！"],["isle.linhao","Excuse me, how do I get to Fourvière from here? Answer: up. Always up.","请问，从这儿去富维耶山怎么走？答案：往上。一直往上。"]],"shout":["Five days, five lost Emmas. Now I'm going skating with Liam — wish me luck.","五天，迷路了五次。我现在要跟 Liam 去滑冰了——祝我好运。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"FOUND IT","next":"emma_snow"}},{"id":"farah_five","host":"more.friends_b.farah","cat":"go","t":{"zh":"伊斯坦布尔 5 天 5 样东西","en":"Five things from Istanbul"},"pic":"farah/bazaar","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-18","2026-12-16"],"n":99,"why":["This week I'm guiding a group from Chengdu: one thing a day that travelled from East to West through my city. Find each one at home, wherever you are.","这周我在带一个成都来的团：每天看一样经过我这座城、从东方走到西方的东西。不管你在哪儿，都在家里找找它。"],"D":[{"k":"郁金香从这儿出发","say":["Tulips went to Holland from the Ottoman gardens. Even the English word probably comes from ours — tülbent, turban cloth. The flower looks like a turban.","郁金香是从奥斯曼的花园传到荷兰的。连英语这个词，大概也来自我们的 tülbent，包头巾的布。这花长得就像一顶头巾。"],"line":"Where does this [come from]?","z":"这是从哪儿来的？","from":"逛市场、逛博物馆","crowd":[["more.friends_a.isabel","Where does this come from? Half the Dutch still lifes in our storeroom have a tulip in them. Now I know.","这是从哪儿来的？我们库房里一半的荷兰静物画都有郁金香。现在我知道了。"],["isle.amara","Where does this come from? I fly to Amsterdam twice a month. Now the tulips at the airport make sense, my dear.","这是从哪儿来的？我一个月飞两次阿姆斯特丹。现在机场那些郁金香我总算看懂了，亲爱的。"]],"shout":["Isabel — a museum director asking ‘where does this come from’. That's the right question, every day.","Isabel——美术馆馆长也在问「这是从哪儿来的」。这就是对的问题，天天都该问。"]},{"k":"盘子叫 china","say":["Our tile makers tried for years to copy Chinese blue and white. We call those tiles çini — from Çin, China. Go and look at a plate in your kitchen.","我们的瓷砖匠人花了很多年想仿出中国的青花。这种瓷砖我们叫 çini，来自 Çin，中国。去看看你厨房里的一个盘子吧。"],"line":"What do you [call] this here?","z":"这个你们这儿叫什么？","from":"到了一个新地方","crowd":[["isle.tom","What do you call this here? In my mum's house it's ‘the good china’. Nobody's allowed to eat off it.","这个你们这儿叫什么？在我妈家它叫「好瓷器」。谁都不许拿它吃饭。"],["isle.kenji","What do you call this here? In Japan, pottery is setomono — from Seto, a pottery town. Same idea!","这个你们这儿叫什么？在日本，陶瓷叫「濑户物」——来自濑户这个做陶的小城。一样的道理！"]],"shout":["Kenji, setomono! A town's name becomes the thing. Çini, china, setomono — three cousins.","Kenji，濑户物！一个地名变成了东西的名字。çini、china、濑户物——三个表亲。"]},{"k":"请别人喝一杯","say":["Coffee came here from Yemen in the 1500s, then went on to Europe. We say a cup of coffee is remembered for forty years. So today, buy someone one.","咖啡十六世纪从也门传到这里，再往欧洲去。我们说，一杯咖啡的情分记四十年。所以今天，请一个人喝一杯吧。"],"line":"Let me [get] this one.","z":"这杯我请。","from":"请客、付账","crowd":[["isle.rosa","Let me get this one! In Mexico we fight for the bill. I lost. Next time.","这杯我请！在墨西哥我们抢着付账。我输了。下次。"],["isle.linhao","Let me get this one — said it to my French groupmate. Now he owes me forty years.","这杯我请——我对法国组员说的。现在他欠我四十年。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Let me get this one. I practised it on the way, then she paid anyway 😂","这杯我请。我一路上都在练，结果还是她付了 😂"]],"shout":["Rosa lost the bill fight. In Istanbul, that's how friendships start.","Rosa 抢账单输了。在伊斯坦布尔，友情就是这么开始的。"]},{"k":"茶的两条路","say":["Tea that went by land is called something like cha — çay, chai. Tea that left by sea from Fujian became tea, thé. Ask someone how they say it.","走陆路的茶，叫法都像 cha——çay、chai。从福建走海路出去的，就成了 tea、thé。去问一个人，他们那儿怎么说。"],"line":"How do you [say] ‘tea’ where you're from?","z":"你们那儿「茶」怎么说？","from":"跟外国朋友聊天","crowd":[["isle.mei","How do you say tea where you're from? I asked my grandma: in Taiwanese it's tê. Sea route!!","你们那儿茶怎么说？我问了阿嬷：台语叫 tê。海路那一派！！"],["isle.kenji","Japanese: ocha. Land route, I think. Team cha.","日语：ocha。应该是陆路。cha 这一队。"],["isle.linhao","French: thé. So my two languages are both sea route. Only Chinese is land.","法语：thé。所以我说的两种外语都是海路的。只有中文是陆路。"]],"shout":["Mei, your grandma just proved four hundred years of history in one word.","Mei，你阿嬷一个词就证明了四百年的历史。"]},{"k":"第五样，是你的","say":["The fifth thing is yours. Something that came to your city from far away — a food, a word, a plant.","第五样东西是你的。一样从远方来到你那座城的东西——一种吃的、一个词、一棵植物。"],"line":"___ [came to] us from ___.","z":"___ 是从 ___ 传到我们这儿的。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.rosa","Tacos al pastor came to us from Lebanon. Shawarma, but with pineapple.","al pastor 塔可是从黎巴嫩传到我们这儿的。就是沙威玛，不过加了菠萝。"],["isle.linhao","Silk came to Lyon from China. So in a way, I followed it here.","丝绸是从中国传到里昂的。这么说，我是跟着它来的。"],["isle.kenji","Ramen came to us from China. Now it travels back the other way.","拉面是从中国传到我们这儿的。现在又反过来往回走了。"]],"shout":["My group from Chengdu flew home this morning. Linhao, you're the sixth thing on my list now.","成都的团今天早上回国了。林浩，你现在是我单子上的第六样东西。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"EAST TO WEST","next":"farah_words"}},{"id":"hana_mealplan","host":"more.friends_e.hana","cat":"life","t":{"zh":"周日一起排好下周的饭","en":"Sunday meal plan, together"},"pic":"hana/plan","days":1,"starts":["2026-11-22","2026-12-20"],"n":271,"why":["The family I'm helping from Lyon ate convenience-store dinners all last week. Twenty minutes on Sunday fixed it. Let's do yours too.","我在帮的那家从里昂来的人，上周天天晚饭吃便利店。周日花二十分钟就改过来了。你的这周，我们也一起排。"],"D":[{"k":"说出这周的三顿","say":["Open your fridge first. Pick three dinners that use what's already there — then say them out loud, so you mean it.","先打开冰箱。挑三顿用得上里面现成东西的晚饭——然后大声说出来，说出来才算数。"],"line":"This week I'm [making] ___, ___ and ___.","z":"这周我做 ___、___ 和 ___。","from":"练习册 · 自己做饭","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.tom","This week I'm making shepherd's pie, leek soup and fish fingers. Fish fingers count, Hana.","这周我做牧羊人派、韭葱汤和炸鱼条。炸鱼条也算，Hana。"],["isle.linhao","This week I'm making tomato and egg, dumplings from the freezer, and… pasta again. It's Lyon.","这周我做番茄炒蛋、冰箱里的速冻饺子，还有……又是意面。毕竟在里昂。"],["isle.nadia","This week I'm making lentil soup, a tray bake and a frozen-veg stir-fry. Told you.","这周我做扁豆汤、一盘烤菜，还有冷冻蔬菜炒一炒。早说了吧。"]],"shout":["Linhao — pasta three times is still a plan. Next Sunday, swap one for the miso soup I posted.","林浩——意面做三次也是排了饭。下周日换一顿成我发的那个味噌汤吧。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"PLANNED","next":"hana_fridge"}},{"id":"isabel_minute","host":"more.friends_a.isabel","cat":"world","t":{"zh":"每天看一幅画一分钟","en":"One painting, one minute"},"pic":"isabel/painting","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-19","2026-12-17"],"n":188,"why":["Our little still life — lemons, a glass, a knife — left for Tokyo yesterday. Its wall is empty for a month. So while it travels, let's each look at one painting a day. One full minute. Any painting: a museum, a book, your phone.","我们馆那幅小静物画——几个柠檬、一杯水、一把刀——昨天飞去东京了，它那面墙要空一个月。它在路上的这几天，我们每天各看一幅画，看满一分钟。哪幅都行：美术馆里的、书里的、手机上的。"],"D":[{"k":"先看满一分钟","say":["Most visitors give a famous painting less than half a minute. Today, set a timer for 60 seconds and don't read the label. Then tell me one thing you noticed.","大多数人在一幅名画前站不到半分钟。今天定一个 60 秒的闹钟，先别看说明牌。然后告诉我你注意到的一样东西。"],"line":"What I [notice] is the light.","z":"我注意到的是光。","from":"聊一幅画","crowd":[["isle.aiko","What I notice is the light — I looked at an old record cover, does that count? It felt like a painting.","我注意到的是光——我看的是一张老唱片封面，算吗？感觉就像一幅画。"],["isle.kenji","What I notice is… the dog. There is a dog in the corner! 40 seconds before I saw it.","我注意到的是……那条狗。角上有一条狗！我看了 40 秒才发现。"],["stars.emma","What I notice is the hands. Everyone's hands are busy. One minute is long, trust me — but worth it.","我注意到的是手。每个人的手都在忙。一分钟真的很长，相信我——但值得。"]],"shout":["Kenji, 40 seconds for the dog — that's exactly why we need the full minute. And Aiko, yes, a cover counts.","Kenji，过了 40 秒才看到那条狗——所以才要看满一分钟。Aiko，算的，封面也算。"]},{"k":"光是从哪来的","say":["Find the brightest spot, then ask: where is the light coming from? A window, a candle, nowhere at all? Painters choose it, like light on a stage.","找到画里最亮的地方，再问：光是从哪来的？一扇窗、一根蜡烛，还是哪儿都不是？光是画家挑的，就像舞台上的灯。"],"line":"The light [comes from] the left.","z":"光是从左边照过来的。","from":"聊一幅画","crowd":[["isle.mei","The light comes from the left. There's a window! I didn't see the window yesterday.","光是从左边照过来的。那儿有一扇窗！昨天我都没看到。"],["more.friends_a.arun","The light comes from the left — and the shadows agree. The painter was a good physicist.","光是从左边照过来的——影子也是这么说的。这位画家是个好物理学家。"],["isle.linhao","The light comes from… everywhere? It's a modern one. I think the painter cheated 😂","光是从……到处？这是一幅现代画。我觉得画家作弊了 😂"]],"shout":["Linhao, not cheating — choosing. 'Light from everywhere' is an answer too. Arun, I'm telling our conservator you said that.","林浩，不是作弊，是挑过的。「光从四面八方来」也是一个答案。Arun，你这句我要转告我们的修复师。"]},{"k":"看角落，不看中间","say":["The middle is where the painter wants you to look. The corners are where the secrets are. Today, spend your minute on the edges.","画中间是画家想让你看的地方，角落里才藏着秘密。今天这一分钟，只看画的四边。"],"line":"I [didn't see] that at first.","z":"我一开始没看到。","from":"聊一幅画","crowd":[["isle.bea","I didn't see that at first — a tiny boat, far away, bottom right. Now it's all I can see.","我一开始没看到——右下角，很远的地方有一条小船。现在我眼里只有它了。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","I didn't see that at first. At the Met, a man was crying in the corner of the painting. Not a real man. I think.","我一开始没看到。在大都会博物馆，一幅画的角落里有个男人在哭。不是真人。应该不是。"],["isle.kenji","I didn't see that at first: the painter's name is hidden on a stone. Like an easter egg.","我一开始没看到：画家的名字藏在一块石头上。像个彩蛋。"]],"shout":["Kenji found a signature on a stone. Painters often hid it like that. You're now officially looking like a curator.","Kenji 在一块石头上找到了签名。画家常常这样藏名字。你现在看画的样子，已经像个策展人了。"]},{"k":"它让你想起什么","say":["Tonight the crate lands in Tokyo — and rests a day before anyone opens it. While we wait: the second sentence. 'It makes me think of…' Only you can finish it.","今晚箱子就落地东京了——要先放一天，才有人打开。等的时候，我们说第二句：「它让我想起……」这句只有你自己能说完。"],"line":"It [reminds me of] my grandma's kitchen.","z":"它让我想起奶奶的厨房。","from":"聊一幅画","crowd":[["isle.mei","It reminds me of my grandma's kitchen. Same yellow light at four o'clock.","它让我想起外婆家的厨房。下午四点也是这样黄黄的光。"],["isle.linhao","It reminds me of my first week in Lyon. Everyone is walking, nobody is looking at me.","它让我想起我刚到里昂的第一周。每个人都在走路，没人看我。"],["isle.aiko","It reminds me of… my grandma's kitchen. Sorry, I just like this sentence. But it really does!","它让我想起……奶奶的厨房。不好意思，我就是喜欢这句。不过真的像！"]],"shout":["Linhao, that painting is now yours. Nobody else could have said that about it.","林浩，那幅画现在是你的了。别人谁也说不出你那句话。"]},{"k":"用两句话聊你的画","say":["Last day. Pick one painting and give it your two sentences: what you notice, and what it makes you think of. That's all you need to talk about art.","最后一天。挑一幅画，送它你的两句话：你注意到什么，它让你想起什么。聊画，有这两句就够了。"],"line":"What I [notice] is ___. It [reminds me of] ___.","z":"我注意到的是 ___。它让我想起 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","What I notice is the empty chair. It reminds me of my first day working from home.","我注意到的是那把空椅子。它让我想起我第一天在家上班。"],["isle.bea","What I notice is the little boat. It reminds me of the ferry to my lola's island.","我注意到的是那条小船。它让我想起去我外婆那座岛的渡船。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","What I notice is his shoes. They remind me of my dad's — always too clean.","我注意到的是他的鞋。它们让我想起我爸的鞋——永远太干净。"]],"shout":["Five days, five minutes of looking. Tomorrow the lid comes off in Tokyo — I'll show you our lemons, safe and sound.","五天，看了五分钟。明天东京那边就开箱了——我给你们看我们的柠檬，平平安安。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"ONE MINUTE","next":"isabel_talk"},"_sources":{"参观者在名画前停留中位数约 17 秒":"Smith, J. K. & Smith, L. F. (2001). Spending Time on Art. Empirical Studies of the Arts, 19(2), 229–236.","箱子到了先放一天再开：沿用 Isabel 11-23 动态的设定，没另找出处":"—"}},{"id":"jade_mornings","host":"more.friends_e.jade","cat":"move","t":{"zh":"7 天早上 10 分钟","en":"10 minutes, 7 mornings"},"pic":"jade/face","days":7,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":502,"why":["Half-marathon in eight weeks and my legs are already complaining — coaches get sore too, mate. No gym, no gear. I call it out, you move, all in English.","八周后跑半马，腿已经开始抗议了——教练也会酸痛的，伙计。不用健身房，不用器材。我喊口令，你跟着动，全程英语。"],"D":[{"k":"深蹲：往后坐","say":["Feet shoulder-width, chest up, and sit back like there's a chair behind you. Ten slow ones.","两脚和肩同宽，胸口挺起，往后坐，就像身后有把椅子。慢慢做十个。"],"line":"Chest up, [sit back].","z":"胸挺起，往后坐。","from":"健身口令","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Chest up, sit back… into the fridge again. My kitchen is too small for squats.","胸挺起，往后坐……又坐到冰箱上了。我的厨房太小，做不了深蹲。"],["isle.mei","Did ten before class. My legs are shaking lol","上课前做了十个。腿在抖 lol"],["isle.amara","Hotel room in Mumbai, 5 a.m. Chest up, sit back. The room service guy saw me.","孟买的酒店房间，早上五点。胸挺起，往后坐。送餐的小哥看到了。"]],"shout":["Kenji, try the hallway, mate. The fridge has had enough.","Kenji，去走廊做吧，伙计。冰箱受够了。"]},{"k":"平板支撑：收紧","say":["Elbows under your shoulders, body straight as a plank of wood — that's why it's called a plank. Twenty seconds. Knees down is fine.","手肘在肩膀正下方，身体直得像一块木板——所以叫 plank。二十秒。膝盖着地也行。"],"line":"[Engage] your core.","z":"收紧核心。","from":"健身口令","crowd":[["new_york.xiaoyu","Engage your core. I engaged it for 12 seconds. Then my core disengaged.","收紧核心。我收了 12 秒。然后核心自己松了。"],["isle.nadia","Twenty seconds on my knees. Boring, simple, done.","膝盖着地二十秒。无聊、简单、做完了。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu, 12 seconds today, 15 next week. That's how it works.","小雨，今天 12 秒，下周 15 秒。就是这么来的。"]},{"k":"弓步：往后一步","say":["Step back, lower the back knee towards the floor, slow. Hold a chair if you wobble — no shame.","往后退一步，后面的膝盖慢慢往地面放。站不稳就扶着椅子——不丢人。"],"line":"Step back, [knee down].","z":"往后退一步，膝盖往下。","from":"健身口令","crowd":[["isle.tom","Step back, knee down. Did them in the school kitchen at 7 before anyone came in. Cheers, Jade.","往后退一步，膝盖往下。七点在学校厨房做的，那时候还没人来。谢了，Jade。"],["isle.linhao","Held the chair the whole time. My flatmate joined me on day three!","全程扶着椅子。第三天室友也加入了！"]],"shout":["Linhao brought a mate. That's my favourite kind of progress.","林浩带了个朋友来。这是我最喜欢的那种进步。"]},{"k":"臀桥：到顶夹紧","say":["Lie on your back, knees bent, push your hips up. At the top, squeeze and hold for two. Then down slow.","躺下，膝盖弯起来，把屁股往上推。到最高处夹紧，停两秒。再慢慢放下。"],"line":"Squeeze at the [top].","z":"到最高处夹紧。","from":"健身口令","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Squeeze at the top. Finally, an exercise you do lying down. My favourite.","到最高处夹紧。终于有个躺着做的动作。我最喜欢。"],["isle.rosa","I did it on the floor and my son sat on me. Extra weight, he says.","我在地上做，我儿子坐到我身上。他说这叫加重。"]],"shout":["Rosa, your son's a natural coach. Maybe not on day four though.","Rosa，你儿子天生是教练。不过第四天就算了吧。"]},{"k":"俯卧撑：手在肩下","say":["Hands under your shoulders. Floor, knees, or against a wall — wall push-ups count, mate. Eight good ones.","手放在肩膀正下方。趴地上、跪着、靠墙都行——靠墙的也算，伙计。做八个标准的。"],"line":"Hands [under] your shoulders.","z":"手放在肩膀正下方。","from":"健身口令","crowd":[["isle.mei","Wall push-ups next to the tea fridge before my shift lol. My manager joined.","上班前在茶饮冰柜旁边做靠墙俯卧撑 lol。店长也加入了。"],["london.oliver","Did them on my knees. Hands under my shoulders. Eight. Nobody needs to know they were ugly.","跪着做的。手在肩膀下面。八个。没人需要知道它们有多难看。"]],"shout":["Oliver, ugly ones that get done beat perfect ones that don't. Every time.","Oliver，做完的难看的，永远比没做的完美的强。"]},{"k":"最后两个，喊出来","say":["Today we do all four, one after another. Breathe out on the way up. When it gets hard, you'll hear me: two more!","今天四个动作连着做。往上的时候呼气。累的时候，你会听到我喊：还有两个！"],"line":"Two more — [you've got this]!","z":"还有两个——你可以的！","from":"健身口令","crowd":[["isle.amara","Two more, you've got this! Shouted it in my Dubai flat. The neighbour knocked on the wall, honestly.","还有两个，你可以的！在迪拜的公寓里喊出来了。说真的，邻居敲墙了。"],["isle.kenji","Two more — you've got this! I said it to myself. It worked. I'm surprised too.","还有两个——你可以的！对自己说的。管用。我自己也吃惊。"]],"shout":["Amara, tell the neighbour to join. Kenji — talking to yourself is coaching yourself, mate.","Amara，叫隔壁一起来。Kenji——自言自语就是在给自己当教练，伙计。"]},{"k":"说说你这一周","say":["Last morning. Seven out of seven or two out of seven — tell me honestly. Then tell me what's next.","最后一个早上。七天做了七天，还是七天做了两天——老实告诉我。再说说接下来做什么。"],"line":"This week I [did] ___ out of seven. Tomorrow I'll ___.","z":"这周七天我做了 ___ 天。明天我要 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["new_york.xiaoyu","This week I did four out of seven. Tomorrow I'll do the plank. For 15 seconds.","这周七天我做了四天。明天我要做平板支撑。15 秒。"],["isle.tom","This week I did seven out of seven. Tomorrow I'll do it with my kids before school.","这周七天我做了七天。明天我要上学前跟孩子们一起做。"],["isle.mei","This week I did five out of seven. Tomorrow I'll do squats while the tea is brewing lol","这周七天我做了五天。明天泡茶的时候做深蹲 lol"]],"shout":["Four, five, seven — all of it counts. My long run is on Saturday. Wish my legs luck.","四天、五天、七天——都算数。我周六长跑。祝我的腿好运吧。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"7 MORNINGS","next":"nadia_5k"}},{"id":"jordi_map","host":"isle.jordi","cat":"world","t":{"zh":"一周看懂一张地图","en":"Read a map, really read it"},"pic":"jordi/corner","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":101,"why":["On Saturday I take 30 students to the Pyrenees. They can find any café on their phones, but give them a paper map and — home! — they're lost. This week we learn to read one. Come with us.","周六我要带 30 个学生去比利牛斯山。他们用手机找哪家咖啡馆都行，可给他们一张纸地图——伙计！——全迷路。这周我们一起学看地图，你也来。"],"D":[{"k":"先看角上的比例尺","say":["Before you look at anything, find the scale in the corner. On our hiking map, 1 centimetre is 250 metres. Now measure with your finger.","先别看别的，找角上的比例尺。我们的登山地图上，1 厘米是 250 米。现在用手指量一量。"],"line":"How [far] is it from here?","z":"离这儿多远？","from":"问路","crowd":[["isle.kenji","How far is it from here? My finger says 2 km to the station. Google says 2.1. Not bad!","离这儿多远？我的手指说到车站 2 公里，谷歌说 2.1。还行！"],["isle.mei","How far is it from here… I asked a tourist this today, but SHE asked ME 😂","离这儿多远……今天我想问一个游客，结果是她来问我 😂"],["new_york.xiaoyu","How fur is it — how FAR is it from here. Okay, 'far' like 'car'.","离这儿多……多远？好吧，far 跟 car 一个音。"]],"shout":["Kenji, 2 against 2.1 — you read the map better than half my class. Vale!","Kenji，2 对 2.1——你比我班上一半的人都会看。不错！"]},{"k":"线挤在一起，就是陡","say":["Those brown lines are contour lines. Each one joins points at the same height. Lines close together: steep. Far apart: easy walking.","那些棕色的线叫等高线，一条线连起一样高的地方。线挤在一起就是陡坡，线隔得远，路就好走。"],"line":"Is it [uphill] all the way?","z":"一路都是上坡吗？","from":"出门前问路线","crowd":[["stars.emma","Is it uphill all the way? — the only question I ask before any hike, trust me.","一路都是上坡吗？——我爬山前只问这一句，相信我。"],["isle.linhao","Is it uphill all the way? I looked at Lyon's map: Fourvière lines are SO close. That's why my legs hurt.","一路都是上坡吗？我看了里昂的地图，富维耶那边的线挤得好紧。难怪我腿疼。"],["isle.bea","Is it up-hill all the way? I say it like two words, is that okay?","一路都是上坡吗？我说成了两个词，可以吗？"]],"shout":["Linhao found his own hill on the map. That's exactly the point — the map explains your legs.","林浩在地图上找到了他自己的坡。要的就是这个：地图能解释你的腿为什么疼。"]},{"k":"地图会把东西变大","say":["On most world maps Greenland looks as big as Africa. Africa is about fourteen times bigger. The Mercator map was made in 1569 for sailors — great for ships, bad for sizes.","大多数世界地图上，格陵兰看着跟非洲一样大。其实非洲大约是它的十四倍。墨卡托地图是 1569 年给航海的人做的：对船好用，对大小不准。"],"line":"It's much [bigger than it looks].","z":"它比看上去大多了。","from":"聊看法","crowd":[["more.friends_b.farah","It's much bigger than it looks — I say this about the Grand Bazaar every single day.","它比看上去大多了——我每天都这么说伊斯坦布尔大巴扎。"],["isle.kenji","It's much bigger than it looks. I checked Japan on a different map. Japan is long!","它比看上去大多了。我在另一种地图上看了日本。日本好长！"],["isle.aiko","It's much bigger than it looks — said this about my ramen bowl at lunch, used it already.","它比看上去大多了——中午说的是我那碗拉面，已经用上了。"]],"shout":["Aiko used it on a bowl of ramen. Geography is everywhere, home.","Aiko 拿它说了一碗拉面。伙计，地理到处都是。"]},{"k":"找到那条河","say":["Old cities grew next to water. Barcelona sits between two rivers, the Llobregat and the Besòs. On your city's map, find the river first — then everything makes sense.","老城市都是挨着水长起来的。巴塞罗那夹在两条河中间：略夫雷加特河和贝索斯河。打开你城市的地图，先找河，其他的就都看懂了。"],"line":"Is it on [this side of] the river?","z":"在河的这一边吗？","from":"问路","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Is it on this side of the river? In Lyon there are two rivers, so this question is life or death.","在河的这一边吗？里昂有两条河，这个问题生死攸关。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Is it on this side of the river? Hangzhou: West Lake isn't a river, but I asked anyway lol","在河的这一边吗？杭州的西湖不是河，但我还是问了哈哈"],["isle.mei","Is it on this side of the river? Taipei has the Tamsui River — I never looked at it on a map before.","在河的这一边吗？台北有淡水河，我以前从来没在地图上看过它。"]],"shout":["Mei walks past that river all the time and only found it on the map today. That's my favourite kind of homework.","Mei 天天从那条河边过，今天才在地图上找到它。我最爱这种作业。"]},{"k":"用你的地图说一句","say":["Last day. Open a map of where you live and tell me something true about it, with the words from this week.","最后一天。打开你住的地方的地图，用这周学的说法，说一句关于它的真话。"],"line":"From my place, it's [about] ___ minutes to ___.","z":"从我家到 ___ 大概要 ___ 分钟。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","From my place, it's about twelve minutes to the river — and it's uphill all the way back.","从我家到河边大概要十二分钟——回来一路都是上坡。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","From my place, it's about forty minutes to the comedy club. Only twenty if the train comes.","从我家到喜剧俱乐部大概要四十分钟。要是车来了就二十分钟。"],["isle.bea","From my place, it's about an hour to Makati. On the map it's 9 km. Traffic is not on the map.","从我家到马卡蒂大概要一小时。地图上才 9 公里。堵车可不在地图上。"]],"shout":["Bea: 'Traffic is not on the map.' I'm stealing that for my class. We're back from the Pyrenees — photos from the moraine tonight.","Bea 说「堵车可不在地图上」——这句我要拿去给学生讲。我们从比利牛斯山回来了，今晚发冰碛那儿的照片。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"MAP READER","next":"jordi_glacier"},"_sources":{"等高线：一条线连起一样高的点，越密越陡":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contour_line","非洲约 3037 万 km²、格陵兰约 217 万 km²（约 14 倍）；墨卡托投影 1569":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercator_projection","巴塞罗那在略夫雷加特河和贝索斯河之间":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography_of_Barcelona","富维耶山、里昂的罗讷河和索恩河":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyon","淡水河流经台北":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamsui_River"}},{"id":"kenji_standup","host":"isle.kenji","cat":"say","t":{"zh":"一周用英语开站会","en":"Speak up at stand-up"},"pic":"kenji/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":97,"why":["Yesterday was my first English stand-up. I only said “No blockers.” This week I want to say more. Maybe you have meetings too? Let's practise one line a day, together.","昨天是我第一次用英语开站会，我只说了一句 No blockers。这周我想多说一点。你可能也要开会吧？我们一起，每天练一句。"],"D":[{"k":"昨天做了什么","say":["Stand-up starts with yesterday. I think one short sentence is enough. Verb in the past, then the thing.","站会先说昨天。我觉得一句短的就够了。动词用过去式，后面接做了什么。"],"line":"Yesterday I [worked on] the login page.","z":"我昨天在弄登录页面。","from":"工作会议","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Yesterday I worked on the slides for our group project. Very many slides.","我昨天在弄小组作业的 PPT。非常多的 PPT。"],["isle.mei","Yesterday I worked on the new winter menu. Does that count as a stand-up?","我昨天在弄冬季新菜单。这算站会吗？"],["isle.daniel","Yesterday I worked on Haruka's interview answers. Short and clear — nice one, Kenji.","我昨天在帮 Haruka 改面试回答。又短又清楚，Kenji 这招好。"]],"shout":["Mei, yes, it counts! Every team has a stand-up, maybe not standing.","Mei，算的！每个团队都有站会，只是不一定站着。"]},{"k":"说出问题在哪","say":["Today I must explain my time zone bug. My plan: say the cause first, details later. Wish me luck.","今天我得讲那个时区 bug。我的计划：先说原因，细节放后面。祝我好运。"],"line":"I found [the root cause]. It's a time zone issue.","z":"我找到根本原因了，是时区的问题。","from":"讲一个 bug","crowd":[["isle.linhao","I found the root cause. It's a time zone issue — my mum calls me at 3 a.m. 😂","我找到根本原因了，是时区的问题——我妈凌晨三点给我打电话 😂"],["isle.aiko","I found the root cause. It's a cable issue. The amp works again!","我找到根本原因了，是线的问题。音箱又能响了！"],["isle.amara","I found the root cause of my jet lag. It's a five-cities-a-week issue.","我找到倒不过时差的根本原因了，是一周飞五座城的问题。"]],"shout":["I did it at stand-up today! Someone said “Nice catch!” Amara — your bug is harder than mine.","我今天在站会上说了！有人回了句 Nice catch！Amara——你的 bug 比我的难修。"]},{"k":"请人帮你看一眼","say":["Asking for help is normal here. This phrase is polite and easy to understand. I learned it from a senior engineer.","在这儿请人帮忙很正常。这个说法客气，一听就懂。我是跟一个老工程师学的。"],"line":"The fix is small, but I'd like [a second pair of eyes].","z":"改动不大，但我想请人再帮我看一眼。","from":"请同事帮忙","crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","My visa form is done, but I'd like a second pair of eyes. Mum is already looking.","签证表填好了，但我想请人再帮我看一眼。我妈已经在看了。"],["more.friends_a.rachel","Lovely line, Kenji. Tip: stress ‘second’ and ‘eyes’ — the rest is quick.","这句很好，Kenji。小提示：重读 second 和 eyes，其他的快快带过。"],["isle.bea","The video is done, but I'd like a second pair of eyes. Who wants to watch 30 seconds of noodles?","视频剪好了，但我想请人帮我看一眼。谁想看 30 秒的面条？"]],"shout":["Rachel's tip helped me a lot. Second… eyes. I practised in the shower.","Rachel 的小提示帮了我大忙。second……eyes。我在洗澡的时候练了。"]},{"k":"卡住时先开口","say":["When I freeze, I say “Quick question” and breathe. It gives me two seconds. Then I ask.","我卡住的时候，就先说 Quick question，然后喘口气。能多争取两秒钟，再问。"],"line":"[Quick question] — can you walk me through it?","z":"问一下——你能一步步给我讲讲吗？","from":"开会时提问","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Quick question — can you walk me through it? Camille walked me through her part. Very clear.","问一下，你能一步步给我讲讲吗？Camille 把她那部分给我一步步讲了，很清楚。"],["isle.mei","Quick question! Can you walk me through the new tea machine? It has 40 buttons.","问一下！新的茶饮机你能一步步教我吗？它有 40 个按钮。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Quick question — can you walk me through why my joke didn't land?","问一下，你能一步步给我讲讲，我那个笑话为什么没人笑吗？"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu — I think nobody can walk you through that. But I laughed.","Xiaoyu——我觉得这个谁也讲不清。不过我笑了。"]},{"k":"说你自己的站会","say":["Last day. Your own stand-up: yesterday and today, two sentences. Work, school, home — all okay.","最后一天。你自己的站会：昨天、今天，两句话。工作、上学、家里的事都行。"],"line":"Yesterday I ___. Today I'm [going to] ___.","z":"我昨天 ___。今天我要 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.linhao","Yesterday I rehearsed with my team. Today I'm going to make hotpot for them. Spicy, of course.","我昨天跟组员排练了。今天我要给他们做火锅。当然是辣的。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Yesterday I passed my visa interview. Today I'm going to tell everyone. Sorry, everyone.","我昨天签证面试通过了。今天我要告诉所有人。所有人，打扰了。"],["more.friends_e.hana","Yesterday I tidied a kitchen with 200 plastic bags in it. Today I'm going to rest.","我昨天收拾了一个塞着 200 个塑料袋的厨房。今天我要休息。"]],"shout":["Five days. On Monday I said two words. Today I talked for twenty minutes with Bangalore. You can too, I think.","五天。周一我只说了两个词，今天我跟班加罗尔的同事说了二十分钟。我觉得你也可以。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"STAND-UP","next":"kenji_demo"}},{"id":"kwame_afrobeats","host":"isle.kwame","cat":"world","t":{"zh":"一周听懂 Afrobeats","en":"Afrobeats, one week"},"pic":"kwame/studio","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-23","2026-12-21"],"n":96,"why":["Chale, my beat Harmattan is past 100k views, and half the comments are asking what Afrobeats even is. So for five days I play you one song a day and we talk about it — the Accra way.","伙计，我那段 beat《Harmattan》播放过十万了，一半的评论在问 Afrobeats 到底是什么。那这五天我每天给你放一首歌，我们聊聊它——阿克拉的聊法。"],"D":[{"k":"先问歌叫什么","say":["Day one: just listen. Afrobeats with an s is today's pop from Lagos and Accra. Afrobeat without the s is Fela Kuti, 1970s. One letter, fifty years. Like the song? Ask its name.","第一天：先听。带 s 的 Afrobeats 是今天拉各斯和阿克拉的流行乐；不带 s 的 Afrobeat 是七十年代 Fela Kuti 的音乐。差一个字母，差五十年。喜欢这首？那就问它叫什么。"],"line":"What's this song [called]?","z":"这首歌叫什么？","from":"聊音乐","crowd":[["isle.aiko","What's this song called? — asked a customer in my record shop today. She showed me her phone. Afrobeats!","这首歌叫什么？——今天我在唱片店问了一个客人。她给我看手机。是 Afrobeats！"],["isle.mei","What's this song call — CALLED. The 'd' is so small, I keep losing it.","这首歌叫……叫什么？那个 d 太小了，我老是丢。"],["isle.amara","What's this song called? My dear Kwame, I'm from Lagos. I KNOW what it's called 😏","这首歌叫什么？亲爱的 Kwame，我是拉各斯长大的。我当然知道它叫什么 😏"]],"shout":["Amara, okay okay, Lagos wins today. Aiko asked a real stranger in a real shop — that's the move.","Amara，好好好，今天算拉各斯赢。Aiko 在真的店里问了一个真的陌生人——就该这么干。"]},{"k":"它听起来像什么","say":["Before Afrobeats there was highlife — Ghana's guitar-and-horns music from the early 1900s. Fela mixed highlife with jazz and funk. Listen for the guitar that keeps going round and round.","Afrobeats 之前有 highlife——二十世纪初就在加纳出现的、用吉他和铜管的音乐。Fela 把 highlife 跟爵士、放克混在一起。注意听那段一直转圈的吉他。"],"line":"It [sounds a bit like] something my dad plays.","z":"听起来有点像我爸常放的歌。","from":"聊音乐","crowd":[["isle.rosa","It sounds a bit like something my dad plays — cumbia! Same happy guitar.","听起来有点像我爸常放的歌——昆比亚！一样欢快的吉他。"],["isle.kenji","It sounds a bit like something my dad plays… city pop? Is that crazy?","听起来有点像我爸常放的歌……城市流行？我是不是疯了？"],["more.friends_a.isabel","It sounds a bit like the music in the café below the museum. I never asked what it was. Now I will.","听起来有点像美术馆楼下咖啡馆放的音乐。我从来没问过是什么。现在我要问了。"]],"shout":["Kenji, not crazy at all, bro. Rosa found cumbia in it. Music travels more than people do.","Kenji，一点不疯，兄弟。Rosa 听出了昆比亚。音乐比人跑得还远。"]},{"k":"I'm coming 是要走","say":["In Accra, 'I'm coming' means I'm leaving now, but I'll be back. My mum waited eight hours once. Outside Ghana, say the safe version.","在阿克拉，「I'm coming」的意思是我先走、等下回来。我妈有一次等了我八个小时。在加纳以外，说保险的那句。"],"line":"[I'll be right back.]","z":"我马上回来。","from":"临时走开","crowd":[["new_york.xiaoyu","I'll be right back. — said it on stage when I forgot my next joke. The crowd laughed anyway.","我马上回来。——我在台上忘了下一个段子时说的。观众还是笑了。"],["isle.bea","I'll be right back. In Manila we say 'wait lang'. So many ways to say five minutes that are not five minutes.","我马上回来。在马尼拉我们说 wait lang。说「五分钟」又不是五分钟的说法可真多。"],["isle.linhao","I'll be right back. Wait, so in Ghana 'I'm coming' is going? My brain hurts, chale.","我马上回来。等等，所以在加纳「我来了」是要走？我脑子疼，伙计。"]],"shout":["Linhao said chale! Ghana is proud of you, for real.","林浩说了 chale！加纳为你骄傲，说真的。"]},{"k":"说它火了","say":["My beat is blowing up because dancers keep using it — four more today. That's how songs travel now: a dance first, the name later. Tell someone about a song that's blowing up where you live.","我的 beat 火起来，是因为舞者一直在用它——今天又多了四个。现在歌就是这么走出去的：先有舞，后有名字。跟人说说你那儿正在火的一首歌。"],"line":"This song is [blowing up] right now.","z":"这首歌最近火了。","from":"聊网上的事","crowd":[["isle.mei","This song is blowing up right now — every customer is humming it. I make drinks to it all day.","这首歌最近火了——每个客人都在哼。我一整天跟着它做饮料。"],["isle.aiko","This song is blowing up right now in Tokyo, but it's from 1984. Old songs blow up too!","这首歌最近在东京火了，可它是 1984 年的。老歌也会火！"],["isle.kenji","This song is blowing up — I mean blowing UP, not blowing. Okay, I sounded like a bomb.","这首歌最近火了——是 blowing up，不是 blowing。好吧，我刚才听起来像颗炸弹。"]],"shout":["Aiko is right: old songs blow up too. Tomorrow's the last day — get your song ready.","Aiko 说得对，老歌也会火。明天最后一天——把你的歌准备好。"]},{"k":"说你单曲循环的歌","say":["Last day, and my question for everyone: what's on repeat for you? Tomorrow Esi and I film part two on the beach in Accra. Your songs are coming with us.","最后一天，我问大家一个问题：你在单曲循环什么？明天我和 Esi 去阿克拉的海边拍第二段。你们的歌我们带着。"],"line":"I've had ___ [on repeat] all week.","z":"这一周我一直在单曲循环 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.mei","I've had your Harmattan on repeat all week. The customers asked what it's called. I told them!","这一周我一直在单曲循环你的《Harmattan》。客人问它叫什么，我告诉他们了！"],["isle.amara","I've had my mum's old highlife tape on repeat all week. On a plane, in the hotel, everywhere.","这一周我一直在单曲循环我妈那盘老 highlife 磁带。飞机上、酒店里，到处放。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","I've had the subway guy's drum on repeat all week. No name. He plays at 14th Street.","这一周我一直在单曲循环地铁里那个大哥的鼓。没有名字。他在 14 街打。"]],"shout":["Medaase — thank you, everybody. Mei, you sent my song to Taipei. Chale, we made this together.","Medaase——谢谢大家。Mei，你把我的歌带到了台北。伙计，这是我们一起做出来的。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"ON REPEAT","next":"kwame_twi"},"_sources":{"Afrobeats（带 s）= 2000 年后西非流行乐的统称":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afrobeats","Afrobeat（不带 s）= Fela Kuti 七十年代，混合 highlife、爵士、放克":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afrobeat","highlife 二十世纪初起源于加纳":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highlife","Medaase = 契维语「谢谢」":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twi"}},{"id":"linhao_phone","host":"isle.linhao","cat":"life","t":{"zh":"一周搞定出国的电话","en":"Phone calls abroad, sorted"},"pic":"linhao/class","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-19","2026-12-17"],"n":143,"why":["In December my parents come to Europe for the first time, and we'll spend three days in London. I have to book, change, ask — all on the phone. For me the phone is scarier than a presentation: no face. So I'm practising one call a day. Join me?","十二月我爸妈第一次来欧洲，我们要在伦敦待三天。订、改、问，全得打电话。对我来说，打电话比做汇报还可怕：看不到脸。所以我每天练一通电话。一起吗？"],"D":[{"k":"一开口就说来意","say":["Camille told me: on the phone, say why you're calling in the first sentence. Then the other person can help you fast.","Camille 跟我说：打电话第一句就说你为什么打来，对方才能马上帮你。"],"line":"Hi, I'd like to [book a table] for four at seven.","z":"你好，我想订一张四个人的桌子，七点。","from":"订餐厅","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Hi, I'd like to book a table for one at seven. Just me. As usual.","你好，我想订一个人的位子，七点。就我自己，跟平时一样。"],["isle.mei","Hi, I'd like to book a table for four at seven — I said ‘seven’ like ‘seben’ at first lol","你好，我想订四个人的桌子，七点——我一开始把 seven 说成了 seben 哈哈"],["stars.emma","Classic! Tip: say the number twice. ‘Four people — four.’ Phones eat numbers, trust me.","经典！小窍门：数字说两遍。Four people — four。电话最容易吞数字，相信我。"]],"shout":["Emma's tip is so useful: say the number twice. I tried it — the restaurant got it the first time.","Emma 的窍门太有用了：数字说两遍。我试了，餐厅一次就听对了。"]},{"k":"打电话改个时间","say":["My parents' flight changed, so I must move the hotel. ‘Instead’ at the end makes it clear what's new.","我爸妈的航班改了，酒店也得跟着改。句尾加个 instead，对方就知道新的是哪天。"],"line":"Could I [move it to] Saturday instead?","z":"能改到周六吗？","from":"改预约","crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","Could I move it to Saturday instead? I asked my dentist this. It worked!","能改到周六吗？我问牙医的时候就用了这句。成了！"],["more.friends_e.hana","Good one. I'd add your name and the old day first: ‘It's Lin, booked for Friday.’ Saves time.","这句好。我会先报名字和原来的日子：It's Lin, booked for Friday。省时间。"],["isle.bea","Could I move it to Saturday instead? Said it to a homestay in Hội An. In English. They said yes!","能改到周六吗？我对会安的一家民宿说的，用英语。他们说可以！"]],"shout":["Hana is a real organiser — name first, old day, then the new day. I wrote it on a sticky note.","Hana 真是会安排的人：先报名字、原来的日子，再说新日子。我写在便利贴上了。"]},{"k":"听不清就请对方拼","say":["Names and emails are the hardest on the phone. Don't guess — ask them to spell it. Everyone does this, even natives.","电话里最难听清的是名字和邮箱。别猜，请对方拼出来。人人都这样，母语的人也是。"],"line":"Sorry, could you [spell that] for me?","z":"不好意思，能帮我拼一下吗？","from":"电话里没听清","crowd":[["london.oliver","I ask this in every interview. Twice, sometimes. Spelling ‘Walthamstow’ is a sport.","我每次采访都要问这句，有时候问两遍。拼 Walthamstow 简直是一项运动。"],["isle.kenji","Sorry, could you spell that for me? Then I typed the email wrong anyway 😅","不好意思，能帮我拼一下吗？结果我邮箱还是打错了 😅"],["isle.mei","Could you spell that for me? Also useful for customers' names on cups!","能帮我拼一下吗？在杯子上写客人名字的时候也用得上！"]],"shout":["Oliver is a journalist and he still asks twice. That made me feel much better.","Oliver 是记者，他都还要问两遍。我一下子轻松多了。"]},{"k":"有问题，客气地说","say":["Complaining is hard for me — I don't want to be rude. Start with ‘I'm afraid’. It's polite, but it's clear something is wrong.","投诉对我来说很难，我不想没礼貌。用 I'm afraid 开头，客气，但对方一听就知道出问题了。"],"line":"I'm afraid there's [a problem with] my order.","z":"不好意思，我的订单有点问题。","from":"投诉","crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","I'm afraid there's a problem with my order — the shop sent two left shoes. True story.","不好意思，我的订单有点问题——店家寄来两只左脚的鞋。真事。"],["isle.amara","Passengers say this to me every day. When they say it nicely, I try extra hard. Honestly.","乘客每天都这么跟我说。说得客气的，我会格外用心帮。真的。"],["isle.kenji","I'm afraid there's a problem with my order. My konbini lunch had no chopsticks.","不好意思，我的订单有点问题。便利店的午饭没给筷子。"]],"shout":["Amara says polite people get extra help. So ‘I'm afraid’ is not weak — it's smart.","Amara 说客气的人会得到更多帮助。所以 I'm afraid 不是软弱，是聪明。"]},{"k":"打你自己的电话","say":["Last day. Think of a call you really need to make — change, cancel, ask. Say the first sentence.","最后一天。想一个你真要打的电话：改、取消、还是问。把第一句说出来。"],"line":"Hi, I'm [calling to] ___ my booking for ___.","z":"你好，我打电话来是想 ___ 我 ___ 的预订。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.rosa","Hi, I'm calling to check my booking for the Saturday market. My daughter was listening. She said, ‘Good, Mamá.’","你好，我打电话来是想确认周六市集的摊位预订。我女儿在旁边听着，她说：「不错嘛，妈。」"],["isle.xiaoyu","Hi, I'm calling to change my booking for the flight to London. Practising for next year!","你好，我打电话来是想改去伦敦的机票。为明年练的！"],["isle.aiko","Hi, I'm calling to cancel my booking for Friday. The band can't come. Sad.","你好，我打电话来是想取消周五的预订。乐队来不了了。好难过。"]],"shout":["I made the real call to the London hotel today. Three minutes, no panic. My mum asked, “Who taught you?” I said: all of you.","今天我真的给伦敦的酒店打了电话。三分钟，一点没慌。我妈问：「谁教你的？」我说：你们大家。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"CALLED","next":"linhao_shop"}},{"id":"linhao_qunliao","learn":"zh","zh_of":"bea_taglish","host":"isle.linhao","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"看懂宿舍群聊","en":"Crack the group chat"},"hook":["学了两年中文的 Camille，看林浩的宿舍群聊一句都看不懂。「栓Q」到底是不是谢谢？","Camille has studied Chinese for two years and can't read one line of Linhao's group chat. Is 栓Q a thank-you or not?"],"pic":"linhao/hotpot","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-21","2026-12-19"],"n":129,"why":["My French teammate Camille has studied Chinese for two years. I showed her my old dorm group chat and she couldn't read one line. ‘Shuān Q? Is that English?’ lol. Five days, five messages from the chat — let's crack them together.","我的法国组员 Camille 学了两年中文。我给她看我们宿舍以前的群聊，她一句都看不懂。「栓Q？这是英语吗？」哈哈。五天，五条群聊消息，我们一起破解。"],"D":[{"k":"绝了是好还是坏","say":["Today's message: ‘这家火锅绝了！’ 绝了 means ‘nothing beats it’ — usually amazing. But said with a sigh, it can mean ‘unbelievable’ in a bad way. Listen to the tone.","今天这条：「这家火锅绝了！」「绝了」就是没得比——一般是夸。可叹着气说，也可能是「离谱」。听语气。"],"line":"This hotpot place is [amazing]!","z":"这家火锅绝了！","from":"群聊","crowd":[["stars.emma","This hotpot place is amazing! — Chengdu, last spring. I cried. Chili tears.","这家火锅绝了！——去年春天在成都。我哭了，辣哭的。"],["chengdu.zhouyao","Online people also say 绝绝子, but now it sounds a bit… 2021.","网上还有人说「绝绝子」，不过现在听起来有点……2021 年。"],["isle.kenji","This ramen place is amazing! I used it for Japanese food. Allowed?","这家拉面绝了！我拿来夸日本菜。可以吧？"]],"shout":["Kenji, totally allowed — anything can be 绝了. Zhou Yao is right, 绝绝子 is a bit last season lol.","Kenji，完全可以——什么都能「绝了」。周瑶说得对，「绝绝子」有点过时了哈哈。"]},{"k":"破防了","say":["My roommate wrote: ‘看完这个视频我破防了。’ 破防 comes from games — your defence breaks. Now it means something hit you right in the heart, sad or moved. It was a word of the year in 2021.","室友写：「看完这个视频我破防了。」「破防」是从游戏来的——防御被打破了。现在是说一下子被戳中了，难过或者感动都行。它是 2021 年的流行语。"],"line":"That video got me — I [lost it].","z":"看完这个视频我破防了。","from":"群聊","crowd":[["more.world.priya","That video got me — a grandma learning to use her phone. I'm fine. I'm not fine.","看完这个视频我破防了——一个奶奶学用手机。我没事。我有事。"],["isle.aiko","I lost it when the record shop next door closed. Thirty years.","隔壁唱片店关门，我破防了。开了三十年。"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Careful: saying a person 破防了 can also mean they got upset in an argument.","注意：说一个人「破防了」，也可能是吵架时被说急了。"]],"shout":["Aiko, I'm sorry about the shop. Zhao Lei's warning is real — context is everything.","Aiko，唱片店的事真难过。赵磊的提醒很对——要看上下文。"]},{"k":"这周末躺平","say":["Friday night in the chat: ‘这周末我躺平了。’ 躺平 is lying flat — doing nothing, on purpose. People also use it about life: not chasing money and promotions. Another 2021 word of the year.","周五晚上的群聊：「这周末我躺平了。」「躺平」就是平躺着，故意什么都不干。也有人拿来说人生：不拼钱、不拼升职。也是 2021 年的流行语。"],"line":"This weekend I'm just [lying flat].","z":"这周末我躺平了。","from":"群聊","crowd":[["isle.amara","This weekend I'm just lying flat. Five cities, now only a sofa. I earned it.","这周末我躺平了。飞了五座城，现在只要沙发。我应得的。"],["beijing.chenhao","Programmers say this every Friday. By Monday, nobody is flat.","程序员每个周五都这么说。到了周一，没人躺得平。"],["isle.rosa","I tried. My stand opens on Saturday. Lying flat — next life.","我试了。周六摊子要开门。躺平下辈子再说。"]],"shout":["Rosa, ‘lying flat — next life’ is real Chinese humour. Chen Hao, too true.","Rosa，「躺平下辈子再说」——你这已经是中国式幽默了。陈浩，太真实了。"]},{"k":"栓Q 不是谢谢","say":["The one Camille hated most: ‘又要加班，栓Q。’ It's internet slang: 栓Q sounds like ‘thank you’, but it means the opposite — ‘great, just great’. Never say it to your boss lol.","Camille 最头疼的一条：「又要加班，栓Q。」这是网络用语，「栓Q」听着像 thank you，意思却正好相反：真是「谢谢」了。千万别对老板说哈哈。"],"line":"Overtime again? [Thanks a lot].","z":"又要加班，栓Q。","from":"群聊","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Overtime again? Thanks a lot. My Japanese colleagues didn't get it. My Chinese one laughed.","又要加班，栓Q。日本同事没懂，中国同事笑了。"],["isle.nadia","Rain again? Thanks a lot. London weather, my favourite.","又下雨，栓Q。伦敦天气，我最爱。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","My daughter says this when I ask about her homework. Now I understand.","我问女儿作业，她就回我「栓Q」。现在我懂了。"]],"shout":["Chen Jian, now you know what your daughter means. Nadia, London weather deserves a 栓Q forever.","Chen Jian，现在你知道女儿什么意思了。Nadia，伦敦天气永远值得一句栓Q。"]},{"k":"发你自己的一条","say":["Last day. Write your own message for the group chat: something you got right this week, plus 拿捏了 — ‘nailed it’. A word of the year in 2022. Camille's: 点奶茶，拿捏了.","最后一天。给群聊写一条你自己的：这周你搞定了什么，再加一句「拿捏了」——稳稳拿下。它是 2022 年的流行语。Camille 的那条：「点奶茶，拿捏了。」"],"line":"___ — [nailed it].","z":"___，拿捏了。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.aiko","Ordering in Chinese at a Taipei night market — nailed it.","台北夜市用中文点吃的，拿捏了。"],["more.world.priya","Phone call with my Shanghai client — nailed it. Mostly.","跟上海客户打电话，拿捏了。差不多吧。"],["isle.bea","Noodles with chopsticks, no fork — nailed it.","用筷子吃面，不用叉子，拿捏了。"]],"shout":["Camille read the whole group chat today and replied 绝了. My roommates are shocked. Five days — you all 拿捏了.","Camille 今天把整个群聊都看懂了，还回了一句「绝了」。我室友都惊了。五天——大家都拿捏了。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"拿捏了","next":"linhao_qunliao2"},"_sources":["「破防」「躺平」入选《咬文嚼字》2021 年十大流行语：中新网 2021-12-08 https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cul/2021/12-08/9624872.shtml","「拿捏」入选《咬文嚼字》2022 年十大流行语：中新网 2022-12-26 https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cul/2022/12-26/9921582.shtml","「栓Q（我真的会谢）」列《语言文字周报》2022 年十大网络流行语之首：京报网 2022-12-26 https://news.bjd.com.cn/2022/12/26/10277297.shtml","「绝绝子」入选国家语言资源监测与研究中心 2021 年度十大网络用语：澎湃 https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_15782003"],"_note":"学中文的人用的中文版（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"linhao_qunliao2","learn":"zh","host":"isle.linhao","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"看懂小组作业群","en":"Crack the class group chat"},"hook":["Camille 被拉进了小组作业群。一晚上 99+ 条，她只回了一个微笑表情——结果大家以为她生气了。","Camille got added to the group-project chat. 99+ messages in one night, and she replied with one 🙂 — everyone thought she was annoyed."],"pic":"linhao/class","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":142,"why":["Round two! Camille can read my dorm chat now. But this term we're doing a group project with four Chinese classmates, and the project chat is another world: 收到, 接龙, @所有人… She sent the 🙂 once. Big mistake lol. Five days, five things that happen in every Chinese class chat.","第二轮！Camille 宿舍群已经看得懂了。可这学期我们跟四个中国同学做小组作业，作业群又是另一个世界：收到、接龙、@所有人……她发过一次那个微笑表情。大错特错哈哈。五天，五件每个中国班级群都会发生的事。"],"D":[{"k":"收到就回收到","say":["Every class chat has this: the teacher or class rep posts a notice, and then — 收到, 收到, 收到, a whole column. 收到 means ‘got it’. Reply so they know you saw it.","每个班级群都这样：老师或班长发个通知，下面一排「收到」「收到」「收到」。「收到」就是我看到了、知道了。回一句，人家知道你看见了。"],"line":"[Got it], thanks!","z":"[收到]，谢谢！","from":"群聊","crowd":[["isle.mei","My Taipei office group replies 收到 too. Some people just send 👌.","我台北公司的群也回「收到」。有人干脆只发个 👌。"],["isle.kenji","Got it, thanks! …I replied that to my Chinese colleague's lunch photo. Wrong moment.","收到，谢谢！……我是对中国同事的午饭照片这么回的。时机不对。"],["beijing.chenhao","My boss counts the 收到s. If yours is missing, she @s you.","我们老板会数「收到」。少了你的，她就 @你。"]],"shout":["Kenji, 收到 to a lunch photo — I laughed for a whole minute. Chen Hao, your boss is scary.","Kenji，对午饭照片回「收到」——我笑了一分钟。陈浩，你老板好吓人。"]},{"k":"接龙是什么龙","say":["Camille: ‘Why is everyone copying the same message?’ That's 接龙 — a relay list. Someone starts: 周五聚餐，要去的接龙：1. 林浩. You copy it, add your name, send it back. WeChat groups even have a 接龙 tool.","Camille：「为什么大家都在复制同一条？」这就是「接龙」。有人开个头：「周五聚餐，要去的接龙：1. 林浩」，你复制下来，加上自己的名字，再发出去。微信群里还有专门的接龙工具。"],"line":"Dinner on Friday — if you're coming, [add your name].","z":"周五聚餐，要去的[接龙]。","from":"群聊","crowd":[["isle.mei","1. 林浩 2. Mei 3. — wait, I'm in Taipei. Deleting myself.","1. 林浩 2. Mei 3.——等等，我在台北。把自己删了。"],["stars.emma","My Shanghai hostel uses 接龙 for free dumpling night. I was number 14!","我在上海住的青旅，免费包饺子那晚也用接龙。我排第 14！"],["more.world.priya","My client's office orders lunch like this. Twenty names, twenty bowls of noodles.","我客户的公司点午饭就这么接龙。二十个名字，二十碗面。"]],"shout":["Emma, number 14 is still worth it — it's dumplings. Mei, deleting yourself from a dinner list is very polite.","Emma，排第 14 也值，那可是饺子。Mei，把自己从聚餐名单里删掉，太有礼貌了。"]},{"k":"@所有人 别错过","say":["When a message starts with @所有人 — ‘@everyone’ — read it. Everyone's phone buzzes, so people use it for real news: deadline moved, room changed. In WeChat groups it's usually the group owner who sends it.","看到开头是「@所有人」的，一定要看。所有人的手机都会响，所以一般是真有事才用：截止日期改了、教室换了。微信群里一般是群主发。"],"line":"[@everyone] Tomorrow's meeting is moved to 3 pm.","z":"[@所有人] 明天的会改到下午三点了。","from":"群聊","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I saw an @所有人 at midnight and panicked. It was the class photo.","半夜看到一条 @所有人，吓了一跳。结果是发合照。"],["beijing.chenhao","Our team lead uses @所有人 for birthday cake too. Cake is real news.","我们组长发生日蛋糕也 @所有人。蛋糕也是正事。"],["isle.nadia","My Chinese class has a group too. @所有人: no class on Monday. Best message ever.","我的中文班也有群。@所有人：周一不上课。史上最好的消息。"]],"shout":["Chen Hao, agreed — cake counts. Nadia, ‘no class on Monday’ is the best @所有人 in history.","陈浩，同意——蛋糕算。Nadia，「周一不上课」是史上最好的 @所有人。"]},{"k":"哈哈哈还是呵呵","say":["Camille's big mistake: the 🙂 face. In Chinese chats it often reads as cold — like 呵呵, a polite ‘heh’ that can feel fake. If it's funny, send 哈哈哈 — more 哈 means funnier. And if someone 拍了拍 you — double-taps your avatar — they just want you to say something.","Camille 的大错：那个微笑表情。在中文群里，它常常让人觉得冷冰冰——跟「呵呵」一样，客气地笑一声，听着有点假。真觉得好笑，就发「哈哈哈」，哈越多越好笑。还有，有人「拍了拍」你——就是双击你的头像——是想让你出来说句话。"],"line":"That's so funny, [hahaha]!","z":"太好笑了[哈哈哈哈]！","from":"群聊","crowd":[["isle.mei","In Taiwan we type 哈哈哈 too. And 笑死 — ‘I'm dying’.","台湾也打「哈哈哈」。还有「笑死」。"],["isle.kenji","I sent 呵呵 to my Chinese colleague for a month. She thought I hated her. We're friends now.","我给中国同事回了一个月「呵呵」。她以为我讨厌她。现在我们是朋友了。"],["stars.emma","My Chengdu friend never types. Just a sticker. A panda. Always the same panda.","我成都的朋友从来不打字，只发表情包。一只熊猫。永远是那只熊猫。"]],"shout":["Kenji — a month of 呵呵! So glad you're friends now. Emma, every Chinese friend has that one sticker.","Kenji——回了一个月「呵呵」！还好你们现在是朋友了。Emma，每个中国朋友都有一张自己的表情包。"]},{"k":"在群里问一句","say":["Last day. Ask your own group something. Start with 有没有人 — ‘does anyone…?’ It's the most useful line in any group: anyone got notes, anyone going, anyone know. Camille's: 有没有人明天帮我带个充电器？ Three people said 我有.","最后一天。在你自己的群里问一句。用「有没有人」开头——群里最好用的一句：有没有人有笔记、有没有人去、有没有人知道。Camille 发的是：「有没有人明天帮我带个充电器？」三个人回了「我有」。"],"line":"[Does anyone] ___?","z":"[有没有人]___？","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.aiko","Does anyone know a good hotpot place near the station? Seven answers in five minutes.","有没有人知道车站附近哪家火锅好吃？五分钟七个人回我。"],["more.world.priya","Does anyone have Monday's slides? Asked my Chinese class group. Got them in one minute.","有没有人有周一的课件？发在我中文班的群里，一分钟就收到了。"],["isle.bea","Does anyone want to practise Chinese with me? Someone 拍了拍 me. That's a yes, right?","有没有人想跟我练中文？有人拍了拍我。这算答应了吧？"]],"shout":["Bea, a 拍了拍 is definitely a yes. Camille has replied 收到 four times this week — she's one of us now. Thanks, everyone — 哈哈哈哈.","Bea，被拍了拍肯定是答应了。Camille 这周已经回过四次「收到」了，她是自己人了。谢谢大家——哈哈哈哈。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"收到","next":"linhao_qunliao3"},"_note":"学中文的人用的活动（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。 接着 linhao_qunliao（Camille）。微信的「接龙」工具、「拍一拍」、群主才能 @所有人 是微信的功能，写法照常识，没写版本号。"},{"id":"linhao_tip","learn":"zh","level":"up","kind":"opinion","host":"isle.linhao","cat":"go","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"该不该给小费？","en":"Should you tip?"},"hook":["同一个问题，五个国家五种答案。五天后你能说出自己的一段","Same question, five countries, five answers — and by Friday, your own paragraph"],"pic":"linhao/dinner","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-24","2026-12-22"],"n":176,"why":["In Lyon I never know whether to tip. My French classmates laugh, my American roommate is shocked. So let's argue about it — politely, in Chinese.","在里昂我老是不知道该不该给小费。法国同学笑我，美国室友吓一跳。这周我们来吵一吵——用中文，吵得有礼貌一点。"],"end":{"stamp":"TIP?","next":"xiaoyu_ai"},"D":[{"k":"表态","type":"build","say":["Day 1: just take a side. 我觉得…… is the easiest way in — calm, not rude. Pick the one closest to you.","第一天：先表个态。「我觉得……」最好用，不冲。选最像你的那句。"],"line":"I [think] ___.","z":"我[觉得]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"我觉得","suf":"。","mine":[["应该给，服务好就给","yes — if the service is good"],["不用给，价格里已经包括了","no — it's already in the price"],["看情况，要看在哪个国家","it depends on the country"]]},"crowd":[["stars.emma","It depends on the country. In France, service is already in the bill.","我觉得看情况，要看在哪个国家。在法国，服务费已经算在账单里了。"],["isle.kenji","No need — in Japan people might even chase you to give it back.","我觉得不用给。在日本，店员可能还会追出来还给你。"]],"shout":["Kenji's story is true — in Japan, leaving money on the table can confuse people.","Kenji 说的是真的——在日本，把钱留在桌上，店员会以为你忘了。"]},{"k":"给理由","type":"build","say":["Now say why. 主要是因为…… = mainly because. One reason, said clearly, beats three.","今天说理由：「主要是因为……」。一个理由说清楚，比说三个强。"],"line":"[Mainly because] ___.","z":"[主要是因为]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"主要是因为","suf":"。","mine":[["服务员的工资本来就不高","waiters' wages are low to begin with"],["每个地方的习惯不一样","every place has its own custom"],["账单上已经有服务费了","there's already a service charge on the bill"]],"hear":["london.oliver","我觉得要看情况，主要是因为英国很多餐厅已经加了服务费。","I think it depends — mainly because many UK restaurants already add a service charge."],"ask":["Why does Oliver say 'it depends'?","Oliver 为什么说「要看情况」？"],"ao":[["Many places already add a service charge",1,"很多店已经加了服务费"],["He never eats out",0,"他从来不出去吃"],["Tipping is illegal in the UK",0,"英国不让给小费"]]},"crowd":[["stars.emma","Mainly because every place has its own custom. I check before every trip.","主要是因为每个地方的习惯不一样。我每次出发前都查一下。"],["isle.mei","Mainly because in Taiwan, restaurants often add 10% already.","主要是因为在台湾，很多餐厅已经加了一成服务费。"]]},{"k":"让步","type":"build","say":["Today: agree a little, then turn. 话是这么说，但…… makes you sound fair, not stubborn.","今天学让步：先承认一点，再转回来。「话是这么说，但……」听起来讲道理，不固执。"],"line":"[That's true, but] ___.","z":"[话是这么说，但]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"话是这么说，但","suf":"。","mine":[["到了别的地方，我会照那边的习惯来","when I'm somewhere else, I go with how they do it there"],["有的服务员真的靠小费生活","some servers really live on tips"],["给多给少都会让人尴尬","giving too much or too little is awkward either way"]],"hear":["stars.emma","话是这么说，但在美国不给小费，服务员真的会很难过。","That's true, but in the US, if you don't tip, the server really loses out."],"ask":["What is Emma doing?","Emma 在做什么？"],"ao":[["Agreeing a little, then turning",1,"先承认一点，再转回来"],["Telling a joke",0,"讲笑话"],["Ordering food",0,"点菜"]],"turn":{"s":"话是这么说，＿在美国不给小费，服务员真的会很难过。","o":[["但",1,""],["所以",0,"所以 is for your conclusion — that's Day 5."],["因为",0,"因为 gives a reason — Day 2."]],"ex":["话是这么说，但……","That's true, but…"]}},"crowd":[["isle.kenji","That's true, but when I'm somewhere else, I go with how they do it there. In New York, I tipped 20%.","话是这么说，但到了别的地方，我会照那边的习惯来。在纽约我给了两成。"]]},{"k":"举例","type":"build","say":["Back it up with one example — a country you know. 就拿……来说.","举一个你知道的国家当例子：「就拿……来说」。"],"line":"[Take] ___ [for example], ___.","z":"[就拿]___[来说]，___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"就拿","suf":"。","mine":[["美国来说，一般要给百分之十五到二十","the US — usually 15 to 20 percent"],["日本来说，给了人家反而不知道怎么办","Japan — people won't know what to do with it"],["中国来说，大部分地方都不用给","China — most places don't expect it"]],"hear":["isle.mei","就拿台湾来说，夜市吃东西从来不用给小费。","Take Taiwan, for example: you never tip at a night market."],"ask":["What example does Mei give?","Mei 举了什么例子？"],"ao":[["Night markets in Taiwan",1,"台湾的夜市"],["Hotels in Japan",0,"日本的酒店"],["Taxis in London",0,"伦敦的出租车"]],"turn":{"s":"＿日本来说，给小费反而会让人不知道怎么办。","o":[["就拿",1,""],["话是这么说",0,"That's for conceding — Day 3."],["主要是因为",0,"That's for reasons — Day 2."]],"ex":["就拿……来说","Take … for example"]}},"crowd":[["london.oliver","Take the UK, for example: a 12.5% service charge is often already on the bill.","就拿英国来说，账单上常常已经有百分之十二点五的服务费了。"],["stars.emma","Take France, for example: service is included by law — people just round up.","就拿法国来说，服务费按规定已经包括了，大家就凑个整。"]]},{"k":"整段说","type":"build","say":["Last day! Add one 所以 line, then say the whole thing. That's your view, in Chinese.","最后一天！加一句「所以……」，再把整段说出来。这就是你用中文说出来的看法。"],"line":"… [So] ___.","z":"……[所以]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"所以","suf":"。","mine":[["我出国前会先查一下当地的习惯","I'll check the local custom before I travel"],["到了那边，我会先问问当地人一般给多少","when I get there, I'll ask people how much they usually give"],["服务好的话，我还是愿意给","if the service is good, I'm still happy to tip"]],"all":true},"crowd":[["isle.kenji","…So I'll check the local custom before I travel. Lesson learned in New York.","……所以我出国前会先查一下当地的习惯。纽约那次学乖了。"]]}],"_note":"进阶活动（2026-11-10，样板 样板/进阶活动玩一遍样板.html）。level: up = 放在「进阶」那一排；type: build = 拼你自己的话（D.b）。只给学中文的人。母语的人还没审。 小费的事实：日本一般不给；法国 1987 年起服务费按规定算在价格里；英国餐厅常加 12.5% 服务费；美国一般 15–20%；中国大陆大部分地方不用给。"},{"id":"mei_ktv","learn":"zh","host":"isle.mei","cat":"world","soil":"culture","hook":["一首《晴天》唱完了，下一首你来点","Sunny Day is done. Your turn to pick the next song"],"t":{"zh":"周五晚上，台北 KTV","en":"Friday night: KTV in Taipei"},"pic":"mei/night","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":131,"why":["After a week of 'Sunny Day', my shop friends said: OK, now sing it for real. So this Friday after closing we're going to KTV — a private room, a big screen with the lyrics, a tablet to pick songs. Five days, and you'll know what to say in that room.","《晴天》听了一个礼拜，店里的朋友说：好，那就真的去唱。所以这周五关店以后我们去 KTV——一个包厢、一个放歌词的大屏幕、一台点歌的平板。五天，你就知道在包厢里该说什么。"],"D":[{"k":"先点一首歌","say":["In a KTV room there's a tablet or a screen, and everyone adds songs to the list. That's 点歌. Today, add the one we learned last week. Tell everyone what you picked.","KTV 包厢里有一台平板或者点歌机，大家轮流把歌加进去，这叫「点歌」。今天，先把上周学的那首点上。跟大家说一声你点了什么。"],"line":"I [picked] Sunny Day.","z":"我[点]了《晴天》。","from":"唱 KTV","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I picked Sunny Day. Then I saw I was number nine in the list. Long wait.","我点了《晴天》。然后发现排在第九首，要等好久。"],["stars.emma","I picked Sunny Day too! Two Sunny Days in one room — trust me, nobody minded.","我也点了《晴天》！一个包厢两首《晴天》——相信我，没人介意。"],["isle.xiaoyu","In Hangzhou we say 唱K too. But 点歌 is the same everywhere.","我们杭州也说「唱K」。不过「点歌」哪里都一样。"]],"shout":["Kenji, number nine is normal lol — order snacks while you wait. Emma, two Sunny Days is a very Taipei night.","Kenji，排第九很正常 lol——等的时候先点个吃的。Emma，两首《晴天》，很台北的一个晚上。"]},{"k":"这首太高了","say":["The chorus comes and — it's so high! Everyone has that moment. Don't stop singing; just laugh and say it's too high for you. Chinese has a neat way: 唱不上去, 'can't sing up there'.","副歌一来——好高！每个人都有这一刻。别停，笑一笑说太高了就好。中文有个很好用的说法：「唱不上去」。"],"line":"It's too high, I [can't reach it].","z":"太高了，我[唱不上去]。","from":"唱 KTV","crowd":[["isle.nadia","It's too high, I can't reach it. So I sang it one octave lower. Like a bear.","太高了，我唱不上去。所以我低了八度唱，像一头熊。"],["london.oliver","I said 我不能唱高. My friend said: you mean 唱不上去. Same pain, better Chinese.","我说「我不能唱高」。朋友说：你是说「唱不上去」吧。一样痛苦，中文好多了。"],["isle.linhao","Tip: KTV machines have a key button. Press it down two steps, problem solved.","小提示：点歌机上有调音的键，降两个调，问题就解决了。"]],"shout":["Nadia, bear voice is a real KTV style lol. Linhao, thank you — everyone, find the key button tonight.","Nadia，熊的声音也是一种 KTV 唱法 lol。林浩，谢啦——大家今晚找找那个降调的键。"]},{"k":"切歌吧","say":["Sometimes a song is just wrong: too slow, too sad, nobody knows it. Then someone grabs the tablet and says 切歌! — skip it. Saying it with a smile is totally fine among friends.","有时候一首歌就是不对：太慢、太悲伤、没人会唱。这时就有人抓起平板喊「切歌！」——跳过去。朋友之间笑着说，完全没问题。"],"line":"This one's too sad, let's [skip it]!","z":"这首太悲伤了，[切歌]吧！","from":"唱 KTV","crowd":[["more.world.priya","This one's too sad, let's skip it! It was my song. I skipped my own song.","这首太悲伤了，切歌吧！那是我点的。我切了我自己的歌。"],["isle.kenji","I said 我们换吧. They understood. But 切歌 sounds so much cooler.","我说「我们换吧」。他们听懂了。可是「切歌」听起来酷多了。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Careful: skipping someone's song while they're singing it — only with good friends lol.","小心：别人正在唱的时候切他的歌——只能对很熟的朋友这样 lol。"]],"shout":["Priya skipped her own song — that's the most honest thing in KTV history. Xiaoyu is right: good friends only.","Priya 切了自己的歌——KTV 史上最诚实的一刻。小雨说得对：只对好朋友。"]},{"k":"给朋友喊一声","say":["When a friend finishes a song, clap and say it! 唱得真好 — 'you sang so well'. In Taiwan you'll also hear 好好听 and 超好听. Even if it wasn't that good. Especially then lol.","朋友唱完，就鼓掌说出来！「唱得真好」。在台湾你还会听到「好好听」「超好听」。就算唱得没那么好也说。尤其是那时候 lol。"],"line":"You [sang that] so well!","z":"你[唱得]真好！","from":"唱 KTV","crowd":[["stars.emma","You sang that so well! I said it to a stranger in the next room. Long story.","你唱得真好！我是对隔壁包厢的陌生人说的。说来话长。"],["london.oliver","I said 你唱真好 — no 得. My friend still smiled. Then taught me 得.","我说成「你唱真好」——少了「得」。朋友还是笑了，然后教了我「得」。"],["isle.linhao","In Lyon my French friends sing Mandopop now. I say 唱得真好 every time. They believe me.","在里昂，我的法国朋友现在也唱华语歌了。我每次都说「唱得真好」。他们信了。"]],"shout":["Emma, of course you made a friend next door. Oliver, with 得 now — next time it'll be perfect.","Emma，你当然会在隔壁交到朋友。Oliver，现在有「得」了——下次就完美了。"]},{"k":"下次你想唱什么","say":["Last day! Five days, and you've picked, failed the high notes, skipped, and cheered. KTV is a place you go back to. So: next time, what do you want to sing? Tell me and I'll add it to our list.","最后一天！五天，你点过歌、唱不上去过、切过歌，也给人喊过好。KTV 是会一去再去的地方。所以：下次你想唱什么？告诉我，我帮你加进我们的歌单。"],"line":"Next time I [want to sing] ___.","z":"下次我[想唱] ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.nadia","Next time I want to sing The Moon Represents My Heart. Slow song. No high notes.","下次我想唱《月亮代表我的心》。慢歌，没有高音。"],["more.world.priya","Next time I want to sing a Bollywood song. Do Taipei KTVs have them? I'll check.","下次我想唱一首宝莱坞的歌。台北的 KTV 有吗？我去查查。"],["isle.kenji","Next time I want to sing Sunny Day again. Line two this time.","下次我还想唱《晴天》。这次唱第二句。"]]}],"end":{"stamp":"ENCORE","next":"mei_concert"},"_sources":{"台湾 KTV 多是包厢、按时间计费，用平板/点歌机点歌，屏幕上放歌词":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karaoke_box","《月亮代表我的心》：邓丽君 1977 年唱红":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Moon_Represents_My_Heart"},"_review":"母语的人还没审"},{"id":"mei_order","host":"isle.mei","cat":"eat","t":{"zh":"饮料店点单挑战","en":"Order it your way"},"pic":"mei/work","days":3,"starts":["2026-11-19","2026-12-17"],"n":162,"why":["I take hundreds of orders a night, and the tourists always freeze at ‘how sweet?’ lol. Three days, and you'll order exactly the cup you want 🧋","我一个晚上接几百单，游客一听到「甜度？」就愣住 lol。三天，你就能点出你自己想要的那一杯 🧋"],"D":[{"k":"先说多甜","say":["In Taiwan you pick the sugar: full, less, half, light, or none. Then the ice. Most of my regulars say it in one breath.","在台湾，糖是你自己选的：全糖、少糖、半糖、微糖、无糖。然后是冰块。我的熟客都是一口气说完。"],"line":"[Half sugar], less ice, please.","z":"半糖少冰，谢谢。","from":"点饮料","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Half sugar, less ice, please. I said it to my kettle. It made green tea.","半糖少冰，谢谢。我对着烧水壶说的。它给我泡了绿茶。"],["stars.emma","Said it at a bubble tea place in Lisbon — the girl replied in Mandarin. I just nodded, trust me.","在里斯本一家奶茶店说了——店员直接用中文回我。相信我，我只能点头。"],["isle.nadia","No sugar, no ice, please. Yes, I'm that customer.","无糖去冰，谢谢。对，我就是那种客人。"]],"shout":["Nadia, ‘that customer’ is my favourite customer. Easiest drink on the menu lol","Nadia，「那种客人」是我最喜欢的客人。全菜单最好做的一杯 lol"]},{"k":"冬天要温的","say":["It's winter, so a lot of people want it warm. And say your topping: pearls, grass jelly, pudding.","冬天了，很多人要温的。再说你要加什么：珍珠、仙草、布丁。"],"line":"Can I get it [warm], with pearls?","z":"可以做温的吗？加珍珠。","from":"点饮料","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Can I get it warm, with pearls? Lyon has one bubble tea shop and now they know me.","可以做温的吗？加珍珠。里昂就一家奶茶店，现在店员都认识我了。"],["isle.amara","Can I get it warm, with pudding? Bangkok next week, I'm practising, honestly.","可以做温的吗？加布丁。下周飞曼谷，我真的在练。"]],"shout":["Linhao, being a regular is the goal. Next time they'll start making it when you walk in 😂","林浩，成为熟客就是目标。下次你一进门他们就开始做了 😂"]},{"k":"点一杯你的","say":["Last day! Put it all together: what drink, how sweet, how cold or warm. Order your real drink, the one you'd actually buy.","最后一天！全部连起来：什么饮料、多甜、冰的还是温的。点你真正会买的那一杯。"],"line":"Can I [get] a ___, ___ sugar, ___?","z":"我要一杯 ___，___，___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.rosa","Can I get a hibiscus tea, no sugar, with ice? Ay, it's like my agua de jamaica.","我要一杯洛神花茶，无糖，加冰。哎，像我做的洛神花水。"],["isle.kenji","Can I get a brown sugar milk tea, half sugar, warm? Okay, I'm ready for Taipei.","我要一杯黑糖奶茶，半糖，温的。好，我准备好去台北了。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Can I get a jasmine green tea, light sugar, less ice? Said it at a shop in Flushing — it worked!","我要一杯茉莉绿茶，微糖，少冰。在法拉盛的店里说了——成功了！"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu ordered for real! And Kenji got his brown sugar milk tea, first try 🧋","小雨真去点了！Kenji 的黑糖奶茶，一次就点到了 🧋"]}],"end":{"stamp":"HALF SUGAR","next":"mei_nightmarket"}},{"id":"mei_qingtian","learn":"zh","zh_of":"kwame_afrobeats","host":"isle.mei","cat":"world","soil":"culture","hook":["一首老歌听一周，听到你会跟着哼","One old song all week, till you hum along"],"t":{"zh":"一首《晴天》听一周","en":"One Mandopop song, all week"},"pic":"mei/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-19","2026-12-17"],"n":148,"why":["Every night at the shop the same song comes on, and half the customers sing along. It's Jay Chou's 'Sunny Day' — it's older than me! For five days I'll play it while I shake drinks, and we'll learn how people here talk about a song.","每天晚上店里都会放到同一首歌，一半的客人会跟着唱。是周杰伦的《晴天》——它比我年纪还大！这五天我边摇饮料边放它，我们来学这边的人怎么聊一首歌。"],"D":[{"k":"先问歌叫什么","say":["Day one: just listen. When a song you like comes on in a shop in Taipei or Shanghai, the easiest thing is to ask. But first, guess: when did this one come out?","第一天：先听。在台北或上海的店里听到喜欢的歌，最简单就是问一句。不过先猜猜：这首歌是哪一年出的？"],"line":"What's this song [called]?","z":"这首歌叫什么？","from":"聊音乐","type":"guess","q":["When did 'Sunny Day' (晴天) come out?","《晴天》是哪一年出的？"],"opts":[["1993",0],["2003",1],["2013",0]],"reveal":["2003 — on Jay Chou's album Ye Hui Mei. Twenty-some years on, people still sing it at KTV.","2003 年，在周杰伦的专辑《叶惠美》里。二十多年了，大家去 KTV 还在唱。"],"crowd":[["beijing.tom","I asked the noodle shop owner what this song is called. He didn't answer — he just sang me the next line.","我问面馆老板这首歌叫什么。他没回答，直接给我唱了下一句。"],["chengdu.emma","I asked: what's the name of this song? Is that too long?","我问的是「这首歌叫什么名字？」是不是太长了？"],["isle.xiaoyu","Ha, every Chinese person my age knows it. Ask anyone, they'll hum a bit.","哈，我们这个年纪的中国人谁不知道。随便问一个，都能哼两句。"]],"shout":["Hailey, not too long at all — 叫什么名字 is totally fine. Tom, the noodle guy singing back is the best answer you'll ever get.","Hailey，一点不长，「叫什么名字」完全可以。Tom，面馆老板直接唱给你听，这是最好的回答。"]},{"k":"是谁唱的","say":["It's Jay Chou, from Taiwan — like me. People joke that he sings as if his mouth is full of rice: the words all run together. So even Chinese speakers turn the lyrics on.","是周杰伦，台湾人，跟我一样。大家开玩笑说他唱歌像嘴里含着饭，字都连在一起。所以连中国人都要开着歌词听。"],"line":"Who [sings] this?","z":"这是谁唱的？","from":"聊音乐","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Who sings this? I asked, and my colleague looked at me like I'd asked who invented rice.","这是谁唱的？我一问，同事看我的眼神，好像我问米饭是谁发明的。"],["shanghai.sophie","I said 谁唱这个 — my roommate got it straight away. She says 这是谁唱的, so now I know two ways.","我说的是「谁唱这个」，室友一下就懂了。她平时说「这是谁唱的」，这下我会两种说法了。"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Jay Chou. On graduation day my whole high school class sang this one.","周杰伦。我们高中毕业那天，全班一起唱的就是这首。"]],"shout":["Sophie, your roommate is a good teacher. When it's already happened, people love 是……的.","Sophie，你室友教得好。问已经发生的事，中国人爱用「是……的」。"]},{"k":"听不清歌词","say":["Today, play it once without the lyrics. Can't catch the words? Totally normal — my mum can't either. Lots of Chinese words sound the same, so videos and KTV always show the lyrics on screen.","今天先不看歌词听一遍。听不清？太正常了，我妈都听不清。中文很多字发音一样，所以视频和 KTV 一直把歌词放在屏幕上。"],"line":"I [can't make out] the lyrics.","z":"我听不清歌词。","from":"聊音乐","crowd":[["isle.amara","I can't make out the lyrics, but I can hum it. That's half, right?","我听不清歌词，可是我会哼。这样算一半吗？"],["guangzhou.amadou","I can't make it out, but I caught one word: 晴天, sunny day. It's raining in Guangzhou, though.","听不清，但我听到一个词：晴天。可是广州在下雨。"],["isle.mei","Same here, and I'm from Taipei. Jay Chou isn't easy for anybody 😂","我也听不清，我还是台北人呢。周杰伦对谁都不简单 😂"]],"shout":["Amadou caught 晴天 — that's the title, so it counts double. And Amara, humming totally counts.","Amadou 听出了「晴天」——那是歌名，算两分。Amara，会哼当然算。"]},{"k":"它让你想起什么","say":["For a lot of people who grew up in the 2000s in China and Taiwan, this song means school: rain, a bike, someone you liked. Ask a Chinese friend what it reminds them of — you'll get a story.","对很多 2000 年代长大的中国人和台湾人来说，这首歌就是上学的时候：下雨、自行车、喜欢过的人。问问中国朋友这首歌让他想起什么——你会听到一个故事。"],"line":"This song [reminds me of] high school.","z":"这首歌让我想起高中。","from":"聊音乐","crowd":[["shanghai.zhaolei","It reminds me of riding to school in the rain, late again. Every time.","这首歌让我想起高中骑车上学，下着雨，又要迟到了。每次都是。"],["beijing.tom","This song reminds me of my first week in Beijing. It was playing everywhere.","这首歌让我想起我在北京的第一个星期。到处都在放。"],["chengdu.emma","I said 这首歌提醒我高中. My teacher laughed — 提醒 is for 'don't forget your keys'.","我说「这首歌提醒我高中」。老师笑了——「提醒」是「别忘了带钥匙」那种。"]],"shout":["Hailey, that's the most common mix-up: 提醒 is a reminder, 想起 is a memory. Zhao Lei, I can see the rain.","Hailey，这是最常见的混用：「提醒」是叫你别忘了，「想起」是回忆。赵磊，我都看见那场雨了。"]},{"k":"说你单曲循环的歌","say":["Last day! One song for a whole week — in Chinese that's 单曲循环, one song on loop. What's yours this week? Tell me, and I'll play it in the shop tonight.","最后一天！一首歌听一整周，中文叫「单曲循环」。你这周在循环什么？告诉我，今晚我在店里放。"],"line":"I've had ___ [on repeat] all week.","z":"这周我一直在单曲循环 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","I've had 'Sunny Day' on repeat. I can sing the first line now. Only the first line.","这周我一直在单曲循环《晴天》。第一句我会唱了。只会第一句。"],["shanghai.sophie","I've had a Shanghai rapper on repeat, and I still can't say his name right.","这周我一直在单曲循环一个上海的说唱歌手，可我还是念不对他的名字。"],["isle.xiaoyu","I've had 'The Moon Represents My Heart' on repeat — for my grandma's birthday. She cried.","这周我一直在单曲循环《月亮代表我的心》，给我奶奶过生日用的。她哭了。"]],"shout":["Kenji, first line today, second line next week. Xiaoyu, tell your grandma Taipei says happy birthday.","Kenji，今天第一句，下周第二句。小雨，替我跟奶奶说，台北祝她生日快乐。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"ON REPEAT","next":"mei_ktv"},"_sources":{"《晴天》：周杰伦，2003 年专辑《叶惠美》":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ye_Hui_Mei","《月亮代表我的心》：邓丽君 1977 年唱红":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Moon_Represents_My_Heart"},"_review":"母语的人还没审"},{"id":"mei_tones","learn":"zh","zh_of":"rachel_th","host":"isle.mei","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"水饺还是睡觉","en":"Dumplings or bedtime?"},"hook":["shuǐjiǎo 是水饺，shuìjiào 是睡觉。差一个声调，你点的就是一碗觉。","shuǐjiǎo is dumplings, shuìjiào is sleep. One tone off and you've ordered a bowl of nap."],"pic":"mei/night","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":203,"why":["Every night at the night market someone asks for a ‘bowl of sleep’ lol. Five days, one tone mix-up a day — the ones I hear most — and you'll never order a nap again.","夜市上每天晚上都有人要「一碗睡觉」lol。五天，每天一个我最常听到的声调搞混，以后你再也不会点一碗觉了。"],"D":[{"k":"水饺不是睡觉","say":["Shuǐjiǎo, dumplings: two third tones together, so the first one goes up — shuí-jiǎo. Shuìjiào, sleep: two sharp drops. One bowl of each? No thanks lol","水饺：两个三声连在一起，第一个变成往上扬——shuí jiǎo。睡觉：两下往下掉。各来一碗？不用了 lol"],"line":"A bowl of [dumplings], please.","z":"来一碗水饺。","from":"夜市点吃的","crowd":[["isle.kenji","A bowl of dumplings, please. My phone wrote 睡觉. Twice. Third try: dumplings!","来一碗水饺。手机写成了「睡觉」，两次。第三次才对！"],["stars.emma","Said it at a stall in Taipei — the lady gave me dumplings, not a bed. Victory, trust me.","来一碗水饺！台北的阿姨给我的是水饺，不是床。相信我，赢了。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","Up, then down. Foreign clients also mix up 买 and 卖 — that one costs real money.","先扬后降。外国客户还会把「买」和「卖」说混——那可是真要花钱的。"]],"shout":["Kenji, your phone is the strictest teacher in Asia. Emma — no bed, just dumplings. Perfect lol","Kenji，你的手机是全亚洲最严的老师。Emma——没有床，只有水饺，完美 lol"]},{"k":"买和卖","say":["Mǎi, third tone, is buy. Mài, fourth tone, is sell. Mix them up and you're offering to sell the boss your own scooter lol. Third tone: go low, then come up a little.","mǎi 三声是买，mài 四声是卖。说混了，你就成了要把自己的机车卖给老板 lol。三声：先低下去，再稍微上来一点。"],"line":"I'd like to [buy] this one.","z":"我想买这个。","from":"在摊子上买东西","crowd":[["isle.aiko","I'd like to buy this one! A record stall in Taipei. He understood — I bought two.","我想买这个！在台北的唱片摊说的。老板听懂了，我买了两张。"],["chengdu.zhouyao","Fun fact: 想买 is two third tones too, so 想 goes up. Xiáng mǎi.","小知识：「想买」也是两个三声，「想」要往上扬。xiáng mǎi。"],["isle.bea","I said mài. The man got excited — he thought I was selling my camera.","我想卖这个……我说成了 mài，老板好兴奋，以为我要卖相机。"]],"shout":["Bea, keep the camera, we need your videos lol. Zhou Yao is right — 想买 goes up first.","Bea，相机留着，我们还要看你的视频 lol。周瑶说得对——「想买」先往上扬。"]},{"k":"汤和糖","say":["Tāng, first tone, high and flat, is soup. Táng, second tone, going up like a question, is sugar. At my drink shop, ‘less táng’ is the most important sentence lol.","tāng 一声，高高平平，是汤。táng 二声，往上扬，像在问问题，是糖。在我们饮料店，「少放点糖」是最重要的一句 lol。"],"line":"Less [sugar], please.","z":"少放点糖。","from":"点饮料","crowd":[["isle.nadia","Less sugar, please. Finally, a Chinese sentence I need every day.","少放点糖。终于有一句我天天用得上的中文了。"],["isle.rosa","I said tāng. The man asked if I want soup in my tea. Ay, no.","少放点汤……老板问我茶里要不要加汤。哎呀，不要！"],["beijing.lina","At the café by the Forbidden City, tourists just say ‘táng, táng’ and point. That works too.","故宫边上的咖啡店，游客就说「糖、糖」，再用手一指。这样也行。"]],"shout":["Rosa, soup tea is not on my menu lol. Nadia — of course that's your sentence.","Rosa，汤茶不在我们的菜单上 lol。Nadia——这句当然是你的。"]},{"k":"问和吻","say":["Wèn, fourth tone, is ask. Wěn, third tone, is kiss. ‘May I wèn you something?’ is fine. ‘May I wěn you?’ — maybe not at the night market lol.","wèn 四声是问，wěn 三声是吻。「我能问你一下吗」没问题。「我能吻你一下吗」——夜市上还是别了 lol。"],"line":"[Excuse me], where's the toilet?","z":"请问，厕所在哪儿？","from":"问路","crowd":[["isle.amara","Excuse me, where's the toilet? Used it at Taoyuan airport. Fourth tone, very firm.","请问，厕所在哪儿？在桃园机场用的。四声，很坚定。"],["isle.kenji","I practised wèn, wèn, wèn on the train. The lady next to me changed seats.","请问，请问，请问……我在电车上练，旁边的阿姨换座位了。"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Tip: in Taiwan people often say 洗手间. Both work.","提醒：在台湾大家常说「洗手间」。两个都可以。"]],"shout":["Kenji lol, that lady was one tone away from a big misunderstanding. Amara, firm is perfect.","Kenji lol，那位阿姨离一场大误会只差一个声调。Amara，坚定就对了。"]},{"k":"点你想吃的","say":["Last day! Order your favourite night-market food. Remember: 想买 is two third tones, so 想 goes up — xiáng mǎi.","最后一天！点一样你最想吃的夜市小吃。记住：「想买」两个三声，「想」往上扬——xiáng mǎi。"],"line":"Boss, I'd [like to buy] ___.","z":"老板，我想买___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.emma","Boss, I'd like to buy a scallion pancake. No — two!","老板，我想买葱油饼。不对，两个！"],["isle.aiko","Boss, I'd like to buy… bubble tea. At Mei's shop, of course.","老板，我想买……珍珠奶茶。当然是在 Mei 的店。"],["more.isle_economy.wanjiru","Boss, I'd like to buy stinky tofu. I'm brave today.","老板，我想买臭豆腐。我今天很勇敢。"]],"shout":["Wanjiru ordered stinky tofu! Respect. Five days — no more bowls of sleep. Come to the night market, I'm listening 🧋","Wanjiru 点了臭豆腐！佩服。五天了——再也没有一碗睡觉。来夜市吧，我听着呢 🧋"]}],"end":{"stamp":"水饺","next":"mei_tones2"},"_sources":["两个三声连读，第一个读成二声（如 你好 ní hǎo、水饺 shuíjiǎo）：普通话变调的常识，见 Wikipedia「Standard Chinese phonology · Tone sandhi」https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Chinese_phonology#Tone_sandhi"],"_note":"学中文的人用的中文版（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"mei_tones2","learn":"zh","host":"isle.mei","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"少冰，不是少病","en":"Less ice, not less illness"},"hook":["bīng 是冰，bìng 是病。在饮料店说错，老板会祝你身体健康。","bīng is ice, bìng is illness. Get it wrong at a drink shop and you'll be wished good health."],"pic":"mei/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":167,"why":["No more bowls of sleep — nice lol. But I keep a list behind the counter of tone mix-ups I hear every week, and it's long. Round two: five new ones, from my drink shop, the breakfast shop next door, the night market and a taxi home.","再也没有一碗睡觉了——很好 lol。可是我在柜台后面有一张单子，记着每个礼拜都会听到的声调搞混，很长。第二轮：五个新的，从我的饮料店、隔壁早餐店、夜市，到坐计程车回家。"],"D":[{"k":"冰和病","say":["Bīng, first tone, high and flat, is ice. Bìng, fourth tone, dropping fast, is illness. At my shop you choose your ice: 正常冰, 少冰, 去冰. Say ‘less bìng’ and I'll just say: OK, stay healthy lol.","bīng 一声，高高平平，是冰。bìng 四声，一下掉下去，是病。在我们店，冰块可以选：正常冰、少冰、去冰。说成「少 bìng」，我只能说：好，祝你健康 lol。"],"line":"[Less ice], please.","z":"[少冰]，谢谢。","from":"点饮料","crowd":[["isle.nadia","Less ice, please. High and flat, like a flat white. That's how I remember it.","少冰，谢谢。高高平平，像一杯平平的咖啡。我就是这么记的。"],["isle.kenji","I said bìng. The girl at the counter laughed and wrote 少冰 on the cup for me.","我说成了 bìng。店员笑了，在杯子上帮我写了「少冰」。"],["isle.xiaoyu","On the mainland you'll hear 少冰 and 去冰 too. Same tones, same drink.","大陆也说「少冰」「去冰」。一样的声调，一样的饮料。"]],"shout":["Kenji, she wrote it on the cup — keep that cup lol. Nadia, a flat white for a flat tone, I love it.","Kenji，她都帮你写在杯子上了——那个杯子留着 lol。Nadia，平平的咖啡配平平的声调，我喜欢。"]},{"k":"包子和报纸","say":["Breakfast shop next door. Bāozi, first tone, is a steamed bun. Bàozhǐ, fourth then third, is a newspaper. Order two bàozhǐ and the boss will look around for today's paper lol.","隔壁早餐店。bāozi 一声，是包子。bàozhǐ，四声加三声，是报纸。说「两个 bàozhǐ」，老板会到处找今天的报纸 lol。"],"line":"Two [steamed buns], please.","z":"来两个[包子]。","from":"早餐店","crowd":[["london.oliver","Two buns, please. The boss said 'meat or veg?' and I panicked. Meat!","来两个包子。老板问「肉的还是菜的？」我慌了。肉的！"],["stars.emma","I asked for two newspapers. He gave me buns anyway. Context wins, trust me.","我要了两份「报纸」。他还是给了我包子。相信我，场合会帮你。"],["more.world.priya","Bāo — high and flat, like a long note. I sang it. Got my buns.","bāo——高高平平，像唱一个长音。我唱出来了，包子到手。"]],"shout":["Emma, context won this time — but not every boss is that kind lol. Oliver, 肉的 is a great panic answer.","Emma，这次场合救了你——可不是每个老板都那么好心 lol。Oliver，慌的时候说「肉的」很好。"]},{"k":"十四还是四十","say":["Night market, a price. Shísì is fourteen: rising, then falling. Sìshí is forty: falling, then rising. Mix them up and you pay almost three times as much. Today, check the price back.","夜市，问价钱。shísì 是十四：先扬后降。sìshí 是四十：先降后扬。说混了，你就多付快三倍。今天，把价钱再问一遍确认。"],"line":"Is it [forty] dollars?","z":"是[四十]块吗？","from":"夜市问价钱","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Is it forty? In Lyon a friend paid forty for a fourteen-euro thing. True story.","是四十块吗？在里昂有个朋友，十四欧的东西付了四十。真事。"],["isle.kenji","Is it forty? The boss just typed 40 on his calculator and showed me. Very clear.","是四十块吗？老板直接在计算器上按了 40 给我看。超清楚。"],["stars.emma","I said shísì and paid forty. Then he gave me twenty-six back. Honest man.","我说的是 shísì，给了四十。他找了我二十六。老实人。"]],"shout":["Kenji, the calculator is the night market's second language lol. Emma, honest bosses everywhere — still, check the tone.","Kenji，计算器是夜市的第二种语言 lol。Emma，哪里都有老实的老板——不过声调还是要确认。"]},{"k":"下车和瞎扯","say":["Taxi home. Xià chē, fourth then first, is ‘get out of the car’. Xiā chě, first then third, means ‘talking nonsense’. Tell the driver you'll get out up ahead — not that you're talking nonsense up ahead lol.","坐计程车回家。xià chē，四声加一声，是下车。xiā chě，一声加三声，是瞎扯。跟司机说你在前面下车——不是说你在前面瞎扯 lol。"],"line":"I'll [get out] up ahead.","z":"我在前面[下车]。","from":"坐计程车","crowd":[["isle.nadia","I'll get out up ahead. Then I said it again at the next corner, because it was the wrong corner.","我在前面下车。到了下一个路口我又说了一遍，因为前一个路口不对。"],["london.oliver","I said xiā chě. The driver laughed so hard he missed the turn.","我说成了 xiā chě。司机笑得太厉害，错过了路口。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Hangzhou drivers will ask 前面哪里停? Say 路口就行, ‘the corner is fine’.","杭州的司机会问「前面哪里停？」你说「路口就行」。"]],"shout":["Oliver, a laughing driver is still a happy driver lol. Xiaoyu, 路口就行 — everyone, add it.","Oliver，笑着的司机也是开心的司机 lol。小雨，「路口就行」——大家加上。"]},{"k":"点你自己的饮料","say":["Last day! Order your own drink at my shop. One more tone trick: 一 changes too. Before 杯 (first tone) it becomes yì — yì bēi. Then add your ice.","最后一天！在我的店点一杯你自己的饮料。再教一个声调小技巧：「一」也会变。在「杯」（一声）前面读成 yì——yì bēi。再加上冰块要多少。"],"line":"Boss, [one] ___, less ice.","z":"老板，[一杯] ___，少冰。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.nadia","Boss, one green tea, no sugar, less ice. My dream order.","老板，一杯绿茶，无糖，少冰。我的梦想菜单。"],["more.world.priya","Boss, one milk tea, less ice. Next time I'll try it with no ice — winter in Taipei is cold!","老板，一杯奶茶，少冰。下次我试试去冰——台北的冬天好冷！"],["isle.kenji","Boss, one bubble tea, less ice. I checked: bīng. Not bìng.","老板，一杯珍珠奶茶，少冰。我确认过了：bīng，不是 bìng。"]]}],"end":{"stamp":"少冰","next":"mei_tones3"},"_sources":["「一」的变调：在一、二、三声前读四声（一杯 yì bēi），在四声前读二声（一个 yí gè）。见 Wikipedia「Standard Chinese phonology · Tone sandhi」https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Chinese_phonology#Tone_sandhi","台湾手摇饮料店常见冰块选项：正常冰、少冰、微冰、去冰（常识）"],"_note":"接 mei_tones（水饺/睡觉、买/卖、汤/糖、问/吻、想买）。这一轮的对子不重复。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"nadia_5k","host":"isle.nadia","cat":"move","t":{"zh":"周六一起跑 5 公里","en":"Saturday 5K together"},"pic":"nadia/run","days":1,"starts":["2026-11-21","2026-12-19"],"n":318,"why":["Every Saturday I do a free 5K in the park before the market. Not fast — I chat the whole way. Run, jog or walk it with me, wherever you are.","我每周六逛菜市场之前，都去公园跑一个免费的 5 公里。不快，一路都在聊天。不管你在哪儿，跑、慢跑、走都行，跟我一起。"],"D":[{"k":"跑完说一句你的","say":["Five K is about 3.1 miles. If you can still talk in short sentences, your pace is fine — walking counts too. Finish, then tell me how it went.","5 公里大约是 3.1 英里。还能一句一句说话，速度就没问题——走路也算。跑完了，告诉我怎么样。"],"line":"I did [five K] today. I ___ most of it, and I felt ___.","z":"我今天走完/跑完了五公里。大部分时间我在 ___，感觉 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","I did five K today. I walked most of it, and I felt like a retired man. A happy one.","我今天走完了五公里。大部分时间是走的，感觉像个退休老头。开心的那种。"],["more.friends_e.jade","I did five K today. I jogged most of it, and I felt my half-marathon legs saying thank you, mate.","我今天跑了五公里。大部分是慢跑，感觉我准备半马的腿在说谢谢，伙计。"],["isle.linhao","I did five K today. I ran most of it along the river, and I felt cold, then warm, then hungry.","我今天跑了五公里。大部分是沿着河跑的，感觉先冷、后暖、然后饿了。"]],"shout":["Kenji walked the whole thing and still showed up. That's the bit that matters — see you next Saturday.","Kenji 全程走路，可他来了。要紧的就是这个——下周六见。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"5K","next":"jade_mornings"}},{"id":"nadia_label","host":"isle.nadia","cat":"eat","t":{"zh":"一周只看包装背面","en":"Read the back, not the front"},"pic":"nadia/label","days":7,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":389,"why":["Every January my clinic fills up with people who bought the ‘healthy’ version. So this week, flip every snack you buy and tell me what's really in it.","每年一月，诊室里都是买了「健康版」的人。所以这周，你买的每样零食都翻到背面，告诉我里面到底是什么。"],"D":[{"k":"第一个配料最多","say":["Ingredients go from most to least. The first one is the biggest part of what you're eating.","配料表是按多少排的，从多到少。排第一的，就是你吃下去最多的那样。"],"line":"The first [ingredient] is sugar.","z":"第一个配料是糖。","from":"看配料表","crowd":[["stars.emma","Pastéis de nata: first ingredient is… sugar. Of course.","葡式蛋挞：第一个配料是……糖。果然。"],["isle.kenji","My protein bar. The first ingredient is… chocolate. I feel betrayed.","我的蛋白棒。第一个配料是……巧克力。我被背叛了。"],["isle.mei","Our tapioca pearls: first is tapioca starch. Phew, at least it's honest lol","我们店的珍珠：第一个是木薯淀粉。还好，起码挺诚实 lol"]],"shout":["Kenji — the bar isn't evil. Now you just know what it is.","Kenji——蛋白棒不是坏东西。只是现在你知道它是什么了。"]},{"k":"比每 100 克","say":["Packs come in all sizes, so compare per 100 grams. Same column, two products, side by side.","包装有大有小，所以要比每 100 克。同一栏，两样东西放在一起看。"],"line":"How much sugar is there [per 100 grams]?","z":"每 100 克里有多少糖？","from":"超市里比东西","crowd":[["london.oliver","Two granolas, per 100 grams: 24 g of sugar versus 6 g. Same price. Story of my life.","两种燕麦脆，每 100 克：24 克糖对 6 克。价格一样。我的人生就是这样。"],["isle.linhao","How much sugar is there per 100 grams? French yoghurt: 4 g. The fruit one: 13 g.","每 100 克有多少糖？原味法国酸奶：4 克。水果味的：13 克。"]],"shout":["Oliver did it right: same column, side by side. That's the whole trick.","Oliver 做对了：同一栏，并排看。窍门就这一个。"]},{"k":"糖有很多名字","say":["Sugar has lots of names on a label: glucose syrup, dextrose, honey, ‘cane juice’. Count them.","配料表上的糖有很多名字：葡萄糖浆、右旋糖、蜂蜜、「蔗汁」。数一数有几个。"],"line":"That's just sugar [with another name].","z":"那不就是换了个名字的糖嘛。","from":"看配料表","crowd":[["new_york.xiaoyu","My cereal has sugar, glucose syrup AND honey. Three sugars in a trench coat.","我的麦片里有糖、葡萄糖浆，还有蜂蜜。三个糖穿着一件风衣假装一个人。"],["isle.tom","Ketchup: sugar is number two. Kids'd be thrilled.","番茄酱：糖排第二。孩子们听了肯定高兴。"],["isle.rosa","Ay, the soda from my kids: ‘high fructose corn syrup’. Valeria says that's sugar too.","哎，我家孩子喝的汽水：「高果糖玉米糖浆」。Valeria 说这也是糖。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu, ‘three sugars in a trench coat’ — I'm using that in clinic.","小雨，「三个糖穿一件风衣」——我要在诊室里用这句。"]},{"k":"一份到底多大","say":["Look at the serving size. It's often smaller than what you'd actually eat in one go.","看看「一份」是多少。它常常比你一次真正吃下去的少。"],"line":"Wait, a [serving] is only half the bag?","z":"等等，一份才半袋？","from":"看营养表","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Wait, a serving is only half the bag? Nobody in history has eaten half a bag.","等等，一份才半袋？人类历史上没人只吃过半袋。"],["more.friends_e.jade","My oat milk: one serving is 250 ml. That's one big coffee, mate. Fair.","我的燕麦奶：一份是 250 毫升。也就一大杯咖啡，伙计。还算公道。"]],"shout":["Kenji's right — so multiply. Eat the bag, double the numbers.","Kenji 说得对——所以要乘一下。吃了一整袋，数字就翻倍。"]},{"k":"盐藏在哪儿","say":["Salt isn't just in crisps. Bread, cereal and sauces carry a lot of it. Check one you'd never suspect.","盐不只在薯片里。面包、麦片、酱料里都有不少。挑一样你从没怀疑过的看看。"],"line":"I didn't [expect] salt in bread.","z":"没想到面包里也有盐。","from":"看营养表","crowd":[["isle.mei","I didn't expect salt in our milk tea powder?? Tiny bit, but still 😳","没想到我们的奶茶粉里也有盐？？一点点，但还是有 😳"],["isle.linhao","My baguette has salt, of course. The French would riot without it.","我的法棍当然有盐。没有盐法国人会上街的。"],["isle.amara","Airline crackers. I didn't expect that much salt, my dear. Now I know why I'm always thirsty up there.","飞机上的饼干。没想到这么咸，亲爱的。现在知道我在天上为什么总口渴了。"]],"shout":["Amara noticed something real — it's worth knowing where the salt comes from.","Amara 注意到了真东西——知道盐从哪来，就值了。"]},{"k":"正面说的话","say":["The front is an advert: ‘natural’, ‘wholesome’, ‘high protein’. The back is the facts. Read both and compare.","正面是广告：「天然」「健康」「高蛋白」。背面才是事实。两边都看，比一比。"],"line":"Don't [believe] the front. [Check] the back.","z":"别信正面，看背面。","from":"跟朋友说","crowd":[["london.oliver","‘Artisan’ crisps. Back says: potatoes, oil, salt. Exactly like the cheap ones, at twice the price.","「手工」薯片。背面写着：土豆、油、盐。跟便宜的一模一样，价钱翻倍。"],["isle.tom","Told my lot at home: don't believe the front, check the back. My daughter now reads every box in the shop. Help.","跟家里人说了：别信正面，看背面。现在我女儿在超市每个盒子都要读一遍。救命。"]],"shout":["Tom, your daughter is my new favourite person.","Tom，你女儿现在是我最喜欢的人。"]},{"k":"说你自己翻到的","say":["Last day. Flip one thing from your own kitchen and tell me the first ingredient. No judging — just knowing.","最后一天。从你自己家厨房拿一样翻过来，告诉我第一个配料。不评判，只是知道。"],"line":"I [flipped] my ___, and the first ingredient was ___.","z":"我把我的 ___ 翻过来看，第一个配料是 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.rosa","I flipped my tortillas, and the first ingredient was corn. Only corn, water and lime. Ay, I'm proud.","我把我的玉米饼翻过来看，第一个配料是玉米。只有玉米、水和石灰。哎，我好骄傲。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","I flipped my instant noodles, and the first ingredient was wheat flour. Fine. I'm keeping them.","我把我的方便面翻过来看，第一个配料是小麦粉。行吧，我还是留着。"],["isle.kenji","I flipped my green tea, and the first ingredient was green tea. Finally, a winner.","我把我的绿茶翻过来看，第一个配料是绿茶。终于有个赢家。"]],"shout":["Seven days of flipping. You'll never read a front the same way again. Next week: what ‘a portion’ really looks like.","翻了七天。以后你再也不会那样看包装正面了。下周：「一份」到底长什么样。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"READ THE BACK","next":"nadia_portion"}},{"id":"oliver_money","host":"london.oliver","cat":"life","t":{"zh":"一周看懂你的钱去哪了","en":"Where did my money go?"},"pic":"oliver/flat","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":115,"why":["I'm writing a piece on why young Londoners all flat-share. Everyone I interview says the same thing: “I don't know where my money goes.” Fair — neither do I. So this week I'm writing down every pound. Do it with me. No advice, just looking.","我在写一篇「伦敦年轻人为什么都在合租」。采访的每个人都说同一句：「我也不知道钱去哪了。」说得对，我也不知道。所以这周我把花的每一镑都记下来。跟我一起吧。不给建议，只是看清楚。"],"D":[{"k":"每一笔都记下来","say":["Today, write down everything you spend. Every coffee, every bus. You don't have to change anything — just look.","今天，把花的每一笔都记下来。每杯咖啡，每趟公交。不用改什么，看着就行。"],"line":"It all [adds up], doesn't it?","z":"一点一点的，加起来可不少，对吧？","from":"聊花钱","crowd":[["isle.mei","It all adds up, doesn't it? Three drinks from my own shop. I work there! Staff discount, but still.","加起来可不少，对吧？我在自己打工的店里买了三杯。我在那儿上班啊！有员工折扣，可还是……"],["isle.kenji","It all adds up. Konbini, konbini, konbini. Every line in my list is konbini.","加起来可不少。便利店、便利店、便利店。我清单上每一行都是便利店。"],["isle.xiaoyu","It all adds up, doesn't it? But I save 2000 yuan every month for my trip, so I checked that first.","加起来可不少，对吧？不过我每个月给出国存 2000 块，所以我先看了这一项。"]],"shout":["Mei buys drinks at her own shop. That's the most honest list I've seen. Mine was four flat whites.","Mei 在自己打工的店里买饮料。这是我见过最诚实的清单。我的是四杯 flat white。"]},{"k":"找出忘了的订阅","say":["Open your bank app and look for anything that comes out every month. Most people find one they forgot. I found two.","打开银行 App，找每个月自动扣的钱。大多数人都会找到一个自己忘了的。我找到两个。"],"line":"I [forgot I was paying for] that.","z":"我都忘了自己还在付这个钱。","from":"看账单","crowd":[["isle.aiko","I forgot I was paying for that — a music app. I work in a record shop. I have all the records.","我都忘了还在付这个——一个听歌 App。我在唱片店上班，唱片全都有。"],["more.friends_e.jade","I forgot I was paying for that. A yoga app. I'm a trainer. Embarrassing.","我都忘了还在付这个。一个瑜伽 App。我是教练啊。好丢人。"],["isle.linhao","I forgot I was paying for that — a Chinese video app. Okay, I still use it. Hotpot videos.","我都忘了还在付这个——一个中文视频 App。好吧，我还在用。看火锅视频。"]],"shout":["Aiko pays for music while selling music. Jade pays for yoga while teaching it. We're all the same, aren't we?","Aiko 一边卖唱片一边付钱听歌，Jade 一边当教练一边付钱上瑜伽。我们都一样，对吧？"]},{"k":"想买的，先放一晚","say":["A reader told me her trick: if she wants something, she waits a day. Half the time, she doesn't want it any more. In English we call that ‘sleeping on it’.","一个读者告诉我她的办法：想买什么，先等一天。一半的时候，第二天就不想要了。英语里这叫 sleep on it（睡一晚再说）。"],"line":"I'll [sleep on it].","z":"我睡一晚再说。","from":"想买东西的时候","crowd":[["isle.bea","I'll sleep on it. Then I woke up and still wanted the camera. Sleeping again tonight.","我睡一晚再说。结果醒来还是想要那个相机。今晚再睡一晚。"],["more.friends_e.hana","I use it for furniture. ‘I'll sleep on it’ has saved my clients a lot of sofas.","我买家具就用这招。「睡一晚再说」帮我的客户省下了好多沙发。"],["isle.daniel","Works for meetings too — y'know, a nicer version of ‘I'll consider it’.","开会也好用——就是「我考虑一下」的好听版本。"]],"shout":["Bea is on night two with the camera. Report back, Bea. My guess: you'll buy it.","Bea 已经为那个相机睡到第二晚了。告诉我们结果吧，Bea。我猜你会买。"]},{"k":"最大的那一块","say":["The rule of thumb is that rent should be about a third of your pay. Everyone I interviewed pays more. For most people, the biggest number is home.","有个大概的说法：房租应该占收入的三分之一左右。我采访的每个人都超了。对大多数人来说，最大的那个数字就是住的地方。"],"line":"Most of my money [goes on] rent.","z":"我大部分的钱都花在房租上了。","from":"聊钱花在哪","crowd":[["isle.jordi","Most of my money goes on rent too. In Barcelona my students live with their parents till thirty.","我大部分的钱也都花在房租上了。在巴塞罗那，我的学生要跟爸妈住到三十岁。"],["isle.linhao","Most of my money goes on rent. The second biggest is food from Chinese shops.","我大部分的钱都花在房租上了。第二多的是中国超市的吃的。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Most of my money goes on… my savings! I live with my parents. Sorry, everyone.","我大部分的钱都花在……存钱上！我跟爸妈住。对不起大家。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu lives with her parents and saves. Honestly, that's the other half of my story.","小雨跟爸妈住，在攒钱。说真的，这正是我稿子的另一半。"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last day. Look at your week. Where did most of it go, and what would you like to spend less on? No right answer.","最后一天。看看你这一周。钱大多去哪了？你想在什么上少花一点？没有标准答案。"],"line":"Most of my money goes on ___, and I'd like to [spend less on] ___.","z":"我的钱大多花在 ___ 上，我想少花点在 ___ 上。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Most of my money goes on rent, and I'd like to spend less on konbini. But konbini is my kitchen.","我的钱大多花在房租上，我想在便利店少花点。可便利店就是我的厨房。"],["isle.mei","Most of my money goes on my phone, and I'd like to spend less on drinks. From my own shop.","我的钱大多花在手机上，我想在饮料上少花点。我自己店里的。"],["isle.amara","Most of my money goes on presents for my family in Lagos, and I'd like to spend less on airport coffee. Never.","我的钱大多花在给拉各斯家里人买礼物上，我想在机场咖啡上少花点。不可能。"]],"shout":["Five days. Nobody is perfect, and that's fine. Next week my flat-share piece comes out — I'm quoting some of you. Anonymously. Probably.","五天。没有人是完美的，这也没关系。下周我的合租稿子就登出来了，我会引用你们几位的话。匿名的。大概吧。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"SORTED","next":"oliver_flatshare"}},{"id":"rachel_th","host":"more.friends_a.rachel","cat":"say","t":{"zh":"5 天把 th 说清楚","en":"Five days to a clean ‘th’"},"pic":"rachel/lesson","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":214,"why":["My student Bruno has his first English talk in two weeks. We're fixing his ‘th’ together — come along.","我的学生 Bruno 两周后要做第一次英语演讲。我们一起把他的 th 练清楚，你也来吧。"],"D":[{"k":"舌头放在牙齿中间","say":["Tongue between your teeth, then blow. Not ‘s’, not ‘f’.","舌头放在上下牙之间，往外吹气。不是 s，也不是 f。"],"line":"I [th]ink so.","z":"我觉得是。","from":"最常用的回话","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I sink so… I think so! Day one done.","我觉……我觉得是！第一天完成。"],["isle.mei","I think so. My tongue feels so weird lol","我觉得是。舌头好奇怪哈哈"],["new_york.xiaoyu","I think so — okay, I said it ten times in the bathroom.","我觉得是——好吧，我在卫生间说了十遍。"]],"shout":["Kenji, your second ‘think’ was perfect. Keep the tongue out!","Kenji，你第二遍的 think 很清楚了。舌头继续伸出来！"]},{"k":"这一次要震动","say":["‘This’ and ‘that’ buzz. Put your hand on your throat — feel it?","this、that 的 th 要震动。手放在喉咙上，感觉到了吗？"],"line":"[Th]at's the [th]ing.","z":"问题就在这儿。","from":"聊看法","crowd":[["isle.linhao","That's the thing. The French ‘th’ doesn't exist, so I'm extra lost.","问题就在这儿。法语里没有 th，我更晕了。"],["isle.mei","That's the thing! Buzzing like a phone.","问题就在这儿！嗡嗡响，像手机。"]],"shout":["Linhao — it's okay. Lost is where learning starts.","林浩——没关系。晕了，就是开始学了。"]},{"k":"两个 th 连着来","say":["Numbers are the hardest. Slow first, then fast.","数字最难。先慢，再快。"],"line":"Let's meet at [th]ree-[th]irty.","z":"三点半见吧。","from":"约时间","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Let's meet at three-thirty. Okay that one is hard.","三点半见。好吧这句真难。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Three-thirty. Tree-tirty. THREE-THIRTY. Got it.","三点半。树点半。三！点！半！会了。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu, I laughed — and then I heard it. That last one was clean.","小雨，我笑了——然后我听清了。最后那遍很干净。"]},{"k":"连起来说","say":["Don't stop between words. ‘Thanks a lot’ is one word.","词和词之间别停。Thanks a lot 当成一个词说。"],"line":"[Th]anks a lot.","z":"太谢谢了。","from":"道谢","crowd":[["isle.mei","Thanks a lot! Said it to a customer today and she smiled.","太谢谢了！今天对一个客人说了，她笑了。"],["isle.linhao","Thanks a lot — one word, one breath.","太谢谢了——一个词，一口气。"]],"shout":["Mei used it with a real customer. That's the whole point.","Mei 对真的客人说了。要的就是这个。"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last day. Make your own sentence with ‘think’ and ‘thing’.","最后一天。用 think 和 thing 说一句你自己的话。"],"line":"I [th]ink the best [th]ing about ___ is ___.","z":"我觉得 ___ 最好的地方是 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["new_york.xiaoyu","I think the best thing about New York is the 2 a.m. pizza.","我觉得纽约最好的是凌晨两点的披萨。"],["isle.kenji","I think the best thing about Osaka is that nobody is in a hurry to eat.","我觉得大阪最好的是吃饭没人赶时间。"],["isle.mei","I think the best thing about Taipei is the night market after rain.","我觉得台北最好的是雨后的夜市。"]],"shout":["Five days. You did it. Bruno's talk is on Friday — I'll tell you how it goes.","五天。你做到了。Bruno 周五演讲——我会告诉你他讲得怎么样。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"TH","next":"rachel_vw"}},{"id":"rosa_tacos","host":"isle.rosa","cat":"eat","t":{"zh":"周末学做 3 种塔可","en":"Three tacos, one weekend"},"pic":"rosa/stall","days":2,"starts":["2026-11-21","2026-12-19"],"n":241,"why":["Valeria made English signs for my stall, so now the tourists ask me how to make them at home. Okay! This weekend, my kitchen is your kitchen.","Valeria 给我的摊子做了英文牌子，现在游客都问我在家怎么做。好啊！这个周末，我的厨房就是你的厨房。"],"D":[{"k":"热饼，做两种","say":["Ay, first the tortillas: dry pan, hot, a few seconds each side. A cold tortilla is a sad tortilla, mija. Today: beans with cheese, and grilled beef with onion and cilantro.","哎，先热玉米饼：干锅，烧热，每面几秒钟。冷掉的饼是伤心的饼，亲爱的。今天做两种：豆子加奶酪，还有烤牛肉加洋葱和香菜。"],"line":"Two, [with everything], please.","z":"来两个，全都加。","from":"在摊子上点","crowd":[["isle.mei","Mum let me near the stove for the tortillas!! Historic. Two, with everything 🌮","我妈居然让我靠近灶台热饼了！！历史性的一刻。来两个，全都加 🌮"],["isle.tom","Bean and cheese one is brilliant. Doing it for the kids' tea on Monday, mate.","豆子奶酪那个太棒了。周一给孩子们当晚饭，兄弟。"],["london.oliver","My tortillas were from the shop and very sad. But the beef? Two, with everything, please.","我的饼是超市买的，很伤心。但那个牛肉？来两个，全都加。"]],"shout":["Mei! Your mamá trusts you now. Next step: the whole kitchen.","Mei！你妈妈开始信任你了。下一步：整个厨房。"]},{"k":"第三种，说你的","say":["Last one: tinga — shredded chicken in tomato and chipotle. It's from Puebla, not from here, but everybody makes it. Then tell me which one was your favourite.","最后一种：tinga，番茄和烟熏辣椒煮的手撕鸡。它是普埃布拉的，不是我们这儿的，可人人都会做。然后告诉我你最喜欢哪一个。"],"line":"My favourite was the ___ one, [with] ___.","z":"我最喜欢的是 ___ 那个，加 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","My favourite was the chicken one, with too much chipotle. My eyes are crying, but I'm happy.","我最喜欢的是鸡肉那个，烟熏辣椒放多了。眼睛在哭，可我很开心。"],["isle.linhao","My favourite was the beef one, with lots of lime. My French flatmates ate all of them.","我最喜欢的是牛肉那个，挤了很多青柠。我的法国室友全吃光了。"],["isle.nadia","My favourite was the bean one, with cheese and salsa verde. Beans on a Sunday — I'm in heaven.","我最喜欢的是豆子那个，加奶酪和青辣酱。周日吃豆子——我上天堂了。"]],"shout":["Linhao, your flatmates ate everything? That means you did it right. Ay, I'm so proud.","林浩，室友全吃光了？那就是做对了。哎，我好骄傲。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"TACOS","next":"rosa_salsa"}},{"id":"suqing_bankcard","learn":"zh","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"life","soil":"days","hook":["手机卡有了，下一步是银行卡：带什么、说什么、密码怎么设、怎么绑到支付宝","You've got the SIM. Next: a bank card — what to bring, what to say, the PIN, and linking it to Alipay"],"t":{"zh":"第二件事：开张银行卡","en":"Second thing in China: a bank card"},"pic":"suqing/teach","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":133,"why":["Last round you got a Chinese number. Good — the bank wants it. My students always come back from the bank tired: a queue number, forms, a PIN pad, a text code. None of it is hard, it's just new. Five days, one bank card, and then your phone can really pay.","上一期你办好了中国手机号。很好——银行要用它。我的学生每次从银行回来都很累：取号、填表、按密码、收验证码。其实都不难，只是没见过。五天，一张银行卡，然后你的手机才算真的能付钱。"],"D":[{"k":"说你要开户","say":["Walk in, take a number from the machine or the staff at the door, and wait. When it's your turn, you don't 'buy' a bank card — you 开户: open an account. The card comes with it.","进门先取号——机器上取，或者问门口的工作人员——然后等着叫号。轮到你了，不是「买」银行卡，是「开户」。卡跟着户头一起办。"],"line":"Hi, I'd like to [open an account].","z":"你好，我想开个户。","from":"办事","crowd":[["shanghai.sophie","Hi, I'd like to open an account. The guard asked 个人还是公司? Personal! Then he gave me a number.","你好，我想开个户。保安问「个人还是公司？」个人！然后他给了我一个号。"],["beijing.tom","I said 我想开一个银行. Everyone laughed. I wanted an account, not a whole bank.","我说「我想开一个银行」。大家都笑了。我要的是户头，不是一整家银行。"],["chengdu.emma","My small local branch sent me to a bigger one. Second try, it worked.","我家附近的小网点让我去大一点的支行。第二次就办成了。"]],"shout":["Tom, opening a whole bank — big dreams. Add 户: 开户. Hailey, a second branch is very normal. You didn't give up.","Tom，开一整家银行——志向远大。加个「户」：开户。Hailey，换一家网点很正常，你没放弃。"]},{"k":"带什么去","type":"guess","say":["Remember 原件 from last time? Bring your passport — the original. And one more thing that you already got last round. Guess.","还记得上次的「原件」吗？带护照，要原件。还有一样，上一期你已经办好了。猜一猜。"],"q":["Besides your passport, what will the bank almost always ask for?","除了护照，银行几乎一定会要什么？"],"opts":[["A Chinese phone number",1],["A photo of your family",0],["Your plane ticket home",0]],"reveal":["A Chinese phone number — the bank sends your codes there. Some banks ask for more, like your residence permit or a letter from your school or company. Rules differ, so call or ask first.","中国手机号——银行的验证码都发到这个号上。有的银行还要别的，比如居留许可、学校或公司的证明。各家不一样，先打电话或者问一下。"],"line":"Is my passport [enough]?","z":"只带护照够吗？","from":"办事","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I asked if my passport was enough. She said: and your Chinese phone number? I had it. Thanks, last week!","我问「只带护照够吗？」她说：「还有中国手机号呢？」我有！谢谢上周的我！"],["guangzhou.amadou","My bank also wanted my residence permit. I always bring everything now. My bag is heavy.","我的银行还要了居留许可。现在我什么都带上，包可重了。"],["more.world.priya","I called first and asked: is my passport enough? Saved a trip. Su Qing taught me that.","我先打电话问「只带护照够吗？」省了一趟。这是苏晴教的。"]],"shout":["Kenji, thank you to last week's you — that's why the SIM came first. Amadou, a heavy bag is a bag that works.","Kenji，谢谢上周的你——所以手机卡要先办。Amadou，包重，说明什么都带对了。"]},{"k":"设密码","say":["At the counter there's a little keypad facing you. Chinese bank cards use a six-digit PIN — 密码. You type it yourself, twice. The staff never need to know it, so don't say it out loud.","柜台上有个小键盘朝着你。中国的银行卡密码是六位数。你自己按，按两遍。工作人员不需要知道，所以别念出来。"],"line":"Do I [set the PIN] myself?","z":"密码是我自己设吗？","from":"办事","crowd":[["beijing.tom","I started reading my PIN out loud in Chinese to practise numbers. The teller said 别说！别说！ Very fast.","我想练数字，就用中文把密码念出来了。柜员说「别说！别说！」特别快。"],["shanghai.sophie","Do I set the PIN myself? Yes. She turned the keypad to me and looked away. So polite.","密码是我自己设吗？是。她把键盘转向我，还把头扭开了。好有礼貌。"],["beijing.chenhao","Programmer's tip: not your birthday, not 123456. Everyone tries those first.","程序员小建议：别用生日，别用 123456。谁都先试这几个。"]],"shout":["Tom, practise numbers on the menu — never on your PIN. Chen Hao, very wise. 123456 is not a secret.","Tom，练数字去看菜单——千万别拿密码练。陈浩说得对，123456 不算秘密。"]},{"k":"收验证码，绑卡","say":["Back home: open Alipay or WeChat and add your card — 绑卡. A six-digit code comes by text to the phone number you gave the bank. No code? Say so at once — maybe the number is wrong.","回家以后：打开支付宝或者微信，添加银行卡——就是「绑卡」。银行会往你留的那个手机号发一个六位数的验证码。没收到？马上说——可能号码留错了。"],"line":"I [didn't get the code].","z":"我没收到验证码。","from":"办事","crowd":[["chengdu.emma","I didn't get the code. Then I saw it — the bank had my old number from England. Back to the counter.","我没收到验证码。后来才发现，银行留的是我在英国的旧号码。又跑了一趟柜台。"],["isle.kenji","I said 我没拿到验证码. The staff understood! Su Qing says you'll often hear 收到 for texts — I'll try it next time.","我说「我没拿到验证码」。工作人员听懂了！苏晴说，短信也常说「收到」，下次我试试。"],["guangzhou.amadou","Card linked! First thing I paid for: one cup of herbal tea. Same as with my SIM.","卡绑好了！第一笔付的是一杯凉茶。跟办手机卡那次一样。"]],"shout":["Hailey, the old number — that's the most common bank story there is. Kenji, 拿到 a parcel, 收到 a text. Now you'll hear it everywhere.","Hailey，留了旧号码——这是最常见的银行故事。Kenji，快递「拿到」，短信「收到」。以后你到处都能听到。"]},{"k":"说你第一笔花在哪","say":["Last day. Your card is linked, your phone can pay. What's the first thing you'll spend on? Something small and real is perfect.","最后一天。卡绑好了，手机能付钱了。第一笔钱你想花在哪儿？小小的、真的，就最好。"],"line":"My card's linked — the first money I'll [spend on] ___.","z":"卡绑好了，第一笔钱我想花在___上。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["beijing.tom","My card's linked — the first money I'll spend on a jianbing. One scan and it's paid, no more hunting for change.","卡绑好了，第一笔钱我想花在煎饼上。手机一扫就付了，再也不用找零钱了。"],["shanghai.sophie","My card's linked — the first money I'll spend on a bike share. Then I can ride to work.","卡绑好了，第一笔钱我想花在共享单车上。这样就能骑车上班了。"],["more.world.priya","Not in China yet — but when I am, my first money goes on a train ticket to Xi'an.","我还没去中国——等我去了，第一笔钱想花在去西安的火车票上。"]],"shout":["Five days: a number, a queue, a PIN, a code. You did the most tiring errand in China. Treat yourself — with your phone.","五天：取号、排队、密码、验证码。中国最累人的一件事你办完了。犒劳一下自己吧——用手机付。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"BANK CARD: DONE","next":"suqing_rent"},"_sources":{"实名制（手机号、银行账户都实名，外国人用护照）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Real-name_system#China"},"_note":"接着 suqing_simcard。只写了各家都一样的常识：护照、中国手机号、自己设六位密码、绑卡要收验证码；没写哪家银行的具体规定和费用。拿不准的：网点让去大支行、居留许可这些只写成个人经历或「有的银行」。「六位数密码」「绑卡验证码发到银行留的手机号」是常识，还没找到可引用的出处，要补。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"suqing_praise","learn":"zh","zh_of":"daniel_praise","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"说了句你好，就被夸了","en":"One ‘nǐ hǎo’ and they say you're fluent"},"hook":["只说了一句你好，对方就说「你中文真好！」——中国人自己被夸，会怎么接？","You said one nǐ hǎo and got ‘Your Chinese is so good!’ What do Chinese people say when they're praised?"],"pic":"suqing/teach","days":6,"starts":["2026-11-18","2026-12-16"],"n":146,"why":["My new students all tell me the same thing: ‘I only said nǐ hǎo and they told me my Chinese is amazing!’ Here's the good news: ‘Thanks! I'm still learning’ is all you need. You'll also hear people answer in a more modest way — so let's learn to catch that too. Six days: five compliments, then your own way.","我班上的新学生都跟我说一样的话：「我就说了一句你好，他们就夸我中文好！」好消息是：说一句「谢谢！还在学呢」就够了。你也会常听到更谦虚的接法，我们也学着听懂它。六天：五句夸奖，最后说说你那边的接法。"],"D":[{"k":"被夸中文好","say":["‘Your Chinese is so good!’ The easiest reply: 谢谢！还在学呢 — thanks, I'm still learning. Friendly and true. You'll also hear people say 哪里哪里 — word for word ‘where, where?’, but it means ‘not at all’. Now you'll know it when you hear it.","「你中文真好！」最简单的接法：「谢谢！还在学呢。」大方又真诚。你也会听到有人说「哪里哪里」，字面是「哪里？哪里？」，其实是谦虚，意思是「没有没有」。下次听到，你就懂了。"],"line":"Thanks! I'm [still learning].","z":"谢谢！还在学呢。","from":"被夸中文","crowd":[["stars.emma","Thanks! I'm still learning. The noodle shop owner in Chengdu laughed and gave me more chili.","谢谢！还在学呢。成都的面馆老板笑了，多给了我一勺辣椒。"],["isle.kenji","Thanks! I'm still learning. True — I only know forty words.","谢谢！还在学呢。是真的，我才会四十个词。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","Foreign buyers at my factory all say this now. Then we start bargaining, and they're not so modest anymore.","现在来厂里的外国客户都会说这句。一砍价，就一点都不谦虚了。"]],"shout":["Emma, extra chili means he likes you. Chen Jian — bargaining is lesson two, haha.","Emma，多给辣椒就是喜欢你。Chen Jian——砍价那是第二课，哈哈。"]},{"k":"被夸衣服好看","say":["Someone says your coat looks nice. Lots of Chinese people answer with the price: ‘Really? It was only fifty kuai.’ It's a way of saying ‘oh, it's nothing special’.","有人夸你外套好看。很多中国人会报个价：「是吗？才五十块。」意思是「没什么特别的」。"],"line":"Really? It was [only] fifty kuai.","z":"是吗？才五十块。","from":"被夸东西","crowd":[["isle.aiko","Really? It was only thirty kuai! Secondhand.","是吗？才三十块！二手的。"],["shanghai.zhaolei","My mum does this every time. Even when it wasn't cheap.","我妈每次都这么说。就算不便宜也这么说。"],["isle.bea","Really? Fifty kuai… I forgot the 才. She looked a bit lost.","是吗？五十块……我忘了说「才」。她有点懵。"]],"shout":["Zhao Lei's mum is the real expert. Bea — without 才 it's just a price tag, ha.","赵磊的妈妈才是高手。Bea——没有「才」，就只是报个价了，哈。"]},{"k":"被领导夸","say":["When your boss praises your work, Chinese people often share the credit: ‘It was all of us.’ It sounds modest — and your team will love you.","领导夸你事情做得好，中国人常把功劳分给大家：「都是大家一起做的。」听起来谦虚，同事也会喜欢你。"],"line":"It was [all of us] — we did it together.","z":"都是大家一起做的。","from":"工作上被夸","crowd":[["more.world.priya","It was all of us — we did it together. My client paused on the video call, then smiled.","都是大家一起做的。客户在视频会上愣了一下，然后笑了。"],["beijing.chenhao","Classic. Then the boss says ‘you did the most’, and you say ‘no, no’ again. It can go a few rounds.","经典。然后领导说「你出力最多」，你再说「没有没有」，能来回好几轮。"],["isle.rosa","It was all of us — we did it together. My daughter did the most!","都是大家一起做的。我女儿做得最多！"]],"shout":["Chen Hao is right — it's a little dance. Two rounds of ‘no, no’ is normal. Three is very polite.","陈浩说得对——这是一支小舞。来回两轮「没有没有」很正常，三轮就是非常客气了。"]},{"k":"你也夸夸别人","say":["Now you give one. Chinese friends love it when you praise the food from their hometown — say it's 地道: authentic, the real thing.","现在轮到你夸别人。中国朋友最爱听你夸他们家乡的菜——说它「地道」，正宗的那种。"],"line":"This is so [authentic]!","z":"这个太地道了！","from":"夸别人","crowd":[["isle.amara","This is so authentic! — a jianbing at the airport. The lady said: ‘Airport ones aren't authentic.’ So honest!","这个太地道了！——机场的煎饼。阿姨说：机场的不地道。好诚实！"],["chengdu.zhouyao","Say it about Chengdu food and you have a friend for life. Say it about hotpot in Beijing and we'll argue.","夸成都菜地道，你就交到一辈子的朋友了。在北京夸火锅地道，我们就要吵一架了。"],["isle.nadia","This is so authentic! — my colleague's homemade dumplings. She sent me home with twenty.","这个太地道了！——同事自己包的饺子。她让我带了二十个回家。"]],"shout":["Amara, that lady is my hero. Nadia — one sentence for twenty dumplings. Good deal.","Amara，那位阿姨是我的偶像。Nadia——一句话换二十个饺子，划算。"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last compliment. Think of something you're getting better at. Someone praises it — answer your way: thanks, plus how it's going.","最后一句夸奖。想一件你越做越好的事。有人夸你——用你自己的方式接：先说谢谢，再说说现在怎么样。"],"line":"Thanks! My ___ still [needs practice].","z":"谢谢！我的___还在练呢。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Thanks! My tones still need practice. Very true.","谢谢！我的声调还在练呢。真的。"],["stars.emma","Thanks! My chopsticks still need practice. Ask the noodle man.","谢谢！我的筷子还在练呢。不信问面馆老板。"],["more.isle_economy.wanjiru","Thanks! My bargaining still needs practice. Chen Jian says I'm already scary.","谢谢！我砍价还在练呢。Chen Jian 说我已经很吓人了。"]],"shout":["Five compliments, all answered. Next time someone says your Chinese is good, you know what to say. Then smile. Tomorrow: how people answer where you're from.","五句夸奖，都接住了。下次有人说你中文好，你知道怎么接了。说完，笑一下。明天说说你那边怎么接。"]},{"k":"说说你那边怎么接","say":["One more day. Where you're from, when someone praises you, what do people usually say? Tell us in Chinese — I'd love to learn your way too.","再加一天。在你那边，被人夸了，一般怎么接？用中文说说——我也想学学你们的接法。"],"line":"Where I'm from, when someone praises us, we usually [say] ___.","z":"在我们那儿，被人夸了，一般会说___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Where I'm from, we usually say ‘No, no, not at all’ — a lot like 哪里哪里. And we bow a little.","在我们那儿，一般说「没有没有」，跟「哪里哪里」很像。说完还会稍微鞠个躬。"],["stars.emma","At home in France, I just say ‘Merci !’ and smile. My grandma always adds ‘c'est gentil’ — that's kind of you.","在法国老家，我一般就说一句 Merci，笑一笑。我奶奶每次都会加一句 c'est gentil，意思是「你真好」。"],["isle.rosa","Where I'm from, we say thank you and give one back: ‘Ay, you too!’","在我们那儿，先说谢谢，再夸回去：「哎呀，你也是！」"]],"shout":["Kenji bows, Emma's grandma says c'est gentil, Rosa gives it right back. Three ways, all good — and I've got a few new ones to try.","Kenji 鞠躬，Emma 的奶奶说 c'est gentil，Rosa 马上夸回去。三种接法，都挺好——我也学到几招新的。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"还在学呢","next":"suqing_suibian"},"_note":"学中文的人用的中文版（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"suqing_simcard","learn":"zh","zh_of":"xiaoyu_visa","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"life","soil":"days","hook":["没有中国手机号，外卖、打车、银行都卡住","No Chinese number? Delivery, taxis and the bank all get stuck"],"t":{"zh":"到中国第一件事：办张卡","en":"First thing in China: a SIM card"},"pic":"suqing/teach","days":5,"free":true,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":212,"why":["Every September my new students ask me the same thing in week one: why is everything so hard? Usually it's because they don't have a Chinese phone number yet — riders call you, apps send codes, the bank wants it. So we start there. Five days, one SIM card, and you'll be ready for a real counter.","每年九月，新学生第一个星期都问我同一个问题：为什么什么事都这么难？多半是因为还没有中国手机号——骑手要打给你，软件要发验证码，银行也要。所以我们从这儿开始。五天，一张手机卡，你就能站到真的柜台前。"],"D":[{"k":"说你要办什么","say":["Step one: walk into a China Mobile, China Unicom or China Telecom shop. At the counter, one verb does all the work: 办. You 办 a card, 办 a plan — almost everything official is 办.","第一步：去中国移动、联通或者电信的营业厅。柜台前，一个字就够用：办。办卡、办套餐，几乎所有正式的事都用「办」。"],"line":"I'd like to [get] a SIM card.","z":"我想办一张手机卡。","from":"办事","crowd":[["beijing.tom","I walked in and said 我要买一张卡. The lady said 'oh, 办卡' and smiled. Now I know.","我进去说「我要买一张卡」。阿姨说「哦，办卡」，笑了。现在我知道了。"],["guangzhou.amadou","In Xiaobei everyone does this on day one. I've done it for three cousins now.","在小北，大家第一天都干这个。我已经帮三个表弟办过了。"],["shanghai.sophie","I said I'd like to get a SIM card, and the guard sent me straight to window 3. It worked!","我说「我想办一张手机卡」，保安就让我去 3 号窗口。成了！"]],"shout":["Tom, 买 isn't wrong — but 办卡 is what the counter hears all day. Amadou, three cousins! You're the family's phone shop.","Tom，「买」不算错，可柜台每天听的是「办卡」。Amadou，三个表弟！你就是你们家的营业厅。"]},{"k":"要带什么","say":["Before you go: what do you bring? Phone numbers in China are real-name — every number is linked to an ID. Guess which one a foreigner needs.","出门前：要带什么？中国的手机号是实名的，每个号码都连着一个证件。猜猜外国人要带哪个。"],"line":"Do I need to bring any [documents]?","z":"需要带什么材料吗？","from":"办事","type":"guess","q":["What does a foreigner bring to get a SIM card in China?","外国人在中国办手机卡要带什么？"],"opts":[["Your passport",1],["A photo of your flat",0],["Your school diploma",0]],"reveal":["Your passport — the real one, not a photo. Some shops also look at your visa page.","护照——要原件，不能是照片。有的营业厅还会看你的签证页。"],"crowd":[["chengdu.emma","I called first and asked if I needed any documents. Saved me a second trip!","我先打电话问了「需要带什么材料吗」。省了我跑第二趟！"],["isle.kenji","I brought a photo of my passport. Not enough. Went back home for it. Learned the word 原件.","我带了护照的照片。不够。回家拿了一趟。学会了「原件」。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","Every foreign buyer who visits our factory asks me this. The answer is always: your passport.","来我们工厂的外国客户都问我这个。答案永远是：护照。"]],"shout":["Kenji, 原件 — you'll never forget that word now. Hailey, calling first is pro level.","Kenji，「原件」这个词你这辈子忘不了了。Hailey，先打电话问，这是高手做法。"]},{"k":"问便宜一点的","say":["The staff will show you plans: so many GB, so many minutes, so much a month. You don't have to take the first one. Ask for something cheaper — softly, with 一点.","工作人员会给你看套餐：多少 G 流量、多少分钟、一个月多少钱。不用拿第一个。想要便宜的就问——客气一点，带个「一点」。"],"line":"Do you have a [cheaper] plan?","z":"有没有便宜一点的套餐？","from":"办事","crowd":[["shanghai.sophie","I asked if they had a cheaper one. She found me a plan for half the price. Half!","我问「有没有便宜一点的」。她给我找了个便宜一半的。一半！"],["beijing.tom","I said 有没有更便宜. She understood. My teacher says add 一点 next time — it sounds nicer.","我说「有没有更便宜」。她听懂了。老师说下次加个「一点」，听着客气。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Tip from a local: ask if there's a student plan. Asking costs nothing.","本地人小提示：问问有没有学生套餐。问一下又不吃亏。"]],"shout":["Sophie, half price with one sentence — best deal of the week. Tom, your teacher is right. Your teacher is me.","Sophie，一句话省一半，这周最划算的就是你。Tom，你老师说得对——你老师就是我。"]},{"k":"绑上你的账号","say":["Last step at the counter: your new number is a key. In China you 'bind' it to WeChat, Alipay, your bank card, delivery apps. The word is 绑 — like tying it on.","柜台前最后一步：新号码就是一把钥匙。在中国，你要把它「绑」到微信、支付宝、银行卡、外卖软件上。就是「绑」——像绑一根绳子。"],"line":"Can I [link] this number to Alipay?","z":"这个号能绑定支付宝吗？","from":"办事","crowd":[["guangzhou.amadou","I asked if this number could be linked to Alipay. Yes. Now I pay for herbal tea with my phone like everybody.","我问「这个号能绑定支付宝吗？」能。现在我跟大家一样，用手机付凉茶钱。"],["chengdu.emma","I said 连 instead of 绑. The guy got it, but he laughed a little.","我把「绑」说成了「连」。小哥听懂了，不过笑了一下。"],["beijing.chenhao","Programmer's tip: write the new number down before you leave. Nobody remembers their own new number.","程序员小建议：走之前把新号码记下来。谁都记不住自己的新号码。"]],"shout":["Amadou paying for herbal tea by phone — that new SIM is already working. Hailey, 连 gets you a smile; 绑定 gets it done.","Amadou 用手机买凉茶——新卡已经用上了。Hailey，说「连」换来一个笑，说「绑定」才能办成。"]},{"k":"说你办的第一件事","say":["Last day. Everyone who moves to China has a 'first thing' story — a SIM, a bank card, a flat, a bike. What was yours? Or what will it be?","最后一天。每个来中国的人都有一个「第一件事」的故事：手机卡、银行卡、房子、自行车。你的是什么？或者，会是什么？"],"line":"The first thing I [got done] in China was ___.","z":"我来中国办的第一件事是 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["beijing.tom","The first thing I got done in China was a SIM card. The second was getting lost.","我来中国办的第一件事是办手机卡。第二件事是迷路。"],["shanghai.sophie","The first thing I got done in China was a bank card. Three hours, two forms.","我来中国办的第一件事是办银行卡。花了三个小时，填了两张表。"],["isle.amara","Next trip, the first thing I'll do is get a SIM at the airport — before the taxi.","下次来，我办的第一件事是在机场办张卡，然后再打车。"]],"shout":["Tom, getting lost is everyone's second thing — and there's an activity for that in Shanghai. Sophie, three hours… now that's a real bank story.","Tom，迷路是每个人的第二件事——上海那边正好有个问路的活动。Sophie，三个小时……这才是真正的银行故事。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"SIM: DONE","next":"suqing_bankcard"},"_sources":{"中国手机号实名登记，外国人用护照":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Real-name_system#China","三家运营商：中国移动、中国联通、中国电信":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telecommunications_in_China"},"_review":"母语的人还没审"},{"id":"suqing_suibian","learn":"zh","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"say","soil":"culture","hook":["问「吃什么」，朋友说「随便」。你说火锅，他说「太辣了」——那到底什么叫随便？","You ask what to eat. Your friend says 随便 — 'anything'. You say hotpot. 'Too spicy.' So what does 随便 really mean?"],"t":{"zh":"「随便」到底是什么意思","en":"What does 随便 really mean?"},"pic":"suqing/hutong","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":164,"why":["After the praise week, my students came back with a new complaint: 'I ask a simple question and get 随便, 都行, 看你, 再说吧. Nobody gives me a real answer!' I laughed, because I do it too. These little words are how Chinese people stay polite. Five days, five vague answers — what they really mean, and what to say back.","上完夸奖那一周，学生们又来抱怨：「我问个简单的问题，听到的都是随便、都行、看你、再说吧。没人给我一个真答案！」我笑了，因为我自己也这么说。这几个词，是中国人客气的办法。五天，五个「含糊」的回答——它们到底什么意思，你又怎么接。"],"D":[{"k":"朋友说「随便」","say":["There's an old joke: the hardest dish to order in China is 随便 — because no restaurant has it. When a friend says 随便, don't guess. Give two choices with 还是. Two is easy to pick from.","有个老笑话：中国最难点的菜叫「随便」——因为哪家饭馆都没有。朋友说「随便」，你别猜，用「还是」给两个选择。两个，最好选。"],"line":"Then hotpot [or] noodles?","z":"那吃火锅还是吃面？","from":"约朋友吃饭","crowd":[["beijing.tom","I asked my roommate: then hotpot or noodles? He thought for ten seconds and said noodles. A real answer! First time.","我问室友：那吃火锅还是吃面？他想了十秒，说吃面。一个真答案！头一回。"],["isle.kenji","I said 火锅或者面? She understood, but my teacher says in a question it's 还是.","我说了「火锅或者面？」她听懂了，不过老师说问问题的时候要用「还是」。"],["chengdu.zhouyao","In Chengdu, if your friend says 随便, the answer is hotpot. Always hotpot.","在成都，朋友说「随便」，答案就是火锅。永远是火锅。"]],"shout":["Tom, ten seconds of thinking — that's how you know it worked. Kenji, right: 或者 for 'either is fine', 还是 when you're asking.","Tom，想了十秒——这就说明管用了。Kenji，对：「或者」是哪个都行，问问题就用「还是」。"]},{"k":"你也说「都行」","say":["Now it's your turn to be polite. A friend asks where you want to sit, what time, which film. If you really don't mind, say 都行 — and hand the choice back with 你定吧.","现在轮到你客气了。朋友问你坐哪儿、几点、看哪部电影。你真的无所谓，就说「都行」，再用「你定吧」把选择还给他。"],"line":"[Either is fine] with me — you decide.","z":"我都行，你定吧。","from":"约朋友","crowd":[["shanghai.sophie","Either is fine with me — you decide. My colleague looked so relieved. She had already booked the place.","我都行，你定吧。同事一下子松了口气，她早就订好地方了。"],["stars.emma","I said 我都可以. Also fine, Su Qing says. Then I ate the spiciest thing in Chengdu.","我说的是「我都可以」。苏晴说也行。然后我吃了成都最辣的东西。"],["beijing.chenhao","Careful: say 都行 three times in a row and your friends will think you don't care at all.","小心：连说三次「都行」，朋友会觉得你根本不在乎。"]],"shout":["Sophie, she had booked already — she was just being polite too. Chen Hao is right: one 都行 is kind, three is lazy.","Sophie，她早订好了——她也只是在客气。陈浩说得对：一次「都行」是体贴，三次就是偷懒了。"]},{"k":"听懂「看你」","say":["看你 means 'it depends on you' — what suits you. Chinese people use it to be kind: you decide the time, so you don't have to rush. Answer the same way, and add 方便就行.","「看你」就是「你看着办」——你怎么方便怎么来。中国人这么说是体贴：时间你定，你就不用赶。你也可以这么回，再加一句「方便就行」。"],"line":"[Up to you] — whatever works for you.","z":"看你，你方便就行。","from":"约时间","crowd":[["chengdu.emma","My landlord asked when he could fix the tap. Up to you, whatever works for you. He came at 8 am. Lesson learned.","房东问什么时候来修水龙头。我说：看你，你方便就行。他早上八点就来了。长记性了。"],["more.world.priya","I said 看你 to my Chinese client. He said 看你 back. We did this twice, then I just said Tuesday.","我跟中国客户说「看你」，他也回我「看你」。来回两次，我干脆说了周二。"],["guangzhou.amadou","In my shop the uncles always say 看你. It means: you are the guest, you choose.","在我店里，阿叔们总说「看你」。意思是：你是客人，你来选。"]],"shout":["Hailey, 8 am — he really took 'whatever works for you' to heart. Priya, two rounds then a real day: that's exactly how it's done.","Hailey，早上八点——他是真把「你方便」当真了。Priya，来回两轮再定一天：就是这么办的。"]},{"k":"「再说吧」是什么","type":"guess","say":["This one confuses everyone. You invite a colleague to climb the Great Wall on Saturday. She smiles and says 下次再说吧. What does she mean?","这句最容易搞错。你约同事周六去爬长城。她笑着说「下次再说吧」。她是什么意思？"],"q":["Your colleague says 下次再说吧. She most likely means:","同事说「下次再说吧」，她多半是说："],"opts":[["Probably not this time — a soft no",1],["Please repeat that, I didn't hear you",0],["Yes, see you Saturday at 8",0]],"reveal":["A soft no. 再说 here isn't 'say it again' — it means 'we'll talk about it later'. Don't push. Leave the door open and move on.","是委婉地拒绝。这里的「再说」不是「再说一遍」，是「以后再商量」。别追着问，留个门，就过去了。"],"line":"OK — let me know [when you're free].","z":"好，那你有空再说。","from":"被委婉拒绝","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I thought 再说吧 meant 'say it again'. So I said my invitation again. Slower. She laughed a lot.","我以为「再说吧」是「再说一遍」，就把邀请又说了一遍，还说得更慢。她笑了好久。"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Local tip: if someone really wants to come, they'll give you a day. No day means no.","本地人小提示：真想来的人会跟你说哪天。不说哪天，就是不来。"],["isle.nadia","OK, let me know when you're free. Two weeks later she asked me to go. So sometimes it's a real 'later'!","好，那你有空再说。两周后她真的来约我了。所以有时候「以后」是真的以后！"]],"shout":["Kenji, saying it again slower is the most polite mistake of the week. Nadia, see? Leave the door open and sometimes it opens.","Kenji，慢慢再说一遍——这是这周最客气的错误。Nadia，看到了吧？门留着，有时候就真开了。"]},{"k":"说你真正的答案","say":["Last day. The best answer to 'what do you want to eat?' is not 随便 — it's 都行, plus one honest thing you don't want. Easy to say, and your friend finally has something to work with.","最后一天。「想吃什么？」最好的回答不是「随便」，是「都行」，再加一个你真不想要的。好说，朋友也终于有个方向了。"],"line":"Anything's fine — [just not] ___.","z":"都行，就是别___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.emma","Anything's fine — just not too spicy. Yes, after Chengdu.","都行，就是别太辣。对，成都之后。"],["beijing.tom","Anything's fine — just not too early. Weekend rule.","都行，就是别太早。周末的规矩。"],["isle.mei","Anything's fine — just not far from a bubble tea shop. Taipei rule.","都行，就是别离奶茶店太远。台北的规矩。"]],"shout":["Five days, five vague answers. Now you can hear what people mean — and you can give a real answer, still nicely. That's the whole trick.","五天，五个含糊的回答。现在你听得出别人的意思了，自己也能给个真答案，还不失客气。诀窍就这些。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"ANYTHING'S FINE","next":"suqing_keqi"},"_note":"接着 suqing_praise（夸奖之后，第二种「客气」）。line 写英文意思，学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/suqing_suibian.json。「最难点的菜叫随便」是常见的笑话，不是数据。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"suqing_work","learn":"zh","level":"up","kind":"work","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"life","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"一周用中文说清楚你的工作","en":"Explain your job in Chinese"},"hook":["选你的职业，五天说清楚：做什么、一天、流程、行话、一分钟","Pick your job — five days: what you do, your day, a process, your jargon, one minute"],"pic":"suqing/teach","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":205,"why":["My students can order dumplings perfectly. Then someone at dinner asks 你是做什么的？ and they freeze. This week we fix that — your job, your words, five days.","我的学生点饺子说得很好。可是饭桌上有人问「你是做什么的」，他们就卡住了。这周我们把这个解决：你的工作、你的话，五天。"],"end":{"stamp":"MY JOB","next":"xiaoyu_ai"},"D":[{"k":"我是做什么的","type":"build","say":["At a dinner in China, someone will ask 你是做什么的？ Today: one line — where you work and what you're in charge of. 负责 is the magic word.","在中国吃饭，一定有人问「你是做什么的」。今天就一句：在哪儿、负责什么。「负责」是万能词。"],"line":"I'm [in charge of] ___ at ___.","z":"我在___[负责]___。","own":true,"from":"聊工作","b":{"pre":"","suf":"。","jobs":{"dev":{"n":["程序员","Developer"],"mine":[["我在一家游戏公司负责后端","I'm in charge of the back end at a games company"],["我在一家小公司负责做手机应用","I build mobile apps at a small company"]]},"nurse":{"n":["护士","Nurse"],"mine":[["我在医院急诊科当护士","I'm a nurse in A&E"],["我在医院负责照顾住院的病人","I look after patients on a ward"]]},"trade":{"n":["做外贸","Import & export"],"mine":[["我在一家小公司负责外贸","I handle import-export at a small company"],["我在公司负责跟国外的客户联系","I deal with overseas clients"]]},"student":{"n":["读研","Grad student"],"mine":[["我在大学读研，学的是化学","I'm doing a master's in chemistry"],["我在大学读博，研究城市交通","I'm doing a PhD on urban transport"]]},"teacher":{"n":["老师","Teacher"],"mine":[["我在一所中学教英语","I teach English at a secondary school"],["我在小学负责教数学","I teach maths at a primary school"]]},"office":{"n":["上班族","Office job"],"mine":[["我在一家公司负责做市场","I'm in charge of marketing at a company"],["我在银行负责客户服务","I do customer service at a bank"]]}}},"crowd":[["isle.nadia","I'm a dietitian at a hospital in London. 负责 felt so grown-up!","我在伦敦一家医院负责营养。说「负责」的时候感觉自己好专业！"],["isle.kenji","I'm in charge of the back end at a games company.","我在一家游戏公司负责后端。"]],"shout":["Nadia, 负责 suits you. Everyone: tomorrow, your day in one line.","Nadia，「负责」很适合你。大家明天：用一句话说你的一天。"]},{"k":"我的一天","type":"build","say":["Your day in one line: 先…… then 然后……. Two steps is enough — nobody wants your whole schedule.","用一句话说你的一天：「先……，然后……」。两步就够了，没人想听你的整张日程表。"],"line":"Every day I [first] ___, [then] ___.","z":"我每天[先]___，[然后]___。","own":true,"from":"聊工作","b":{"pre":"我每天","suf":"。","jobs":{"dev":{"n":["程序员","Developer"],"mine":[["先开个短会，然后写一整天代码","first a quick meeting, then code all day"],["先看看昨晚有没有出问题，然后改代码","first check if anything broke overnight, then fix code"]]},"nurse":{"n":["护士","Nurse"],"mine":[["先交班，然后一个个看病人","first the handover, then see patients one by one"],["先看今天有几个新病人，然后发药","first see how many new patients, then give out medicine"]]},"trade":{"n":["做外贸","Import & export"],"mine":[["先回国外客户的邮件，然后去工厂看货","first reply to overseas clients, then check goods at the factory"],["先看今天的订单，然后跟工厂打电话","first look at today's orders, then call the factory"]]},"student":{"n":["读研","Grad student"],"mine":[["先去实验室做实验，然后写论文","first experiments in the lab, then write my thesis"],["先看文献，然后跟导师开会","first read papers, then meet my supervisor"]]},"teacher":{"n":["老师","Teacher"],"mine":[["先上两节课，然后改作业","first teach two classes, then mark homework"],["先备课，然后下午上课","first prepare lessons, then teach in the afternoon"]]},"office":{"n":["上班族","Office job"],"mine":[["先开早会，然后做报表","first the morning meeting, then reports"],["先回邮件，然后见客户","first reply to emails, then meet clients"]]}},"hear":["isle.kenji","我每天先开个短会，然后写一整天代码。","Every day I have a quick meeting first, then code all day."],"ask":["What does Kenji do first?","Kenji 每天先做什么？"],"ao":[["A short meeting",1,"开个短会"],["Write code",0,"写代码"],["Go to the gym",0,"去健身"]]},"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Every day I first have a quick stand-up, then code all day.","我每天先开个短会，然后写一整天代码。"],["more.world.priya","Every day I first check the accounts, then call clients.","我每天先看账，然后给客户打电话。"]]},{"k":"一件事怎么做","type":"build","say":["Pick one thing you do at work and walk us through it: 首先……，接着……，最后……. That's how people explain a process.","挑一件你工作里常做的事，一步步说：「首先……，接着……，最后……」。中文里讲流程就这么说。"],"line":"[First] ___, [next] ___, [finally] ___.","z":"[首先]___，[接着]___，[最后]___。","own":true,"from":"聊工作","b":{"pre":"首先","suf":"。","jobs":{"dev":{"n":["程序员","Developer"],"mine":[["看需求，接着写代码，最后测试","read the requirements, next write code, finally test"],["找到问题，接着改代码，最后再上线","find the bug, next fix it, finally release it"]]},"nurse":{"n":["护士","Nurse"],"mine":[["问病人哪儿不舒服，接着量血压，最后叫医生","ask what's wrong, next take blood pressure, finally call the doctor"],["核对病人的名字，接着给药，最后记下来","check the patient's name, next give the medicine, finally write it down"]]},"trade":{"n":["做外贸","Import & export"],"mine":[["跟客户谈价格，接着下订单，最后安排发货","agree a price, next place the order, finally arrange shipping"],["看样品，接着跟工厂确认，最后报关","check samples, next confirm with the factory, finally do customs"]]},"student":{"n":["读研","Grad student"],"mine":[["查资料，接着做实验，最后写结果","read up, next run the experiment, finally write up the results"],["定题目，接着收数据，最后分析","pick a topic, next collect data, finally analyse it"]]},"teacher":{"n":["老师","Teacher"],"mine":[["复习昨天的，接着讲新课，最后做练习","review yesterday, next teach the new part, finally practise"],["讲一个故事，接着让学生讨论，最后总结","tell a story, next let students discuss, finally sum up"]]},"office":{"n":["上班族","Office job"],"mine":[["定目标，接着做方案，最后跟老板汇报","set a goal, next make a plan, finally report to the boss"],["收客户的问题，接着找同事解决，最后回客户","take the client's question, next solve it with a colleague, finally reply"]]}}},"crowd":[["isle.nadia","First I ask what they usually eat, next I check their blood results, finally I make a plan.","首先问病人平时吃什么，接着看验血结果，最后做个计划。"]]},{"k":"把行话讲给外行听","type":"build","say":["Every job has words outsiders don't get. Take one and say 说白了就是…… — 'basically, it means…'.","每份工作都有外行听不懂的词。挑一个，用「说白了就是……」讲成大白话。"],"line":"___ [basically means] ___.","z":"___[说白了就是]___。","own":true,"from":"聊工作","b":{"pre":"","suf":"。","jobs":{"dev":{"n":["程序员","Developer"],"mine":[["后端说白了就是让服务器别卡","the back end basically means keeping the servers from lagging"],["上线说白了就是让大家都能用上","a release basically means everyone can use it"]]},"nurse":{"n":["护士","Nurse"],"mine":[["分诊说白了就是先看谁最急","triage basically means seeing who's most urgent first"],["交班说白了就是把病人的情况告诉下一班","handover basically means telling the next shift about the patients"]]},"trade":{"n":["做外贸","Import & export"],"mine":[["报关说白了就是给货办个出门证","a customs declaration basically gets the goods a pass to leave"],["打样说白了就是先做一个给客户看看","sampling basically means making one first for the client to check"]]},"student":{"n":["读研","Grad student"],"mine":[["做文献综述说白了就是看看别人都研究过什么","a literature review basically means checking what others have studied"],["答辩说白了就是给老师们讲你的论文","a defence basically means presenting your thesis to the professors"]]},"teacher":{"n":["老师","Teacher"],"mine":[["备课说白了就是提前想好怎么讲","lesson planning basically means working out how to teach it beforehand"],["家长会说白了就是跟爸妈聊孩子","a parents' meeting basically means talking to parents about their kids"]]},"office":{"n":["上班族","Office job"],"mine":[["做市场说白了就是让更多人知道我们","marketing basically means getting more people to know us"],["写周报说白了就是告诉老板这周干了什么","a weekly report basically means telling the boss what you did this week"]]}},"hear":["isle.nadia","分诊说白了就是先看谁最急。","Triage basically means seeing who's most urgent first."],"ask":["What is Nadia doing?","Nadia 在做什么？"],"ao":[["Explaining a work word in plain words",1,"用大白话讲一个行话"],["Describing her day",0,"说她的一天"],["Saying why she likes her job",0,"说她为什么喜欢这份工作"]],"turn":{"s":"报关＿给货办个出门证。","o":[["说白了就是",1,""],["主要是因为",0,"That gives a reason — not what we need here."],["话是这么说",0,"That's for conceding a point."]],"ex":["说白了就是……","basically, in plain words…"]}},"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Debugging basically means finding where it broke.","调试说白了就是找哪儿坏了。"],["more.world.priya","Month-end closing basically means making sure every penny adds up.","月结说白了就是每一分钱都要对得上。"]]},{"k":"一分钟说你的工作","type":"build","say":["Last day! Put your four lines together and add one ending. That's your one-minute answer to 你是做什么的？","最后一天！把前四天的话连起来，再加一句收尾。这就是你回答「你是做什么的」的一分钟。"],"line":"… [All in all] ___.","z":"……[总之]___。","own":true,"from":"聊工作","b":{"pre":"总之，","suf":"。","all":true,"mine":[["虽然累，但是挺有意思的","it's tiring, but quite interesting"],["我挺喜欢我的工作的","I quite like my job"],["有机会可以一起聊聊","let's talk about it sometime"]]},"crowd":[["isle.nadia","…All in all, it's tiring, but really interesting. Said it to my Chinese colleague — she clapped!","……总之，虽然累，但是挺有意思的。说给我的中国同事听，她给我鼓掌了！"]]}],"_note":"进阶活动（2026-11-10，样板 样板/进阶活动玩一遍样板.html）。level: up = 放在「进阶」那一排；type: build = 拼你自己的话（D.b）。只给学中文的人。母语的人还没审。 b.jobs = 选了职业以后，每天可选的说法跟着换（存在 act.v1 的 job）。"},{"id":"suqing_zero","learn":"zh","zh_of":"yuriko_spanish","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"say","soil":"lang","showDays":true,"t":{"zh":"一周后一个人去西安","en":"Zero Chinese, Xi'an in seven days"},"hook":["Lucas 一句中文不会，下周六要一个人去西安吃街边小吃。七天，够不够？","Lucas speaks zero Chinese and goes to Xi'an alone next Saturday for the street food. Are seven days enough?"],"pic":"suqing/jianbing","days":7,"starts":["2026-11-22","2026-12-20"],"n":238,"why":["My new beginners' class has a student from Brazil, Lucas. He knows zero Chinese — and next Saturday he's going to Xi'an alone, for the street food. Seven days, seven lines he'll really use there. Learn them with him.","我新开的零基础班有个巴西学生 Lucas。他一句中文都不会——下周六要一个人去西安吃街边小吃。七天，七句他在那儿真会用上的话。跟他一起学吧。"],"D":[{"k":"第一句你好","say":["你好 is two third tones, so the first one goes up: ní hǎo. Then add 很高兴认识你 — nice to meet you. Lucas sings it now.","「你好」是两个三声，第一个往上扬：ní hǎo。再加一句「很高兴认识你」。Lucas 现在说得像唱歌。"],"line":"Hi, [nice to meet you].","z":"你好，很高兴认识你。","from":"认识新朋友","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Hi, nice to meet you. I said it to the Chinese guy at my gym. Are we friends now?","你好，很高兴认识你。我对健身房的中国人说的。现在我们是朋友了吗？"],["isle.rosa","Hi, nice to meet you! A Chinese family came to my stand. They clapped.","你好，很高兴认识你！一家中国人来我的摊子，他们鼓掌了。"],["beijing.lina","Tourists say this to me at the Forbidden City every day. It always makes my day.","每天都有游客在故宫对我说这句。每次都让我开心一整天。"]],"shout":["Rosa got applause on day one! Lina is right — that's why this is always the first line.","Rosa 第一天就有人鼓掌！李娜说得对，所以第一句永远教这个。"]},{"k":"来一个肉夹馍","say":["In Beijing the morning food is jianbing from a cart. In Xi'an it's 肉夹馍 — like a Chinese burger. Either way, you don't need ‘I would like’. Just 来一个: ‘give me one’.","北京的早上是路边小车上的煎饼，西安是肉夹馍——有点像中国的汉堡。不管哪个，都不用说「我想要」，就说「来一个」。"],"line":"[I'll have one] roujiamo, please.","z":"来一个肉夹馍。","from":"路边小吃","crowd":[["stars.emma","I'll have one roujiamo — I've had them in Xi'an. Trust me, get two.","来一个肉夹馍。我在西安吃过。相信我，来两个。"],["isle.amara","I'll have one jianbing. Beijing layover, 6 am, perfect.","来一个煎饼。北京转机，早上六点，完美。"],["chengdu.zhouyao","In Chengdu we say 来一个 too — for everything.","在成都我们也说「来一个」——什么都这么说。"]],"shout":["Emma says two. Lucas has written it down. Amara, a 6 am jianbing is the best jianbing.","Emma 说要两个，Lucas 已经记下来了。Amara，早上六点的煎饼最好吃。"]},{"k":"这个多少钱","say":["多少钱 — how much. In Xi'an most stalls have a QR code to pay, but asking is still step one. Point, ask, smile.","「多少钱」。西安的小摊大多贴着付款二维码，可先开口问还是第一步。指一下，问一句，笑一下。"],"line":"[How much] is this?","z":"这个多少钱？","from":"买东西","crowd":[["isle.bea","How much is this? At a Chinese supermarket in Manila. She answered in Tagalog, lol.","这个多少钱？在马尼拉的中国超市问的。她用他加禄语回我，哈哈。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","At my factory the answer is always: ‘Depends how many.’","在我们厂，答案永远是：看你要多少。"],["isle.aiko","How much is this? At a Chinese bookshop in Tokyo. 1,500 yen!","这个多少钱？在东京的中文书店问的。一千五百日元！"]],"shout":["Chen Jian, ha — ‘depends how many’ is lesson two. Bea, Tagalog still counts as an answer.","Chen Jian，哈——「看你要多少」是第二课。Bea，他加禄语也算回答了。"]},{"k":"没听懂就再问","say":["Lucas's favourite: 再说一遍 — say it again. People in Xi'an talk fast, with a local accent. Asking again isn't rude. It's smart.","Lucas 最喜欢的一句：「再说一遍」。西安人说话快，还带口音。再问一遍不是没礼貌，是聪明。"],"line":"Sorry, could you [say that again]?","z":"不好意思，能再说一遍吗？","from":"没听懂","crowd":[["isle.amara","Sorry, could you say that again? Three times with a taxi driver. He was so patient!","不好意思，能再说一遍吗？跟出租车师傅用了三次。他很有耐心！"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Tip: if you only catch the last word, repeat it as a question. People love that.","小窍门：只听清最后一个词，就把它当问题重复一遍。大家都很喜欢。"],["more.world.priya","Sorry, could you say that again? My teacher says I say it in my sleep now.","不好意思，能再说一遍吗？我的老师说我现在做梦都在说这句。"]],"shout":["Amara, three times is fine — the driver was probably happy to chat. Zhao Lei's tip really works.","Amara，三次没关系——师傅大概也很乐意聊。赵磊的小窍门真的好用。"]},{"k":"请说慢一点","say":["Second rescue line: 慢一点 — a bit slower. Put 能说 in front and 吗 at the end, and it's polite.","第二句救命的话：「慢一点」。前面加「能说」，后面加「吗」，就很客气了。"],"line":"Could you speak a bit [slower]?","z":"能说慢一点吗？","from":"没听懂","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Could you speak a bit slower? My Chinese colleague did — then switched to English. Hmm.","能说慢一点吗？中国同事真慢下来了——然后换成了英语。嗯……"],["stars.yuriko","Could you speak a bit slower? Same line I need most in Spanish. Languages are friends.","能说慢一点吗？跟我西语里最需要的那句一样。语言都是朋友。"],["beijing.chenhao","As a Beijinger: sorry. We really do talk fast.","作为北京人，抱歉。我们说话确实快。"]],"shout":["Kenji, try 说中文吧 — ‘Chinese, please’. That's the bonus line. Chen Hao, apology accepted.","Kenji，试试「说中文吧」——附加的一句。陈浩，道歉收到了。"]},{"k":"吃到好吃的就夸","say":["In Xi'an, Lucas will eat biangbiang noodles — the character for biáng is one of the most complicated in Chinese. When it's good, say 太好吃了! Cooks love it.","在西安，Lucas 要吃 biangbiang 面——那个 biáng 字是中文里最复杂的字之一。好吃就说「太好吃了！」做饭的人最爱听。"],"line":"This is [so good]!","z":"太好吃了！","from":"吃饭","crowd":[["isle.rosa","So good! At a Chinese restaurant in Guadalajara. The owner gave me free dumplings.","太好吃了！在瓜达拉哈拉的中国餐馆说的。老板送了我饺子。"],["isle.nadia","So good! — my colleague's mum's dumplings. As a dietitian: I had twelve.","太好吃了！——同事妈妈包的饺子。作为营养师：我吃了十二个。"],["chengdu.zhouyao","Say it in Chengdu and the next thing you'll hear is ‘try this one too’. Be careful.","在成都说这句，下一句你会听到「这个也尝尝」。小心点。"]],"shout":["Rosa's free dumplings are the trophy of the week. Nadia — twelve is a scientific number.","Rosa 的饺子是这周的奖杯。Nadia——十二个是科学的数字。"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last day! Tell someone where you're from and one thing you like. Lucas leaves for Xi'an tomorrow — his line is 我是巴西人，我喜欢吃辣.","最后一天！告诉别人你从哪儿来、喜欢什么。Lucas 明天就去西安了——他的那句是「我是巴西人，我喜欢吃辣」。"],"line":"I'm from ___, and I [like] ___.","z":"我是___人，我喜欢___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.emma","I'm French, and I like walking. Every city, every street.","我是法国人，我喜欢走路。每个城市，每条街。"],["more.isle_economy.wanjiru","I'm Kenyan, and I like tea. Chinese tea too!","我是肯尼亚人，我喜欢喝茶。中国茶也喜欢！"],["isle.aiko","I'm Japanese, and I like old records. And Chinese pop from the 80s.","我是日本人，我喜欢老唱片。还有八十年代的华语歌。"]],"shout":["Lucas sent a photo from Xi'an: two roujiamo, one bowl of biangbiang noodles, and a huge smile. Seven days — from zero to lunch. 你们真棒.","Lucas 从西安发来一张照片：两个肉夹馍、一碗 biangbiang 面，还有一个大笑脸。七天——从零到吃上午饭。你们真棒。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"你好","next":"suqing_zero2"},"_note":"学中文的人用的中文版（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"suqing_zero2","learn":"zh","host":"more.friends_a.suqing","cat":"go","soil":"lang","showDays":true,"hook":["Lucas 真的一个人到了西安。五天，每天一条他发回来的消息：肉夹馍、城墙、拍照、回民街。","Lucas really made it to Xi'an alone. Five days, one message from him each day: roujiamo, the city wall, a photo, the Muslim Quarter."],"t":{"zh":"Lucas 一个人在西安","en":"Lucas, alone in Xi'an"},"pic":"suqing/jianbing","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":187,"why":["Lucas made it. Seven days of Chinese, and now he's in Xi'an by himself — and he texts me every evening: 'Teacher, today they asked me something I didn't learn!' So round two is his real trip. Each day, the one line he needed and didn't have. Learn it before you need it.","Lucas 去成了。学了七天中文，现在一个人在西安——每天晚上给我发消息：「老师，今天他们问了我一句没学过的！」所以第二期就是他真实的这趟旅行。每天一句他当时需要、却还不会的话。你先学会，用的时候就不慌。"],"D":[{"k":"肉夹馍要哪种","say":["Lucas's first message: 'I said 来一个肉夹馍, and the man asked me something back!' At a roujiamo stall they often ask: fatty and lean mixed, or lean only? Lucas wanted lean only — 纯瘦.","Lucas 的第一条消息：「我说了来一个肉夹馍，老板又问了我一句！」在肉夹馍摊上，老板常会问：要肥瘦的还是纯瘦的？Lucas 想要全是瘦肉的——就说「纯瘦」。"],"line":"One roujiamo, [lean only], please.","z":"来一个肉夹馍，要纯瘦的。","from":"路边小吃","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I said 不要胖的. The man laughed so much he gave me extra meat. Fat meat is 肥, not 胖!","我说「不要胖的」。老板笑得不行，还多给了我肉。肉要说「肥」，不是「胖」！"],["stars.emma","Get the mixed one. Trust me, the fat is the point.","要肥瘦的。相信我，好吃就好吃在那点肥。"],["isle.nadia","One roujiamo, lean only, please. Dietitian's choice. Okay, I also ate half of my friend's mixed one.","来一个肉夹馍，要纯瘦的。营养师的选择。好吧，我还吃了朋友那个肥瘦的一半。"]],"shout":["Kenji, 不要胖的 — he'll remember you forever. People are 胖, meat is 肥. Nadia, half of your friend's counts as research.","Kenji，「不要胖的」——老板这辈子都忘不了你。人说「胖」，肉说「肥」。Nadia，吃朋友的一半，算科研。"]},{"k":"城墙上租自行车","say":["Day two, Lucas went up the city wall. It goes all the way around the old city, almost 14 kilometres, and you can ride a bike on top. He couldn't find where to rent one. One question fixes that.","第二天，Lucas 上了城墙。城墙绕着老城一整圈，将近十四公里，上面能骑自行车。他找不到在哪儿租车，一句话就解决了。"],"line":"Excuse me, where can I [rent a bike]?","z":"请问，在哪儿租自行车？","from":"问路","crowd":[["beijing.tom","Excuse me, where can I rent a bike? The guard pointed. Then I rode the whole wall. My legs are not my friends today.","请问，在哪儿租自行车？保安指了一下。然后我骑了整圈城墙。今天我的腿不是我的朋友。"],["chengdu.emma","I asked 在哪儿买自行车. The lady said: you want to buy one? To take home?","我问「在哪儿买自行车」。阿姨说：你要买一辆？带回家？"],["more.world.priya","Saving this line for my trip. Also learned 还车 — giving it back. Important!","这句我存起来，旅行用。还学了「还车」——还回去。很重要！"]],"shout":["Tom, your legs will forgive you tomorrow. Hailey — 买 a bike to take home, ha. 租 is for a few hours.","Tom，你的腿明天会原谅你的。Hailey——买一辆带回家，哈。骑几个小时是「租」。"]},{"k":"请人帮你拍照","say":["Lucas at the Bell Tower: 'Teacher, I have a hundred selfies and zero photos of me with the tower.' Ask someone. Chinese people are used to it — most will happily say 好啊.","Lucas 在钟楼：「老师，我拍了一百张自拍，可一张都没有我跟钟楼一起的。」找个人问一下。中国人很习惯了，多半会痛快地说「好啊」。"],"line":"Could you [take a photo] of me?","z":"能帮我拍张照吗？","from":"旅行","crowd":[["isle.mei","Could you take a photo of me? A grandma in Taipei took twenty and told me to smile more.","能帮我拍张照吗？台北一位阿嬷给我拍了二十张，还叫我多笑一点。"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Bonus line: 把塔拍进去 — 'get the tower in'. Otherwise you'll get a perfect photo of your face.","送一句：「把塔拍进去」。不然你会得到一张很完美的大头照。"],["isle.kenji","I said 能帮我拍照片吗. She understood. Then she asked me to take one of her too.","我说「能帮我拍照片吗？」她听懂了。然后她也让我给她拍一张。"]],"shout":["Mei, twenty photos and smiling advice — grandmas are the best photographers. Zhao Lei's 把塔拍进去 is the line Lucas needed most.","Mei，二十张外加笑容指导——阿嬷才是最好的摄影师。赵磊那句「把塔拍进去」，才是 Lucas 最需要的。"]},{"k":"回民街的泡馍","type":"guess","say":["Last night Lucas went to the Muslim Quarter near the Drum Tower and ordered 羊肉泡馍, lamb soup with bread. The waiter put a round, hard bread and an empty bowl in front of him. Then walked away. Guess what Lucas had to do.","昨晚 Lucas 去了鼓楼旁边的回民街，点了一碗羊肉泡馍。服务员在他面前放了一个圆圆的、硬硬的馍，一个空碗，就走了。猜猜 Lucas 得干什么。"],"q":["In a traditional 羊肉泡馍 place, what do you do with the bread first?","在老式的羊肉泡馍馆，馍拿到手先干什么？"],"opts":[["Tear it into small pieces yourself",1],["Give it back — it's only for show",0],["Put it in your bag for tomorrow",0]],"reveal":["You tear it yourself, into small pieces — that's called 掰馍. Then the kitchen cooks it in the soup. It's slow, and that's the fun: people chat while they tear.","自己掰，掰成小块——这叫「掰馍」。掰好了，后厨再拿去煮。很慢，可好玩就好玩在这儿：大家边掰边聊天。"],"line":"Excuse me, [how do I eat] this?","z":"不好意思，这个怎么吃？","from":"吃饭","crowd":[["stars.emma","Excuse me, how do I eat this? The uncle at the next table showed me. Then he said my pieces were too big.","不好意思，这个怎么吃？旁边桌的大叔教了我。然后他说我掰得太大了。"],["isle.amara","I started eating the dry bread. Nobody stopped me for a whole minute. Then everyone did.","我直接啃起了干馍。一整分钟没人拦我。然后所有人都来拦我。"],["beijing.chenhao","Beijinger confession: I also asked how to eat it, my first time in Xi'an.","北京人坦白：我第一次去西安，也问了这个怎么吃。"]],"shout":["Emma, 'too big' means he cared. Amara, one minute of dry bread is a brave minute. Chen Hao, thank you — see, even locals ask.","Emma，嫌你掰得大，说明他在乎。Amara，啃了一分钟干馍，勇敢的一分钟。陈浩，谢谢——看，连中国人也要问。"]},{"k":"说你最想做的事","say":["Lucas's last message: 'Teacher, the best thing in Xi'an was riding the wall at sunset.' Now you. Pick a city — Xi'an or anywhere — and say the one thing you most want to do there.","Lucas 最后一条消息：「老师，西安最好的是傍晚在城墙上骑车。」现在轮到你。挑一个城市——西安或者别的地方——说你最想在那儿做的一件事。"],"line":"When I get to ___, the thing I [most want] to do is ___.","z":"到了___，我最想___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.nadia","When I get to Xi'an, the thing I most want to do is eat roujiamo on the wall. Lean only. Probably.","到了西安，我最想在城墙上吃肉夹馍。纯瘦的。大概吧。"],["more.world.priya","When I get to Beijing, the thing I most want to do is find Su Qing's hutong.","到了北京，我最想找到苏晴住的那条胡同。"],["isle.kenji","When I get to Chengdu, I most want to see pandas. And not get lost.","到了成都，我最想看熊猫。还有，别迷路。"]],"shout":["Lucas came home with a photo of himself and the Bell Tower — the tower fully in. From zero to travelling alone in two weeks. You can too.","Lucas 回来带了一张他跟钟楼的合影——钟楼拍进去了。两个星期，从零到一个人旅行。你也行。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"XI'AN SOLO","next":"suqing_zero3"},"_sources":{"西安城墙一圈约 13.7 公里，城墙上可以租自行车":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortifications_of_Xi%27an","回民街在鼓楼附近":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muslim_Quarter,_Xi%27an","羊肉泡馍要自己把馍掰成小块":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paomo"},"_note":"接着 suqing_zero（Lucas 学了七天去西安），第二期是他在西安的五天。地方都是真的：城墙、钟楼、鼓楼旁的回民街。没写价钱。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"tom_veg","host":"isle.tom","cat":"eat","t":{"zh":"让小孩多吃一口菜","en":"One more bite of veg"},"pic":"tom/kitchen","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":88,"why":["Ten years, three hundred lunches a day — I've learnt a few tricks for getting veg into small people. Got a kid at home, or a grown-up who won't touch greens? Could be you. Come along.","十年，每天三百份午饭——让小家伙吃菜，我攒了几招。家里有孩子，或者有个死活不碰青菜的大人？说不定就是你自己。一起来。"],"D":[{"k":"只要一小口","say":["Don't ask for a plateful. Ask for one bite. One bite is small enough to say yes to.","别要求吃一盘。只要一口。一口小到让人愿意说好。"],"line":"Just [one bite], then tell me what you think.","z":"就尝一口，然后告诉我怎么样。","from":"饭桌上","crowd":[["isle.rosa","Just one bite! My son tried the zucchini. He said it tastes like ‘nothing’. Ay, that's a win.","就尝一口！我儿子尝了西葫芦。他说吃起来「什么味都没有」。哎，这就算赢了。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","I am the grown-up who won't eat greens. One bite of spinach. Still alive.","我就是那个不吃青菜的大人。吃了一口菠菜。还活着。"]],"shout":["Rosa, ‘tastes like nothing’ is a brilliant first review, mate. Nothing beats ‘yuck’.","Rosa，「什么味都没有」是很棒的第一条评价。总比「好难吃」强。"]},{"k":"给菜起个名字","say":["Here broccoli is ‘dinosaur trees’. Kids eat more when they've named it themselves. Let them pick.","我们这儿的西兰花叫「恐龙树」。小孩自己起了名字，就吃得更多。让他们来起。"],"line":"What should we [call] it?","z":"我们给它起个什么名字？","from":"跟小孩说话","crowd":[["isle.mei","My little cousin called carrots ‘orange swords’ and ate four lol","我小表弟把胡萝卜叫「橙色宝剑」，吃了四根 lol"],["isle.kenji","No kids, so I asked my plant what to call the peas. It said nothing. Very rude.","没孩子，所以我问我的盆栽豌豆该叫什么。它没理我。真没礼貌。"]],"shout":["Mei — orange swords! I'm nicking that for the Christmas menu.","Mei——橙色宝剑！我要偷来用在圣诞菜单上。"]},{"k":"让他们帮忙","say":["Kids eat what they've helped make. Give them a job: wash it, tear it, stir it.","小孩会吃自己帮忙做的东西。给他们一个活儿：洗、撕、搅。"],"line":"Can you [help me] wash these?","z":"能帮我洗一下这些吗？","from":"厨房里","crowd":[["isle.rosa","Can you help me wash these? My daughter said ‘only if I can film it.’ Teenagers.","能帮我洗一下吗？我女儿说「除非让我拍下来」。青春期的孩子啊。"],["isle.linhao","Asked my flatmate to help wash the bok choy. Now he wants to cook it every week.","让室友帮我洗小白菜。现在他每周都想做。"]],"shout":["Linhao, you've converted a Frenchman to bok choy. That's diplomacy.","林浩，你让一个法国人爱上了小白菜。这叫外交。"]},{"k":"今天不吃也没事","say":["No isn't forever. Lots of kids need to try a new food loads of times before they like it. So no fuss — just try again another day.","不吃不是永远不吃。很多小孩要试很多很多次，才会喜欢一样新东西。所以别闹——改天再试。"],"line":"That's okay. [Maybe next time].","z":"没关系，下次再试。","from":"饭桌上","crowd":[["isle.nadia","That's okay, maybe next time. Saying this to adults in clinic too, honestly.","没关系，下次再试。说实话，我在诊室里对大人也这么说。"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Tried the spinach again. Still no. That's okay. Maybe next time, spinach.","又试了菠菜。还是不行。没关系。菠菜，下次再说。"]],"shout":["Xiaoyu tried it twice. That's two more than most grown-ups. Keep going.","小雨试了两次。比大多数大人多两次。继续。"]},{"k":"说你自己小时候","say":["Last day. Everyone hated a veg once. Tell me yours — and what you think of it now.","最后一天。每个人小时候都讨厌过一样菜。说说你的——还有你现在怎么看它。"],"line":"When I was a kid, I [hated] ___. Now I ___.","z":"我小时候讨厌 ___。现在我 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","When I was a kid, I hated green peppers. Now I eat them, but I still don't trust them.","我小时候讨厌青椒。现在我吃，但还是不信任它。"],["isle.mei","When I was a kid, I hated bitter melon. Now I order it at the night market with my mum 🥒","我小时候讨厌苦瓜。现在我跟我妈在夜市会点它 🥒"],["isle.amara","When I was a kid, I hated okra. Now I miss my grandma's okra soup in every city, my dear.","我小时候讨厌秋葵。现在每到一座城，我都想外婆的秋葵汤，亲爱的。"]],"shout":["Five days, cheers everyone. Amara, I hope there's okra soup waiting in Lagos. Next up: Christmas lunch for two hundred.","五天，谢谢大家。Amara，希望拉各斯有一碗秋葵汤在等你。下一个：两百个孩子的圣诞午餐。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"ONE MORE BITE","next":"tom_xmas"}},{"id":"xiaoyu_ai","learn":"zh","level":"up","kind":"opinion","host":"isle.xiaoyu","cat":"say","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"AI 会抢走你的工作吗？","en":"Will AI take my job?"},"hook":["一周一个吵不完的问题：表态、给理由、让步、举例，最后说出你自己的一段","One question, five days: take a side, give a reason, concede, give an example — then say your whole view"],"pic":"xiaoyu/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":241,"why":["Everyone in my office asks this at lunch. Most people just say 'no idea'. This week, let's learn to actually answer — five lines, five days, and by Friday you can say a whole paragraph of what YOU think.","我们公司午饭时人人都在问这个。大部分人只会说「不知道」。这周我们学着真的回答：五天五句，到周五你能用中文说一整段你自己的看法。"],"end":{"stamp":"MY VIEW","next":"linhao_tip"},"D":[{"k":"表态","type":"build","say":["Day 1: just take a side. 我觉得…… is the easiest way in — calm, not rude. Pick the one closest to you.","第一天：先表个态。「我觉得……」最好用，不冲。选最像你的那句。"],"line":"I [think] ___.","z":"我[觉得]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"我觉得","suf":"。","mine":[["不会，至少我的工作不会","I don't think so — not my job, anyway"],["会，有一部分会","Yes, partly"],["说不好，要看是什么工作","Hard to say — it depends on the job"]]},"crowd":[["isle.kenji","I think partly. Half my code is already written by AI, lol.","我觉得会，有一部分会。我一半的代码已经是 AI 写的了，哈哈。"],["isle.nadia","I don't think so — not my job, anyway. A machine can't calm a scared patient.","我觉得不会，至少我的工作不会。机器安慰不了害怕的病人。"],["london.oliver","Hard to say. Half our newsroom is worried.","我觉得说不好。我们编辑部一半的人都在担心。"]],"shout":["Nadia gave a reason without being asked — 至少我的工作不会. That 至少 is gold.","Nadia 没人问就给了理由——「至少我的工作不会」。这个「至少」用得太好了。"]},{"k":"给理由","type":"build","say":["Now say why. 主要是因为…… = mainly because. One reason, said clearly, beats three.","今天说理由：「主要是因为……」。一个理由说清楚，比说三个强。"],"line":"[Mainly because] ___.","z":"[主要是因为]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"主要是因为","suf":"。","mine":[["我的工作要跟人打交道","my job is about dealing with people"],["我的工作每天都不一样","my work is different every day"],["很多简单的活儿 AI 已经能做了","AI can already do a lot of the simple tasks"]],"hear":["isle.kenji","我觉得会，主要是因为写代码的活儿 AI 越来越会了。","I think yes — mainly because AI keeps getting better at coding."],"ask":["Does Kenji think AI will take some of his work?","Kenji 觉得 AI 会抢走他的一部分活儿吗？"],"ao":[["Yes — and he says why",1,"会，他还说了理由"],["No, not at all",0,"完全不会"],["He isn't sure",0,"他说不好"]]},"crowd":[["isle.mei","Mainly because my job is about people. Nobody wants a robot asking 'how sweet?'","主要是因为我的工作要跟人打交道。谁想让机器人问「几分甜」啊。"],["london.oliver","Mainly because AI can already write the simple stories.","主要是因为简单的稿子 AI 已经能写了。"]],"shout":["Mei made me laugh — and she used 主要是因为 perfectly. One reason, done.","Mei 把我逗笑了——「主要是因为」用得刚刚好。一个理由，说完。"]},{"k":"让步","type":"build","say":["Today: agree a little, then turn. 话是这么说，但…… makes you sound fair, not stubborn.","今天学让步：先承认一点，再转回来。「话是这么说，但……」听起来讲道理，不固执。"],"line":"[That's true, but] ___.","z":"[话是这么说，但]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"话是这么说，但","suf":"。","mine":[["AI 写东西确实比我快","AI does write faster than me"],["有些事 AI 还是做不了","there are things AI still can't do"],["AI 也会出错","AI makes mistakes too"]],"hear":["isle.kenji","话是这么说，但写代码只是我工作的一半。","That's true, but coding is only half my job."],"ask":["Does Kenji think AI will take his job?","Kenji 觉得 AI 会抢走他的工作吗？"],"ao":[["Yes, he's worried",0,"会，他很担心"],["Not really — he pushes back",1,"不太会，他反驳了"],["He doesn't say",0,"他没说"]],"turn":{"s":"话是这么说，＿写代码只是我工作的一半。","o":[["但",1,""],["因为",0,"因为 gives a reason — that was Day 2!"],["比如",0,"比如 is for examples — that's tomorrow."]],"ex":["话是这么说，但……","That's true, but…"]}},"crowd":[["isle.nadia","That's true, but there are things AI still can't do. Like holding a hand.","话是这么说，但有些事 AI 还是做不了。比如握着病人的手。"],["isle.kenji","That's true, but AI makes mistakes too. I fix them every day.","话是这么说，但 AI 也会出错。我每天都在帮它改。"]],"shout":["Kenji used his own life — 我每天都在帮它改. That's what makes a 但 land.","Kenji 用的是自己的事——「我每天都在帮它改」。「但」后面放真事，才有分量。"]},{"k":"举例","type":"build","say":["Back it up with one example. 就拿……来说 — take … for example.","举一个例子撑住你的看法：「就拿……来说」。"],"line":"[Take] ___ [for example], ___.","z":"[就拿]___[来说]，___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"就拿","suf":"。","mine":[["写邮件来说，它一秒就写完了","writing emails — it's done in a second"],["看病来说，病人还是想见真人","seeing a doctor — patients still want a real person"],["翻译来说，它已经很好用了","translation — it's already really useful"]],"hear":["london.oliver","就拿新闻来说，简单的稿子 AI 已经能写了。","Take news, for example: AI can already write simple stories."],"ask":["What is Oliver doing?","Oliver 在做什么？"],"ao":[["Giving an example from his work",1,"拿自己的工作举例子"],["Saying he's quitting",0,"说他要辞职"],["Asking a question",0,"在问问题"]],"turn":{"s":"＿开车来说，很多城市已经有无人驾驶出租车了。","o":[["就拿",1,""],["但",0,"但 is for turning — that was Day 3."],["因为",0,"因为 gives a reason — Day 2."]],"ex":["就拿……来说","Take … for example"]}},"crowd":[["isle.mei","Take ordering, for example: my shop got a machine, and people still queue for me.","就拿点单来说，我们店放了一台机器，大家还是排队找我。"],["isle.kenji","Take writing emails, for example: it's done in a second.","就拿写邮件来说，它一秒就写完了。"]],"shout":["Mei's example was a real story from her shop. That's the best kind.","Mei 举的是她店里的真事。这种例子最好。"]},{"k":"整段说","type":"build","say":["Last day! Add one 所以 line, then say the whole thing. That's your view, in Chinese.","最后一天！加一句「所以……」，再把整段说出来。这就是你用中文说出来的看法。"],"line":"… [So] ___.","z":"……[所以]___。","own":true,"from":"聊观点","b":{"pre":"所以","suf":"。","mine":[["我会学着用它，而不是怕它","I'll learn to use it, not fear it"],["我觉得不用太担心","I don't think we need to worry too much"],["我们都得学点新东西","we all need to learn something new"]],"all":true},"crowd":[["isle.nadia","…So I don't think we need to worry too much. Five days ago I could only say 我觉得不会!","……所以我觉得不用太担心。五天前我只会说「我觉得不会」！"],["isle.kenji","…So I'll learn to use it, not fear it. Sent to my Chinese team!","……所以我会学着用它，而不是怕它。发给我的中国同事了！"]]}],"_note":"进阶活动（2026-11-10，样板 样板/进阶活动玩一遍样板.html）。level: up = 放在「进阶」那一排；type: build = 拼你自己的话（D.b）。只给学中文的人。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"xiaoyu_phone","learn":"zh","zh_of":"linhao_phone","host":"isle.xiaoyu","cat":"life","soil":"lang","hook":["在中国，电话多半是别人打给你","In China, most calls are someone calling you"],"t":{"zh":"电话响了，是外卖小哥","en":"The phone rings: it's your delivery"},"pic":"xiaoyu/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-18","2026-12-16"],"n":176,"why":["I work in e-commerce, so my life is parcels and food delivery. Funny thing: in China you hardly ever call anyone — you order in an app. But then the rider calls YOU, fast, from a noisy street. Five days, five calls, and you'll pick up without panicking.","我做电商运营，天天跟快递、外卖打交道。好玩的是：在中国你很少主动打电话，都在软件里下单。可是骑手会打给你，说得飞快，旁边还很吵。五天，五个电话，你接起来就不慌了。"],"D":[{"k":"先说喂","say":["Every call starts with 喂. On the phone it usually goes up, like a question: wéi? Then add 您好. Today, just pick up.","每个电话都从「喂」开始。接电话时一般往上扬，像在问问题：wéi？再加一句「您好」。今天，先把电话接起来。"],"line":"[Hello?] Who's calling?","z":"喂，您好，哪位？","from":"打电话","crowd":[["shanghai.sophie","My first call: hello? And then silence, because I panicked. Today I added 您好 too!","我第一次接电话：「喂？」然后就没声了，因为我慌了。今天我还说了「您好」！"],["beijing.sun","I'm a courier. Ten seconds a call, dozens of calls a day. A clear 喂 makes my day.","我是快递员。一个电话十秒，一天几十个。一声清楚的「喂」就让我很开心。"],["isle.kwame","I said 喂 the Ghana way — long and singing. The rider laughed and sang it back.","我用加纳的口气说了「喂——」，拖得很长。骑手笑了，也那样回了我一句。"]],"shout":["Sun, thank you for every one of those calls. Sophie, silence is OK — 您好 is already a whole conversation.","小孙，谢谢你的每一个电话。Sophie，没声也没事——一句「您好」已经是完整的对话了。"]},{"k":"外卖到楼下了","say":["The rider calls: 'Hi, your food's here, I'm downstairs.' Lots of housing compounds — 小区 — don't let riders in, so you meet at the gate. Learners often say 社区, but your home is in a 小区.","骑手打来：「您好，您的外卖到了，在楼下。」很多小区不让骑手进，你就去门口拿。学的人常说「社区」，可你住的地方叫「小区」。"],"line":"I'll [meet you at the gate] of the compound.","z":"我在小区门口等你。","from":"打电话","crowd":[["chengdu.emma","I said I'd wait at the compound gate — and I really waited. He came from the other gate 😅","我说「我在小区门口等你」，也真的在等。结果他从另一个门来了 😅"],["shanghai.xiaoli","Rider here. Please say WHICH gate — east, west, north. Big compounds have four.","我是骑手。麻烦说是哪个门——东门、西门、北门。大小区有四个门。"],["beijing.tom","I said 社区门口. He found me anyway. Then I learned 小区.","我说成了「社区门口」。他还是找到我了。后来我才学会「小区」。"]],"shout":["Xiao Li, thank you — east gate or west gate, everyone write that down. Hailey, next time say 东门.","小李，谢谢你——东门还是西门，大家记下来。Hailey，下次说「东门」。"]},{"k":"快递放哪儿","say":["Next call: the courier. 'Are you home? Where shall I leave it?' You don't have to run downstairs. Say leave it at the door — or in the parcel locker.","下一个电话：快递员。「你在家吗？放哪儿？」你不用跑下楼。说「放门口」——或者放快递柜。"],"line":"Just [leave it at the door], thanks.","z":"放门口就行，谢谢。","from":"打电话","crowd":[["guangzhou.amadou","'Just leave it at the door' — my favourite sentence in Chinese. It saved my lazy Sunday.","「放门口就行」——我最喜欢的一句中文。救了我懒洋洋的周日。"],["beijing.sun","Courier again: if you say the locker, I'll text you the pickup code. Faster for both of us.","又是快递员：你说「放快递柜」，我就把取件码发给你。咱俩都快。"],["isle.kenji","I said 放在门的前面. He said 'OK, 门口' — same thing, much shorter.","我说「放在门的前面」。他说「好，门口」——一样的意思，短多了。"]],"shout":["Amadou, lazy Sundays are what 放门口 was made for. Kenji, 门口 — two characters, done.","Amadou，「放门口」就是为懒洋洋的周日发明的。Kenji，「门口」两个字，搞定。"]},{"k":"打电话订位","say":["Now YOU call — a hot pot place on a Friday night. They fill up. Say the time first, then how many: tonight at seven, two people.","现在轮到你打——周五晚上的火锅店。会满的。先说时间，再说几个人：今晚七点，两个人。"],"line":"I'd like to [book a table] — tonight at seven, two people.","z":"我想订个位子，今晚七点，两个人。","from":"打电话","crowd":[["shanghai.sophie","I said 我想预订一张桌子. The lady said 'a booking, right?' — yes, that.","我说「我想预订一张桌子」。阿姨说「订位是吧？」——对，就是这个。"],["beijing.chenhao","Engineer's tip: say the number of people twice. Restaurants are loud.","程序员小建议：人数说两遍。饭店很吵。"],["chengdu.emma","I booked hot pot for six! On the phone! Tonight at seven, six people. My hands are shaking.","我订了六个人的火锅！打电话订的！「今晚七点，六个人。」我手还在抖。"]],"shout":["Hailey, six people and a hot pot — you're the hero of that table tonight. Sophie, 订位 — that's the word.","Hailey，六个人的火锅——今晚那桌你最厉害。Sophie，就是「订位」。"]},{"k":"打你自己的电话","say":["Last day. You've picked up, met a rider, saved a parcel, booked a table. Now make your own call: who would you ring, and what do you want to ask? Start with 我想问一下.","最后一天。你接过电话、等过骑手、留过快递、订过位子。现在打你自己的电话：打给谁，想问什么？用「我想问一下」开头。"],"line":"Hi, [I'd like to ask] ___.","z":"喂，您好，我想问一下 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["beijing.tom","Hi, I'd like to ask — can you deliver to my school? They can!","喂，您好，我想问一下，你们能送到我们学校吗？能！"],["shanghai.sophie","Hi, I'd like to ask if you're open on Mondays. I called. In Chinese. On my own.","喂，您好，我想问一下，你们周一开门吗？我打了。用中文。一个人打的。"],["isle.amara","Hi, I'd like to ask if I can move to a higher floor. Practising for my Shanghai layover.","喂，您好，我想问一下，能换到高一点的楼层吗？为上海转机练的。"]],"shout":["Sophie, on your own, in Chinese — that's the whole activity in one call. Tom, delivery to school? I'm jealous.","Sophie，一个人、用中文——这一个电话就是整个活动。Tom，能送到学校？我好羡慕。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"PICKED UP","next":"xiaoyu_shopping"},"_sources":{"「喂」接电话时常读第二声 wéi":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%E5%96%82"},"_review":"母语的人还没审"},{"id":"xiaoyu_shopping","learn":"zh","host":"isle.xiaoyu","cat":"life","soil":"lang","hook":["在中国，网上买东西比出门买还快","In China, shopping online is faster than going out"],"t":{"zh":"快递到了，取件码多少？","en":"Your parcel's here: what's the code?"},"pic":"xiaoyu/work","days":5,"free":true,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":189,"why":["You can pick up the phone now. Next: the parcels themselves. In China almost everything comes by delivery — clothes, rice, even a sofa. I work in e-commerce, so I see the other side too: the chat with customer service, the returns, the review. Five days, one parcel, from pickup to review.","电话你已经会接了。下一步：快递本身。在中国几乎什么都是送来的——衣服、大米，连沙发都是。我做电商运营，所以也看得到另一边：跟客服聊、退货、评价。五天，一个包裹，从取件到好评。"],"D":[{"k":"去取快递","say":["Your parcel is often not at your door — it's at a pickup station or a parcel locker near your compound. The app texts you a pickup code. Go and say it. Short is best.","你的快递常常不在门口，而在小区附近的驿站或者快递柜里。软件会给你发一个取件码。去了直接说，越短越好。"],"line":"Hi, I'm here to [pick up a parcel]. The code is 3-2-1-8.","z":"你好，我[取快递]，取件码 3218。","from":"取快递","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Hi, pick-up, code 3218. Said it in four seconds. The guy didn't even look up.","你好，取快递，取件码 3218。四秒说完。小哥头都没抬。"],["london.oliver","I said the code in English by mistake. He just said: show me your phone. Fair.","我一不小心用英文念了取件码。他就说：手机给我看看。也对。"],["isle.linhao","Tip: 四 and 十 sound close. Say each number slowly, one by one.","提醒：「四」和「十」听起来很像。号码一个一个慢慢念。"]],"shout":["Kenji, four seconds — you're faster than me. Oliver, showing your phone always works; next time try saying it once first.","Kenji，四秒——比我还快。Oliver，给手机看永远管用；下次先试着念一遍。"]},{"k":"问客服有没有大一号","say":["Before you buy, you chat with customer service in the app. On Taobao they often call you 亲 — 'dear'. It's normal, it's friendly, it's everywhere lol. Ask if they have a bigger size.","买之前，你会在软件里跟客服聊。淘宝的客服常常叫你「亲」。这很正常，很亲切，到处都是 lol。问问有没有大一号的。"],"line":"Do you have this [one size bigger]?","z":"这件有[大一号]的吗？","from":"跟客服聊","crowd":[["stars.emma","Asked for one size bigger. They replied: 'Dear, yes!' in two seconds. I felt so loved.","问了有没有大一号的。两秒就回：「亲，有的哦！」我感觉被爱了。"],["isle.nadia","I asked 有没有更大的. They sent me a size chart. Then I learned 大一号.","我问的是「有没有更大的」。他们发了张尺码表给我。后来我才学会「大一号」。"],["more.world.priya","Chinese sizes run small for me. I always ask for one bigger now.","中国的尺码对我来说偏小。现在我都问大一号的。"]],"shout":["Emma, 亲 means they love everyone, but OK lol. Nadia, a size chart is a good answer too.","Emma，「亲」是对谁都爱，不过也行 lol。Nadia，发尺码表也是好回答。"]},{"k":"七天无理由退货","say":["It doesn't fit. Good news: in China, most things you buy online can be sent back within seven days of getting them, with no reason needed — it's in the consumer law. Some things don't count, like fresh food or custom-made things. Tell the shop you want to return it.","不合适。好消息：在中国，网上买的大部分东西，收到后七天内都可以退，不用说理由——这是消费者权益保护法里写的。也有不算的，比如生鲜、定做的东西。跟店家说你想退货。"],"line":"It doesn't fit, I'd like to [return it].","z":"不合适，我想[退货]。","from":"跟客服聊","crowd":[["isle.kenji","It doesn't fit, I'd like to return it. They said OK and sent a courier to my door the next day.","不合适，我想退货。他们说好，第二天就派快递员上门来取了。"],["london.oliver","I said 我想还它. Customer service was confused — 还 is for things you borrowed.","我说的是「我想还它」。客服没懂——「还」是借来的东西用的。"],["isle.linhao","Many orders come with return-shipping insurance, 运费险. Check before you pay for postage.","很多订单带「运费险」。寄回去之前先看看要不要自己付运费。"]],"shout":["Oliver, 还 for borrowed, 退 for bought — good one to remember. Linhao, 运费险 has saved me so much money.","Oliver，借的用「还」，买的用「退」——这个要记住。林浩，「运费险」帮我省了好多钱。"]},{"k":"给个好评","say":["The second one fits! Now the shop sends a message: 'Dear, if you're happy, please give us a five-star review!' Reviews matter a lot to sellers here. If you're really happy, tell them you gave one.","第二件合适了！这时店家会发消息：「亲，满意的话给个五星好评哦！」在这里，评价对卖家很重要。真满意的话，就告诉他们你给了。"],"line":"It's great, I [gave you a good review].","z":"东西很好，我给了[好评]。","from":"跟客服聊","crowd":[["isle.nadia","It's great, I gave a good review — and wrote three lines. In Chinese! Mostly emojis.","东西很好，我给了好评，还写了三行。用中文！大部分是表情。"],["stars.emma","I gave a good review with a photo of me wearing it. The shop replied with five hearts.","我给了好评，还发了一张穿上的照片。店家回了五颗爱心。"],["isle.kenji","Honest question: what if it's not great? I wrote 一般. That's a real review word, right?","说实话：如果不好呢？我写了「一般」。这也是真的评价用语吧？"]],"shout":["Kenji, yes — 一般 is honest and very Chinese. Emma, a photo review: shops love those.","Kenji，对——「一般」很诚实，也很中国。Emma，带照片的评价，店家最喜欢。"]},{"k":"你在网上买了什么","say":["Last day! Pickup, size, return, review — the whole life of a parcel. Now tell me about your own: what did you buy online lately? Something useful, something silly, anything.","最后一天！取件、尺码、退货、好评——一个包裹的一生你都走过了。现在说说你自己的：你最近在网上买了什么？有用的、好笑的，都行。"],"line":"Lately I [bought ___ online].","z":"我最近[在网上买了] ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["london.oliver","Lately I bought a rice cooker online. Arrived the next morning. Rice by lunch.","我最近在网上买了一个电饭锅。第二天早上就到了。中午就吃上了米饭。"],["more.world.priya","Lately I bought winter boots online. One size bigger, of course.","我最近在网上买了一双冬天的靴子。当然是大一号的。"],["isle.linhao","Lately I bought Chinese snacks online — in France. Took three weeks. Worth it.","我最近在网上买了中国零食——在法国买的。等了三个礼拜。值了。"]]}],"end":{"stamp":"DELIVERED","next":"xiaoyu_1111"},"_sources":{"七天无理由退货：《消费者权益保护法》第二十五条，经营者采用网络等方式销售商品，消费者有权自收到商品之日起七日内退货且无需说明理由；定作的、鲜活易腐的、在线下载的数字化商品、交付的报纸期刊等除外；退回运费由消费者承担，另有约定的按约定":"https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/中华人民共和国消费者权益保护法"},"_review":"母语的人还没审","_note":"淘宝客服常用「亲」称呼买家：常识，没找出处。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"xiaoyu_visa","host":"isle.xiaoyu","cat":"life","t":{"zh":"签证面试 7 天陪练","en":"Visa interview, 7-day prep"},"pic":"xiaoyu/visa","days":7,"free":true,"ui":"zh","starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":208,"why":["My student visa interview is in a few days, in Shanghai. Every day my friend plays the officer and asks me 4–5 questions that real people say they were really asked. If you have an interview coming too, practice with me — do one day, or keep going. (What to bring and what they ask: always check the official website.)","我的留学签证面试就在这几天，在上海。每天让朋友当签证官，连着问我 4–5 个真人面签时真的被问到的问题。你要是也快面试了，就跟我一起练——练一天，或者一口气往下练都行。（要带什么、会问什么，一定看官方网站。）"],"D":[{"k":"来干什么","say":["The first ten seconds matter. Look up, smile, say good morning. My friend says I always forget to look up.","头十秒很要紧。抬头，笑一下，说早上好。我朋友说我老是忘了抬头。"],"line":"Good morning. [Here's] my passport.","z":"早上好，这是我的护照。","from":"到窗口","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Good morning. Here's my passport. I remember my hands were shaking this summer. Look up — good advice.","早上好，这是我的护照。我记得今年夏天我手一直在抖。抬头——这个建议好。"],["isle.amara","With a Nigerian passport I've said this at a hundred visa desks. Smile first, my dear. It helps you, not them.","拿着尼日利亚护照，这句我在一百个签证窗口说过了。先笑，亲爱的。是帮你自己，不是帮他们。"],["isle.kenji","Good morning. Here's my passport. I said it to my mirror. The mirror said nothing.","早上好，这是我的护照。我对着镜子说的，镜子什么也没说。"]],"shout":["Amara has done this a hundred times. “Smile first — it helps you.” I wrote it on my hand.","Amara 做过一百次了。「先笑——是帮你自己。」我把它写在手上了。"],"iv":[{"q":"Good morning. Can I have your passport, please?","v":["Morning. Passport, please.","Hi there. Passport and I-20, please.","Good morning. Can I see your passport?"],"z":"早上好，请给我你的护照。","n":"每一场都这样开头","a":"Good morning. [Here's] my passport.","az":"早上好，这是我的护照。","s":"Good morning.","ideas":["Here's my passport","Here's my passport and I-20","Here you are"],"w":[["passport","护照"],["Here's …","这是……（递东西时说）"],["I-20","学校签发的入学资格证明（I-20 表）"]]},{"q":"What's the purpose of your trip?","v":["Why are you going to the US?","What are you going to do in the US?","What's the purpose of your visa?","What brings you here today?"],"z":"你去美国干什么？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 1 篇被问过 · 机构题单里最常见","a":"I'm going to the US [to study]. I'm doing a master's.","az":"我去美国读书，读硕士。","s":"I'm going to the US","ideas":["to study","to do a master's","to study design"],"w":[["purpose","目的"],["trip","这一趟"],["to study","去读书"],["master's","硕士"]]},{"q":"Which school are you going to?","v":["Which university will you attend?","Where will you study?","What's the name of your school?"],"z":"你去哪所学校？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 2 篇被问过","a":"I'm going to [a design school in] Pennsylvania.","az":"我去宾夕法尼亚的一所设计学院。","s":"I'm going to","ideas":["a design school in Pennsylvania","a design school","a university in Pennsylvania"],"w":[["school","学校（美国人读大学也说 school）"],["design","设计"],["Pennsylvania","宾夕法尼亚州"]]},{"q":"When does your program start?","v":["When do classes start?","When does your semester begin?","When is your first day of class?"],"z":"什么时候开学？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 1 篇被问过","a":"It [starts in] January. It's the spring semester.","az":"一月开学，是春季学期。","s":"It starts in","ideas":["January","mid-January","early January"],"w":[["program","项目"],["start","开始"],["January","一月"],["spring semester","春季学期"]]}]},{"k":"你的专业","say":["They'll ask why you're going. One sentence, like a fact. I practiced mine until it sounded like me, not a textbook.","他们会问你去干什么。一句话，像在说一件事实。我练到它听着像我自己，不像课本。"],"line":"I'm [going for] a master's in design.","z":"我是去读设计硕士的。","from":"说来意","crowd":[["stars.yuriko","‘Going for’ sounds confident. You can change the end: a master's in business, in nursing…","going for 听着有底气。后面可以换：a master's in business、in nursing……"],["isle.mei","I'm going for a master's in… bubble tea? One day. Maybe.","我是去读……珍珠奶茶硕士的？总有一天。也许吧。"],["isle.linhao","I'm going for a master's in engineering. That was my line too. Short is best.","我是去读工程硕士的。我当时也是这句。短最好。"]],"shout":["Yuriko showed us how to change the end. So it's not my sentence any more — it's yours.","Yuriko 教我们把后半句换掉。这样它就不只是我的句子，是你的了。"],"iv":[{"q":"What will you study?","v":["What's your major?","What are you going to study there?","What's your program?","What will you be studying?"],"z":"你去学什么？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 8 篇被问过 · 几乎都是第一题","a":"I'm [going for] a master's in design.","az":"我是去读设计硕士的。","s":"I'm going for","ideas":["a master's in design","a master's degree","a two-year master's"],"w":[["major","专业"],["going for","去读（某个学位）"],["master's in …","……硕士"]]},{"q":"Can you tell me a bit about your program?","v":["What will you learn in this program?","Tell me about your program.","What's the program about?"],"z":"说说你的项目吧。","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 2 篇被问过","a":"It's about [design for healthcare], like hospital signs and patient apps.","az":"是给医疗做设计的，比如医院的指示牌、给病人用的 App。","s":"It's about","ideas":["design for healthcare","hospital signs","patient apps"],"w":[["healthcare","医疗"],["hospital","医院"],["patient","病人"],["app","手机应用"]]},{"q":"What did you study for your bachelor's?","v":["What was your undergraduate major?","What did you study in college?","What was your major in college?"],"z":"你本科学的什么？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 2 篇被问过","a":"I [studied] visual design at a university in Hangzhou.","az":"我本科在杭州的一所大学学视觉设计。","s":"I studied","ideas":["visual design","at a university in Hangzhou","graphic design"],"w":[["bachelor's","本科学位"],["undergraduate","本科"],["visual design","视觉设计"]]},{"q":"How long is your program?","v":["How long will you study in the US?","How many years is your master's?","How long does your master's take?"],"z":"你的项目读几年？","n":"常见题单里有","a":"It's [two years]. I'll finish in December 2028.","az":"两年，2028 年 12 月读完。","s":"It's","ideas":["two years","a two-year program","a year and a half"],"w":[["how long","多长时间"],["finish","读完"],["two years","两年"]]}]},{"k":"谁出钱","say":["They may ask how you'll pay. Say it simply and truthfully. I've saved for a year, so I'm a bit proud of this one.","他们可能会问钱怎么解决。说得简单、说实话就好。我攒了一年，所以这句我说得有点骄傲。"],"line":"My parents are [paying for] it, and I've saved some too.","z":"我爸妈出钱，我自己也攒了一些。","from":"说钱的事","crowd":[["london.oliver","‘I've saved some too’ — honestly, that's the line most of my readers wish they could say.","「我自己也攒了一些」——说真的，我的读者大多希望自己能说出这句。"],["isle.kenji","My parents are… asking when I get married. Not paying. Different story.","我爸妈在……问我什么时候结婚。不出钱。是另一个故事了。"],["isle.linhao","My parents are paying for it, and I've saved some too. Same as me this summer. Thanks, Mom and Dad.","我爸妈出钱，我自己也攒了一些。跟我今年夏天一样。谢谢爸妈。"]],"shout":["One good example is easier to remember than a long list. I'm saying mine on the metro, very quietly.","一个好例子比一长串好记。我在地铁上小声念我的那个。"],"iv":[{"q":"Who is paying for your studies?","v":["Who will be your sponsor?","Who's funding your education?","How are you going to pay for this?","Who's covering your tuition?"],"z":"谁给你出学费？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 6 篇被问过","a":"My parents [are paying for] it, and I've saved some too.","az":"我爸妈出钱，我自己也攒了一些。","s":"My parents are","ideas":["paying for it","covering everything","paying, and I've saved some too"],"w":[["pay for","为……付钱"],["sponsor","资助人"],["saved","攒下了（钱）"],["tuition","学费"]]},{"q":"What do your parents do?","v":["What do your parents do for a living?","What are your parents' jobs?","What does your father do?"],"z":"你父母是做什么的？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 6 篇被问过 · 常紧跟在「谁出钱」后面","a":"[My father is] an engineer, and my mother is a nurse at a hospital.","az":"我爸爸是工程师，我妈妈是医院的护士。","s":"My father is","ideas":["an engineer, and my mother is a nurse","a teacher","a small business owner"],"w":[["engineer","工程师"],["nurse","护士"],["teacher","老师"],["for a living","靠什么谋生"]]},{"q":"How much will it cost you each year?","v":["How much do you expect to spend each year in the US?","What's the total cost for one year?","How much will you need per year?"],"z":"一年要花多少钱？","n":"常见题单里有 · 要跟 I-20 上的数一致","a":"[About sixty thousand dollars a year], including living costs. It's on my I-20.","az":"一年大约六万美元，包括生活费。I-20 上写着。","s":"About","ideas":["sixty thousand dollars a year","sixty thousand dollars a year, including living costs","sixty thousand dollars, including living costs"],"w":[["cost","花费"],["amount","金额"],["living costs","生活费"],["tuition","学费"]]},{"q":"Do you have a scholarship?","v":["Did you get a scholarship?","Did the school give you any funding?","Are you getting any financial aid?"],"z":"你有奖学金吗？","n":"常见题单里有","a":"[Not this year, but] I'll apply for one in my second year.","az":"今年没有，第二年我会申请。","s":"Not this year, but","ideas":["I'll apply next year","I'll apply for one in my second year","my parents can cover it"],"w":[["scholarship","奖学金"],["apply for","申请"],["financial aid","助学金"]]},{"q":"Where are you from?","v":["Where's your hometown?","Where is your hukou?","Where does your family live?"],"z":"你是哪里人？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 1 篇被问过（上海，2025：问户口在哪）","a":"[I'm from] Hangzhou. My family lives there.","az":"我是杭州人，家在那儿。","s":"I'm from","ideas":["Hangzhou","Hangzhou, in Zhejiang","Zhejiang"],"w":[["hometown","家乡"],["hukou","户口"],["family","家人"]]}]},{"k":"为什么选这所","say":["My interview is getting close. Whatever happens, remember: if you didn't hear, just ask. It's normal.","面试越来越近了。不管怎样，记住：没听清就问，很正常。"],"line":"Sorry, could you [say that again]?","z":"不好意思，能再说一遍吗？","from":"没听清","crowd":[["stars.yuriko","Asking again is a skill, not a mistake. I used the Spanish one twice in my test.","请人再说一遍是本事，不是错误。我考西语的时候用了两次。"],["isle.linhao","Sorry, could you say that again? Good luck, Xiaoyu!!","不好意思，能再说一遍吗？小雨加油！！"],["new_york.xiaoyu","Sorry, could you say that again? I say this at every open mic. Usually about my own joke.","不好意思，能再说一遍吗？我每次开放麦都说这句。通常是问我自己的笑话。"]],"shout":["I tried it with my friend today. I didn't hear one question, I asked, and they said it again. Nothing bad happened.","今天跟朋友试了一下：有一题没听清，我就问了，对方又说了一遍，什么事都没有。"],"iv":[{"q":"Why did you choose this school?","v":["Why this university?","Why did you pick this program?","What made you choose this school?","Why do you want to go to this school?"],"z":"为什么选这所学校？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 3 篇被问过","a":"I [chose this program because] it works with real hospitals.","az":"我选这个项目，是因为它跟真正的医院合作。","s":"I chose this program because","ideas":["it works with real hospitals","the teachers are great","it has practical projects"],"w":[["choose","选（过去式 chose）"],["work with","跟……合作"],["real","真正的"]]},{"q":"How many schools did you apply to?","v":["Did any other schools accept you?","How many offers did you get?"],"z":"你申请了几所学校？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 1 篇被问过","a":"I [applied to] five schools and got two offers.","az":"我申请了五所，拿到两个录取。","s":"I applied to","ideas":["five schools","five schools and got two offers","five schools, and this was my first choice"],"w":[["apply to","申请（学校）"],["offer","录取"],["first choice","第一志愿"]]},{"q":"How did you hear about this university?","v":["How did you find out about this school?","How did you find this program?","Who told you about this school?"],"z":"你是怎么知道这所学校的？","n":"常见题单里有","a":"[I heard about it from] a teacher at my university who studied there.","az":"是我们学校一位在那儿读过书的老师告诉我的。","s":"I heard about it from","ideas":["a teacher","a friend","the school's website"],"w":[["hear about","听说"],["university","大学"],["studied there","在那儿读过书"]]},{"q":"And how long is your program?","v":["How long will you be studying there?","How long is it again?"],"z":"签证官说得很快，你没听清：先请他再说一遍，再答","n":"好几篇经验帖都提醒：没听清就请对方再说，别乱猜","a":"Sorry, could you [say that again]? … It's two years.","az":"不好意思，能再说一遍吗？……两年。","s":"Sorry, could you","ideas":["say that again","speak a bit slower","repeat the question"],"w":[["Sorry?","不好意思？（没听清）"],["say that again","再说一遍"],["slower","慢一点"]]}]},{"k":"出过国吗","say":["If they ask for a paper, you don't need a long answer. Just hand it over. I've put everything in one folder.","他们要材料的时候，不用说一大段，递过去就好。我把东西都放进一个文件夹了。"],"line":"Yes, I have it [right here].","z":"有的，就在这儿。","from":"递材料","crowd":[["isle.linhao","Yes, I have it right here. And a copy. And a copy of the copy. My bank taught me this.","有的，就在这儿。还有复印件，还有复印件的复印件。我那家银行教会我的。"],["more.friends_e.hana","Tip from an organizer: one folder, in the order they'll ask. Then ‘right here’ is really right there.","整理师的小建议：一个文件夹，按他们会要的顺序放好。这样 right here 才真的在手边。"],["isle.mei","Yes, I have it right here — said it to my manager about my schedule. Felt very professional.","有的，就在这儿——跟店长交排班表的时候说的。感觉自己好专业。"]],"shout":["Hana's folder tip is so good. My mom says she did that already. Of course she did.","Hana 的文件夹窍门太好了。我妈说她早就这么弄了。当然啦。"],"iv":[{"q":"Have you been to the US before?","v":["Have you ever been to America?","Have you visited the United States before?"],"z":"你以前去过美国吗？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 2 篇被问过","a":"No, [this will be my first time].","az":"没有，这会是第一次。","s":"No,","ideas":["this will be my first time","never","this will be my first visit"],"w":[["been to","去过"],["first time","第一次"],["before","以前"]]},{"q":"Have you been to any other countries?","v":["Have you traveled abroad before?","Have you ever gone abroad?"],"z":"你去过别的国家吗？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 1 篇被问过","a":"Yes, I [went to] Japan for a week, just to travel.","az":"去过，去日本玩了一个星期。","s":"Yes, I went to","ideas":["Japan","Japan for a week","Thailand with my family"],"w":[["country","国家"],["abroad","国外"],["travel","旅行"]]},{"q":"Do you have any relatives in the US?","v":["Do you have family in the United States?","Any relatives in America?"],"z":"你在美国有亲戚吗？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 1 篇被问过 · 要跟 DS-160 上填的一致","a":"No, I [don't have any] relatives in the US.","az":"没有，我在美国没有亲戚。","s":"No, I don't have","ideas":["any relatives","any family there","any relatives in the US"],"w":[["relatives","亲戚"],["family","家人"],["any","任何（否定句里）"]]},{"q":"Can I see your study plan?","v":["Do you have a study plan with you?","Can I take a look at your study plan?","Did you bring your study plan?"],"z":"能看一下你的学习计划吗？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 3 篇被问过（都是理工科硕士，要看简历和学习计划）","a":"Yes, I have it [right here].","az":"有的，就在这儿。","s":"Yes, I have it","ideas":["right here","with me","here, with my CV"],"w":[["study plan","学习计划"],["right here","就在这儿"],["here you are","给你"]]}]},{"k":"毕业以后","say":["Today is my interview — I'm on the early train to Shanghai. They often end with what you'll do after. Be honest and specific: a city, a kind of job. ‘Come back and work’ is too vague.","今天就是我的面试，我坐早班高铁去上海。最后常问毕业以后。说实话，说具体：一个城市、一种工作。光说「回国工作」太空了。"],"line":"I [plan to] come back to Hangzhou and work in design.","z":"我打算回杭州做设计。","from":"说以后","iv":[{"q":"What do you plan to do after you graduate?","v":["What will you do after graduation?","What are your plans after your studies?","What's your plan after you finish?","What kind of job do you want after this?"],"z":"毕业以后你打算做什么？","n":"11 篇真实面签经过里 2 篇被问过","a":"I [plan to] come back to Hangzhou and work as a product designer for a hospital app.","az":"我打算回杭州，给医院的 App 做产品设计。","s":"I plan to","ideas":["come back to Hangzhou","work as a designer","design apps for hospitals"],"w":[["graduate","毕业"],["plan to","打算"],["product designer","产品设计师"]]},{"q":"Will you come back to China?","v":["Are you going to return home after your studies?","Are you planning to go back after you graduate?","Will you go back to China when you finish?"],"z":"你会回国吗？","n":"常见题单里有","a":"Yes. [My family is] in Hangzhou, and the jobs I want are there.","az":"会。我家在杭州，我想做的工作也在那儿。","s":"Yes. My family is","ideas":["in Hangzhou","all in Hangzhou","in Hangzhou, and so are the jobs I want"],"w":[["come back","回来"],["return home","回国"],["job","工作"]]},{"q":"Why do you need this degree for that job?","v":["How will this degree help you?","Why do you need a master's for that?"],"z":"这个学位对那份工作有什么用？","n":"常见题单里有","a":"[Hospitals in China] are building more apps, and they need designers who understand patients.","az":"国内的医院在做越来越多的 App，需要懂病人的设计师。","s":"Hospitals in China","ideas":["are building more apps","need designers who understand patients","are hiring more designers"],"w":[["degree","学位"],["understand","懂、理解"],["build","做、搭建"]]}],"crowd":[["isle.linhao","I plan to go back to Shenzhen and work for a hardware company. That was my answer this summer. Still the plan.","我打算回深圳，去一家做硬件的公司。这是我今年夏天的回答，现在还是这个打算。"],["isle.amara","Specific is good. Years ago I said ‘I plan to open a studio in Lagos.’ I did. Say yours like it's already true.","具体就好。好多年前我说「我打算在拉各斯开个工作室」，后来真开了。说你的，就像它已经是真的一样。"],["isle.kenji","I plan to… sleep for a week after my exams. Then find a job. Honest answer!","我打算……考完先睡一个星期，然后再找工作。很诚实的回答！"]],"shout":["Kenji made me laugh on the train. Every family is a different story, right?","Kenji 让我在高铁上笑出了声。每家都是不一样的故事，对吧？"]},{"k":"真的一场","say":["Last day. Where are you going, and what for? Study, work, a trip — say your own line.","最后一天。你要去哪儿、去干什么？读书、工作、旅行都行，说你自己的一句。"],"line":"I'm [going to] ___ to ___.","z":"我要去 ___，去 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.yuriko","I'm going to Guadalajara to eat birria and speak only Spanish. Mostly to eat birria.","我要去瓜达拉哈拉，吃 birria，只说西语。主要是吃 birria。"],["isle.mei","I'm going to Tokyo to visit Aiko's record shop. Next summer. Promise.","我要去东京，去逛 Aiko 的唱片店。明年夏天。说定了。"],["isle.amara","I'm going to Lagos to see my grandma. Four more flights, then holiday.","我要回拉各斯看外婆。再飞四趟，就放假了。"]],"shout":["Interview done — approved! They keep the passport for a few days to put the visa in. Next problem: who looks after my cat? Mom says “not me”. Mom is buying cat food.","面试完了——通过了！护照要留几天贴签证。下一个问题：猫谁来养？我妈说「我才不管」。我妈正在买猫粮。"],"iv":{"mock":true,"fixed":[[0,0],[0,1],[1,0],[2,0],[2,1]],"pick":[[3,0],[3,1],[4,0],[4,2],[5,0],[5,1],[1,2],[2,4]],"n":3,"rare":[{"q":"Why not study this in China?","v":["Why do you want to study in the US and not at home?","There are good design programs in China. Why go abroad?"],"z":"为什么不在国内读？","n":"只在机构题单里有，11 篇真实经过里没出现过","a":"[There are good programs in China too, but] this one has more hands-on projects with hospitals.","az":"国内也有好项目，但这个跟医院合作的实践项目更多。","s":"There are good programs in China too, but","ideas":["this one is more hands-on","this one works with hospitals","I want a different way of teaching"],"w":[["hands-on","动手实践的"],["project","项目"],["abroad","国外"]]}]}}],"end":{"stamp":"APPROVED","next":"xiaoyu_arrive"},"iv_src":"问题来自 真人写的 F-1 面签经过（5 篇帖子，共 11 人的经历：其中一篇写了 6 位硕士同学；上海 3 篇）（知乎：zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/389976147（上海 2021.7）、/p/642893059（上海 2023.7）、/p/383221715（6 位硕士 2021）、/p/67591487（北京）；testdaily.cn/104001（上海 2025.5）），问法另参考机构题单（zhihu.com/question/60022832）。回答是小雨的情况，我们写的。"},{"id":"xiaoyu_zaohui","learn":"zh","zh_of":"kenji_standup","host":"isle.xiaoyu","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"早会别只说没问题","en":"More than ‘no problem’ at the morning meeting"},"hook":["新来的同事每天早会只说三个字：没问题。五天后他能说多少？","Our new colleague says one thing at every morning meeting: 没问题, no problem. Five days on — how much can he say?"],"pic":"xiaoyu/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-11-17","2026-12-15"],"n":118,"why":["Our team got a new colleague from Germany, Lukas. Every morning meeting he says the same three characters: 没问题 — no problem. I know that feeling — I'm practising English for my own interview. So this week, let's help him say more. One line a day.","我们组来了个德国同事 Lukas。每天早会他就说三个字：没问题。我懂那种感觉——我自己也在练英语面试。这周我们帮他多说一点，一天一句。"],"D":[{"k":"昨天做了什么","say":["Our morning meeting starts with yesterday. Keep it short: 昨天我主要在…… and then the thing. 主要 means ‘mostly’ — you don't need to list everything.","早会先说昨天。短一点就好：「昨天我主要在……」再说是什么事。「主要」就是大部分时间在干这个，不用全列出来。"],"line":"Yesterday I was [mostly] working on the login page.","z":"昨天我主要在弄登录页面。","from":"早会","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Yesterday I was mostly working on the login page. In Chinese! My Chinese colleague was shocked.","昨天我主要在弄登录页面。用中文说的！中国同事吓了一跳。"],["beijing.chenhao","Tip: 做 works too, but you'll hear 弄 a lot — for fiddling with code, that's the word in our office.","小提示：说「做」也行，不过你会常听到「弄」——改代码这种事，我们办公室都说「弄」。"],["more.world.priya","Yesterday I was mostly doing the month-end accounts. My Shanghai client said 辛苦了!","昨天我主要在做月底的账。上海的客户说：辛苦了！"]],"shout":["Chen Hao knows — 弄 is the most useful verb in any office. And Priya got a 辛苦了. That's a big one.","陈浩说得对——「弄」是办公室里最好用的词。Priya 还收到了一句「辛苦了」，分量很重的。"]},{"k":"今天打算干嘛","say":["Then today. 打算 means ‘plan to’. Lukas said 今天我会测试 — people got it. 打算 adds one thing: it's your plan for today.","然后说今天。「打算」就是计划要做。Lukas 说「今天我会测试」，大家都听懂了。「打算」多说了一层：这是你今天定好的事。"],"line":"Today I [plan to] finish the testing.","z":"今天打算把测试做完。","from":"早会","crowd":[["isle.amara","Today I plan to finish my packing. Three cities this week.","今天打算把行李收拾完。这周三座城。"],["stars.yuriko","Today I plan to finish marking. Fifty essays. Send help.","今天打算把作文改完。五十篇。救命。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","At our factory the morning meeting is standing up, five minutes. 打算 is enough.","我们厂的早会是站着开的，五分钟。说「打算」就够了。"]],"shout":["Yuriko, fifty essays — 加油. Chen Jian's five-minute meeting is my dream.","Yuriko，五十篇——加油。Chen Jian 的五分钟早会是我的梦想。"]},{"k":"卡住了就说","say":["Lukas never says he's stuck. In Chinese it's easy: 卡住了 — like a drawer that won't open. Saying it early is normal here.","Lukas 从来不说自己卡住了。中文很简单：「卡住了」——就像抽屉拉不开。早点说出来，在我们这儿很正常。"],"line":"I'm [stuck] on this part.","z":"这块我卡住了。","from":"早会","crowd":[["isle.kenji","I'm stuck on this part. Time zones, again. Always time zones.","这块我卡住了。又是时区，永远是时区。"],["beijing.chenhao","Say it before lunch, not at 6 pm. Trust a Zhongguancun programmer.","午饭前说，别等到六点。相信一个中关村程序员。"],["isle.nadia","I'm stuck on this part — the hospital's new Chinese leaflet. A colleague helped me in two minutes.","这块我卡住了——医院新的中文小册子。同事两分钟就帮我弄好了。"]],"shout":["Chen Hao's rule: before lunch. Kenji — time zones are everybody's enemy.","陈浩的规矩：午饭前说。Kenji——时区是所有人的敌人。"]},{"k":"请人帮你看一眼","say":["Asking for help: 麻烦你 is ‘sorry to trouble you’. Add 帮我看一下 — ‘have a quick look for me’. Very polite, very normal.","请人帮忙：「麻烦你」就是「不好意思，打扰一下」。再加一句「帮我看一下」。很客气，也很平常。"],"line":"[Sorry to bother you] — could you take a quick look?","z":"麻烦你帮我看一下？","from":"请同事帮忙","crowd":[["more.isle_economy.wanjiru","Sorry to bother you, could you take a quick look? Sent it to a supplier in Guangzhou on WeChat.","麻烦你帮我看一下？在微信上发给广州的供应商的。"],["isle.aiko","Sorry to bother you, could you take a look? My Chinese is slow, but people always help.","麻烦你帮我看一下？我中文说得慢，但大家都会帮忙。"],["beijing.chenhao","And when they've helped, say 谢了 — short and friendly.","人家帮完，说一句「谢了」——短，亲切。"]],"shout":["Wanjiru used it with a real supplier! And yes, Chen Hao — 谢了 is the perfect ending.","Wanjiru 对真的供应商用上了！陈浩说得对——「谢了」是最好的结尾。"]},{"k":"说你自己的早会","say":["Last day. Your own morning meeting: yesterday and today, two sentences. Work, school, home — all fine. Lukas did his today. More than three characters!","最后一天。你自己的早会：昨天和今天，两句话。上班、上学、在家都行。Lukas 今天说了他的——不止三个字了！"],"line":"Yesterday I ___, and today I'm [going to] ___.","z":"昨天我___，今天准备___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","Yesterday I fixed the bug, and today I'm going to sleep. Joking. Testing.","昨天我把 bug 修好了，今天准备睡觉。开玩笑的，准备测试。"],["stars.emma","Yesterday I walked 20,000 steps, and today I'm going to eat. A lot.","昨天我走了两万步，今天准备吃。吃很多。"],["more.world.priya","Yesterday I finished the accounts, and today I'm going to call my Shanghai client — in Chinese.","昨天我把账做完了，今天准备给上海的客户打电话——用中文。"]],"shout":["Lukas talked for a whole minute today. Our manager clapped. Thank you all — Priya, tell me how the call goes!","Lukas 今天说了整整一分钟。我们经理都鼓掌了。谢谢大家——Priya，电话打得怎么样，告诉我！"]}],"end":{"stamp":"早会","next":"xiaoyu_zhoubao"},"_note":"学中文的人用的中文版（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。"},{"id":"xiaoyu_zhoubao","learn":"zh","host":"isle.xiaoyu","cat":"say","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"周会上把这一周说清楚","en":"Tell your week at the weekly meeting"},"hook":["Lukas 早会不止说「没问题」了。可周五的周会要说一整周，他又只剩两个字：还行。","Lukas says more than 没问题 at morning meetings now. But Friday's weekly meeting covers the whole week — and he's back to two characters: 还行, ‘it's OK’."],"pic":"xiaoyu/work","days":5,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":104,"why":["Good news: Lukas talks at the morning meeting now. Bad news: on Friday we have the weekly meeting. My manager asked about his week and he said 还行. That's all. So this round is the weekly report: what you did, how far you got, where you're stuck, what's next. I write a Chinese weekly report every Friday too, so these are the real lines.","好消息：Lukas 早会能说了。坏消息：周五我们开周会，经理问他这周怎么样，他说「还行」。就两个字。所以这一轮练周报：做了什么、进度怎么样、卡在哪、下周干嘛。我自己每周五也要写中文周报，下面这些都是真会用的。"],"D":[{"k":"这周做了什么","say":["A weekly report starts with the big picture: 这周主要做了 — ‘this week I mainly did’ — then two or three things. You know 主要 from the morning meeting. Now stretch it to a whole week.","周报先说大的：「这周主要做了」，后面跟两三件事。「主要」你早会就会了，现在把它拉长到一周。"],"line":"This week I [mainly did] two things: the login page and testing.","z":"这周[主要做了]两件事：登录页面和测试。","from":"周报","crowd":[["shanghai.zhaolei","This week I mainly did two things: my internship report and a group project. Plus three 8 am classes. Tired.","这周主要做了两件事：实习周报和小组作业。还有三个早八。累了。"],["isle.kenji","This week I mainly did two things: fixed bugs, and made new bugs.","这周主要做了两件事：修 bug，再写出新的 bug。"],["more.world.priya","This week I mainly did three things — I counted them on my fingers in the meeting.","这周主要做了三件事——开会的时候我是掰着手指头说的。"]],"shout":["Kenji, fixing bugs and making bugs — that's every programmer's weekly report. Priya, counting on your fingers is allowed. I do it too.","Kenji，修 bug 再写 bug——这是每个程序员的周报。Priya，掰手指头可以的，我也这么干。"]},{"k":"进度到哪了","say":["Next: 进度, progress. Managers ask 进度怎么样? Lukas said 还行. Give a real answer: 正常 (on track), 有点慢 (a bit behind), or a number like 百分之八十. Saying 有点慢 is fine — hiding it is worse.","然后是「进度」。经理会问「进度怎么样？」Lukas 说「还行」。换个真回答：正常、有点慢，或者说个数，比如百分之八十。老实说「有点慢」没关系——藏着才麻烦。"],"line":"[Progress] on testing is a bit slow.","z":"测试这块[进度]有点慢。","from":"周会","crowd":[["beijing.chenhao","At my company people say 进度正常 even when it isn't. Then Thursday night — panic.","我们公司就算不正常也说「进度正常」。然后周四晚上——慌了。"],["more.isle_economy.chenjian","Factory version: this order is 80% done. Numbers make my boss happy.","工厂版本：这批货完成百分之八十了。说数字老板最开心。"],["isle.nadia","Progress on my Chinese is a bit slow. Too many night shifts. But slow still counts.","我学中文的进度有点慢。夜班太多。不过慢也是在往前走。"]],"shout":["Chen Hao, the Thursday-night panic is too real. Chen Jian is right — one number says more than 还行.","陈浩，周四晚上那个慌太真实了。Chen Jian 说得对——一个数字比「还行」有用多了。"]},{"k":"卡在哪儿","say":["Last round you learned 卡住了. In a weekly report, say where: 卡在 + the thing. ‘I'm stuck’ worries your manager. ‘I'm stuck on the payment API’ gets you help.","上一轮学了「卡住了」。周报里要说卡在哪：「卡在」+ 那件事。光说卡住了，经理会担心；说「卡在支付接口上了」，就有人来帮你。"],"line":"Right now I'm [stuck on] the payment API.","z":"现在[卡在]支付接口上了。","from":"周会","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Right now I'm stuck on time zones. Week two. Same enemy.","现在卡在时区上了。第二周了，还是同一个敌人。"],["stars.yuriko","Not an office, but: I'm stuck on lesson 6 of my Spanish book. Does it count?","不是上班，不过：我卡在西语书第六课上了。算吗？"],["beijing.chenhao","Write it in the report AND say it in the meeting. Someone always answers 我看看.","周报里写，周会上也说。总会有人回一句「我看看」。"]],"shout":["Yuriko, it counts. And Chen Hao's 我看看 — that's the magic answer you're waiting for.","Yuriko，算的。陈浩说的「我看看」——就是你在等的那句。"]},{"k":"请人帮你看看","say":["When you're stuck, ask right there in the meeting: 能不能帮我看一下? — ‘could you take a look?’ It's softer than just 帮我看, and people say yes. Lukas asked our team lead today. She said 会后我来找你 — I'll come and find you after the meeting.","卡住了，周会上就直接问：「能不能帮我看一下？」比光说「帮我看」软多了，大家都会答应。Lukas 今天问了我们组长，组长说：「会后我来找你。」"],"line":"[Could you] take a look at this error for me?","z":"[能不能]帮我看一下这个报错？","from":"请同事帮忙","crowd":[["more.isle_economy.wanjiru","Could you take a look at this invoice? Asked my Guangzhou supplier again. He said 马上 — right away.","能不能帮我看一下这张发票？又问了广州的供应商。他说：「马上。」"],["isle.aiko","Could you take a look at my Chinese email? My roommate changed three words. Only three!","能不能帮我看一下我的中文邮件？室友改了三个词。才三个！"],["shanghai.zhaolei","Intern tip: ask before the meeting ends. After that, everyone runs to lunch.","实习生小建议：会还没散就问。散了大家都冲去吃饭了。"]],"shout":["Aiko, only three words — your email was good. Zhao Lei, I'm taking your tip to my own team.","Aiko，才改三个词——你邮件写得很好啊。赵磊，你这条我要拿去给我们组用。"]},{"k":"说你自己的这一周","say":["Last day. Your own weekly report, two lines: what you mainly did this week, and what you'll aim for next week — 争取 means ‘try hard to’. Work, study, home — all count. Lukas gave his on Friday. Our manager said 不错.","最后一天。你自己的周报，两句：这周主要做了什么，下周争取做什么——「争取」就是努力要做到。上班、上学、过日子都算。Lukas 周五说了他的，经理说了句「不错」。"],"line":"This week I mainly ___; next week I'll [aim to] ___.","z":"这周我主要___，下周[争取]___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.kenji","This week I mainly fought time zones; next week I'll aim to win.","这周我主要在跟时区打架，下周争取打赢。"],["more.world.priya","This week I mainly did my client's accounts; next week I'll aim to call Shanghai without notes.","这周我主要在做客户的账，下周争取不看稿给上海打电话。"],["stars.emma","This week I mainly ate my way round Shanghai; next week I'll aim to eat less. No promises.","这周我主要在上海吃吃吃，下周争取少吃点。不保证。"]],"shout":["Lukas's report took two whole minutes, and not one 还行. Priya, no notes next week — I believe in you.","Lukas 的周报说了整整两分钟，一句「还行」都没有。Priya，下周不看稿——我相信你。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"周报","next":"xiaoyu_huibao"},"_note":"学中文的人用的活动（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。 接着 xiaoyu_zaohui（Lukas）。"},{"id":"yuriko_spanish","host":"stars.yuriko","cat":"say","t":{"zh":"跟我一起从零学西语","en":"Spanish from zero, with me"},"pic":"yuriko/spanish","days":7,"starts":["2026-11-22","2026-12-20"],"n":176,"why":["I just booked my winter trip to Guadalajara — my first trip where I'll only speak Spanish. I'm still a beginner, and I still make big mistakes. So let's start from zero together: seven days, seven lines.","我刚订好了寒假去瓜达拉哈拉的票，第一次去一个只说西语的地方。我还是初学者，也还会说错大笑话。我们从零开始，一起来：七天，七句。"],"D":[{"k":"先用西语打招呼","say":["Good news: Spanish has only five vowel sounds — a, e, i, o, u — and they never change. ‘Hola’: the h is silent.","好消息：西语只有五个元音——a、e、i、o、u，读音从来不变。Hola 里的 h 不发音。"],"line":"[Hola], ¿qué tal?","z":"你好，最近怎么样？","from":"打招呼","crowd":[["isle.kenji","Hola, ¿qué tal? I said ‘ho-ra’ first. Japanese r and l are the same for me, I think.","Hola，¿qué tal? 我一开始说成了 ho-ra。我觉得日语里 r 和 l 对我来说是一样的。"],["isle.mei","Hola, ¿qué tal? My first ever Spanish! It sounds like a song.","Hola，¿qué tal? 我人生第一句西语！听着像唱歌。"],["isle.rosa","¡Muy bien, gracias! Now you have to answer me, mija.","我很好，谢谢！现在你得回我了，孩子。"]],"shout":["Rosa answered us! Kenji — same problem for me. Tongue up behind your teeth for the ‘l’.","Rosa 回我们了！Kenji——我也有一样的问题。说 l 的时候，舌头抵在上牙后面。"]},{"k":"跟新朋友认识","say":["When you meet someone, say this. In Mexico you'll hear it all the time. The u sounds like ‘oo’.","跟人认识的时候说这句。在墨西哥你会一直听到。u 读成「乌」。"],"line":"Mucho [gusto].","z":"很高兴认识你。","from":"认识新朋友","crowd":[["more.friends_a.isabel","Mucho gusto, Yuriko. In Madrid we also say ‘encantada’. Both are lovely.","很高兴认识你，Yuriko。在马德里我们也说 encantada。两个都很好。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Mucho gusto! I said it to my cat. She was not impressed.","很高兴认识你！我对我家猫说了，它一点都不感动。"],["isle.linhao","Mucho gusto. Spanish and Italian are cousins — Luca says I sound almost Italian now.","很高兴认识你。西语和意大利语是亲戚——Luca 说我现在听着差点像意大利人了。"]],"shout":["Isabel taught us a second one — ‘encantada’, or ‘encantado’ if you're a man. Gracias, Isabel!","Isabel 又教了我们一个：encantada，男生说 encantado。谢谢 Isabel！"]},{"k":"在咖啡馆点一杯","say":["My very first Spanish sentence in a real café. ‘Por favor’ makes everything friendly.","这是我在真的咖啡馆里说的第一句西语。加上 por favor，什么都客气了。"],"line":"Un café con leche, [por favor].","z":"一杯拿铁（牛奶咖啡），谢谢。","from":"点单","crowd":[["stars.emma","Un café con leche, por favor — I lived on these in Spain. Trust me, it works.","一杯牛奶咖啡，谢谢——我在西班牙就靠这个活着。相信我，管用。"],["isle.mei","Un té con leche, por favor. Is that milk tea? No pearls though…","Un té con leche, por favor。这是奶茶吗？不过没有珍珠……"],["isle.kenji","Un café con leche, por favor. Practised at the konbini. The staff were confused.","一杯牛奶咖啡，谢谢。在便利店练的，店员一脸懵。"]],"shout":["Mei made her own version! Yes, té con leche is tea with milk. Pearls — you'll have to bring them.","Mei 自己改了一句！对，té con leche 就是加奶的茶。珍珠嘛，你得自己带。"]},{"k":"没听懂就请人重说","say":["My favourite line. I used it twice in my speaking test, and I passed! Asking again is not a mistake.","我最喜欢的一句。口语考试我用了两次，还过了！请人再说一遍不是犯错。"],"line":"¿Me lo puede [repetir]?","z":"您能再说一遍吗？","from":"没听清","crowd":[["isle.xiaoyu","¿Me lo puede repetir? Same idea as my visa interview! It really works.","您能再说一遍吗？跟我签证面试那句是一个意思！真的管用。"],["isle.jordi","Perfect, and very polite. With friends you can say ‘¿Cómo?’ — short and easy.","很好，很客气。跟朋友说 ¿Cómo? 就行，短又简单。"],["isle.amara","¿Me lo puede repetir? I'll need this on my Madrid flight next week.","您能再说一遍吗？下周飞马德里就用得上。"]],"shout":["Jordi gave us the casual one: ‘¿Cómo?’ Now you have a polite one and a friendly one.","Jordi 给了我们一个随口的：¿Cómo? 现在你有一句客气的，一句随便的。"]},{"k":"在市场问多少钱","say":["Markets in Mexico are full of good things. ‘Cuesta’ — say ‘kwes-ta’, quick and light.","墨西哥的市场里好东西可多了。cuesta 读成 kwes-ta，快一点，轻一点。"],"line":"¿Cuánto [cuesta]?","z":"多少钱？","from":"买东西","crowd":[["isle.rosa","¿Cuánto cuesta? For you, mija, the first taco is free. The second one, no.","多少钱？给你的话，孩子，第一个塔可免费。第二个不行。"],["isle.bea","¿Cuánto cuesta? In Tagalog we say ‘magkano’. And we have ‘pera’ for money — from Spanish!","多少钱？他加禄语说 magkano。我们管钱叫 pera——是从西语来的！"],["isle.aiko","¿Cuánto cuesta? I want to ask this at a record fair in Mexico City one day.","多少钱？哪天我想在墨西哥城的唱片市集上问这句。"]],"shout":["Bea showed us Spanish words living in Tagalog. Languages travel, like us.","Bea 给我们看了住在他加禄语里的西语词。语言也会旅行，跟我们一样。"]},{"k":"吃到好吃的就夸","say":["Rosa says I must eat birria. When I do, I'll say this. The r at the start rolls — try ‘rrr’, like a little engine.","Rosa 说我一定要吃 birria（墨西哥炖肉）。吃到的时候，我就说这句。开头的 r 要打嘟噜——试试 rrr，像个小马达。"],"line":"¡Qué [rico]!","z":"真好吃！","from":"吃饭的时候","crowd":[["isle.rosa","¡Qué rico! This is the one my customers say most. Second most: ‘otro, por favor’ — another one!","真好吃！这是我的客人说得最多的一句。第二多的是 otro, por favor——再来一个！"],["isle.kenji","¡Qué rico! My r is not rolling. It is more like a small cough.","真好吃！我的 r 打不出嘟噜，更像轻轻咳了一声。"],["isle.linhao","¡Qué rico! Said it to my own hotpot. It's true.","真好吃！对着我自己做的火锅说的。是真的。"]],"shout":["Kenji — a small cough is how mine started too. Rosa gave us a bonus line: ‘Otro, por favor!’","Kenji——我的一开始也像咳嗽。Rosa 还送了一句：Otro, por favor！（再来一个！）"]},{"k":"说你自己的一句","say":["Last day! Tell someone where you're from and one thing you like. In a month, I'll say mine in Guadalajara.","最后一天！告诉别人你是哪儿人，再说一样你喜欢的东西。一个月以后，我就在瓜达拉哈拉说我的了。"],"line":"Soy de ___ y me [gusta] ___.","z":"我是 ___ 人，我喜欢 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["isle.mei","Soy de Taipei y me gusta el té con leche. Of course.","我是台北人，我喜欢奶茶。那当然。"],["isle.xiaoyu","Soy de Hangzhou y me gusta el lago. West Lake at six a.m., my practice place.","我是杭州人，我喜欢湖。早上六点的西湖，我的练习场。"],["isle.kenji","Soy de un pueblo pequeño y me gusta… el natto. Nobody believes me.","我是一个小地方来的，我喜欢……纳豆。没人信。"]],"shout":["Seven days, seven lines — that's enough to say hello, order, ask and eat. ¡Nos vemos en Guadalajara!","七天，七句——打招呼、点单、发问、吃饭都够了。瓜达拉哈拉见！"]}],"end":{"stamp":"¡HOLA!","next":"yuriko_spanish2"}},{"id":"zhaolei_food","learn":"zh","host":"shanghai.zhaolei","cat":"eat","soil":"culture","hook":["问路学会了，Emma 的下一个问题：上海早上吃什么？生煎怎么咬才不烫嘴？","Emma can ask the way now. Her next question: what do you eat in Shanghai in the morning — and how do you bite a shengjian without burning your mouth?"],"t":{"zh":"在上海，每天吃一顿","en":"Eat your way round Shanghai"},"pic":"emma/hanoi","days":5,"free":true,"starts":["2026-12-01","2026-12-29"],"n":211,"why":["Last week Emma found every place she was looking for. Then she told me: ‘Zhao Lei, I've only eaten convenience-store food.’ Not OK. I've lived here three years on a student budget, so I know the cheap, good places. Five days, five meals, all ordered in Chinese.","上周 Emma 想找的地方都找到了。然后她跟我说：「赵磊，我天天吃便利店。」这可不行。我在上海靠学生的钱活了三年，便宜好吃的地方我熟。五天，五顿饭，全用中文点。"],"D":[{"k":"生煎来一两","say":["Breakfast: shengjian — pan-fried pork buns, crispy on the bottom, soup inside. Many shops sell them by the 两, and one 两 is usually four buns. So you say 来一两. Wait a moment before you bite — they're very hot.","早饭：生煎。底是脆的，里面有汤。很多店按「两」卖，一两一般四个。所以你说「来一两」。别急着咬——特别烫。"],"line":"Hi, [one portion] of shengjian, please.","z":"老板，[来一两]生煎。","from":"点吃的","crowd":[["stars.emma","One portion of shengjian, please! Four buns, gone in four minutes. Trust me, worth the burn.","老板，来一两生煎！四个，四分钟吃完。相信我，烫也值。"],["shanghai.wang","There's a shengjian shop next to my rice-roll stall. Every morning: 来一两, 来二两, all morning long.","我粢饭团摊旁边就是生煎店。每天早上，来一两、来二两，听一上午。"],["isle.kenji","In Osaka I order gyoza by the plate. Here it's by weight? I love it.","在大阪我按盘点饺子。这里按两？我喜欢。"]],"shout":["Emma, four in four minutes — the owner must be proud. Auntie Wang, thank you for the morning soundtrack.","Emma，四分钟四个——老板肯定很骄傲。王阿姨，谢谢你的早晨背景音。"]},{"k":"小笼包小心烫","say":["Lunch: xiaolongbao, little soup dumplings in a bamboo steamer. The local way: bite a small hole, sip the soup, then dip it in vinegar with ginger. When the basket arrives, someone always says 小心烫 — careful, it's hot! Guess first: where are the famous ones from?","午饭：小笼包。小蒸笼里一个个小包子，里面有汤。本地人的吃法：先咬个小口，喝汤，再蘸姜丝醋。蒸笼一上来，总有人说「小心烫」。先猜：最有名的小笼包是哪儿的？"],"line":"Take a small bite first — [careful, it's hot].","z":"先咬个小口，[小心烫]。","from":"一起吃饭","type":"guess","q":["Shanghai's best-known xiaolongbao are named after a town. Which one?","上海最有名的小笼包，是用一个镇的名字叫的。哪个镇？"],"opts":[["Nanxiang",1],["Wuzhen",0],["Zhouzhuang",0]],"reveal":["Nanxiang — a town in Jiading, in the northwest of Shanghai. Now you can eat Nanxiang xiaolongbao all over the city.","南翔——在上海西北边的嘉定。现在全上海都吃得到南翔小笼。"],"crowd":[["stars.emma","I didn't listen to ‘careful, it's hot’. Soup on my chin, my phone, and Zhao Lei.","我没听「小心烫」。汤到了下巴上、手机上，还有赵磊身上。"],["shanghai.sophie","Now I say 小心烫 to my French friends. They think it's a Chinese blessing.","我现在对法国朋友也说「小心烫」。他们以为这是中国的祝福语。"],["isle.mei","Taipei has famous xiaolongbao too. Same rule: small bite, then the soup.","台北也有有名的小笼包。规矩一样：先咬小口，再喝汤。"]],"shout":["Emma, my shirt is still in the wash. Sophie, honestly, 小心烫 is a kind of blessing.","Emma，我的衣服还在洗。Sophie，说真的，「小心烫」也算一种祝福。"]},{"k":"扫码点餐","say":["Dinner at a noodle shop. No menu on the table — just a QR code. That's 扫码点餐: scan it with your phone, order, and often pay right there. Not sure? Ask the staff: 是扫码点餐吗?","晚饭去面馆。桌上没有菜单，只有一个二维码。这就是「扫码点餐」：手机一扫，点菜，很多店当场就付了。拿不准就问服务员：「是扫码点餐吗？」"],"line":"Do you [scan the code to order] here?","z":"你们这儿是[扫码点餐]吗？","from":"点吃的","crowd":[["stars.emma","Do you scan to order here? She said yes and pointed at the table. The code was under my elbow.","你们这儿是扫码点餐吗？她说是，指了指桌子。二维码就在我胳膊肘底下。"],["beijing.tom","Tip: add your foreign bank card to Alipay before you come. Then scanning is easy.","小建议：来之前先在支付宝绑好外国的银行卡，扫码就简单了。"],["shanghai.zhang","I'm old-school, I ask for a paper menu. Many places still keep one.","我老派，我要纸菜单。很多店还留着一份的。"]],"shout":["Emma, the code under your elbow — classic Emma. Tom's tip is gold: sort out paying before you land.","Emma，二维码在你胳膊肘底下——很 Emma。Tom 这条太有用了：落地前先把付钱的事弄好。"]},{"k":"买单，剩下的打包","say":["Too much food? Normal — people here order lots and share. Ask to 打包, take the rest away in a box. To pay, people in Shanghai wave and say 买单. In the north you'll hear 结账 more. Both work.","点多了？很正常——这儿大家点很多一起吃。吃不完就「打包」，装盒子带走。要付钱，上海人招个手说「买单」，北方人更常说「结账」。两个都行。"],"line":"Excuse me, [the bill], please — and we'll take the rest away.","z":"服务员，[买单]！剩下的打包。","from":"吃完饭","crowd":[["stars.emma","The bill, please — and we'll take the rest away! Tomorrow's breakfast: cold noodles. No regrets.","服务员，买单！剩下的打包。明天的早饭：凉掉的面。不后悔。"],["beijing.tom","In Beijing I said 买单 and the waiter answered 结账是吧. Both fine.","在北京我说「买单」，服务员回我「结账是吧」。都行。"],["isle.rosa","At my taco stand there's no 买单 — you pay first. But 打包? Every day.","我的塔可摊没有「买单」——先付钱。不过「打包」？天天有。"]],"shout":["Emma, cold noodles for breakfast — very student life. Tom, that waiter was being nice: he taught you the northern word.","Emma，早饭吃凉面，很有学生生活的味道。Tom，那位服务员是好心——顺便教了你北方的说法。"]},{"k":"你最想吃的那一样","say":["Last day. Tell me your one dish: when you go to Shanghai — or anywhere in China — what's the first thing you'll eat? Use 一定要, ‘I've definitely got to’. Emma's: 回上海，我一定要再吃一次生煎.","最后一天。说你的那一样：你去上海——或者中国别的地方——第一个要吃的是什么？用「一定要」。Emma 说的是：「回上海，我一定要再吃一次生煎。」"],"line":"When I go to ___, I've [definitely got to] eat ___.","z":"去___，我[一定要]吃___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.emma","When I come back to Shanghai, I've definitely got to eat shengjian again. Four. In four minutes.","回上海，我一定要再吃一次生煎。四个，四分钟。"],["isle.aiko","When I go to Xi'an, I've definitely got to eat biangbiang noodles. I can't write the character.","去西安，我一定要吃 biangbiang 面。那个字我不会写。"],["more.world.priya","When I go to Shanghai for work, I've definitely got to eat xiaolongbao — my client said he'd pay.","去上海出差，我一定要吃小笼包——客户说他请。"]],"shout":["Five meals, all in Chinese. Emma, the shengjian owner knows your face now. Aiko, most people can't write biang either — don't worry.","五顿饭，全用中文。Emma，生煎店老板都认得你了。Aiko，biang 那个字大部分人也不会写——别担心。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"吃饱了","next":"zhaolei_night"},"_sources":{"生煎：上海的煎包，底脆、里面有汤":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shengjian_mantou","南翔小笼包出自上海嘉定的南翔镇":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xiaolongbao","一两 = 50 克（市制）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tael"},"_note":"学中文的人用的活动（2026-11-10）。line 写英文意思（学中文的人看到的中文那句在 中文/<id>.json）。母语的人还没审。 接着 zhaolei_shanghai（Emma 在上海）。pic 照上一期用 emma/hanoi（赵磊还没有照片）。「一两一般四个」是常见的卖法，不是每家都一样。"},{"id":"zhaolei_shanghai","learn":"zh","zh_of":"emma_toronto","host":"shanghai.zhaolei","cat":"go","soil":"days","hook":["人民广场站出口多到数不清，问一句就出来了","People's Square has exits everywhere. One question gets you out"],"t":{"zh":"在上海，每天问一次路","en":"Ask the way in Shanghai, once a day"},"pic":"emma/hanoi","days":5,"free":true,"starts":["2026-11-20","2026-12-18"],"n":236,"why":["I've studied in Shanghai for three years and I still get lost inside People's Square station. My friend Emma lands here this week and wants to do everything in Chinese. So every day I'll pick one real spot, and you ask the way with her.","我在上海读了三年书，到现在还会在人民广场站里迷路。我朋友 Emma 这周来上海，她想全程用中文。所以我每天挑一个真的地方，你跟她一起问路。"],"D":[{"k":"人民广场站","say":["Day one: People's Square, right in the middle of the city. Several metro lines meet underneath, and the exits go everywhere. Guess first: how many lines?","第一天：人民广场，市中心。地下好几条地铁线交汇，出口到处都是。先猜：几条线？"],"line":"Excuse me, how do I [get to] Nanjing East Road?","z":"请问，去南京东路怎么走？","from":"问路","type":"guess","q":["How many metro lines meet at People's Square?","人民广场站有几条地铁线？"],"opts":[["1",0],["3",1],["7",0]],"reveal":["Three — lines 1, 2 and 8. That's why people get lost down there. So ask!","三条——1 号线、2 号线、8 号线。所以大家在下面会迷路。那就问吧！"],"crowd":[["stars.emma","'Excuse me, how do I get to Nanjing East Road?' First try! A grandpa walked me all the way to the stairs. Trust me, Shanghai is kind.","「请问，去南京东路怎么走？」第一次！一个爷爷直接把我带到楼梯口。相信我，上海人很好。"],["shanghai.sophie","I asked where Nanjing East Road is. That works too, but 怎么走 gets you the route, not just a finger pointing.","我问的是「南京东路在哪里」。也行，可是问「怎么走」，人家会告诉你路线，不只是指一下。"],["shanghai.zhang","Thirty years driving a taxi here. Tourists always ask for the Bund. Easy: walk Nanjing Road, keep going east.","我开了三十年出租。游客老问外滩。简单：走南京路，一直往东。"]],"shout":["Emma, a grandpa guide on day one — lucky you. Sophie is right: 怎么走 gets you the whole route.","Emma，第一天就有爷爷带路，你运气真好。Sophie 说得对：问「怎么走」，路线全给你。"]},{"k":"几号口出","say":["Shanghai metro exits have numbers. Ask which exit before you go up, or you'll pop out on the wrong side of a very wide road.","上海地铁的出口都有号码。上去之前先问几号口，不然你会从一条很宽的马路的另一边冒出来。"],"line":"[Which exit] should I take?","z":"我应该从几号口出去？","from":"问路","crowd":[["stars.emma","'Which exit?' The station lady said twelve and I heard two. Wrong side of the road. Classic Emma.","「几号口？」站务阿姨说「十二号口」，我听成了「二号口」。走到了马路对面。很 Emma。"],["guangzhou.ajie","I work in a metro station in Guangzhou: we hear this question all day. Ask — we like being asked.","我在广州地铁站上班：这个问题我们一天听好多遍。问吧，我们喜欢被问。"],["isle.kenji","In Tokyo I live by exit numbers. Same rule in Shanghai. 几号口 — I already knew this one!","在东京我就是靠出口号码活的。上海也一样。「几号口」——这句我早就会！"]],"shout":["Emma, 二 and 十二 — the classic. Ajie, thank you for answering all of us all day.","Emma，「二」跟「十二」，经典。阿杰，谢谢你们一整天回答我们。"]},{"k":"一直走到头","say":["From Nanjing East Road station, walk east along the pedestrian street. Keep going — at the end it opens up, and there's the Bund and the river. When someone says 一直走, just check you got it.","从南京东路站出来，沿着步行街往东走。一直走——走到头，眼前一下子开阔了，就是外滩和黄浦江。别人说「一直走」，你确认一句就行。"],"line":"So I just [keep going straight]?","z":"就是一直往前走吗？","from":"问路","crowd":[["stars.emma","'So I just keep going straight?' He said 'yes, it's at the end.' And then — the river. I filmed everything.","「一直往前走吗？」他说「对，走到头就是。」然后——江就在眼前。我全拍下来了。"],["beijing.tom","Tried it in Beijing: 'just keep going straight?' The old man said yes and then talked for two minutes. I caught the yes.","在北京也试了：「一直往前走吗？」大爷说「对」，然后又说了两分钟。我只听懂了「对」。"],["shanghai.wang","Tourists ask me every morning. I say keep going, all the way to the end. Then they come back for a rice roll.","游客每天早上都问我。我说「一直走，走到头」。回来的时候他们都会买个粢饭团。"]],"shout":["Tom, catching one 对 out of two minutes counts. Auntie Wang, save a rice roll for Emma tomorrow.","Tom，两分钟里抓住一个「对」，算数。王阿姨，明天给 Emma 留一个粢饭团。"]},{"k":"远不远","say":["Last stop: Wukang Mansion, the old wedge-shaped building everyone photographs. It's across town. Before you start walking, ask if it's far — Shanghai roads are long.","最后一站：武康大楼，那栋像船头一样、大家都在拍的老楼。它在城市另一边。走之前先问远不远——上海的路很长。"],"line":"Is it [far from here]?","z":"离这儿远不远？","from":"问路","crowd":[["stars.emma","'Is it far from here?' 'Very far, take line 10.' So I took line 10. Trust me, the building is worth it.","「离这儿远不远？」「很远，坐 10 号线。」我就坐了 10 号线。相信我，那栋楼值得。"],["shanghai.linxiao","My café is two minutes from Wukang Mansion. Everyone asks me if it's far. I say no — and they stay for a coffee.","我的咖啡馆离武康大楼两分钟。大家都问我远不远，我说不远，然后他们就留下来喝咖啡了。"],["guangzhou.amadou","I asked 远吗. He got it right away! Some people say 远不远 too.","我问的是「远吗」。对方一下就听懂了！也有人说「远不远」。"]],"shout":["Emma asked, understood the answer and took line 10. Lin Xiao, that's the smartest café plan I've ever heard.","Emma 问了一句、听懂了回答，就坐上了 10 号线。林晓，这是我听过最聪明的开咖啡馆办法。"]},{"k":"给别人指路","say":["Last day. Now someone asks YOU the way. Pick a place near where you live and tell them how to get there: first this, then that.","最后一天。现在有人问你路了。挑一个你住的地方附近的地方，告诉他怎么走：先……再……"],"line":"To get to ___, [first] ___, then ___.","z":"去 ___，先 ___，再 ___。","from":"你自己的话","own":true,"crowd":[["stars.emma","To get to my hostel: first take line 10, then walk five minutes. I gave directions in Chinese! In Shanghai!","去我住的青旅，先坐 10 号线，再走五分钟。我用中文给人指路了！在上海！"],["beijing.tom","To get to my place: first come out of exit B, then turn left, and stop at the jianbing stall.","去我家，先从地铁 B 口出来，再往左走，看到煎饼摊就到了。"],["shanghai.sophie","To get to school: first cross the road, then keep going straight. I told a new French student — in Chinese, to be fair.","去学校，先过马路，再一直往前走。我对一个新来的法国学生说的。公平起见，用中文说的。"]],"shout":["Emma, you came to Shanghai to ask the way and you're leaving giving directions. Tom, a jianbing stall is the best landmark in China.","Emma，你来上海问路，走的时候在给别人指路。Tom，煎饼摊是全中国最好的地标。"]}],"end":{"stamp":"FOUND IT","next":"zhaolei_food"},"_sources":{"人民广场站：1、2、8 号线换乘":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People%27s_Square_station","南京东路步行街往东走到外滩":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanjing_Road","武康大楼，最近的地铁站是交通大学站（10、11 号线）":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wukang_Mansion"},"_review":"母语的人还没审"}];
window.ACTS_LANG = {"nadia_label":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"the first ingredient","mean":"排第一的配料","learner":["Sugar is the most.","意思到了；说 mostly sugar，对方马上知道「几乎全是糖」"],"natural":["The first ingredient is sugar. / It's mostly sugar.","看标签说前一句；跟朋友聊天说后一句"],"note":["On a label, it's 'ingredients'. Chatting with a friend, just say 'It's mostly sugar.'","标签上叫 ingredients；跟朋友聊天，一句 It's mostly sugar 就够了。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your friend asks: \"What's in it?\"","朋友问你：里面是什么？"],"o":[["It's mostly sugar.",1],["Check the back first.",0],["Flip it over.",0]],"ok":"对。mostly 放在名词前面：mostly sugar。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It's mostly sugar."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","ingredient 的重音在哪？我老读错",[["isle.nadia","in-GREE-dee-ent. The stress is on the second part.","in-GREE-dee-ent，重音在第二个音节。"]]],["isle.mei","英国包装上的 Contains: 和 Ingredients: 一样吗？",[["isle.nadia","Not the same. 'Ingredients' is the full list. 'Contains' or 'May contain' is about allergens — like milk, nuts or gluten.","不一样。Ingredients 是全部配料；Contains / May contain 说的是过敏原，比如牛奶、坚果、麸质。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"per 100 grams","mean":"每 100 克","learner":["How much sugar in 100 gram?","少了 is there，gram 也要加 s"],"natural":["How much sugar is there per 100 grams?","比两样东西，就看每 100 克"],"note":["'Per' is quick and light — it sounds like 'puh'. Per hundred grams.","per 读得又轻又快，像 puh：per hundred grams。"],"quiz":{"q":["You're comparing two yogurts.","你在比两盒酸奶。"],"o":[["This one has less sugar per 100 grams.",1],["Flip it over.",0],["Check the back first.",0]],"ok":"对。has less sugar 在前，per 100 grams 放最后。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：This one has less sugar per 100 grams."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","gram 后面一定要加 s 吗？",[["isle.nadia","Yes — 100 grams. Only one gram has no s. On the label you'll just see 'g'.","要加：100 grams。只有 one gram 不加。标签上一般只写 g。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"another name for","mean":"……的另一个名字","learner":["It's sugar's other name.","听得懂；another name for 是现成的说法，拿来就能用"],"natural":["It's just another name for sugar.","glucose syrup、dextrose、maltose……都是"],"note":["Sugar hides behind many names. If it ends in '-ose', or says 'syrup', it's sugar.","糖有很多名字。词尾是 -ose，或者带 syrup 的，都是糖。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your friend asks: \"Is dextrose sugar?\"","朋友问：Dextrose 是糖吗？"],"o":[["Yes — it's just another name for sugar.",1],["No — it's a kind of salt.",0],["No — dextrose has no sugar.",0]],"ok":"对：another name for sugar。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Yes — it's just another name for sugar."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","syrup 怎么读？我们店里天天说",[["isle.nadia","Most people say SIR-up. Some Americans say SUR-up. Both are fine.","大多数人读 SIR-up，有些美国人读 SUR-up，两种都行。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"a serving","mean":"一份（标签上算营养的那一份）","learner":["One serving is the half bag?","少了 only，half 前面也不用 the"],"natural":["Wait, a serving is only half the bag?","Wait 开头，一听就是吃惊"],"note":["The numbers on the front are often for one serving — not the whole bag.","正面那些数字，常常只算一份，不是一整包。"],"quiz":{"q":["The label says \"Serves 4\". That means…","标签上写 Serves 4，意思是……"],"o":[["It's enough for four people.",1],["Four people made it.",0],["It has four ingredients.",0]],"ok":"对：够四个人吃。","no":"Serves 4 = 够四个人吃。"}},"talk":[["stars.emma","serving 和 portion 有区别吗？",[["isle.nadia","On labels they mean the same. 'Portion' sounds more British, 'serving' more American.","标签上意思一样。portion 更英式，serving 更美式。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"I didn't expect…","mean":"没想到……","learner":["I don't think bread has salt.","像在说你不信，不像吃惊"],"natural":["I didn't expect salt in bread. / Who knew bread had so much salt?","后一句更口语，带点自嘲"],"note":["Bread is one of the biggest sources of salt in the UK diet — because we eat so much of it.","在英国，面包是吃进去的盐里最大的来源之一——因为吃得多。"],"quiz":{"q":["You find salt in your cereal.","你在麦片里发现了盐。"],"o":[["I didn't expect salt in cereal!",1],["Check the back first.",0],["This one has less sugar per 100 grams.",0]],"ok":"对：didn't + expect（原形）。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I didn't expect salt in cereal!"}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","salt 和 sodium 是一回事吗？",[["isle.nadia","Sodium is part of salt. UK labels say 'salt', US labels say 'sodium'. Salt is about sodium times 2.5.","钠是盐的一部分。英国标签写 salt，美国写 sodium。盐 ≈ 钠 × 2.5。"]]]]},"5":{"lang":{"chunk":"Check the back.","mean":"看看背面","learner":["Front is not true, look back.","look back 是「回头看」，不是看背面"],"natural":["Don't believe the front. Check the back.","两个短句，比一个长句有劲"],"note":["'Natural', 'light', 'no added sugar' — the front is there to sell. The back has to tell the truth.","natural、light、no added sugar——正面是为了卖，背面才必须说实话。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your friend picks a cereal that says \"Natural\".","朋友拿了一盒写着 Natural 的麦片。"],"o":[["Check the back first.",1],["It's enough for four people.",0],["I didn't expect salt in cereal!",0]],"ok":"对：check the back。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Check the back first."},"word":{"w":"no added sugar","tag":"包装上常见","zh":"意思是没「另外加」糖——水果本身的糖还在。","eg":"No added sugar — but it's still 60% fruit juice.","src":"英国食品标准局（Food Standards Agency）对营养声明的说明"}},"talk":[["isle.mei","low-fat 和 light 有啥不一样？",[["isle.nadia","'Light' means at least 30% less of something than the normal version — check what. And low-fat often means more sugar.","light 是比普通版至少少 30% 的某样东西——要看少的是什么。low-fat 的常常糖更多。"]]]]},"6":{"lang":{"chunk":"flip it over","mean":"翻过来","learner":["I see the back of my chips.","能懂，但少了「翻」这个动作"],"natural":["I flipped my crisps over, and the first ingredient was potato.","英国叫 crisps，美国叫 chips"],"note":["'Flip it over' and 'turn it over' both work. 'Flip' sounds quicker, more casual.","flip it over、turn it over 都行。flip 听起来更随手。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want your friend to look at the label.","你想让朋友看标签。"],"o":[["It's enough for four people.",0],["Flip it over.",1],["I didn't expect salt in cereal!",0]],"ok":"对：Flip it over。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Flip it over."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","说昨天翻的那包，是 the first ingredient was 还是 is？",[["isle.nadia","Telling the story of yesterday — 'was'. Reading the bag right now — 'is'.","讲昨天的事用 was；手里正拿着念，用 is。"]]]]}},"oliver_money":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"it all adds up","mean":"积少成多，加起来不少","learner":["Small money becomes big money.","意思对，对方能懂；It all adds up 更短，好记"],"natural":["It all adds up, doesn't it?","三杯咖啡、两次外卖……"],"note":["Careful: 'It doesn't add up' means something else — it doesn't make sense.","小心：It doesn't add up 是另一个意思——说不通、对不上。"],"quiz":{"q":["You spent £3 on coffee every day this month.","这个月你每天花 3 镑买咖啡。"],"o":[["It really adds up.",1],["Most of my money goes on food.",0],["I'd like to spend less on taxis.",0]],"ok":"对：It really adds up。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It really adds up."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","doesn't it 结尾要升调吗？",[["london.oliver","If you're sure, go down. If you're really asking, go up. Here, you're sure — go down.","你很确定就降调；真的在问才升调。这里是确定的，降调。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"I forgot I was paying for…","mean":"我都忘了我一直在付……的钱","learner":["I forgot I pay this.","少了「一直在」的感觉"],"natural":["I forgot I was paying for that.","was paying = 一直在付，自己没注意"],"note":["Free trials are built for this sentence. They hope you forget.","免费试用就是冲着这句话设计的——他们希望你忘了。"],"quiz":{"q":["You find a gym app on your bank statement.","你在账单上看到一个健身 app。"],"o":[["I forgot I was paying for it.",1],["Most of my money goes on food.",0],["I'll sleep on it, thanks.",0]],"ok":"对：I forgot I was paying for it。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I forgot I was paying for it."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","取消订阅是 cancel 还是 unsubscribe？",[["london.oliver","Cancel a subscription — apps, gyms, streaming. Unsubscribe — from emails or a YouTube channel.","app、健身房、视频会员用 cancel；邮件、YouTube 频道用 unsubscribe。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"sleep on it","mean":"想一晚再决定","learner":["I will think tomorrow.","听着像明天才开始想"],"natural":["I'll sleep on it.","礼貌、不用解释，店员一听就懂"],"note":["Shops love 'today only'. 'I'll sleep on it' is the polite way out.","店里最爱说「只有今天」。I'll sleep on it 是最客气的脱身法。"],"quiz":{"q":["The salesperson says: \"It's 20% off, today only.\"","店员说：今天打八折，只有今天。"],"o":[["I'll sleep on it, thanks.",1],["Most of my money goes on food.",0],["It really adds up.",0]],"ok":"对：I'll sleep on it。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'll sleep on it, thanks."}},"talk":[["stars.emma","sleep on it 在工作里能用吗？",[["london.oliver","Yes, even with your boss: 'Let me sleep on it and get back to you tomorrow.'","能，跟老板也能说：Let me sleep on it and get back to you tomorrow。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"goes on","mean":"（钱）花在……上","learner":["My most money is rent.","most 放错了位置"],"natural":["Most of my money goes on rent.","英国人常说 goes on；美国人常说 goes to / goes toward"],"note":["Say it like this and anyone will nod. Rent is the big one for almost everyone in London.","这么说谁都会点头。在伦敦，几乎每个人最大的一块都是房租。"],"quiz":{"q":["Food is your biggest spend.","你花得最多的是吃。"],"o":[["Most of my money goes on food.",1],["I forgot I was paying for it.",0],["I'll sleep on it, thanks.",0]],"ok":"对：Most of my money goes on food。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Most of my money goes on food."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","rent 和 lease 有区别吗？",[["london.oliver","Rent is the money you pay every month. A lease is the contract you sign.","rent 是每个月付的钱；lease 是你签的租约。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"spend less on","mean":"少花点在……上","learner":["I want less spend taxi.","词都对，顺序乱了"],"natural":["I'd like to spend less on taxis.","I'd like to 比 I want to 软一点"],"note":["Pick one thing, not five. 'Spend less on everything' never works — I've tried.","挑一样，别挑五样。「什么都少花点」从来没用，我试过。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to cut down on taxis.","你想少打车。"],"o":[["I'd like to spend less on taxis.",1],["It really adds up.",0],["I forgot I was paying for it.",0]],"ok":"对：spend less on + 东西。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'd like to spend less on taxis."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","cut back on 和 spend less on 一样吗？",[["london.oliver","Pretty much. 'Cut back on' is a bit more casual, and it works for things like sugar or screen time too.","差不多。cut back on 更口语一点，还能用在糖、屏幕时间这些上。"]]]]}},"aiko_shimokita":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"go digging for","mean":"去淘（旧货、唱片）","learner":["I will go to find old records.","意思到了，但没有「淘」的乐趣"],"natural":["I'd go digging for old records.","dig = 在一堆东西里翻"],"note":["Record fans call it 'crate digging' — flipping through box after box of old records.","玩唱片的人叫它 crate digging——在一箱箱旧唱片里翻。"],"quiz":{"q":["You love looking for old clothes in second-hand shops.","你喜欢在二手店里翻旧衣服。"],"o":[["I love digging for vintage clothes.",1],["I love throwing away old clothes.",0],["I love buying new clothes online.",0]],"ok":"对：digging for + 东西。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：I love digging for vintage clothes."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","vintage 和 second-hand 一样吗？",[["isle.aiko","Second-hand is anything used. Vintage is old and a bit special — usually twenty years or more.","二手是用过的就算；vintage 是有年头、有点味道的，一般二十年以上。"]]]]}},"amara_jetlag":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"stay up","mean":"熬着不睡","learner":["I don't sleep until ten.","听着像失眠"],"natural":["I'm staying up till ten, local time.","local time 一说，大家就知道你刚落地"],"note":["Sunlight and a normal dinner time tell your body where it is. Naps tell it the opposite.","晒太阳、按当地时间吃饭，身体就知道自己在哪；补觉正好相反。"],"quiz":{"q":["It's 6 pm where you are and your friend says 'Go to bed!'","当地下午六点，朋友劝你去睡。"],"o":[["No, I'm staying up till ten.",1],["What's good for lunch around here?",0],["The first thing I do is call my mum.",0]],"ok":"对：staying up till ten。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：No, I'm staying up till ten."}},"talk":[["stars.emma","stay up 和 wake up 别搞混？",[["isle.amara","Wake up — you open your eyes. Stay up — you don't go to bed.","wake up 是醒来；stay up 是不去睡。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"good for breakfast","mean":"早饭吃什么好","learner":["Where can eat breakfast?","少了主语，像电报"],"natural":["What's good for breakfast around here?","问的是本地人的推荐"],"note":["Ask the hotel staff, not the app. They know where they eat themselves.","问酒店前台，别问 app。他们知道自己去哪吃。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want a local's tip for lunch.","你想要本地人推荐的午饭。"],"o":[["No, I'm staying up till ten.",0],["What's good for lunch around here?",1],["The first thing I do is call my mum.",0]],"ok":"对：What's good for lunch around here?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：What's good for lunch around here?"}},"talk":[["isle.tom","around here 和 near here 一样吗？",[["isle.amara","Almost. 'Around here' feels more relaxed — the whole area, not one spot.","差不多。around here 更随意，指这一片，不是某一个点。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"the first thing I do is","mean":"我做的第一件事是","learner":["When I land, first I am drink water.","am 和 drink 撞在一起了"],"natural":["When I land, the first thing I do is drink water.","is 后面直接跟动词"],"note":["After 'the first thing I do is', just use the verb: drink, call, shower.","the first thing I do is 后面直接跟动词：drink、call、shower。"],"quiz":{"q":["What do you do first after a long flight?","长途飞行落地，你先做什么？"],"o":[["What's good for lunch around here?",0],["No, I'm staying up till ten.",0],["The first thing I do is call my mum.",1]],"ok":"对：is + call。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：The first thing I do is call my mum."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","land 只能说飞机吗？人也能 land？",[["isle.amara","Yes! 'I land at six' is totally normal. The plane lands, and so do you.","能！I land at six 很常见。飞机落地，你也落地。"]]]]}},"arun_know":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"How do we know?","mean":"我们（人类）怎么知道的","learner":["Why we know that?","why 问原因，不是「怎么知道」"],"natural":["How do we know that?","科学家每天都问这句"],"note":["It's not rude. In science, it's the best question there is.","这不是抬杠。在科学里，这是最好的问题。"],"quiz":{"q":["Someone says, 'The Sun is 150 million kilometres away.'","有人说：太阳离我们一亿五千万公里。"],"o":[["Really? How do we know that?",1],["It takes about forty minutes.",0],["That's a good question… let me think.",0]],"ok":"对：How do we know that?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Really? How do we know that?"}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","how do we know 和 how do you know 有区别吗？",[["more.friends_a.arun","'How do you know?' asks one person — it can sound a bit challenging. 'How do we know?' asks how people found out.","how do you know 是问对方，有时听着像质疑；how do we know 问的是人类怎么知道的。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"good question","mean":"问得好","learner":["Your question is very good.","像在给人打分"],"natural":["That's a really good question.","真诚地说，对方会很开心"],"note":["Teachers often say it to buy a few seconds to think. Now you know the trick.","老师常用这句给自己争取几秒钟想一想。现在你也会了。"],"quiz":{"q":["Someone asks you something hard and you need a second.","有人问了个难题，你需要想一下。"],"o":[["Really? How do we know that?",0],["That's a good question… let me think.",1],["I used to think spiders were insects.",0]],"ok":"对：That's a good question。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：That's a good question… let me think."}},"talk":[["isle.bea","great question 是不是有点假？",[["more.friends_a.arun","Only if you say it to every question. Use it when you really mean it.","每个问题都这么说才假。真心觉得好再说。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"it takes about…","mean":"大概要……（时间）","learner":["It need eight minutes.","need 不这么用"],"natural":["It takes about eight minutes.","说路上、等待要多久都用它"],"note":["Sunlight takes about eight minutes to reach us. So you always see the Sun as it was eight minutes ago.","阳光大约八分钟到地球。所以你看到的，永远是八分钟前的太阳。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your train ride is about forty minutes.","你坐火车大概四十分钟。"],"o":[["Really? How do we know that?",0],["I might be wrong, but I think it closes at six.",0],["It takes about forty minutes.",1]],"ok":"对：It takes about forty minutes。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It takes about forty minutes."}},"talk":[["isle.amara","about 和 around 一样吗？",[["more.friends_a.arun","Here, yes. 'About eight minutes', 'around eight minutes' — both fine.","这里一样，about / around eight minutes 都行。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"I might be wrong, but…","mean":"我可能说错了，不过……","learner":["Maybe I am wrong but…","也行，might be wrong 更柔和"],"natural":["I might be wrong, but I think it's far.","先给自己留余地，再说想法"],"note":["Good scientists say this a lot. It makes people listen more, not less.","好的科学家常这么说。这样别人反而更愿意听。"],"quiz":{"q":["You think the shop closes at six, but you're not sure.","你觉得店六点关门，但不确定。"],"o":[["I might be wrong, but I think it closes at six.",1],["That's a good question… let me think.",0],["Really? How do we know that?",0]],"ok":"对：I might be wrong。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I might be wrong, but I think it closes at six."}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","might 和 may 在这句里能换吗？",[["more.friends_a.arun","Yes. 'I may be wrong' just sounds a little more formal.","能换。I may be wrong 稍微正式一点。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"used to think","mean":"以前以为","learner":["Before I think the Sun is small.","时态乱了，对方会以为你现在还这么想"],"natural":["I used to think the Sun was small, but now I know it's huge.","used to = 以前是这样，现在不是了"],"note":["Changing your mind isn't failing. It's what learning looks like.","改变想法不是失败，学东西就是这个样子。"],"quiz":{"q":["Talk about something you believed as a kid.","说一件你小时候信过的事。"],"o":[["Really? How do we know that?",0],["I used to think spiders were insects.",1],["That's a good question… let me think.",0]],"ok":"对：used to + think。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I used to think spiders were insects."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","used to 的 d 要读出来吗？",[["more.friends_a.arun","Not really — it sounds like 'yoos-tuh'.","基本不读，听起来像 yoos-tuh。"]]]]}},"bea_taglish":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"restroom","mean":"洗手间（美式）","learner":["Where is toilet?","少了 the，也有点直"],"natural":["Excuse me, where's the restroom?","加个 excuse me 就很客气"],"note":["Back home we say 'CR' — comfort room. Americans say restroom; Brits say toilet or loo.","在菲律宾我们说 CR（comfort room）。美国人说 restroom，英国人说 toilet 或 loo。"],"quiz":{"q":["You're in a London pub.","你在伦敦的酒吧里。"],"o":[["Excuse me, where are the toilets?",1],["Hang on a sec.",0],["Could you say that more slowly?",0]],"ok":"对：where are the toilets（英国常用复数）。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Excuse me, where are the toilets?"}},"talk":[["isle.amara","restroom、bathroom、toilet 到底用哪个？",[["isle.bea","US: restroom in public, bathroom at home. UK: toilet or loo. Philippines: CR!","美国：外面说 restroom，家里说 bathroom。英国：toilet 或 loo。菲律宾：CR！"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"turn off","mean":"关掉（灯、电器）","learner":["Could you close the light?","菲律宾英语就这么说；在别的地方说 turn off，大家更容易懂"],"natural":["Could you turn off the light?","开是 turn on，关是 turn off"],"note":["Back home we say 'close the light' and 'open the TV'. In most English, it's turn off and turn on.","在我们那儿说 close the light、open the TV。大多数地方的英语说 turn off、turn on。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want someone to switch off the TV.","你想让人把电视关掉。"],"o":[["Back home we call it CR.",0],["Could you turn off the TV?",1],["Hang on a sec.",0]],"ok":"对：turn off the TV。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Could you turn off the TV?"}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","turn off 和 switch off 一样吗？",[["isle.bea","Yes. 'Switch off' sounds a bit more British.","一样，switch off 更英式一点。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"a sec","mean":"一下下（second 的简写）","learner":["Please wait one second.","能懂，有点像客服"],"natural":["Hold on a sec, let me check.","朋友之间最常用"],"note":["In Taglish we say 'wait lang' — just a moment.","Taglish 里我们说 wait lang，意思是等一下下。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your friend asks something and you need to look at your phone.","朋友问你事，你得看一下手机。"],"o":[["Excuse me, where are the toilets?",0],["Could you say that more slowly?",0],["Hang on a sec.",1]],"ok":"对：Hang on a sec。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Hang on a sec."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","sec 能写在消息里吗？",[["isle.bea","Totally. Even shorter: 'one sec' or just 'sec'.","能，更短的：one sec，或者就一个 sec。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"more simply","mean":"简单一点","learner":["Please speak easy.","easy 不这么用"],"natural":["Sorry, could you say that more simply?","听不懂就问，没人会介意"],"note":["Asking isn't rude. Most people are happy to slow down.","问一句不失礼，大多数人都乐意说慢点。"],"quiz":{"q":["The person talks too fast.","对方说太快了。"],"o":[["Could you say that more slowly?",1],["Back home we call it CR.",0],["Hang on a sec.",0]],"ok":"对：say that more slowly。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Could you say that more slowly?"}},"talk":[["new_york.xiaoyu","simply 和 slowly 我老读混",[["isle.bea","SIM-plee has an m. SLOW-lee starts with 'slow'. Say them side by side three times.","SIM-plee 有个 m；SLOW-lee 开头是 slow。连着各说三遍。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"back home","mean":"在我老家／我们那儿","learner":["In my country we say…","也对，back home 更亲切"],"natural":["Back home we say 'CR', but in English it's 'restroom'.","城市、国家，你从哪来都能用"],"note":["'Back home' works for a town, a country — anywhere you're from.","back home 指你从哪来：一个镇、一个国家都行。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell someone what your town calls something.","告诉别人你们那儿管一样东西叫什么。"],"o":[["Hang on a sec.",0],["Back home we call it CR.",1],["Could you turn off the TV?",0]],"ok":"对：Back home。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Back home we call it CR."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","back home 和 at home 有区别吗？",[["isle.bea","At home = in your house. Back home = the place you come from.","at home 是在家里；back home 是你来的那个地方。"]]]]}},"daniel_praise":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"proud of","mean":"为……骄傲","learner":["Thank you, not really.","这正是这周想改的"],"natural":["Thanks — I'm really proud of that one.","收下夸奖，再说一点自己的感受"],"note":["In English, a simple 'Thanks!' is polite. Saying 'no, no' can sound like you think they're wrong.","英语里一句 Thanks 就很得体。说「没有没有」，听着像在说对方错了。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your boss says, 'Great presentation!'","老板说：讲得真好！"],"o":[["Thanks — I'm really proud of it.",1],["Thanks! I got it on sale.",0],["Sorry, I'm late.",0]],"ok":"对：proud of it。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Thanks — I'm really proud of it."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","proud 会不会听着太骄傲？",[["isle.daniel","Not at all. 'Proud of' sounds warm, not arrogant. Arrogant would be 'I know.'","不会。proud of 听着很温暖；骄傲的说法是 I know。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"got it in a sale","mean":"打折买的","learner":["Thanks, it's very cheap.","像在贬低自己的东西"],"natural":["Thanks! I got it in a sale.","开心地收下，还顺便分享"],"note":["Brits say 'in a sale' or 'in the sales'. Americans say 'on sale'.","英国人说 in a sale / in the sales，美国人说 on sale。"],"quiz":{"q":["A friend likes your jacket.","朋友夸你的外套。"],"o":[["Sorry, I'm late.",0],["Thanks! I got it on sale.",1],["Thanks — I've been practising every day.",0]],"ok":"对：I got it on sale。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Thanks! I got it on sale."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","被夸衣服，说 It's cheap 可以吗？",[["isle.daniel","You can, but it sounds like you're putting it down. 'I got it on sale' sounds happier.","可以，但听着像在贬低它。I got it on sale 更开心。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"been working on it","mean":"一直在练","learner":["Thanks, I practise every day.","也对；说 working on it，对方还听得出你一直在下功夫"],"natural":["Thanks — I've been working on it.","让人知道你下了功夫"],"note":["This one is my favourite. It's honest, and it invites the next question.","这句我最喜欢：诚实，还给对方留了接着问的口子。"],"quiz":{"q":["A friend says, 'Your English is getting so good!'","朋友说：你英语越来越好了！"],"o":[["Thanks! I got it on sale.",0],["Sorry, I'm late.",0],["Thanks — I've been working on it.",1]],"ok":"对：I've been working on it。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Thanks — I've been working on it."}},"talk":[["stars.yuriko","work on 能用在自己身上吗？",[["isle.daniel","Yes, like 'I'm working on my patience.' It means you're trying to get better.","能，比如 I'm working on my patience，意思是你在努力变好。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"means a lot","mean":"对我意义很大","learner":["Thank you, I'm very touched.","有点重"],"natural":["Thanks — that means a lot coming from you.","让对方知道：是你说的，所以更珍贵"],"note":["Use it when the person really matters to you — a teacher, a boss, someone you admire.","对你真正在乎的人说：老师、老板、你佩服的人。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your teacher praises your essay.","老师夸你的作文。"],"o":[["Thanks — that means a lot.",1],["Thanks! I got it on sale.",0],["Sorry, I'm late.",0]],"ok":"对：that means a lot。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Thanks — that means a lot."}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","coming from you 是什么意思？",[["isle.daniel","It means 'because you're the one saying it' — you respect them.","意思是「因为是你说的」——你尊重这个人。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"happy with how it turned out","mean":"对结果挺满意","learner":["I'm satisfied with result.","像在写报告"],"natural":["I'm really happy with how it turned out.","turned out = 最后变成"],"note":["Say what you're happy with. It's not bragging — it's being honest.","说出你满意的地方，这不是炫耀，是诚实。"],"quiz":{"q":["You made a cake and it looks great.","你烤的蛋糕很成功。"],"o":[["Sorry, I'm late.",0],["I'm happy with how it turned out.",1],["Thanks! I got it on sale.",0]],"ok":"对：how it turned out。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：I'm happy with how it turned out."}},"talk":[["isle.rosa","turn out 可以说不好的结果吗？",[["isle.daniel","Sure: 'It didn't turn out the way I planned.'","可以：It didn't turn out the way I planned。"]]]]}},"eleni_lines":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"not up to me","mean":"不由我决定","learner":["I can't control it.","也对，not up to me 更日常"],"natural":["That's not up to me.","斯多葛的第一课"],"note":["Epictetus said: some things are up to us, and some are not. Start by sorting them.","爱比克泰德说：有些事由我们，有些不由我们。先把它们分开。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your train is cancelled.","你的火车取消了。"],"o":[["That's not up to me.",1],["It isn't the same anymore.",0],["My effort is up to me. The weather isn't.",0]],"ok":"对：not up to me。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：That's not up to me."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","up to you 和 up to me 怎么用？",[["isle.eleni","'It's up to you' means you decide. 'It's not up to me' means I can't decide it.","It's up to you = 你决定；It's not up to me = 不由我决定。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"What do you mean by…?","mean":"你说的……是指什么？","learner":["What is 'normal' meaning?","顺序乱了"],"natural":["What do you mean by 'normal'?","苏格拉底一辈子都在问这句"],"note":["Socrates asked this all the time: what do you mean by 'brave'? By 'good'? Most arguments are about words.","苏格拉底总在问：你说的「勇敢」是什么？「好」是什么？大多数争论其实在争词。"],"quiz":{"q":["Someone says a restaurant is 'cheap'. You want to know how cheap.","有人说那家店很便宜，你想知道多便宜。"],"o":[["I'm not sure, actually.",0],["What do you mean by 'cheap'?",1],["Let's talk it over tomorrow.",0]],"ok":"对：mean by。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：What do you mean by 'cheap'?"}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","What do you mean? 会不会听着不客气？",[["isle.eleni","Tone matters. Smile, slow down, and add 'exactly': 'What do you mean, exactly?'","看语气。笑一下、放慢，加个 exactly：What do you mean, exactly?"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"not the same anymore","mean":"已经不一样了","learner":["It is different now than before.","绕了一圈"],"natural":["It's not the same anymore.","简单、有分量"],"note":["Heraclitus: you can't step into the same river twice. The river changes — and so do you.","赫拉克利特：人不能两次踏进同一条河。河在变，你也在变。"],"quiz":{"q":["You go back to your old school.","你回到以前的学校。"],"o":[["My effort is up to me. The weather isn't.",0],["What do you mean by 'cheap'?",0],["It isn't the same anymore.",1]],"ok":"对：It isn't the same anymore。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It isn't the same anymore."}},"talk":[["isle.aiko","anymore 一定放句尾吗？",[["isle.eleni","Usually, yes: 'It's not the same anymore.'","一般放句尾：It's not the same anymore。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"I'm not sure, actually.","mean":"其实我也不太确定","learner":["I don't know clearly.","像没想好就说"],"natural":["I'm not sure, actually.","诚实，又不尴尬"],"note":["Socrates was called wise because he knew what he didn't know. 'I'm not sure' is where thinking starts.","苏格拉底被称为智慧，是因为他知道自己不知道。「我不确定」是思考的开始。"],"quiz":{"q":["Someone asks you a hard question.","有人问你一个难题。"],"o":[["I'm not sure, actually.",1],["What do you mean by 'cheap'?",0],["It isn't the same anymore.",0]],"ok":"对：I'm not sure, actually。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'm not sure, actually."}},"talk":[["more.friends_a.arun","actually 放句尾是什么语气？",[["isle.eleni","Softer. It sounds honest — a little surprised at yourself.","更柔和，听着很诚实，还有点自己也意外的感觉。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"talk it over","mean":"好好聊一聊","learner":["Let's discuss this problem.","像开会"],"natural":["Let's talk it over with a coffee.","两个人、一杯咖啡"],"note":["In Athens, philosophy happened in the agora — out loud, with other people, not alone in a room.","在雅典，哲学发生在市集上——大声说、跟人聊，不是一个人关在屋里。"],"quiz":{"q":["You and a friend disagree about a plan.","你和朋友对计划有分歧。"],"o":[["It isn't the same anymore.",0],["Let's talk it over tomorrow.",1],["What do you mean by 'cheap'?",0]],"ok":"对：talk it over。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Let's talk it over tomorrow."}},"talk":[["stars.emma","talk it over 和 discuss 一样吗？",[["isle.eleni","Similar, but 'talk it over' is friendlier — two people and a coffee, not a meeting.","差不多，但 talk it over 更亲切——两个人一杯咖啡，不是开会。"]]]]},"5":{"lang":{"chunk":"not as bad as I think","mean":"没我想的那么糟","learner":["It is not so bad than I think.","so 和 than 不搭"],"natural":["It's probably not as bad as I think.","as … as 是一对"],"note":["Seneca wrote that we suffer more in imagination than in reality.","塞涅卡写过：我们在想象中受的苦，比现实中多。"],"quiz":{"q":["You're worried about a test.","你在担心一场考试。"],"o":[["What do you mean by 'cheap'?",0],["My effort is up to me. The weather isn't.",0],["It's not as bad as it looks.",1]],"ok":"对：not as bad as。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It's not as bad as it looks."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","not as bad as 和 not that bad 一样吗？",[["isle.eleni","'Not that bad' is shorter. 'Not as bad as I think' compares it with what's in your head.","not that bad 更短；not as bad as I think 是跟你脑子里想的比。"]]]]},"6":{"lang":{"chunk":"is up to me / isn't","mean":"由我／不由我","learner":["My work I can control, weather I can't.","意思对，但句子散了"],"natural":["My effort is up to me. The weather isn't.","第二句省掉了 up to me"],"note":["Write your two lists. Then put your energy only into the first one.","写下两张单子，然后只把力气花在第一张上。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say one thing you control and one you don't.","说一件你能决定的、一件你决定不了的。"],"o":[["My effort is up to me. The weather isn't.",1],["Let's talk it over tomorrow.",0],["It isn't the same anymore.",0]],"ok":"对：is up to me。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：My effort is up to me. The weather isn't."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","第二句 isn't 后面省掉了什么？",[["isle.eleni","'Isn't up to me.' English often drops what we just said.","省掉了 up to me。英语常把刚说过的省掉。"]]]]}},"emma_toronto":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"which way","mean":"往哪边走","learner":["Where is Union Station going?","像在问车站要去哪"],"natural":["Sorry, which way is Union Station?","只问方向，最快"],"note":["Toronto people are very polite — lots of chats start with 'Sorry'. Where you're from, what do people say first?","多伦多人特别客气，很多话都从一句 Sorry 开始。你那边，开口先说什么？"],"quiz":{"q":["You're lost and need the station.","你迷路了，要找车站。"],"o":[["Sorry, which way is the station?",1],["Can I get there without going outside?",0],["How do I get to the museum?",0]],"ok":"对：which way is the station?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Sorry, which way is the station?"}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","which way 和 where 有区别吗？",[["stars.emma","'Where is it?' asks for the place. 'Which way?' just asks for the direction — quicker.","where is it 问地点；which way 只问方向，更快。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"Does this go to…?","mean":"这车到……吗？","learner":["This bus go Kensington?","像电报"],"natural":["Does this go to Kensington Market?","上车前问司机"],"note":["On a Toronto streetcar, just ask the driver before you get on.","在多伦多坐有轨电车，上车前问一下司机就好。"],"quiz":{"q":["You're not sure this bus goes to the airport.","你不确定这车去不去机场。"],"o":[["Sorry, I didn't catch that.",0],["Does this bus go to the airport?",1],["Can I get there without going outside?",0]],"ok":"对：Does this bus go to…?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Does this bus go to the airport?"}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","streetcar 和 tram 一样吗？",[["stars.emma","Same thing. Toronto says streetcar; most of Europe says tram.","一样。多伦多叫 streetcar，欧洲大多叫 tram。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"didn't catch that","mean":"没听清","learner":["I can't understand your words.","听着像对方说错了"],"natural":["Sorry, I didn't catch that. Could you say it again?","怪自己的耳朵，不怪对方"],"note":["This is the most useful sentence in any new city. I use it every day.","这是新城市里最有用的一句。我每天都在用。"],"quiz":{"q":["You didn't hear what the driver said.","你没听清司机说什么。"],"o":[["Does this bus go to the airport?",0],["Can I get there without going outside?",0],["Sorry, I didn't catch that.",1]],"ok":"对：didn't catch。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Sorry, I didn't catch that."}},"talk":[["isle.bea","didn't catch 和 didn't understand 有什么区别？",[["stars.emma","'Didn't catch' means I didn't hear it. 'Didn't understand' means I heard it, but it didn't make sense.","didn't catch 是没听见；didn't understand 是听见了没懂。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"without going outside","mean":"不用出门","learner":["Can I walk inside to go there?","绕"],"natural":["Can I get there without going outside?","without + -ing"],"note":["Toronto has PATH — around 30 km of walkways under downtown. In winter, everyone asks this.","多伦多有 PATH——市中心地下大约 30 公里的步行道。冬天人人都问这句。"],"quiz":{"q":["It's minus fifteen and you want to stay indoors.","零下十五度，你不想出门。"],"o":[["Can I get there without going outside?",1],["Sorry, I didn't catch that.",0],["Sorry, which way is the station?",0]],"ok":"对：without going。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Can I get there without going outside?"}},"talk":[["isle.aiko","underground 在英国不是地铁吗？",[["stars.emma","Yes! In London the Underground is the subway. In Toronto, 'underground' just means below the street.","对！伦敦的 Underground 是地铁。在多伦多，underground 就是街道下面。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"how do I get to…","mean":"去……怎么走","learner":["How to go to the museum?","像在搜索框里打字"],"natural":["Excuse me, how do I get to the museum from here?","问的是路线"],"note":["Ask, then repeat the first step back: 'Left at the lights?' People will correct you if you're wrong.","问完，把第一步复述一遍：Left at the lights? 错了对方会纠正你。"],"quiz":{"q":["You need directions to the museum.","你要去博物馆。"],"o":[["Sorry, I didn't catch that.",0],["How do I get to the museum?",1],["Sorry, which way is the station?",0]],"ok":"对：get to the museum。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：How do I get to the museum?"}},"talk":[["isle.mei","get to 和 go to 有啥不同？",[["stars.emma","'Get to' is about the route — how you arrive. 'Go to' is just where.","get to 讲的是怎么到；go to 只说去哪。"]]]]}},"farah_five":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"come from","mean":"从……来","learner":["Where is this from coming?","顺序乱了"],"natural":["Where does this come from?","问东西的来历"],"note":["Tulips came to the Netherlands from the Ottoman Empire in the 1500s. Most people think they're Dutch.","郁金香是十六世纪从奥斯曼帝国传到荷兰的。很多人以为它本来就是荷兰的。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to know where this tea is from.","你想知道这茶是哪儿来的。"],"o":[["Where does this tea come from?",1],["How do you say 'thank you' in Turkish?",0],["Coffee came to Europe from the Middle East.",0]],"ok":"对：does … come from。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Where does this tea come from?"}},"talk":[["more.friends_a.isabel","come from 和 be from 一样吗？",[["more.friends_b.farah","'I'm from Istanbul' is about people. 'Come from' works for things too: coffee comes from Ethiopia.","I'm from Istanbul 说人；come from 也能说东西：coffee comes from Ethiopia。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"What do you call this?","mean":"这个叫什么？","learner":["How do you call this?","能懂，很多人这么说；问「叫什么」，英语用 what"],"natural":["What do you call this here?","加个 here，问的是本地叫法"],"note":["Many languages ask 'how' here, so lots of people say 'How do you call it?'. In English it's 'what'.","很多语言这里用「怎么」，所以常有人说 How do you call it。英语用 what。"],"quiz":{"q":["You see a sweet you don't know.","你看到一种不认识的甜点。"],"o":[["Coffee came to Europe from the Middle East.",0],["What do you call this here?",1],["Let me get this one.",0]],"ok":"对：What do you call this?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：What do you call this here?"}},"talk":[["isle.tom","How do you call this 为什么不对？",[["more.friends_b.farah","'Call' needs a name — a 'what'. 'How' asks about the way, like 'How do you make this?'","call 后面要一个名字，所以问 what；how 问的是方法，比如 How do you make this?"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"Let me get this one.","mean":"这次我来（请客）","learner":["I pay for you.","太直"],"natural":["Let me get this one.","轻松又客气"],"note":["In Turkey, the host usually pays for the tea. Offering to pay is polite — and a little friendly fight is normal.","在土耳其，一般是主人请茶。抢着付是礼貌，「争一下」也很正常。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to pay for your friend's coffee.","你想请朋友喝咖啡。"],"o":[["How do you say 'thank you' in Turkish?",0],["Coffee came to Europe from the Middle East.",0],["Let me get this one.",1]],"ok":"对：Let me get this one。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Let me get this one."}},"talk":[["isle.rosa","This one's on me 也可以吗？",[["more.friends_b.farah","Yes — 'This one's on me' or 'It's my treat'. Both are friendly.","可以——This one's on me、It's my treat 都很亲切。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"How do you say…?","mean":"……怎么说？","learner":["How say 'tea' in your country?","少了 do you"],"natural":["How do you say 'tea' where you're from?","where you're from 比 in your country 更亲切"],"note":["Most languages say either 'cha' or 'tea'. 'Cha' spread over land; 'tea' travelled by sea with Dutch traders.","大多数语言里，茶要么叫 cha，要么叫 tea。cha 走陆路传开，tea 是跟着荷兰商船走海路的。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to learn 'thank you' in Turkish.","你想学土耳其语的「谢谢」。"],"o":[["How do you say 'thank you' in Turkish?",1],["Let me get this one.",0],["Where does this tea come from?",0]],"ok":"对：in Turkish。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：How do you say 'thank you' in Turkish?"}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","日语的 ocha，是 cha 那一家吗？",[["more.friends_b.farah","Yes! Japanese is in the 'cha' family — like Chinese, Hindi 'chai' and Turkish 'çay'.","对！日语是 cha 那一家，跟中文、印地语的 chai、土耳其语的 çay 一样。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"came to us from","mean":"是从……传到我们这儿的","learner":["Coffee is come from Ethiopia to us.","is come 不对"],"natural":["Coffee came to us from Ethiopia.","came to + 哪里 + from + 哪里"],"note":["Pick one thing in your kitchen. Ask where it started. You'll be surprised how far it travelled.","在厨房里挑一样东西，问问它从哪来的。你会惊讶它走了多远。"],"quiz":{"q":["Talk about how coffee reached Europe.","说说咖啡怎么到的欧洲。"],"o":[["How do you say 'thank you' in Turkish?",0],["Coffee came to Europe from the Middle East.",1],["What do you call this here?",0]],"ok":"对：came to Europe from…","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Coffee came to Europe from the Middle East."}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","came to us 能说 came to here 吗？",[["more.friends_b.farah","No — just 'came here'. 'Here' doesn't need 'to'.","不行，说 came here。here 前面不加 to。"]]]]}},"hana_mealplan":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"I'm making…","mean":"我要做（已经安排好）","learner":["This week I will cook rice and…","也对，I'm making 听着已经安排好了"],"natural":["This week I'm making curry, soup and a stir-fry.","说已经定下的计划，用 I'm + -ing"],"note":["Twenty minutes on Sunday saves you seven evenings of 'What do I eat?'","周日花二十分钟，省下一周七个晚上的「吃什么」。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell a friend your plan for the week.","跟朋友说这周的饭。"],"o":[["This week I'm making curry.",1],["Last week I made curry.",0],["I never cook at home.",0]],"ok":"对：I'm making。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：This week I'm making curry."}},"talk":[["isle.tom","cook 和 make 用哪个？",[["more.friends_e.hana","'Make' + the dish: make curry. 'Cook' on its own: I cook every day.","做某道菜用 make：make curry；单说做饭用 cook：I cook every day。"]]]]}},"isabel_minute":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"What I notice is…","mean":"我注意到的是……","learner":["I see the light is special.","能懂，但少了「注意到」"],"natural":["What I notice is the light.","先说你看到的，不急着评价"],"note":["Look for a full minute before you read the label. Your eyes find more than you think.","看满一分钟再去读说明牌。你的眼睛会比你想的看到更多。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell someone the first thing you see in a painting.","说出你在一幅画里第一眼看到的。"],"o":[["What I notice is the colour.",1],["It reminds me of my hometown.",0],["It reminds me of summer.",0]],"ok":"对：What I notice is…","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：What I notice is the colour."}},"talk":[["isle.aiko","notice 和 see 有什么区别？",[["more.friends_a.isabel","'See' just happens. 'Notice' means something caught your attention.","see 是自然看到；notice 是有什么抓住了你的注意。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"comes from","mean":"从……照过来／来自","learner":["The light is from left side.","少了 the，也不够活"],"natural":["The light comes from the left.","光、声音、气味都能用"],"note":["In many old paintings the light comes from the left. One reason often given: right-handed painters kept the window on their left, so their hand didn't cast a shadow.","很多老画的光从左边来。常见的一种说法：惯用右手的画家把窗户放在左边，手就不会挡出影子。"],"quiz":{"q":["Describe where the light is coming from.","说说光是从哪照来的。"],"o":[["It reminds me of summer.",0],["The light comes from the window.",1],["It reminds me of my hometown.",0]],"ok":"对：comes from。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：The light comes from the window."}},"talk":[["more.friends_a.arun","light 有复数吗？",[["more.friends_a.isabel","Light, like sunlight, has no s. 'Lights' are lamps.","光（像阳光）不加 s；lights 是灯。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"didn't see that at first","mean":"一开始没看到","learner":["First I don't see it.","时态乱了"],"natural":["I didn't see that at first.","at first = 一开始（后来变了）"],"note":["That's the whole game. The second minute shows you what the first one missed.","这就是玩法：第二分钟会给你看第一分钟漏掉的东西。"],"quiz":{"q":["You suddenly spot a cat in the corner of a painting.","你突然在画的角落发现一只猫。"],"o":[["It reminds me of my hometown.",0],["It reminds me of summer.",0],["I didn't see the cat at first.",1]],"ok":"对：didn't see。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I didn't see the cat at first."}},"talk":[["isle.bea","at first 和 first 一样吗？",[["more.friends_a.isabel","'At first' means in the beginning — but then it changed. 'First' is number one in order.","at first 是一开始（后来变了）；first 是第一个、首先。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"reminds me of","mean":"让我想起","learner":["It makes me remember my grandma.","能懂，但绕"],"natural":["It reminds me of my grandma's kitchen.","最常用的说法"],"note":["A painting is half what the painter made and half what you bring to it.","一幅画，一半是画家画的，一半是你带来的。"],"quiz":{"q":["A song makes you think of your hometown.","一首歌让你想起家乡。"],"o":[["It reminds me of my hometown.",1],["I didn't see the cat at first.",0],["The light comes from the window.",0]],"ok":"对：reminds me of。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It reminds me of my hometown."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","remind 和 remember 我老搞混",[["more.friends_a.isabel","You remember something. Something reminds you of it.","你 remember 一件事；一样东西 reminds you of 它。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"What I notice … it reminds me of …","mean":"我注意到……它让我想起……","learner":["I see the blue, I think of sea.","能懂，再连起来就更好"],"natural":["What I notice is the blue. It reminds me of the sea.","两句：先看到，再联想"],"note":["Two sentences is enough to talk about any painting. Try it at your next museum.","两句话就能聊任何一幅画。下次去美术馆试试。"],"quiz":{"q":["A painting makes you think of summer.","一幅画让你想到夏天。"],"o":[["The light comes from the window.",0],["It reminds me of summer.",1],["I didn't see the cat at first.",0]],"ok":"对：It reminds me of summer。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It reminds me of summer."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","What I notice is 开头会不会太长？",[["more.friends_a.isabel","It's a nice way to slow down. Or just say: 'I notice the light.'","它让你慢下来，挺好。也可以直接说 I notice the light。"]]]]}},"jade_mornings":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"sit back","mean":"往后坐（深蹲）","learner":["Sit down slowly.","像坐椅子，膝盖会往前冲"],"natural":["Chest up, sit back.","像身后有把椅子"],"note":["In a squat, sit back like there's a chair behind you. Knees stay behind your toes as much as you can.","深蹲时往后坐，像身后有把椅子。膝盖尽量别冲过脚尖。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell a friend how to start a squat.","教朋友怎么开始深蹲。"],"o":[["Sit back, like there's a chair.",1],["I did four out of seven.",0],["Squeeze at the top, then lower slowly.",0]],"ok":"对：Sit back。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Sit back, like there's a chair."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","squat 怎么读？",[["more.friends_e.jade","SKWOT — one syllable. 'Squad' is a team!","SKWOT，一个音节。squad 是一支队伍！"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"engage your core","mean":"收紧核心","learner":["Make your stomach hard.","能懂；健身课上教练常喊 engage your core，听熟了跟得上口令"],"natural":["Engage your core.","教练最常喊的一句"],"note":["Coaches say 'engage', 'brace' or 'tighten your core' — all the same idea.","教练说 engage、brace、tighten your core，都是一个意思。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want someone to keep their middle tight.","你想让人把腰腹收紧。"],"o":[["Sit back, like there's a chair.",0],["Keep your core tight.",1],["Squeeze at the top, then lower slowly.",0]],"ok":"对：Keep your core tight。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Keep your core tight."}},"talk":[["isle.nadia","core 就是腹肌吗？",[["more.friends_e.jade","More than abs — it's your belly, sides and lower back working together.","不只是腹肌——肚子、两侧和下背一起。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"knee down","mean":"膝盖往下（弓步）","learner":["Leg back and sit down.","动作对，说法乱"],"natural":["Step back, knee down.","口令要短"],"note":["A lunge: one foot forward, one back, and drop the back knee towards the floor.","弓步：一只脚在前，一只在后，后面的膝盖往地上落。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell someone how to do a reverse lunge.","教人做后撤弓步。"],"o":[["Come on, you've got this!",0],["I did four out of seven.",0],["Step back and lower your knee.",1]],"ok":"对：lower your knee。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Step back and lower your knee."}},"talk":[["isle.tom","lunge 怎么读？",[["more.friends_e.jade","LUNJ — rhymes with 'sponge'.","LUNJ，跟 sponge 押韵。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"squeeze at the top","mean":"到最高处夹紧","learner":["At high place, use power.","听不懂"],"natural":["Squeeze at the top.","臀桥时最常听到"],"note":["In a glute bridge, lift your hips, squeeze at the top for a second, then lower slowly.","臀桥：把臀抬起来，最高处夹紧一秒，再慢慢放下。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell someone what to do at the highest point.","告诉别人到最高点做什么。"],"o":[["Squeeze at the top, then lower slowly.",1],["Come on, you've got this!",0],["I did four out of seven.",0]],"ok":"对：at the top。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Squeeze at the top, then lower slowly."}},"talk":[["isle.rosa","squeeze 还能用在哪？",[["more.friends_e.jade","Squeeze a lemon, squeeze someone's hand — any time you press hard.","挤柠檬、握紧谁的手——用力挤压都能用。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"hands under your shoulders","mean":"手在肩膀正下方","learner":["Put hands on the floor near shoulder.","不够准"],"natural":["Hands under your shoulders.","平板支撑、俯卧撑都用"],"note":["For a plank or a push-up, stack your hands right under your shoulders. Your wrists will thank you.","平板、俯卧撑，手要叠在肩膀正下方。手腕会感谢你。"],"quiz":{"q":["Tell someone where to put their hands for a push-up.","告诉别人俯卧撑手放哪。"],"o":[["Come on, you've got this!",0],["Put your hands under your shoulders.",1],["Sit back, like there's a chair.",0]],"ok":"对：under your shoulders。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Put your hands under your shoulders."}},"talk":[["london.oliver","plank 怎么读？",[["more.friends_e.jade","PLANK — like a long piece of wood. Because that's what you look like!","PLANK，就是一块长木板。因为你看起来就像一块木板！"]]]]},"5":{"lang":{"chunk":"you've got this","mean":"你可以的","learner":["You can, come on!","能懂，少了点劲"],"natural":["Two more — you've got this!","最后几个时喊"],"note":["Say it to yourself too. Out loud. It works better than you think.","也对自己说，出声说。比你想的管用。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your friend is tired on the last rep.","朋友最后一个快撑不住了。"],"o":[["Squeeze at the top, then lower slowly.",0],["Step back and lower your knee.",0],["Come on, you've got this!",1]],"ok":"对：you've got this。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Come on, you've got this!"}},"talk":[["isle.amara","you've got this 和 you can do it 一样吗？",[["more.friends_e.jade","Same feeling. 'You've got this' sounds younger, more like a coach.","意思一样。you've got this 更年轻，更像教练。"]]]]},"6":{"lang":{"chunk":"___ out of seven","mean":"七天里的……天","learner":["I did five days in seven days.","太长"],"natural":["This week I did five out of seven.","out of 说比例"],"note":["Five out of seven is a great week. Missing a day isn't failing — stopping is.","七天做五天就很好。漏一天不算失败，停下才算。"],"quiz":{"q":["You exercised four days this week.","你这周练了四天。"],"o":[["I did four out of seven.",1],["Sit back, like there's a chair.",0],["Squeeze at the top, then lower slowly.",0]],"ok":"对：four out of seven。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I did four out of seven."}},"talk":[["new_york.xiaoyu","out of 还能用在分数上吗？",[["more.friends_e.jade","Yes: 'eight out of ten'. Same idea.","能：eight out of ten，一样的意思。"]]]]}},"jordi_map":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"How far…?","mean":"多远？","learner":["How long is it from here?","how long 问时间或长度，问距离用 how far"],"natural":["How far is it from here?","问距离"],"note":["Funny thing: people often answer in minutes, not metres. 'About ten minutes.'","有意思的是：人们常用时间回答，不用米。About ten minutes。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to know the distance to the beach.","你想知道离海滩多远。"],"o":[["How far is the beach from here?",1],["Is it uphill all the way?",0],["Africa is much bigger than it looks.",0]],"ok":"对：How far is…?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：How far is the beach from here?"}},"talk":[["isle.mei","how far 能用时间回答吗？",[["isle.jordi","Yes! 'Ten minutes' is a perfectly normal answer.","能！Ten minutes 是很正常的回答。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"uphill","mean":"上坡","learner":["Is the road going up?","能懂"],"natural":["Is it uphill all the way?","带学生爬山前必问"],"note":["On a paper map, contour lines close together mean steep. Far apart means easy.","纸地图上，等高线挤在一起就是陡，离得远就是缓。"],"quiz":{"q":["You're worried the walk is steep.","你担心路很陡。"],"o":[["Africa is much bigger than it looks.",0],["Is it uphill all the way?",1],["How far is the beach from here?",0]],"ok":"对：uphill all the way。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Is it uphill all the way?"}},"talk":[["stars.emma","uphill 还有别的意思吗？",[["isle.jordi","'An uphill battle' — something hard that takes a long time.","an uphill battle：一件难、要很久的事。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"bigger than it looks","mean":"比看上去大","learner":["It is more big than we see.","more big 不对"],"natural":["It's much bigger than it looks.","much + 比较级"],"note":["On most world maps, Greenland looks as big as Africa. In fact, Africa is about fourteen times bigger.","很多世界地图上，格陵兰看起来跟非洲一样大。其实非洲大约是它的十四倍。"],"quiz":{"q":["Talk about Africa on a world map.","说说世界地图上的非洲。"],"o":[["Is it uphill all the way?",0],["Is it on this side of the river?",0],["Africa is much bigger than it looks.",1]],"ok":"对：much bigger。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Africa is much bigger than it looks."}},"talk":[["more.friends_b.farah","much 和 very 都能放 bigger 前面吗？",[["isle.jordi","Only 'much': much bigger. 'Very bigger' is wrong.","只能用 much：much bigger。very bigger 是错的。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"this side of","mean":"……的这一边","learner":["Is it at here side of river?","乱了"],"natural":["Is it on this side of the river?","on this side of + 地方"],"note":["Rivers split cities. Asking this first can save you a very long walk.","河把城市分成两半。先问这句，能省一大段路。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to know if the hotel is across the river.","你想知道酒店在不在河对岸。"],"o":[["Is it on this side of the river?",1],["Africa is much bigger than it looks.",0],["How far is the beach from here?",0]],"ok":"对：on this side of。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Is it on this side of the river?"}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","对岸怎么说？",[["isle.jordi","'On the other side of the river.' In London they just say 'south of the river'.","on the other side of the river。伦敦人直接说 south of the river。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"it's about … minutes to …","mean":"到……大概……分钟","learner":["From my home to station, ten minutes about.","about 放错了"],"natural":["From my place, it's about ten minutes to the station.","about 放在数字前"],"note":["Draw your own map: home, school or work, the shop. You'll see your city differently.","画一张自己的地图：家、学校或公司、常去的店。你会换个眼光看你的城市。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say how far your station is.","说说你家离车站多远。"],"o":[["How far is the beach from here?",0],["It's about ten minutes to the station.",1],["Africa is much bigger than it looks.",0]],"ok":"对：about ten minutes to…","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It's about ten minutes to the station."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","说走路十分钟怎么说最自然？",[["isle.jordi","'A ten-minute walk.' Or 'ten minutes on foot'. Both are fine.","a ten-minute walk，或者 ten minutes on foot，都行。"]]]]}},"kenji_standup":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"worked on","mean":"在弄、在做（某项工作）","learner":["Yesterday I do the login page.","时态不对，do 也太笼统"],"natural":["Yesterday I worked on the login page.","站会第一句"],"note":["A stand-up has three parts: yesterday, today, and anything blocking you. Short is good.","站会三件事：昨天、今天、有没有卡住。越短越好。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say what you did yesterday.","说你昨天做了什么。"],"o":[["Yesterday I worked on the search page.",1],["Quick question — where's the config file?",0],["Can I get a second pair of eyes on this?",0]],"ok":"对：worked on。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Yesterday I worked on the search page."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.linhao","blocker 是什么？",[["isle.daniel","Anything stopping your work — like waiting for someone's review.","任何挡住你干活的东西，比如在等别人 review。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"the root cause","mean":"根本原因","learner":["I found the reason of the bug.","能懂，root cause 更像工程师"],"natural":["I found the root cause. It's a time zone issue.","先说找到了，再说是什么"],"note":["Say the answer first, then the detail. People in a stand-up are busy.","先说结论，再说细节。站会上大家都忙。"],"quiz":{"q":["You finally know why the bug happens.","你终于知道 bug 为什么出现了。"],"o":[["Can I get a second pair of eyes on this?",0],["I found the root cause.",1],["Quick question — where's the config file?",0]],"ok":"对：the root cause。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I found the root cause."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.aiko","time zone 重音在哪？",[["isle.daniel","TIME-zone — the stress is on 'time'.","TIME-zone，重音在 time。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"a second pair of eyes","mean":"再请一个人帮着看","learner":["Please check my code again.","像在下命令"],"natural":["The fix is small, but I'd like a second pair of eyes.","客气地请人 review"],"note":["Asking for help in a stand-up isn't weak. It saves everyone time.","站会上请人帮忙不丢人，大家都省时间。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want someone to look at your change.","你想请人看一下你的改动。"],"o":[["I found the root cause.",0],["Quick question — where's the config file?",0],["Can I get a second pair of eyes on this?",1]],"ok":"对：a second pair of eyes。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Can I get a second pair of eyes on this?"},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.xiaoyu","这句话会不会太口语？",[["isle.daniel","It's perfect at work — friendly and polite.","工作里刚刚好，友好又客气。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"quick question","mean":"问一下","learner":["I have one question, can I ask?","绕"],"natural":["Quick question — can you walk me through it?","两个词就打开话题"],"note":["'Quick question' tells people it won't take long. That's why they say yes.","Quick question 告诉对方不会占用多久，所以对方愿意答。"],"quiz":{"q":["You can't find the config file.","你找不到配置文件。"],"o":[["Quick question — where's the config file?",1],["Today I'm going to fix the tests.",0],["Can I get a second pair of eyes on this?",0]],"ok":"对：Quick question。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Quick question — where's the config file?"},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.mei","walk me through 是什么意思？",[["isle.daniel","'Explain it step by step.' Like walking through it together.","一步一步讲给我听，像一起走一遍。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"I'm going to…","mean":"我今天要……","learner":["Today I will maybe fix the tests.","maybe 让人不放心"],"natural":["Yesterday I fixed the bug. Today I'm going to write the tests.","昨天 + 今天，两句就够"],"note":["Two sentences. That's a whole stand-up update. You don't need more.","两句话就是一次完整的站会发言，不用更多。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say your plan for today.","说你今天的计划。"],"o":[["Quick question — where's the config file?",0],["Today I'm going to fix the tests.",1],["Can I get a second pair of eyes on this?",0]],"ok":"对：I'm going to fix。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Today I'm going to fix the tests."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.linhao","today I will 可以吗？",[["isle.daniel","Sure, but 'I'm going to' sounds like a plan you already have.","可以，但 I'm going to 听着是早就计划好的。"]]]]}},"kwame_afrobeats":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"What's it called?","mean":"叫什么名字？","learner":["How is this song called?","能懂，很多人这么说；问歌名，英语用 what"],"natural":["What's this song called?","called 放最后"],"note":["Afrobeat, no s, is Fela Kuti's sound from the 1970s. Afrobeats, with an s, is today's pop from Nigeria and Ghana.","Afrobeat（没有 s）是 Fela Kuti 七十年代的音乐；Afrobeats（有 s）是现在尼日利亚和加纳的流行乐。"],"quiz":{"q":["You love a song in a café and want its name.","你在咖啡馆听到一首很喜欢的歌。"],"o":[["What's this song called?",1],["I'll be right back.",0],["This song is blowing up on TikTok.",0]],"ok":"对：What's this song called?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：What's this song called?"}},"talk":[["isle.aiko","Afrobeats 和 Afrobeat 真的不一样？",[["isle.kwame","Yes! One letter, fifty years apart.","真的！差一个字母，差了五十年。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"sounds a bit like","mean":"听起来有点像","learner":["It's like my father's song.","能懂"],"natural":["It sounds a bit like something my dad plays.","a bit 让话更软"],"note":["Afrobeats grew out of highlife, jazz, funk and hip-hop. So it sounds a bit like everything — that's the point.","Afrobeats 从 highlife、爵士、放克和嘻哈里长出来，所以听着有点像什么都有——这正是它的味道。"],"quiz":{"q":["A new song reminds you of jazz.","一首新歌让你想到爵士。"],"o":[["What's this song called?",0],["It sounds a bit like jazz.",1],["I'll be right back.",0]],"ok":"对：sounds a bit like jazz。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：It sounds a bit like jazz."}},"talk":[["isle.rosa","sounds like 和 looks like 一样用吗？",[["isle.kwame","Exactly. Sounds like, looks like, smells like, tastes like.","一样：sounds like、looks like、smells like、tastes like。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"I'll be right back.","mean":"我马上回来","learner":["Wait me, I come back soon.","wait 后面要 for"],"natural":["I'll be right back.","离开一下时最常说"],"note":["In chat, people just type 'brb'.","发消息时，大家直接打 brb。"],"quiz":{"q":["You need to leave for a minute.","你要离开一下。"],"o":[["What's this song called?",0],["This song is blowing up on TikTok.",0],["I'll be right back.",1]],"ok":"对：I'll be right back。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'll be right back."}},"talk":[["new_york.xiaoyu","brb 能对老板用吗？",[["isle.kwame","Better not. With your boss, 'Back in five minutes' is safer.","最好别。跟老板说 Back in five minutes 更稳。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"blowing up","mean":"（突然）火了","learner":["This song is very famous now.","也对，blowing up 是「一下子火起来」"],"natural":["This song is blowing up right now.","说正在火"],"note":["A song can blow up overnight now — one dance on TikTok and the whole world knows it.","现在一首歌能一夜爆红——TikTok 上一支舞，全世界都知道了。"],"quiz":{"q":["A song is suddenly everywhere online.","一首歌突然到处都是。"],"o":[["This song is blowing up on TikTok.",1],["I'll be right back.",0],["I've had it on repeat all week.",0]],"ok":"对：blowing up。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：This song is blowing up on TikTok."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","blow up 不是爆炸吗？",[["isle.kwame","That too! For songs and people, it means getting really popular, really fast.","也是！说歌和人，就是一下子火起来。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"on repeat","mean":"单曲循环","learner":["I single loop this song.","single loop 是「单曲循环」直接搬过来的，对方多半听不懂"],"natural":["I've had it on repeat all week.","on repeat = 一直在放"],"note":["Tell me what's on repeat for you. That's how I find new music.","告诉我你在循环什么歌，我就是这样找新歌的。"],"quiz":{"q":["You keep playing one song.","你一直在放同一首歌。"],"o":[["This song is blowing up on TikTok.",0],["I've had it on repeat all week.",1],["I'll be right back.",0]],"ok":"对：on repeat。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I've had it on repeat all week."}},"talk":[["isle.amara","说 single loop，别人听得懂吗？",[["isle.kwame","Probably not. Say 'on repeat' — everyone gets that.","多半听不懂。说 on repeat，谁都懂。"]]]]}},"linhao_phone":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"book a table","mean":"订位","learner":["I want a table, four people, seven.","能懂，像电报"],"natural":["Hi, I'd like to book a table for four at seven.","人数 + 时间，一句说完"],"note":["On the phone, say the number of people and the time first. That's all they need.","电话里先说人数和时间，对方要的就这些。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want a table for two.","你要订两个人的位。"],"o":[["I'd like to book a table for two.",1],["Could I move it to Friday?",0],["There's a problem with my order.",0]],"ok":"对：book a table for two。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'd like to book a table for two."},"by":"london.oliver"},"talk":[["isle.mei","book 和 reserve 一样吗？",[["london.oliver","Same thing. 'Book' is more common in the UK.","一样。英国更常说 book。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"move it to","mean":"改到","learner":["Can I change the day to Saturday?","也行"],"natural":["Could I move it to Saturday instead?","instead = 换成"],"note":["'Instead' at the end makes it clear you're swapping, not adding.","句尾加 instead，对方就知道是换，不是加。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to change your booking to Friday.","你想把预订改到周五。"],"o":[["I'm calling to cancel my booking.",0],["Could I move it to Friday?",1],["I'd like to book a table for two.",0]],"ok":"对：move it to Friday。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Could I move it to Friday?"},"by":"london.oliver"},"talk":[["more.friends_e.hana","change 也行吗？",[["london.oliver","Yes: 'Could I change it to Friday?' Both work.","行：Could I change it to Friday? 两个都可以。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"spell that","mean":"拼一下","learner":["Please tell me the letters.","能懂"],"natural":["Sorry, could you spell that for me?","电话里最常用"],"note":["Names on the phone are hard for everyone. Natives ask 'Could you spell that?' all the time.","电话里的名字谁都难听清，母语的人也常问 Could you spell that?"],"quiz":{"q":["You didn't get the name of the street.","你没听清街名。"],"o":[["I'm calling to cancel my booking.",0],["There's a problem with my order.",0],["Could you spell that for me?",1]],"ok":"对：spell that for me。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Could you spell that for me?"},"by":"london.oliver"},"talk":[["isle.kenji","电话里 B 和 P 听不清怎么办？",[["london.oliver","Use words: 'B for Bravo, P for Papa.' Or just 'B as in banana'.","用词来说：B for Bravo、P for Papa，或者 B as in banana。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"a problem with","mean":"……有点问题","learner":["My order is wrong thing.","不完整"],"natural":["I'm afraid there's a problem with my order.","I'm afraid 让坏消息软一点"],"note":["Start calm. People help faster when you're polite on the phone.","开口平静一点。电话里客气，对方帮得更快。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your delivery is missing an item.","你的外卖少了一样。"],"o":[["There's a problem with my order.",1],["Could I move it to Friday?",0],["Could you spell that for me?",0]],"ok":"对：a problem with。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：There's a problem with my order."},"by":"london.oliver"},"talk":[["isle.xiaoyu","I'm afraid 是害怕吗？",[["london.oliver","No — here it just makes bad news softer. 'I'm afraid we're closed.'","不是，这里只是让坏消息软一点：I'm afraid we're closed。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"I'm calling to…","mean":"我打电话来是想……","learner":["I call because I want cancel.","能懂，有点乱"],"natural":["Hi, I'm calling to change my booking for Friday.","第一句就说来意"],"note":["Say why you're calling in the first sentence. Then the person knows how to help.","第一句就说为什么打来，对方就知道怎么帮你。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want to cancel your booking.","你想取消预订。"],"o":[["Could you spell that for me?",0],["I'm calling to cancel my booking.",1],["There's a problem with my order.",0]],"ok":"对：I'm calling to cancel。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'm calling to cancel my booking."},"by":"london.oliver"},"talk":[["isle.rosa","cancelled 还是 canceled？",[["london.oliver","Cancelled in the UK, canceled in the US. Both are right.","英国写 cancelled，美国写 canceled，都对。"]]]]}},"mei_order":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"half sugar, less ice","mean":"半糖少冰","learner":["Sugar half, ice little.","顺序反了"],"natural":["Half sugar, less ice, please.","先甜度，再冰块"],"note":["In Taiwan, shops ask two things: sugar and ice. Full, less, half, light, or no sugar.","在台湾，店员只问两件事：甜度和冰块。全糖、少糖、半糖、微糖、无糖。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want it not too sweet and with no ice.","你要不太甜、去冰。"],"o":[["Half sugar, no ice, please.",1],["Can I get a large milk tea?",0],["Can I get it warm, please?",0]],"ok":"对：Half sugar, no ice。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Half sugar, no ice, please."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","less ice 和 light ice 一样吗？",[["isle.mei","In our shop, yes. Some shops say 'light ice'.","我们店里一样。有的店说 light ice。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"warm","mean":"温的","learner":["Can it be not cold?","绕"],"natural":["Can I get it warm, with pearls?","冷热 + 加料"],"note":["Most drinks can be hot, warm or iced. Just ask.","大多数饮料都能做热的、温的或冰的，问就好。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want your milk tea warm.","你想要温的奶茶。"],"o":[["Half sugar, no ice, please.",0],["Can I get it warm, please?",1],["Can I get a large milk tea?",0]],"ok":"对：get it warm。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Can I get it warm, please?"}},"talk":[["isle.amara","pearls 和 boba 一样吗？",[["isle.mei","Yes. Many Americans say 'boba'; most menus say 'pearls' or 'tapioca'.","一样。很多美国人说 boba，菜单上多写 pearls 或 tapioca。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"Can I get…?","mean":"我要一杯……","learner":["I want one milk tea.","不算失礼，只是有点直"],"natural":["Can I get a large milk tea, half sugar, less ice?","点单的万能开头"],"note":["'Can I get…' is the most common way to order in the US. In the UK, 'Could I have…' is a bit more usual.","Can I get… 是美国最常见的点单说法；英国更常说 Could I have…"],"quiz":{"q":["Order a large milk tea.","点一杯大杯奶茶。"],"o":[["Half sugar, no ice, please.",0],["Can I get it warm, please?",0],["Can I get a large milk tea?",1]],"ok":"对：Can I get…?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Can I get a large milk tea?"}},"talk":[["isle.rosa","I want a… 是不是不礼貌？",[["isle.mei","Not rude, just a bit direct. Add 'please' and a smile — totally fine.","不算不礼貌，只是直接。加个 please、笑一下就好。"]]]]}},"nadia_5k":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"five K","mean":"五公里","learner":["I run five kilometre today.","kilometres 要加 s"],"natural":["I did five K today.","跑步的人常这么说，你会常听到"],"note":["Runners say 'five K' for five kilometres. The free Saturday 5K, parkrun, started in a London park in 2004 — and walking counts.","跑步的人把五公里叫 five K。周六免费的 5 公里跑 parkrun，2004 年从伦敦的一个公园开始——走路也算。"],"quiz":{"q":["You ran five kilometres this morning.","你今早跑了五公里。"],"o":[["I ran five K this morning.",1],["I walked to the shop this morning.",0],["I'm running five K tomorrow.",0]],"ok":"对：I ran five K。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：I ran five K this morning."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","jog 和 run 有什么区别？",[["isle.nadia","Jogging is slower and relaxed. Running is faster. At parkrun, walking counts too!","jog 慢一点、轻松一点；run 快一些。parkrun 上走路也算！"]]]]}},"rachel_th":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"th /θ/","mean":"think 的 th：不出声","learner":["I sink so.","s 代替了 th，意思变成「下沉」"],"natural":["I think so.","舌尖放在上下牙之间，吹气"],"note":["Put the tip of your tongue between your teeth and blow. No voice.","舌尖放在上下牙之间，吹气，不出声。"],"quiz":{"q":["Which word has the same 'th' as think?","哪个词的 th 跟 think 一样？"],"o":[["thanks",1],["this",0],["the",0]],"ok":"对：thanks 跟 think 一样，不出声。","no":"this、the 的 th 要出声；thanks 跟 think 一样不出声。"}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","我老说成 sink，怎么办？",[["more.friends_a.rachel","Use a mirror. If you can't see your tongue, it's 's'. Show me the tongue!","照镜子。看不见舌头，就是 s。把舌头露出来！"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"th /ð/","mean":"that 的 th：出声","learner":["Zat's ze sing.","z 和 s 代替了 th"],"natural":["That's the thing.","that、the 出声；thing 不出声"],"note":["'That' and 'the' use the voiced th — same tongue, but turn your voice on. Touch your throat: it buzzes.","that、the 的 th 要出声——舌头位置一样，把声音打开。摸摸喉咙，会震。"],"quiz":{"q":["Which one buzzes, like 'that'?","哪个像 that 一样要出声？"],"o":[["thanks",0],["this",1],["thing",0]],"ok":"对：this 出声。","no":"thing、thanks 不出声；this 跟 that 一样出声。"}},"talk":[["isle.linhao","That's the thing 是什么意思？",[["more.friends_a.rachel","'That's the problem', or 'that's the important point'.","「问题就在这儿」，或者「关键就在这儿」。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"three-thirty","mean":"三点半","learner":["Tree-tirty.","t 代替了 th"],"natural":["Let's meet at three-thirty.","两个 th 都不出声"],"note":["Don't add a vowel: 'three', not 'tha-ree'.","别加元音：three，不是 tha-ree。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say 3:30.","说出 3:30。"],"o":[["Thanks a lot!",0],["I think the best thing about it is the food.",0],["three-thirty",1]],"ok":"对：three-thirty。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：three-thirty"}},"talk":[["new_york.xiaoyu","half past three 也可以吗？",[["more.friends_a.rachel","Yes — 'half past three' is very British. Both are fine.","可以——half past three 很英式，两个都行。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"thanks a lot","mean":"太谢谢了","learner":["Sanks a lot.","s 代替了 th"],"natural":["Thanks a lot.","笑着说，声调往上走"],"note":["Careful with tone: 'Thanks a lot' in a flat, slow voice can sound sarcastic!","注意语气：平平地、慢慢地说 Thanks a lot，会听着像讽刺！"],"quiz":{"q":["Someone holds the door for you.","有人帮你扶着门。"],"o":[["Thanks a lot!",1],["three-thirty",0],["I think the best thing about it is the food.",0]],"ok":"对：th 舌尖出来。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Thanks a lot!"}},"talk":[["isle.mei","thanks a lot 会不会听着讽刺？",[["more.friends_a.rachel","Only with a flat, slow voice. Smile and let your voice go up.","只有平平慢慢地说才会。笑着说，声调往上。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"I think the best thing about…","mean":"我觉得……最好的是……","learner":["I sink the best sing…","两个 th 都变成 s"],"natural":["I think the best thing about London is the parks.","think、thing 不出声，the 出声"],"note":["Three th sounds in one sentence. Slow down the first time, then speed up.","一句话里三个 th。第一遍慢，再加快。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say what you like most about your city.","说说你最喜欢你城市的什么。"],"o":[["three-thirty",0],["I think the best thing about it is the food.",1],["Thanks a lot!",0]],"ok":"对：the best thing about it is…","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I think the best thing about it is the food."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","best thing 中间要停吗？",[["more.friends_a.rachel","Link them: best-thing. The t almost disappears.","连起来：best-thing，t 几乎听不见。"]]]]}},"rosa_tacos":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"with everything","mean":"全都加","learner":["Two tacos, put all.","put all 对方可能听不出是「全都加」；with everything 一听就懂"],"natural":["Two, with everything, please.","在塔可摊最常听到"],"note":["At a taco stand in Mexico, say 'con todo' — with everything: onion, coriander and salsa.","在墨西哥的塔可摊说 con todo——全都加：洋葱、香菜、莎莎酱。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want all the toppings.","你想要所有配料。"],"o":[["Two, with everything, please.",1],["Two, with nothing on, please.",0],["Two, no onions, please.",0]],"ok":"对：with everything。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Two, with everything, please."}},"talk":[["isle.mei","coriander 和 cilantro 是一个东西吗？",[["isle.rosa","Yes! Brits say coriander, Americans say cilantro.","是！英国人说 coriander，美国人说 cilantro。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"the ___ one","mean":"……的那个","learner":["I like chicken best taco.","顺序乱"],"natural":["My favourite was the chicken one, with pineapple.","the ___ one 代替重复的名词"],"note":["'The chicken one' saves you saying 'taco' again. English loves 'one'.","the chicken one 就不用再说一次 taco。英语很爱用 one。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say which taco you liked best.","说你最喜欢哪个塔可。"],"o":[["I didn't try the chicken one.",0],["My favourite was the chicken one.",1],["Two chicken tacos, please.",0]],"ok":"对：the chicken one。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：My favourite was the chicken one."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","favourite 和 favorite 一样吗？",[["isle.rosa","Same word. 'Favourite' with a u in the UK, 'favorite' in the US.","同一个词：英国写 favourite，美国写 favorite。"]]]]}},"tom_veg":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"one bite","mean":"就一口","learner":["You must eat it.","一说就对着干"],"natural":["Just one bite, then tell me what you think.","只要一口，还让孩子当裁判"],"note":["Kids often need to try a new food many times — eight to fifteen is often quoted — before they like it.","孩子常要尝很多次才会喜欢一种新食物——常说是八到十五次。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want your kid to taste the broccoli.","你想让孩子尝一下西兰花。"],"o":[["Just try one bite.",1],["When I was a kid, I hated mushrooms.",0],["Can you help me wash these?",0]],"ok":"对：one bite。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Just try one bite."}},"talk":[["new_york.xiaoyu","bite 和 bit 怎么分？",[["isle.tom","Bite has 'eye' in it: b-EYE-t. Bit is short.","bite 里有个 eye 的音：b-EYE-t；bit 很短。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"What should we call it?","mean":"给它起个什么名字？","learner":["What name we give?","能懂"],"natural":["What should we call it?","让孩子来起名"],"note":["Give it a fun name — 'dinosaur trees' for broccoli. It works better than you'd think.","起个好玩的名字——把西兰花叫「恐龙树」。比你想的管用。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want your kid to name a new dish.","你想让孩子给新菜起名。"],"o":[["When I was a kid, I hated mushrooms.",0],["What should we call it?",1],["Can you help me wash these?",0]],"ok":"对：What should we call it?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：What should we call it?"}},"talk":[["isle.mei","name 能当动词吗？",[["isle.tom","Yes: 'Let's name it Dinosaur Trees.'","能：Let's name it Dinosaur Trees。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"help me","mean":"帮我","learner":["You wash these, okay?","像派活"],"natural":["Can you help me wash these?","一起做，孩子更愿意吃"],"note":["Kids who help cook are more likely to taste. Washing is the easiest job to give.","帮着做饭的孩子更愿意尝。洗菜是最容易交出去的活。"],"quiz":{"q":["You want your kid to help with the carrots.","你想让孩子帮忙弄胡萝卜。"],"o":[["That's okay. Maybe next time.",0],["Just try one bite.",0],["Can you help me wash these?",1]],"ok":"对：help me wash。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Can you help me wash these?"}},"talk":[["isle.rosa","help me to wash 也对吗？",[["isle.tom","Yes, both are fine. Without 'to' is more common when speaking.","都对。口语里不加 to 更常见。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"Maybe next time.","mean":"下次再试","learner":["Why you don't eat?","听着像责怪"],"natural":["That's okay. Maybe next time.","不逼，留个门"],"note":["Pressure makes it worse. Calm and lots of tries — that's what works.","逼得越紧越糟。平静、多试几次，才管用。"],"quiz":{"q":["Your kid doesn't want to try today.","孩子今天不想尝。"],"o":[["That's okay. Maybe next time.",1],["When I was a kid, I hated mushrooms.",0],["Can you help me wash these?",0]],"ok":"对：Maybe next time。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：That's okay. Maybe next time."}},"talk":[["isle.nadia","就这么算了，会不会太松？",[["isle.tom","It's not giving up. It's keeping the door open for tomorrow.","不是放弃，是给明天留个门。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"When I was a kid, I hated…","mean":"我小时候讨厌……","learner":["Small time I don't like…","small time 是「小时候」直接搬过来的，对方听不懂"],"natural":["When I was a kid, I hated mushrooms. Now I love them.","小时候 + 现在，两句对比"],"note":["Most adults have one food they hated as kids and love now. That's the story to tell your kids.","大多数大人都有一样小时候讨厌、现在爱吃的东西。这就是讲给孩子听的故事。"],"quiz":{"q":["Talk about a food you didn't like as a child.","说一样你小时候不爱吃的东西。"],"o":[["What should we call it?",0],["When I was a kid, I hated mushrooms.",1],["That's okay. Maybe next time.",0]],"ok":"对：When I was a kid。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：When I was a kid, I hated mushrooms."}},"talk":[["isle.kenji","hate 会不会太重？",[["isle.tom","For food, it's normal: 'I hate olives.' Everyone says it.","说吃的很正常：I hate olives，大家都这么说。"]]]]}},"xiaoyu_visa":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"Here's…","mean":"这是……（递东西时）","learner":["This is my passport, give you.","多了一截"],"natural":["Good morning. Here's my passport.","递过去时说"],"note":["The first ten seconds matter. Smile, say good morning, hand it over.","头十秒很重要。笑一下、说早上好、把护照递过去。"],"quiz":{"q":["You hand your passport to the officer.","你把护照递给签证官。"],"o":[["Good morning. Here's my passport.",1],["I'm going to London to study.",0],["Sorry, could you say that again?",0]],"ok":"对：Here's my passport。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Good morning. Here's my passport."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.linhao","Here you are 和 Here's 有区别吗？",[["isle.daniel","Both are fine. 'Here you are' when you hand it over; 'Here's my passport' says what it is.","都行。递过去说 Here you are；Here's my passport 还说了是什么。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"going for a master's","mean":"去读硕士","learner":["I go to study master design.","乱"],"natural":["I'm going for a master's in design.","going for = 去读、去争取"],"note":["Say the degree and the subject. That's the question behind every other question.","说清楚学位和专业。其他问题都绕着这个转。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say what you're going to study.","说你要去读什么。"],"o":[["Sorry, could you say that again?",0],["I'm going for a master's in design.",1],["Yes, it's right here.",0]],"ok":"对：a master's in design。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'm going for a master's in design."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["stars.yuriko","master's 为什么有 's？",[["isle.daniel","It's short for 'master's degree'.","是 master's degree 的简写。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"I chose … because…","mean":"我选……是因为……","learner":["Because it is very good school.","没说具体好在哪"],"natural":["I chose this programme because it works with real hospitals.","一个真实的细节"],"note":["Officers want one clear reason. One real detail beats five big words.","签证官要一个清楚的理由。一个真实的细节，胜过五个大词。"],"quiz":{"q":["Give your reason for choosing a school.","说你为什么选这个学校。"],"o":[["My parents are paying for it.",0],["Good morning. Here's my passport.",0],["I chose it because of the teachers.",1]],"ok":"对：because of + 名词。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I chose it because of the teachers."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.kenji","programme 和 program 一样吗？",[["isle.daniel","UK writes 'programme' for courses. US writes 'program' for everything.","英国说课程写 programme；美国全写 program。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"say that again","mean":"再说一遍","learner":["What? Again.","不礼貌"],"natural":["Sorry, could you say that again?","冷静、礼貌"],"note":["Asking once is normal and calm. Guessing the answer is worse.","问一次很正常，也显得冷静。瞎猜反而更糟。"],"quiz":{"q":["You didn't hear the officer's question.","你没听清签证官的问题。"],"o":[["Sorry, could you say that again?",1],["My parents are paying for it.",0],["I'm going for a master's in design.",0]],"ok":"对：say that again。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Sorry, could you say that again?"},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.linhao","面试里没听清会扣分吗？",[["isle.daniel","No. Asking once is fine. It shows you're listening carefully.","不会。问一次没关系，说明你在认真听。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"right here","mean":"就在这儿","learner":["Yes, it is here.","对，少了点自信"],"natural":["Yes, I have it right here.","right = 正好、就"],"note":["Put your papers in the order they'll ask. 'Right here' sounds best when it's true.","把材料按会问的顺序放好。right here 说出来是真的时候最好听。"],"quiz":{"q":["The officer asks for your bank letter.","签证官要你的银行证明。"],"o":[["I'm going to London to study.",0],["Yes, it's right here.",1],["Sorry, could you say that again?",0]],"ok":"对：right here。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Yes, it's right here."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.mei","right here 的 right 是「对」的意思吗？",[["isle.daniel","No — it means 'exactly'. Right here, right now.","不是，是「正好、就」：right here、right now。"]]]]},"5":{"lang":{"chunk":"paying for","mean":"出钱","learner":["My parents give the money.","能懂"],"natural":["My parents are paying for it, and I've saved some too.","说谁付钱，再补一句自己"],"note":["Simple and true. They don't need a speech — they need to believe you.","简单、真实就好。他们不要演讲，要的是相信你。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say who is paying for your studies.","说谁出学费。"],"o":[["I chose it because of the teachers.",0],["Yes, it's right here.",0],["My parents are paying for it.",1]],"ok":"对：paying for it。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：My parents are paying for it."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.kenji","I've saved some 后面省了什么？",[["isle.daniel","'Some money.' We drop it because it's clear.","省了 money，意思很清楚就不说了。"]]]]},"6":{"lang":{"chunk":"I'm going to … to …","mean":"我要去……（地方）去……（做什么）","learner":["I go to London for study.","能懂；签证面试说 I'm going … to study，计划和目的都更清楚"],"natural":["I'm going to London to study design.","to + 动词说目的"],"note":["Place, then purpose. Seven days of practice — this sentence is yours now.","先说去哪，再说去干嘛。练了七天，这句已经是你的了。"],"quiz":{"q":["Say where you're going and why.","说你要去哪、去干嘛。"],"o":[["I'm going to London to study.",1],["Sorry, could you say that again?",0],["Yes, it's right here.",0]],"ok":"对：to London to study。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：I'm going to London to study."},"by":"isle.daniel"},"talk":[["isle.amara","to study 和 for studying 哪个对？",[["isle.daniel","'To study' is the clearer one: I'm going to London to study.","to study 最清楚：I'm going to London to study。"]]]]}},"yuriko_spanish":{"0":{"lang":{"chunk":"¿Qué tal?","mean":"怎么样？（打招呼）","learner":["Hola, ¿cómo estás usted?","estás 和 usted 混在一起了"],"natural":["Hola, ¿qué tal?","随时随地都能用"],"note":["En México también vas a oír: ¿Qué onda?","在墨西哥你还会听到 ¿Qué onda?（很随意的「怎么样」）。"],"quiz":{"q":["¿Cómo saludas a un amigo?","怎么跟朋友打招呼？"],"o":[["¿Qué tal?",1],["Un café, por favor.",0],["Me gustan los tacos.",0]],"ok":"对：¿Qué tal?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：¿Qué tal?"},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["isle.kenji","Hola 的 h 要读吗？",[["isle.rosa","No. The h is silent in Spanish: OH-la.","不读。西语里 h 不发音：OH-la。"]]]]},"1":{"lang":{"chunk":"Mucho gusto.","mean":"很高兴认识你","learner":["Muy contento conocer.","少了几个小词，像电报；Mucho gusto 一句就够"],"natural":["Mucho gusto.","男女都能说"],"note":["Un hombre dice «encantado», una mujer «encantada». «Mucho gusto» sirve para todos.","男的说 encantado，女的说 encantada；Mucho gusto 谁都能说。"],"quiz":{"q":["Conoces a alguien nuevo.","你认识了一个新朋友。"],"o":[["¡Qué rico!",0],["Mucho gusto.",1],["¿Cuánto cuesta?",0]],"ok":"对：Mucho gusto。","no":"那句意思不一样。这里说：Mucho gusto."},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["isle.xiaoyu","别人说 Mucho gusto，我回什么？",[["isle.rosa","«Igualmente» — likewise.","回 Igualmente（我也是）。"]]]]},"2":{"lang":{"chunk":"por favor","mean":"请","learner":["Un café con leche, gracias.","也礼貌，por favor 用在点单时"],"natural":["Un café con leche, por favor.","放在句尾"],"note":["«Por favor» al final, como «please». Y siempre «gracias» al recibirlo.","por favor 放句尾，像 please；拿到时一定说 gracias。"],"quiz":{"q":["Pides un café.","你点一杯咖啡。"],"o":[["¿Qué tal?",0],["Mucho gusto.",0],["Un café, por favor.",1]],"ok":"对：por favor。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Un café, por favor."},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["stars.emma","gracias 怎么读？",[["isle.rosa","In Mexico: GRAH-see-as. In much of Spain you'll hear GRAH-thee-as.","墨西哥读 GRAH-see-as；西班牙很多地方读 GRAH-thee-as。"]]]]},"3":{"lang":{"chunk":"¿Me lo puede repetir?","mean":"您能再说一遍吗？","learner":["¿Otra vez?","太短，有点冲"],"natural":["¿Me lo puede repetir?","puede = 您（客气）"],"note":["«Puede» es formal (usted). Con amigos: «¿Me lo repites?»","puede 是对「您」说的；跟朋友说 ¿Me lo repites?"],"quiz":{"q":["No entendiste al camarero.","你没听懂服务员说什么。"],"o":[["¿Me lo puede repetir?",1],["Un café, por favor.",0],["¡Qué rico!",0]],"ok":"对：¿Me lo puede repetir?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：¿Me lo puede repetir?"},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["isle.jordi","更慢一点怎么说？",[["isle.rosa","«Más despacio, por favor.»","Más despacio, por favor（请慢一点）。"]]]]},"4":{"lang":{"chunk":"¿Cuánto cuesta?","mean":"多少钱？","learner":["¿Cuánto es dinero?","对方能猜到，但 dinero 是多出来的；问价说 ¿Cuánto cuesta?"],"natural":["¿Cuánto cuesta?","问一样东西"],"note":["Para dos o más cosas: «¿Cuánto cuestan?»","两样或更多：¿Cuánto cuestan?"],"quiz":{"q":["Quieres saber el precio de un sombrero.","你想知道一顶帽子多少钱。"],"o":[["¡Qué rico!",0],["¿Cuánto cuesta?",1],["Mucho gusto.",0]],"ok":"对：¿Cuánto cuesta?","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：¿Cuánto cuesta?"},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["isle.bea","在市场能讲价吗？",[["isle.rosa","At markets, a little — smile and ask «¿Me hace un descuento?». In shops, no.","市场里可以一点点——笑着问 ¿Me hace un descuento?；商店里就别了。"]]]]},"5":{"lang":{"chunk":"¡Qué rico!","mean":"真好吃！","learner":["Muy delicioso comida.","顺序乱"],"natural":["¡Qué rico!","最常听到的夸吃的"],"note":["Para la comida decimos «rico» o «sabroso». «Delicioso» también sirve en todas partes.","夸吃的说 rico 或 sabroso；delicioso 哪里都通。"],"quiz":{"q":["Pruebas un taco buenísimo.","你尝到一个超好吃的塔可。"],"o":[["¿Cuánto cuesta?",0],["¿Me lo puede repetir?",0],["¡Qué rico!",1]],"ok":"对：¡Qué rico!","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：¡Qué rico!"},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["isle.linhao","rico 不是「有钱」吗？",[["isle.rosa","Both! Rico means rich — and for food, delicious.","都是！rico 是有钱，说吃的就是好吃。"]]]]},"6":{"lang":{"chunk":"me gusta / me gustan","mean":"我喜欢（一样 / 好几样）","learner":["Yo gusto los tacos.","gustar 不这么用"],"natural":["Soy de China y me gustan los tacos.","复数东西用 gustan"],"note":["«Me gusta» + una cosa: me gusta el café. «Me gustan» + varias: me gustan los tacos.","一样东西用 me gusta：me gusta el café；好几样用 me gustan：me gustan los tacos。"],"quiz":{"q":["Dices que te gustan los tacos.","说你喜欢塔可。"],"o":[["Me gustan los tacos.",1],["¡Qué rico!",0],["¿Cuánto cuesta?",0]],"ok":"对：Me gustan los tacos。","no":"那句是别的时候说的。这里说：Me gustan los tacos."},"by":"isle.rosa"},"talk":[["isle.mei","Soy de China 还是 Soy china？",[["isle.rosa","Both work! «Soy de China» — I'm from China. «Soy china» — I'm Chinese (said by a woman).","都行！Soy de China 是「我来自中国」；Soy china 是「我是中国人」（女生说）。"]]]]}},"target":{"yuriko_spanish":["西语","Spanish","es-MX"]}};
window.ACTS_NEXT = [{"id":"next_0","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"一周数 sorry","en":"Sorry Count"},"hook":"你一天说几次 sorry？英国人呢？","host":"daniel","pic":"npc:daniel/teach","days":7,"showDays":true,"what":"英语里 sorry 不只是道歉：挤过人群、没听清、想插话都说。这一周数一数你说了几次、在什么时候说。","daily":"每说一次 sorry，点一下，选是哪种：道歉、借过、没听清、客气。","end":"你的 sorry 有一半其实是「借过」。全世界谁说得最多？","hostNm":"Daniel","hostJob":"在大阪教英语的美国人"},{"id":"next_1","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"口音侦探","en":"Accent Detective"},"hook":"10 秒，猜他从哪来","host":"rachel","pic":"npc:rachel/mic","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"英语有几百种口音。每天听一段 10 秒的真人录音，猜说话的人来自哪里。","daily":"听、猜、看答案，再跟着说一遍这句。","end":"最后一天录你自己的，看全世界把你猜成哪里。","hostNm":"Rachel","hostJob":"伦敦的发音老师"},{"id":"next_2","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"抓住你的口头禅","en":"Catch Your Catchphrase"},"hook":"你最常说的那句，是什么？","host":"rachel","pic":"npc:rachel/lesson","days":7,"showDays":false,"what":"每个人都有一句不自觉就说的话。问一个朋友，然后一周里抓住自己说它的时刻。","daily":"说了就记一下：当时在干嘛、跟谁。","end":"你的口头禅在什么时候出现？英语里它怎么说？","hostNm":"Rachel","hostJob":"伦敦的发音老师"},{"id":"next_3","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"一首歌听七天","en":"One Song, Seven Days"},"hook":"每天多听懂一句","host":"kwame","pic":"npc:kwame/studio","days":7,"showDays":true,"what":"同一首歌，每天听一遍，每天多听懂一句。","daily":"听，点出今天新听懂的那句，跟着哼。","end":"第七天跟着唱完整首，录下来送给世界。","hostNm":"Kwame","hostJob":"阿克拉的音乐学生"},{"id":"next_4","soil":"lang","t":{"zh":"教全世界念对你的名字","en":"Say My Name"},"hook":"你的名字，别人念对过吗？","host":"suqing","pic":"npc:suqing/teach","days":3,"showDays":false,"what":"录下你的名字和它的意思，听全世界的人怎么念。","daily":"第一天录名字，第二天听别人念、选念得最像的，第三天说名字的故事。","end":"你名字的心意，用英语讲给一个陌生人听。","hostNm":"苏晴","hostJob":"在北京教外国人中文"},{"id":"next_5","soil":"self","t":{"zh":"爷爷奶奶 20 岁挣多少","en":"When Grandma Was 20"},"hook":"问一个长辈，听一段你不知道的日子","host":"carmen","pic":"npc:hiroshi/family","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"每天问长辈一个问题：20 岁挣多少、一碗面多少钱、第一份工作、怎么认识的、最难的一年。","daily":"问、录下来、记一句他说的话。","end":"一本小采访：你是从哪来的。","hostNm":"Carmen","hostJob":"布宜诺斯艾利斯文化记者"},{"id":"next_6","soil":"self","t":{"zh":"把包倒在桌上","en":"Empty Your Bag"},"hook":"你出门离不开什么？","host":"amara","pic":"npc:amara/airport","days":1,"showDays":false,"what":"出门前把包里的东西全倒在桌上，一样样拍下来、说出它的英文名。","daily":"一次就好：倒、拍、说。","end":"你离不开的三样东西，跟全世界的包比一比。","hostNm":"Amara","hostJob":"迪拜空乘"},{"id":"next_7","soil":"self","t":{"zh":"相册第一名是啥","en":"Camera Roll No.1"},"hook":"你最常注意的是什么？","host":"bea","pic":"npc:bea/filming","days":7,"showDays":false,"what":"翻开手机相册，看看你拍得最多的是什么：吃的、猫、天空，还是人？","daily":"每天往前翻一周，点一下这一周拍得最多的那类。","end":"你最常注意的东西，就是你在乎的东西。","hostNm":"Bea","hostJob":"马尼拉短视频博主"},{"id":"next_8","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"手机替你记的账","en":"Screen Time, Honestly"},"hook":"你以为你一天看手机多久？","host":"lena","pic":"npc:lena/lab","days":14,"showDays":true,"what":"大多数人会把自己看手机的时间猜少。14 天里每晚先猜、再看手机记下的真数字；第二周做一个小实验。","daily":"每晚 1 分钟：先猜，再看「屏幕使用时间」，点一下用得最多的 app。","end":"两周的「猜的」和「真的」并排，你差了多少？","hostNm":"Lena","hostJob":"柏林·注意力心理学家"},{"id":"next_9","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"你是猫头鹰还是百灵鸟","en":"Owl or Lark?"},"hook":"你天生是早睡型还是晚睡型？","host":"jihoon","pic":"npc:jihoon/lab","days":14,"showDays":true,"what":"早睡型和晚睡型是天生的，有名字，叫 chronotype。两周里每天记几点睡、几点起、白天哪个时候最清醒。","daily":"早上 30 秒：几点睡、几点醒、今天精神怎么样。","end":"你的作息曲线，和全世界、和你的家人比一比。","hostNm":"Park Ji-hoon","hostJob":"首尔·睡眠科学家"},{"id":"next_10","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"此刻窗外","en":"Out My Window"},"hook":"同一扇窗，看一个月","host":"ingrid","pic":"npc:ingrid/window","days":30,"showDays":false,"what":"每天同一个时间，拍一张窗外。光线变了、天黑得越来越早、雨来了又走。","daily":"每天 10 秒：同一扇窗拍一张，点一下今天的天气。","end":"30 格连起来，就是季节走过你的窗。","hostNm":"Ingrid","hostJob":"特罗姆瑟·气象员"},{"id":"next_11","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"你的衣柜去过几个国家","en":"Where Your Clothes Have Been"},"hook":"你身上那件，经过了谁的手？","host":"rina","pic":"npc:rina/label","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"翻开衣服里的小标签。Rina 每天在达卡检查上千件出口的衣服，她告诉你一件 T 恤怎么走到你的衣柜。","daily":"每天翻 3 件，记国家。","end":"一张你的衣柜世界地图。","hostNm":"Rina","hostJob":"达卡·服装质检工程师"},{"id":"next_12","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"你的晚饭坐过飞机吗","en":"Food Miles"},"hook":"一顿饭走了多少公里？","host":"bram","pic":"npc:bram/port","days":7,"showDays":false,"what":"看贴纸、看袋子，每样东西都写着一个国家。Bram 在鹿特丹港看着一船船香蕉靠岸。","daily":"每天记下晚饭里走得最远的一样。","end":"你一周的晚饭加起来走了多远。","hostNm":"Bram","hostJob":"鹿特丹·港口冷链经理"},{"id":"next_13","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"垃圾桶出卖了你","en":"What Your Bin Says"},"hook":"你扔掉最多的是什么？","host":"yuki","pic":"npc:yuki/sort","days":7,"showDays":false,"what":"Yuki 的小镇把垃圾分成几十类，几乎不扔东西。","daily":"每晚看一眼垃圾桶，点一下最多的是哪类。","end":"你的一周垃圾账，和她的小镇比一比。","hostNm":"Yuki","hostJob":"零垃圾小镇·回收中心"},{"id":"next_14","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"种一颗豆子","en":"Grow a Bean"},"hook":"30 天，看它长","host":"theo","pic":"npc:theo/beans","days":30,"showDays":false,"what":"一颗豆子、一个杯子、一点水。Theo 每年春天带小学生种。","daily":"每天拍它一张。","end":"30 张连起来：它怎么朝着光转，你有多少耐心。","hostNm":"Theo","hostJob":"伦敦·植物园园丁"},{"id":"next_15","soil":"pro","t":{"zh":"收集小开心","en":"Jar of Small Joys"},"hook":"让你开心的事，比你想的小","host":"sara","pic":"npc:sara/jar","days":21,"showDays":false,"what":"我们很容易记住坏事，好事一下就忘了。每天抓住一个小开心，写一句放进罐子。","daily":"每天 1 分钟：写一句今天的小开心，点一下它来自哪里。","end":"21 天后打开罐子：你的开心最多来自哪里？","hostNm":"Sara","hostJob":"多伦多心理咨询师"},{"id":"next_16","soil":"culture","t":{"zh":"你家的东西走了多远","en":"Things That Travelled"},"hook":"茶、咖啡、瓷碗，是从哪条路来的？","host":"farah","pic":"npc:farah/museum","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"郁金香、咖啡、瓷器都在伊斯坦布尔转过手。","daily":"每天找家里一样东西，查它最早从哪来。","end":"一张你家东西的旅行地图。","hostNm":"Farah","hostJob":"伊斯坦布尔博物馆讲解员"},{"id":"next_17","soil":"days","t":{"zh":"天黑接力","en":"Darkness Relay"},"hook":"冬至前，黑夜怎么绕着地球走","host":"ingrid","pic":"npc:ingrid/station","days":28,"showDays":false,"what":"冬至前四周，每天记下你那里几点天黑，跟全世界接力。","daily":"天黑时拍一张、记时间。","end":"你的冬天有多长，Ingrid 那里太阳干脆不升起。","hostNm":"Ingrid","hostJob":"特罗姆瑟·气象员"},{"id":"next_18","soil":"days","t":{"zh":"年夜饭桌","en":"New Year's Table"},"hook":"你家年夜饭桌上一定有的那道","host":"suqing","pic":{"emoji":"🧧","bg":"#f6dcd2"},"days":3,"showDays":false,"what":"春节前后，全世界的人拍自己家团圆饭桌上一定有的那道菜。","daily":"拍、说它为什么一定要有。","end":"一桌全世界的年夜饭。","hostNm":"苏晴","hostJob":"在北京教外国人中文"},{"id":"next_19","soil":"days","t":{"zh":"开学第一周","en":"First Week Back"},"hook":"这学期你最想学会的一件事","host":"jade","pic":"npc:jade/park","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"开学这周，定一件这学期想学会的小事，每天做一点。","daily":"每天记一句今天做了什么。","end":"第五天：说给全世界，学期末再来看。","hostNm":"Jade","hostJob":"墨尔本跑步教练"},{"id":"next_20","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"这周全世界在吵什么","en":"The World Is Arguing"},"hook":"一件事，每个国家的人怎么看","host":"oliver","pic":"npc:oliver/tube","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"一个正在发生、有出处的热议话题。每天看一个国家的人怎么说。","daily":"读一个国家的看法，选你同不同意。","end":"最后一天你站一边，用英语说为什么。","hostNm":"Oliver","hostJob":"伦敦财经记者"},{"id":"next_21","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"一个梗的旅行","en":"A Meme's Journey"},"hook":"这个梗是从哪来的？","host":"bea","pic":"npc:bea/filming","days":3,"showDays":false,"what":"这周火的一个梗，从哪个国家、哪个平台出来，到了别的语言里变成什么样。","daily":"看它的一站，猜下一站。","end":"你会怎么用它。","hostNm":"Bea","hostJob":"马尼拉短视频博主"},{"id":"next_22","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"跟着火的挑战做","en":"Try the Trend"},"hook":"这周大家都在做的那件小事","host":"zoe","pic":"npc:zoe/filming","days":3,"showDays":false,"what":"一个正在流行、安全的小挑战。","daily":"你做一遍，看全世界的版本。","end":"你的版本，送给世界。","hostNm":"Zoe","hostJob":"墨尔本大学生博主"},{"id":"next_23","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"今年的新词","en":"New Words"},"hook":"最近冒出来的说法，你会用吗？","host":"carmen","pic":"npc:carmen/work","days":5,"showDays":false,"what":"每天一个最近冒出来的英语新说法：什么意思、谁在用、从哪来。","daily":"听、猜意思、看真实的例子。","end":"你会用哪一个，用在哪。","hostNm":"Carmen","hostJob":"布宜诺斯艾利斯文化记者"},{"id":"next_24","soil":"hot","t":{"zh":"吵架周","en":"Pick a Side Week"},"hook":"两边都有道理的事，你站哪边？","host":"eleni","pic":"npc:eleni/class","days":7,"showDays":true,"what":"一个两边都有道理的热议题。每天听一方的一个理由。","daily":"听、给这个理由打分。","end":"你站哪边，这周改没改主意。","hostNm":"Eleni","hostJob":"雅典哲学老师"}];
window.ACTS_ZH = {"_by":"isle.xiaoyu","aiko_shimokita":{"0":{"line":"我先去[淘] ___，再去吃 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"淘","mean":"táo · hunt for good finds (second-hand, cheap)","tip":"淘 is what people say for digging through vintage shops or markets: 淘古着, 淘唱片. 先…再… = first…then.","learner":["我会先去挖唱片。","挖 is digging in the ground — for shopping, say 淘."],"natural":["先去淘点二手唱片，再去吃咖喱。","How you'd plan the day with a friend."],"quiz":{"q":["你在古着店，想找点便宜的好东西。","You're in a vintage shop, looking for cheap good stuff."],"o":[["我想淘几件古着。",1],["我想卖掉几件旧衣服。",0],["我想买几件新衣服。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 淘 + 几件 + the thing.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 我想淘几件古着。"}}}},"amara_jetlag":{"0":{"line":"我要[撑到]当地时间十点再睡。","lang":{"chunk":"撑到","mean":"chēng dào · hold on until","tip":"撑 = keep going when you're tired. 撑到…再睡 = hold on until… and only then sleep.","learner":["我要熬夜到十点。","熬夜 means staying up very late — 10 p.m. isn't late."],"natural":["我得撑到晚上十点再睡。","Tired, but holding on."],"quiz":{"q":["你很困，但想坚持到九点。","You're very sleepy, but want to last till nine."],"o":[["我要撑到九点再睡。",1],["这附近晚饭吃什么好？",0],["我一到家就洗澡。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 撑到 + time + 再睡.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我要撑到九点再睡。"}}},"1":{"line":"这附近早饭[吃什么好]？","lang":{"chunk":"吃什么好","mean":"chī shénme hǎo · what's good to eat","tip":"…吃什么好？ is how you ask a local for a tip. 这附近 = around here.","learner":["这里什么是好的早饭？","Understood! Putting 这附近 first makes it quicker to follow."],"natural":["这附近早饭吃什么好？","Easy question for a stranger or a hotel desk."],"quiz":{"q":["你想问当地人晚饭去哪吃。","You want a local's tip for dinner."],"o":[["这附近晚饭吃什么好？",1],["我要撑到九点再睡。",0],["我一到家就洗澡。",0]],"ok":"Yes — place, meal, then 吃什么好.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这附近晚饭吃什么好？"}}},"2":{"line":"我一落地，[第一件事]就是 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"第一件事","mean":"dì yī jiàn shì · the first thing","tip":"一…就… = as soon as… then. 第一件事就是 + what you do. 件 is the measure word for 事.","learner":["当我落地，第一个事情我做是洗澡。","Hard to follow — the listener waits too long for the verb. 一…就… gets it across fast."],"natural":["我一落地，第一件事就是洗澡。","一…就…, short and spoken."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：你回到家第一件事做什么？你会先洗澡。","A friend asks what you do first when you get home. You shower."],"o":[["我一到家就洗澡。",1],["这附近晚饭吃什么好？",0],["我要撑到九点再睡。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 一 + action, 就 + next action.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我一到家就洗澡。"}}}},"arun_know":{"0":{"line":"我们是[怎么知道]的？","lang":{"chunk":"怎么知道","mean":"zěnme zhīdào · how do (we) know","tip":"是…的 asks how something happened: 你是怎么知道的？ A friendly, curious question.","learner":["我们如何知道那个？","Understood! 如何 is more for writing — 怎么 sounds more like chatting."],"natural":["这是怎么知道的？","Curious, like a kid asking."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说：阳光八分钟才到地球。","Your friend says: sunlight takes eight minutes to reach Earth."],"o":[["你是怎么知道的？",1],["问得好！",0],["大概要二十分钟。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 怎么 goes before 知道.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 你是怎么知道的？"}}},"1":{"line":"这个问题[问得真好]。","lang":{"chunk":"问得真好","mean":"wèn de zhēn hǎo · really well asked","tip":"Verb + 得 + 好 praises how someone did it: 问得好, 说得好. Short and warm.","learner":["这是一个很好的问题。","Understood, and polite! People also just say 问得好."],"natural":["问得好！","Quick, and it shows you liked the question."],"quiz":{"q":["一个小朋友问你：天为什么是蓝的？","A child asks you: why is the sky blue?"],"o":[["问得好！",1],["你是怎么知道的？",0],["大概要二十分钟。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 问 + 得 + 好.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 问得好！"}}},"2":{"line":"[大概]要八分钟。","lang":{"chunk":"大概","mean":"dàgài · about, roughly","tip":"要 + time = it takes… 大概 goes in front when you're not exact.","learner":["它拿八分钟。","拿 is 'take' with your hands — for time, say 要."],"natural":["大概要八分钟。","Simple and spoken."],"quiz":{"q":["从你家到学校，差不多二十分钟。","From your home to school is around twenty minutes."],"o":[["大概要二十分钟。",1],["你是怎么知道的？",0],["问得好！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 大概 + 要 + time.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 大概要二十分钟。"}}},"3":{"line":"我说得[不一定对]，不过我觉得挺远的。","lang":{"chunk":"不一定对","mean":"bù yídìng duì · not necessarily right","tip":"A soft way to guess out loud. 挺 + adjective = quite: 挺远, 挺难.","learner":["我可能是错的，但是……","我是错的 can sound like 'I am a wrong person'. 我说得不一定对 is clearer."],"natural":["我说得不一定对啊，不过……","Friendly, you're just guessing."],"quiz":{"q":["你不太确定，猜雷暴大概三公里远。","You're not sure, but guess the storm is about three km away."],"o":[["我说得不一定对，大概三公里吧。",1],["你是怎么知道的？",0],["问得好！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 不一定 goes before 对.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我说得不一定对，大概三公里吧。"}}},"4":{"line":"我[以前以为] ___，现在才知道 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"以前以为","mean":"yǐqián yǐwéi · used to (wrongly) think","tip":"以为 = thought, but it was wrong. 想 or 觉得 don't say 'wrong'. 才知道 = only now know.","learner":["我以前想月亮会自己发光。","想 doesn't say you were wrong — 以为 does."],"natural":["我以前以为月亮自己会发光，现在才知道是反射太阳光。","Old idea, new idea."],"quiz":{"q":["你以前觉得蓝鲸是鱼，其实不是。","You used to think blue whales were fish. They're not."],"o":[["我以前以为蓝鲸是鱼。",1],["问得好！",0],["你是怎么知道的？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 以前以为 + what you thought.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我以前以为蓝鲸是鱼。"}}}},"eleni_lines":{"0":{"line":"这[不是我能决定的]。","lang":{"chunk":"不是我能决定的","mean":"bú shì wǒ néng juédìng de · not mine to decide","tip":"The everyday way to say 'not up to me'. Calm, not angry.","learner":["这不取决我。","取决 needs 于 (取决于), and it's formal for chat."],"natural":["这不是我能决定的。","How you say it to a friend."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：明天会下雨吗？","Your friend asks: will it rain tomorrow?"],"o":[["下不下雨，不是我能决定的。",1],["你说的「大家」是指谁？",0],["这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 不是 + 我能决定 + 的.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 下不下雨，不是我能决定的。"}}},"1":{"line":"你说的「正常」[是指]什么？","lang":{"chunk":"是指","mean":"shì zhǐ · do you mean","tip":"你说的… 是指什么？ = what do you mean by…? Polite, and makes people think.","learner":["你意思「正常」是什么？","意思 is a noun — it can't work like the verb 'mean'."],"natural":["你说的「正常」是指什么？","Asking, not attacking."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说：大家都这样。","Your friend says: everyone does that."],"o":[["你说的「大家」是指谁？",1],["这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。",0],["我不太确定，可能九点。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 你说的… 是指谁/什么.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 你说的「大家」是指谁？"}}},"2":{"line":"早就[不一样了]。","lang":{"chunk":"不一样了","mean":"bù yíyàng le · not the same anymore","tip":"了 at the end = something changed. 早就 = long ago already.","learner":["它不是相同的了。","People may pause on 它 and 相同 here. 不一样了 is easier to follow."],"natural":["早就不一样了。","A little sad, and easy to follow."],"quiz":{"q":["你回到小时候住的地方。","You go back to where you lived as a child."],"o":[["这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。",1],["你说的「大家」是指谁？",0],["可能没你想的那么难。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 跟以前 + 不一样了.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。"}}},"3":{"line":"其实我也[不太确定]。","lang":{"chunk":"不太确定","mean":"bú tài quèdìng · not really sure","tip":"不太 + adjective softens it. 其实 = actually, to be honest.","learner":["我不是确定。","Don't use 是 before 确定 — just 不确定 or 不太确定."],"natural":["其实我也说不准。","说不准 = can't say for sure."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：那家店几点开门？","Your friend asks: what time does that shop open?"],"o":[["我不太确定，可能九点。",1],["你说的「大家」是指谁？",0],["这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 不太确定 = not quite sure.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我不太确定，可能九点。"}}},"4":{"line":"我们[边喝咖啡边聊]吧。","lang":{"chunk":"边喝咖啡边聊","mean":"biān hē kāfēi biān liáo · chat over a coffee","tip":"边…边… = do two things at once. 边喝边聊 is what friends say.","learner":["我们和咖啡说话吧。","和咖啡 means 'with the coffee' as a person — you'd be talking to your cup!"],"natural":["找个地方坐坐，边喝边聊。","Inviting someone to keep talking."],"quiz":{"q":["你想和朋友一边走一边聊。","You want to walk and chat with a friend."],"o":[["我们边走边聊吧。",1],["你说的「大家」是指谁？",0],["这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 边 + action, 边 + action.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我们边走边聊吧。"}}},"5":{"line":"可能[没我想的那么]糟。","lang":{"chunk":"没我想的那么","mean":"méi wǒ xiǎng de nàme · not as … as I think","tip":"没 + someone + 想的那么 + adjective = it's not as bad as they imagine.","learner":["可能不是像我想一样坏。","Understood! 没那么糟 is quicker to follow — and 坏 is more for people or broken things."],"natural":["说不定没那么糟。","What you tell yourself, or a friend."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友明天考试，很紧张。","Your friend has an exam tomorrow and is nervous."],"o":[["可能没你想的那么难。",1],["这儿变了，跟以前不一样了。",0],["周末去哪儿，我说了算。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 没 + 你想的 + 那么 + 难.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 可能没你想的那么难。"}}},"6":{"line":"___ [我说了算]，___ 我说了不算。","lang":{"chunk":"我说了算","mean":"wǒ shuō le suàn · it's my call","tip":"说了算 = what I say goes. 说了不算 = I don't get to decide.","learner":["几点睡觉是由我的。","由 needs a verb after it (由我决定); 是由我的 sounds broken."],"natural":["几点睡觉我说了算，天气我说了不算。","Everyday, a little playful."],"quiz":{"q":["周末去哪儿，你来决定。","You get to choose where to go this weekend."],"o":[["周末去哪儿，我说了算。",1],["你说的「大家」是指谁？",0],["可能没你想的那么难。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 我 + 说了算.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 周末去哪儿，我说了算。"}}}},"farah_five":{"0":{"line":"这是[从哪儿来的]？","lang":{"chunk":"从哪儿来的","mean":"cóng nǎr lái de · where … come from","tip":"从 + place + 来: the place goes before 来. 哪儿 is spoken; 哪里 also works.","learner":["这个来从哪里？","In Chinese, 从 + place comes before 来."],"natural":["这是从哪儿来的？","Curious, about food, words, anything."],"quiz":{"q":["你在市场看到一种没见过的水果。","At the market you see a fruit you've never seen."],"o":[["这是从哪儿来的？",1],["「谢谢」日语怎么说？",0],["这顿我请。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 从哪儿 before 来.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这是从哪儿来的？"}}},"1":{"line":"这个你们这儿[叫什么]？","lang":{"chunk":"叫什么","mean":"jiào shénme · what is it called","tip":"叫 already means 'is called' — no 是 needed. 你们这儿 = here, where you live.","learner":["你们叫它是什么？","Drop 是: 叫 is enough."],"natural":["这个你们这儿叫什么？","Asking a local, pointing at it."],"quiz":{"q":["你指着一个盘子，想知道它的名字。","You point at a plate and want its name."],"o":[["这个叫什么？",1],["土豆是从美洲传过来的。",0],["这顿我请。",0]],"ok":"Yes — thing + 叫什么.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这个叫什么？"}}},"2":{"line":"这杯[我请]。","lang":{"chunk":"我请","mean":"wǒ qǐng · it's on me","tip":"请 = treat someone. 这杯/这顿 + 我请. People often fight to pay: 我来我来！","learner":["让我付这一杯。","Understood! People also say 这杯我请."],"natural":["这杯我请！","Quick, before they pay."],"quiz":{"q":["吃完饭，你想付钱。","After dinner, you want to pay."],"o":[["这顿我请。",1],["「谢谢」日语怎么说？",0],["土豆是从美洲传过来的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 这顿 + 我请.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这顿我请。"}}},"3":{"line":"你们那儿「茶」[怎么说]？","lang":{"chunk":"怎么说","mean":"zěnme shuō · how do you say","tip":"Word + 怎么说 = how do you say it. With a language: 「茶」日语怎么说？","learner":["茶在你的语言怎么说？","Add 里 after 语言 and it's clear. Even easier: just name the language."],"natural":["「茶」用你们的话怎么说？","Friendly, curious."],"quiz":{"q":["你想问日本朋友「谢谢」怎么说。","You ask a Japanese friend how to say 'thank you'."],"o":[["「谢谢」日语怎么说？",1],["这顿我请。",0],["土豆是从美洲传过来的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — word, language, 怎么说.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 「谢谢」日语怎么说？"}}},"4":{"line":"___ 是从 ___ [传到]我们这儿的。","lang":{"chunk":"传到","mean":"chuán dào · spread to, came to","tip":"传到 = passed along until it reached a place. 是从…传到…的 tells the story of where it came from.","learner":["辣椒来到我们从美洲。","从 + place goes before the verb."],"natural":["辣椒是从美洲传到中国的。","How you'd tell the story."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：土豆最早是哪儿的？","A friend asks where potatoes first came from."],"o":[["土豆是从美洲传过来的。",1],["这个叫什么？",0],["「谢谢」日语怎么说？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 是从 + place + 传过来的.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 土豆是从美洲传过来的。"}}}},"hana_mealplan":{"0":{"line":"这周我[打算做] ___、___ 和 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"打算做","mean":"dǎsuan zuò · plan to make","tip":"打算 = plan to. 做 = cook, make (做饭, 做咖喱).","learner":["这周我在做咖喱。","在做 means you're cooking right now — for a plan, say 打算."],"natural":["这周我打算做番茄炒蛋、咖喱和炒饭。","Your plan for the week, out loud."],"quiz":{"q":["说你周末的计划：去爬山。","Say your weekend plan: go hiking."],"o":[["周末我打算去爬山。",1],["上周末我去爬山了。",0],["周末我不想出门。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 打算 + what you'll do.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 周末我打算去爬山。"}}}},"isabel_minute":{"0":{"line":"我[注意到]的是光。","lang":{"chunk":"注意到","mean":"zhùyì dào · notice","tip":"我注意到的是… = 'what I notice is…'. Swap 光 for anything: 手, 狗, 颜色.","learner":["我看见光。","Fine — but 注意到 says you looked closely."],"natural":["我注意到的是光。","Points at one thing you noticed."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：这幅画你先注意到什么？你先看到的是手。","A friend asks what you noticed first in the painting. It was the hands."],"o":[["我注意到的是手。",1],["这幅画让我想起小时候。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 注意到 stays together.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我注意到的是手。"}}},"1":{"line":"光是[从左边]照过来的。","lang":{"chunk":"从左边","mean":"cóng zuǒbian · from the left","tip":"是…的 tells how something happened. 照过来 = shines over this way.","learner":["光来自左边。","Understood! 来自 is more for writing; 是从…照过来的 sounds like chatting at the painting."],"natural":["光是从左边照过来的。","How you'd say it standing at the painting."],"quiz":{"q":["光从窗户照进来。","The light comes in through the window."],"o":[["光是从窗户照进来的。",1],["这幅画让我想起小时候。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 从 + place + 照进来.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 光是从窗户照进来的。"}}},"2":{"line":"我[一开始]没看到。","lang":{"chunk":"一开始","mean":"yì kāishǐ · at first","tip":"一开始 = at first (then later something changed).","learner":["第一次我没看到。","第一次 means 'the first time ever'."],"natural":["我一开始没看到。","At first I didn't see it."],"quiz":{"q":["画的角落里有只猫，你刚才没看到。","There's a cat in the corner of the painting. You didn't see it at first."],"o":[["我一开始没注意。",1],["光是从窗户照进来的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 一开始 = at first.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我一开始没注意。"}}},"3":{"line":"它[让我想起]奶奶的厨房。","lang":{"chunk":"让我想起","mean":"ràng wǒ xiǎngqǐ · reminds me of","tip":"让我想起 + something = it makes me think of it.","learner":["它提醒我奶奶的厨房。","提醒 is 'remind someone to do something'."],"natural":["它让我想起奶奶的厨房。","A memory coming back."],"quiz":{"q":["这幅画让你想到小时候。","The painting makes you think of your childhood."],"o":[["这幅画让我想起小时候。",1],["光是从窗户照进来的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 让我想起 for a memory.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这幅画让我想起小时候。"}}},"4":{"line":"我注意到的是 ___。它[让我想起] ___。","lang":{"chunk":"让我想起","mean":"ràng wǒ xiǎngqǐ · reminds me of","tip":"Two short sentences are fine. Your own painting, your own memory.","learner":["我注意到的是狗，它提醒我我的狗。","提醒 is for to-dos."],"natural":["我注意到的是那条狗，它让我想起我家的狗。","条 is the measure word for dogs."],"quiz":{"q":["画里的狗跟你家的狗很像。","The dog in the painting looks like your dog."],"o":[["那条狗让我想起我家的狗。",1],["光是从窗户照进来的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 让我想起 + what you remember.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 那条狗让我想起我家的狗。"}}}},"jade_mornings":{"0":{"line":"胸挺起来，[往后坐]。","lang":{"chunk":"往后坐","mean":"wǎng hòu zuò · sit back","tip":"Coaches in China say 往后坐 for a squat — like sitting on a chair behind you. 往 + direction goes before the action.","learner":["向后坐下。","向后 is understood; in class you'll hear 往后. But 坐下 means sitting all the way down."],"natural":["屁股往后坐，像坐椅子一样。","What you hear in a class."],"quiz":{"q":["教练让你做深蹲。","The coach wants you to squat."],"o":[["屁股往后坐。",1],["加油，坚持住！",0],["杯子在桌子下面。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 往后 comes before 坐.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 屁股往后坐。"}}},"1":{"line":"[核心收紧]，别塌腰。","lang":{"chunk":"核心收紧","mean":"héxīn shōujǐn · brace your core","tip":"Chinese coaches say the body part first: 核心收紧, 肩膀放松. 别塌腰 = don't let your lower back drop.","learner":["收紧你的核心。","Understood! Drop 你的 and put the body part first — short, the way you'll hear it in class."],"natural":["核心收紧。","Body part, then the action — like a coach."],"quiz":{"q":["教练让你肩膀别用力。","The coach wants your shoulders relaxed."],"o":[["肩膀放松。",1],["加油，坚持住！",0],["杯子在桌子下面。",0]],"ok":"Yes — body part + 放松.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 肩膀放松。"}}},"2":{"line":"往后[退一步]，膝盖往下。","lang":{"chunk":"退一步","mean":"tuì yí bù · step back","tip":"退 = move backwards. You also say 往后退一步 to make room for someone.","learner":["往后面走一步。","走 sounds like walking forward. Going back is 退."],"natural":["往后退一步。","Short and clear."],"quiz":{"q":["叫朋友往前走一步。","Tell a friend to take one step forward."],"o":[["往前走一步。",1],["加油，坚持住！",0],["杯子在桌子下面。",0]],"ok":"Yes — forward is 走, back is 退.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 往前走一步。"}}},"3":{"line":"到最高点[夹紧]，停两秒。","lang":{"chunk":"夹紧","mean":"jiājǐn · squeeze","tip":"夹紧 = squeeze together (glutes, knees). 停两秒 = hold for two seconds.","learner":["在顶上挤。","挤 is for crowds or toothpaste, not muscles."],"natural":["到最高点夹紧，停两秒。","What you'll hear in a glute bridge."],"quiz":{"q":["教练让你停三秒。","The coach says: hold for three seconds."],"o":[["停三秒。",1],["加油，坚持住！",0],["杯子在桌子下面。",0]],"ok":"Yes — no 个 with 秒.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 停三秒。"}}},"4":{"line":"手放在[肩膀正下方]。","lang":{"chunk":"肩膀正下方","mean":"jiānbǎng zhèng xiàfāng · right under your shoulders","tip":"正 = exactly. In Chinese the place comes first, then 下面 / 下方: 肩膀下面, 桌子下面.","learner":["手放在下面你的肩膀。","Hard to follow — put the place first: 肩膀下面."],"natural":["手放在肩膀正下方。","正 makes it 'right under'."],"quiz":{"q":["你的水杯在桌子下面。","Your cup is under the table."],"o":[["杯子在桌子下面。",1],["加油，坚持住！",0],["我这周跑了两天。",0]],"ok":"Yes — thing first, then 下面.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 杯子在桌子下面。"}}},"5":{"line":"还有两个，[你可以的]！","lang":{"chunk":"你可以的","mean":"nǐ kěyǐ de · you've got this","tip":"你可以的 = you can do it. Coaches also shout 加油 and 坚持住 (hang in there).","learner":["你有这个！","People won't get this one — 'you've got this' doesn't carry over. Try 你可以的."],"natural":["你可以的！再坚持一下！","Cheering someone on."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友跑到最后一百米了。","Your friend is on the last 100 metres."],"o":[["加油，坚持住！",1],["屁股往后坐。",0],["肩膀放松。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 加油 and 坚持住 are what you'll hear shouted.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 加油，坚持住！"}}},"6":{"line":"这周七天我[练了] ___ 天，明天我要 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"练了","mean":"liàn le · worked out","tip":"练 = train, work out. 练了三天 = worked out on three days. The number + 天 comes after the verb.","learner":["我做了三天的七天。","'Three out of seven' doesn't carry over. Say 七天练了三天."],"natural":["这周七天我练了三天。","Just the two numbers."],"quiz":{"q":["你这周跑了两天。","You ran on two days this week."],"o":[["我这周跑了两天。",1],["加油，坚持住！",0],["杯子在桌子下面。",0]],"ok":"Yes — time first, then 跑了两天.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我这周跑了两天。"}}}},"jordi_map":{"0":{"line":"离这儿[多远]？","lang":{"chunk":"多远","mean":"duō yuǎn · how far","tip":"For distance Chinese uses 离: A 离 B 多远？ 地铁站离这儿多远？","learner":["从这里多远？","Something is missing. Use 离: 离这儿多远？"],"natural":["离这儿多远？走路能到吗？","What you ask on the street."],"quiz":{"q":["你想知道车站有多远。","You want to know how far the station is."],"o":[["车站离这儿多远？",1],["回来一路都是下坡。",0],["在马路对面。",0]],"ok":"Yes — A 离 B 多远.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 车站离这儿多远？"}}},"1":{"line":"一路都是[上坡]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"上坡","mean":"shàngpō · uphill","tip":"上坡 uphill, 下坡 downhill, 平路 flat. 一路 = all the way.","learner":["一路都上山吗？","上山 is going up a mountain. A road going up is 上坡."],"natural":["一路都是上坡吗？","Before a walk or a bike ride."],"quiz":{"q":["回来的路一直往下走。","The way back goes down all the way."],"o":[["回来一路都是下坡。",1],["车站离这儿多远？",0],["非洲比格陵兰大多了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — going down is 下坡.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 回来一路都是下坡。"}}},"2":{"line":"其实它[比看上去]大多了。","lang":{"chunk":"比看上去","mean":"bǐ kàn shàngqu · than it looks","tip":"A 比 B 大多了 = A is much bigger than B. 其实 = actually — you're correcting what people think.","learner":["它比看上去很大。","很 can't go in a 比 sentence. Use 大多了 or 大得多."],"natural":["其实它比看上去大多了。","Surprising someone with a fact."],"quiz":{"q":["非洲和格陵兰，哪个大？","Africa or Greenland — which is bigger?"],"o":[["非洲比格陵兰大多了。",1],["回来一路都是下坡。",0],["车站离这儿多远？",0]],"ok":"Yes — A 比 B 大多了.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 非洲比格陵兰大多了。"}}},"3":{"line":"是在[河这边]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"河这边","mean":"hé zhèbiān · this side of the river","tip":"这边 / 那边 = this side / that side. The place comes first: 河这边, 马路对面.","learner":["在这边的河吗？","The word order makes it sound like 'at this river'."],"natural":["在河这边还是那边？","Asking someone who's giving you directions."],"quiz":{"q":["那家店在马路另一边。","The shop is across the road."],"o":[["在马路对面。",1],["车站离这儿多远？",0],["非洲比格陵兰大多了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — place first: 马路对面.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 在马路对面。"}}},"4":{"line":"从我家到 ___ [大概]要 ___ 分钟。","lang":{"chunk":"大概","mean":"dàgài · about, roughly","tip":"大概 = about, roughly. It goes before 要: 大概要十分钟. 走路 or 坐地铁 can go in front: 走路大概要十分钟.","learner":["从我家到车站要关于十分钟。","关于 means 'about a topic', not 'roughly'."],"natural":["从我家到车站，走路大概要十分钟。","Telling a friend how far you live."],"quiz":{"q":["学校走路二十分钟左右。","School is around 20 minutes' walk."],"o":[["走路大概要二十分钟。",1],["车站离这儿多远？",0],["非洲比格陵兰大多了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 大概要 + time.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 走路大概要二十分钟。"}}}},"linhao_qunliao":{"0":{"line":"这家火锅[绝了]！","lang":{"chunk":"绝了","mean":"jué le · amazing / unbelievable","tip":"Usually praise: 这家店绝了! With a sigh it can mean ‘unbelievable’ in a bad way. Listen to the tone.","learner":["这家火锅很绝。","Understood! 绝了 is the set phrase — say it and it lands as big praise."],"natural":["这家火锅绝了！","Big praise among friends."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说：这部电影绝了！意思是：","A friend says 这部电影绝了! It means:"],"o":[["太好看了",1],["电影没了",0],["电影很长",0]],"ok":"Yes — 绝了 = nothing beats it.","no":"Here 绝了 is praise: it was amazing."}}},"1":{"line":"看完这个视频我[破防了]。","lang":{"chunk":"破防了","mean":"pò fáng le · it hit me hard (sad or moved)","tip":"From games: your defence breaks. Now: something touched you or hurt you. A word of the year in 2021.","learner":["我的防破了。","Just say 我破防了 — it's one fixed phrase."],"natural":["看完我破防了。","Moved, maybe a few tears."],"quiz":{"q":["看到一个很感人的视频，你说：","You watch a very touching video:"],"o":[["我破防了。",1],["我躺平了。",0],["这家火锅绝了！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 破防了.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 我破防了。"}}},"2":{"line":"这周末我[躺平]了。","lang":{"chunk":"躺平","mean":"tǎng píng · lie flat, do nothing on purpose","tip":"For a weekend: just resting. For life: not chasing money or promotions. A word of the year in 2021.","learner":["这周末我平躺了。","平躺 is just how your body lies. 躺平 is the attitude."],"natural":["这周末我躺平了。","A Friday-night group-chat classic."],"quiz":{"q":["「躺平」最接近：","躺平 is closest to:"],"o":[["什么都不想拼",1],["去医院看病",0],["去健身房",0]],"ok":"Yes — not pushing yourself.","no":"躺平 = choosing not to push yourself."}}},"3":{"line":"又要加班，[栓Q]。","lang":{"chunk":"栓Q","mean":"shuān Q · ‘thanks a lot’ (not happy)","tip":"It's ‘thank you’ in a funny accent, but it means you're annoyed. Only online and with friends.","learner":["老板，栓Q！","Your boss won't hear a thank-you. Say 谢谢."],"natural":["又下雨，栓Q。","A joke among friends."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说「又堵车，栓Q」，他心情：","A friend says 又堵车，栓Q. His mood:"],"o":[["不开心",1],["很感谢",0],["很兴奋",0]],"ok":"Yes — it's a sarcastic thank-you.","no":"栓Q here means he's annoyed."}}},"4":{"line":"___，[拿捏了]。","lang":{"chunk":"拿捏了","mean":"ná niē le · nailed it, got it under control","tip":"The thing you did + 拿捏了. Proud, but playful. A word of the year in 2022.","learner":["我拿捏了点奶茶。","Put the thing first: 点奶茶，拿捏了."],"natural":["用中文点奶茶，拿捏了。","Short and proud."],"quiz":{"q":["你第一次用筷子成功了，你发：","You managed chopsticks for the first time. You post:"],"o":[["用筷子，拿捏了。",1],["我破防了。",0],["又堵车，栓Q。",0]],"ok":"Yes — the thing first, then 拿捏了.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 用筷子，拿捏了。"}}}},"linhao_qunliao2":{"0":{"line":"[收到]，谢谢！","lang":{"chunk":"收到","mean":"shōudào · got it (I've seen this)","tip":"Reply 收到 to any notice in a group. 收到 + 谢谢 sounds friendly; in work groups some people just send 👌.","learner":["我明白了，谢谢您的信息。","Polite and clear! In a group chat, a quick 收到 does the same job."],"natural":["收到，谢谢！","What everyone in the group is typing."],"quiz":{"q":["班长在群里发了明天交作业的通知，你回：","The class rep posts tomorrow's homework deadline. You reply:"],"o":[["收到，谢谢！",1],["哈哈哈哈！",0],["有没有人明天去图书馆？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 收到 for any notice.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 收到，谢谢！"}}},"1":{"line":"周五聚餐，要去的[接龙]。","lang":{"chunk":"接龙","mean":"jiēlóng · relay list (copy it, add your name)","tip":"Copy the whole list, add your number and name at the bottom, send it back. Don't start a new list.","learner":["我想去，请加我的名字。","People will get it, but in a 接龙 you add yourself: copy, add, send."],"natural":["1. 林浩 2. Camille","Just copy, add your name, send."],"quiz":{"q":["群里有人发了聚餐接龙，你也想去：","Someone posts a dinner 接龙 and you want to go:"],"o":[["复制接龙，加上自己的名字再发出去",1],["回一个「呵呵」",0],["把群设成免打扰",0]],"ok":"Yes — copy, add your name, send.","no":"In a 接龙 you add yourself to the list."}}},"2":{"line":"[@所有人] 明天的会改到下午三点了。","lang":{"chunk":"@所有人","mean":"@ suǒyǒu rén · @everyone","tip":"所有人 = everyone. A message with @所有人 makes every phone in the group buzz — so it's usually important. 改到 = moved to.","learner":["明天的会改变到下午三点了。","改变 is a big change (改变生活). Moving a time: 改到."],"natural":["@所有人 明天的会改到下午三点了。","Short, clear, nobody misses it."],"quiz":{"q":["群里有一条 @所有人 的消息，你应该：","There's an @所有人 message in the group. You should:"],"o":[["马上点开看",1],["不看，先睡觉",0],["回一个「呵呵」",0]],"ok":"Yes — @所有人 means read it now.","no":"@所有人 is usually important. Read it."}}},"3":{"line":"太好笑了[哈哈哈哈]！","lang":{"chunk":"哈哈哈哈","mean":"hāhāhāhā · hahaha","tip":"More 哈 = funnier. 呵呵 (hēhē) and the 🙂 face often read as cold or fake in Chinese chats. 笑死 = I'm dying (of laughter).","learner":["呵呵，太好笑了。","呵呵 can sound cold, even sarcastic. For something really funny: 哈哈哈."],"natural":["太好笑了哈哈哈哈！","Real laughing."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友在群里发了个特别好笑的视频，你回：","A friend posts a really funny video. You reply:"],"o":[["哈哈哈哈笑死！",1],["呵呵。",0],["收到。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 哈哈哈 for real laughing.","no":"呵呵 sounds cold and 收到 is for notices. Try 哈哈哈."}}},"4":{"line":"[有没有人]___？","lang":{"chunk":"有没有人","mean":"yǒu méi yǒu rén · does anyone…?","tip":"有没有人 + 知道 / 有 / 想 / 去… The easiest way to ask a whole group.","learner":["谁可以给我笔记吗？","Mixes two patterns. Say 有没有人有笔记？ or 谁有笔记？"],"natural":["有没有人有周一的笔记？","Short — someone always answers."],"quiz":{"q":["想问群里谁明天去图书馆：","Ask the group who's going to the library tomorrow:"],"o":[["有没有人明天去图书馆？",1],["收到，谢谢！",0],["哈哈哈哈！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 有没有人 + what you want to know.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 有没有人明天去图书馆？"}}}},"linhao_tip":{"0":{"line":"我[觉得]___。","lang":{"chunk":"觉得","mean":"juéde · think, feel (about an opinion)","tip":"我觉得 + your view is the softest way to take a side. 我认为 sounds more formal, like in an essay.","learner":["我认为要看在哪儿。","Fine, people get it! 觉得 is lighter for a chat."],"natural":["我觉得要看在哪儿。","Light, for chatting over dinner."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：在纽约吃完饭，要给小费吗？你想说说你的看法。","A friend asks: in New York, do you tip after dinner? You want to give your view."],"o":[["我觉得应该给。",1],["服务员，买单！",0],["这家店离这儿远吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 我觉得 + your view.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我觉得应该给。"}}},"1":{"line":"[主要是因为]___。","lang":{"chunk":"主要是因为","mean":"zhǔyào shì yīnwèi · mainly because","tip":"Give one main reason, not a list. 主要 tells people this is the big one.","learner":["因为……因为……还有因为……","Three 因为 in a row sounds like an excuse."],"natural":["主要是因为服务员的工资本来就不高。","One reason, said clearly."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：你为什么觉得在纽约要给小费？","A friend asks why you think people should tip in New York."],"o":[["主要是因为服务员的工资本来就不高。",1],["我觉得不用给。",0],["服务员，买单！",0]],"ok":"Right — 主要是因为 + reason.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 主要是因为服务员的工资本来就不高。"}}},"2":{"line":"[话是这么说，但]___。","lang":{"chunk":"话是这么说，但","mean":"huà shì zhème shuō, dàn · that's true, but","tip":"Admit a point first, then turn. It makes you sound fair, not stubborn. Also: 没错，不过……","learner":["你说得不对。","Too direct — people feel attacked."],"natural":["话是这么说，但服务好我还是想给一点。","You agree a little, then hold your view."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说：「法国的服务费已经算在价格里了。」你同意，但服务好的话还是想多给一点：","A friend says: 'In France, service is already in the price.' You agree, but if the service is good you still want to leave a bit extra:"],"o":[["话是这么说，但服务好我还是想多给一点。",1],["主要是因为账单上已经有服务费了。",0],["服务员，买单！",0]],"ok":"Yes — the turn needs 但.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 话是这么说，但服务好我还是想多给一点。"}}},"3":{"line":"[就拿]___[来说]，___。","lang":{"chunk":"就拿……来说","mean":"jiù ná … lái shuō · take … for example","tip":"Wrap your example: 就拿 + thing + 来说, then what happens. One real example beats three reasons.","learner":["比如说美国，比如说日本，比如说……","A list of 比如 — no example actually lands."],"natural":["就拿日本来说，一般不用给小费。","One example, then what happens."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友不信有的地方不用给小费。你拿日本举个例子：","A friend doesn't believe some places don't expect tips. You use Japan as your example:"],"o":[["就拿日本来说，一般不用给小费。",1],["就拿美国来说，一般要给百分之十五到二十。",0],["我觉得应该给。",0]],"ok":"Right — 就拿……来说.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 就拿日本来说，一般不用给小费。"}}},"4":{"line":"……[所以]___。","lang":{"chunk":"所以","mean":"suǒyǐ · so (your conclusion)","tip":"End with 所以 + where you land. Then say the whole paragraph — that's your view, in Chinese.","learner":["所以，嗯，就是这样。","A 所以 with nothing after it."],"natural":["所以我出国前会先查一下当地的习惯。","A clear landing."],"quiz":{"q":["你说完了每个国家都不一样，最后要收个尾：","You've said every country is different. Now wrap it up:"],"o":[["所以我出国前会先查一下当地的习惯。",1],["主要是因为服务员的工资本来就不高。",0],["服务员，买单！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 所以 lands it.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 所以我出国前会先查一下当地的习惯。"}}}},"mei_ktv":{"0":{"line":"我[点]了《晴天》。","lang":{"chunk":"点","mean":"diǎn · to pick (a song), to order (food)","tip":"点 is the verb for choosing from a list: 点歌 at KTV, 点菜 at a restaurant, 点饮料 at a drink shop.","learner":["我选择了《晴天》。","Correct and understood! 点了一首 sounds more like chatting."],"natural":["我点了一首《晴天》。","What you say as you tap the tablet."],"quiz":{"q":["在饭店，你跟服务员说你要什么菜，这叫：","At a restaurant, telling the waiter what dishes you want is called:"],"o":[["点菜",1],["点歌",0],["点头",0]],"ok":"Yes — 点菜 for food, 点歌 for songs.","no":"Food is 点菜. 点歌 is for KTV."}}},"1":{"line":"太高了，我[唱不上去]。","lang":{"chunk":"唱不上去","mean":"chàng bu shàngqù · can't reach (the high notes)","tip":"Verb + 不上去 = can't get up there: 唱不上去 (too high), 爬不上去 (too steep). 唱得上去 = you can.","learner":["太高了，我不能唱。","不能 sounds like you're not allowed to sing."],"natural":["这首太高了，我唱不上去。","You'll hear this a lot at KTV."],"quiz":{"q":["这首歌的高音你唱不了。你说：","You can't hit the high notes. You say:"],"o":[["我唱不上去。",1],["切歌吧！",0],["你中文说得真好！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 唱 + 不上去.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我唱不上去。"}}},"2":{"line":"这首太悲伤了，[切歌]吧！","lang":{"chunk":"切歌","mean":"qiē gē · skip the song","tip":"切歌 = skip to the next song, at KTV or in a music app. 吧 makes it a friendly suggestion.","learner":["这首太悲伤了，我们跳过歌吧。","Understood, but long. 切歌 is the quick KTV word — everyone in the room gets it."],"natural":["切歌切歌！","Shouted, with a laugh, among friends."],"quiz":{"q":["你不想听这首了，想听下一首。你说：","You want to move on to the next song. You say:"],"o":[["切歌吧！",1],["我唱不上去。",0],["下次我还想去。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 切歌吧!","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 切歌吧！"}}},"3":{"line":"你[唱得]真好！","lang":{"chunk":"唱得","mean":"chàng de · (the way you) sang","tip":"Verb + 得 + how: 唱得真好, 说得很好, 跑得很快. Without 得 it sounds broken.","learner":["你唱真好！","Missing 得 — learners drop it a lot."],"natural":["唱得真好！超好听！","In Taiwan you'll hear 超好听 a lot."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友中文说得很好。你夸他：","Your friend speaks Chinese well. Praise them:"],"o":[["你中文说得真好！",1],["我唱不上去。",0],["下次我还想去。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 说得真好.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 你中文说得真好！"}}},"4":{"line":"下次我[想唱] ___。","lang":{"chunk":"想唱","mean":"xiǎng chàng · want to sing","tip":"想 + verb = want to do it: 想唱, 想吃, 想去. Softer than 要.","learner":["下次我要唱了 ___。","No 了 here — it hasn't happened yet."],"natural":["下次我想唱《月亮代表我的心》。","Song names go in 《》."],"quiz":{"q":["你想下次再去 KTV。你说：","You want to go to KTV again next time:"],"o":[["下次我还想去。",1],["切歌吧！",0],["你中文说得真好！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 下次 + 还想 + verb.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 下次我还想去。"}}}},"mei_order":{"0":{"line":"[半糖]少冰，谢谢。","lang":{"chunk":"半糖","mean":"bàn táng · half sugar","tip":"Tea shops have sugar levels: 全糖, 少糖, 半糖, 微糖, 无糖. Ice: 正常冰, 少冰, 去冰.","learner":["一半的糖，少一点冰。","Understood, but long."],"natural":["半糖少冰。","Four characters — quick, and the staff get it straight away."],"quiz":{"q":["你不要糖。","You want no sugar."],"o":[["无糖。",1],["一杯珍珠奶茶。",0],["要热的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 无糖 is the word on every menu.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 无糖。"}}},"1":{"line":"可以做[温的]吗？加珍珠。","lang":{"chunk":"温的","mean":"wēn de · warm","tip":"Temperatures in tea shops: 冰的 (iced), 常温 (room temp), 温的 (warm), 热的 (hot).","learner":["可以温吗？","Missing 的 — 温的 means 'a warm one'."],"natural":["可以做温的吗？","Polite and normal."],"quiz":{"q":["你想要热的。","You want it hot."],"o":[["要热的。",1],["一杯珍珠奶茶。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 热的 = a hot one.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 要热的。"}}},"2":{"line":"我要[一杯] ___，___，___。","lang":{"chunk":"一杯","mean":"yì bēi · a cup of","tip":"杯 is the measure word for drinks. Then the drink, then sugar, then ice.","learner":["我要一个奶茶。","People will understand, but 杯 is the word for drinks."],"natural":["我要一杯奶茶，半糖，少冰。","Drink, sugar, ice — in that order."],"quiz":{"q":["点一杯珍珠奶茶。","Order one bubble tea."],"o":[["一杯珍珠奶茶。",1],["要热的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 一杯 + drink.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 一杯珍珠奶茶。"}}}},"mei_qingtian":{"0":{"line":"这首歌[叫什么]？","lang":{"chunk":"叫什么","mean":"jiào shénme · what's it called","tip":"For a song, a film or a shop: 这首歌叫什么? Adding 名字 (叫什么名字) is fine too, just longer.","learner":["这首歌的名字是什么？","Correct and understood! 叫什么 is shorter and sounds more like a chat."],"natural":["这首歌叫什么？","What you'd ask in a shop or a friend's car."],"quiz":{"q":["你想知道这家店叫什么。","You want to know the shop's name."],"o":[["这家店叫什么？",1],["我听不清。",0],["我单曲循环了一整天。",0]],"ok":"Yes — thing + 叫什么.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这家店叫什么？"}}},"1":{"line":"这是[谁唱的]？","lang":{"chunk":"谁唱的","mean":"shéi chàng de · who sang it","tip":"是……的 asks about something already done: 谁唱的, 谁做的, 在哪儿买的.","learner":["谁唱这个？","Understood! 是谁唱的 is the easy everyday way to ask."],"natural":["这是谁唱的？","The everyday way."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友带来一个蛋糕。你问是谁做的。","A friend brings a cake. Ask who made it."],"o":[["这是谁做的？",1],["我听不清。",0],["我单曲循环了一整天。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 是 + who + verb + 的.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这是谁做的？"}}},"2":{"line":"我[听不清]歌词。","lang":{"chunk":"听不清","mean":"tīng bu qīng · can't hear clearly","tip":"听不清 = you hear it but can't catch the words. 听不懂 = you catch the words but don't understand them.","learner":["我听不懂歌词。","That means you don't understand them — not that you can't catch them."],"natural":["我听不清他在唱什么。","You can't catch what he's singing."],"quiz":{"q":["音乐太大声，你听不清朋友说的话。你说：","The music is too loud to catch your friend. You say:"],"o":[["我听不清。",1],["这家店叫什么？",0],["这是谁做的？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 听不清: too loud, too fast, too mumbly.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我听不清。"}}},"3":{"line":"这首歌让我[想起]高中。","lang":{"chunk":"想起","mean":"xiǎngqǐ · to remember, be reminded of","tip":"让我想起 + a time or a person. 提醒 is a reminder to do something (提醒我带钥匙).","learner":["这首歌提醒我高中。","提醒 means 'remind me to do something', not a memory."],"natural":["这首歌让我想起高中。","A memory coming back."],"quiz":{"q":["这个味道让你想到奶奶家。你说：","This smell brings back grandma's home. You say:"],"o":[["这个味道让我想起奶奶家。",1],["这是谁做的？",0],["我单曲循环了一整天。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 让我想起 + the memory.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这个味道让我想起奶奶家。"}}},"4":{"line":"这周我一直在[单曲循环] ___。","lang":{"chunk":"单曲循环","mean":"dānqǔ xúnhuán · one song on repeat","tip":"单曲循环 is the button in music apps and an everyday word: 我最近在单曲循环这首.","learner":["我这周一直重复听 ___。","Understood! 单曲循环 is the short word for it — handy to know."],"natural":["这首我已经单曲循环一周了。","Sounds like a real fan."],"quiz":{"q":["你一首歌听了一整天。你说：","You played one song all day. You say:"],"o":[["我单曲循环了一整天。",1],["这家店叫什么？",0],["这是谁做的？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 单曲循环 stays together.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我单曲循环了一整天。"}}}},"mei_tones":{"0":{"line":"来一碗[水饺]。","lang":{"chunk":"水饺","mean":"shuǐjiǎo (said shuíjiǎo) · boiled dumplings","tip":"Two third tones in a row: the first one rises, so 水饺 sounds like shuíjiǎo. 睡觉 shuìjiào = sleep.","learner":["来一碗睡觉。","shuìjiào — two falling tones — means sleep, lol."],"natural":["来一碗水饺。","Dip and rise: shuí-jiǎo."],"quiz":{"q":["哪个是「水饺」？","Which one is ‘dumplings’?"],"o":[["shuǐjiǎo",1],["shuìjiào",0],["shūjiāo",0]],"ok":"Yes — two third tones.","no":"Dumplings = shuǐjiǎo, two third tones."}}},"1":{"line":"我想[买]这个。","lang":{"chunk":"买","mean":"mǎi · to buy (卖 mài = to sell)","tip":"买 mǎi dips low; 卖 mài drops fast. 想买 is two third tones, so say xiáng mǎi.","learner":["我想卖这个。","mài means ‘sell’ — the boss will think you're selling."],"natural":["我想买这个。","xiáng mǎi zhège."],"quiz":{"q":["你要付钱把它带走，说：","You want to pay and take it. Say:"],"o":[["我想买这个。",1],["我想卖这个。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 买 mǎi = buy.","no":"卖 is sell. You want 买."}}},"2":{"line":"少放点[糖]。","lang":{"chunk":"糖","mean":"táng · sugar (汤 tāng = soup)","tip":"Second tone goes up, like a question: táng? First tone stays high and flat: tāng.","learner":["少放点汤。","tāng is soup. In your tea? No, lol."],"natural":["少放点糖。","shǎo fàng diǎn táng — what you say at a drink shop."],"quiz":{"q":["奶茶太甜了，下次你说：","Your milk tea was too sweet. Next time you say:"],"o":[["少放点糖。",1],["少放点汤。",0]],"ok":"Yes — táng, rising.","no":"Soup is tāng. Sugar is táng."}}},"3":{"line":"[请问]，厕所在哪儿？","lang":{"chunk":"请问","mean":"qǐngwèn · excuse me (may I ask)","tip":"问 wèn is a sharp fourth tone. 吻 wěn (third tone) means kiss — careful, lol.","learner":["请吻，厕所在哪儿？","wěn = kiss. Say wèn, falling fast."],"natural":["请问，厕所在哪儿？","In Taiwan you'll also hear 洗手间在哪里？"],"quiz":{"q":["「请问」的「问」是几声？","Which tone is 问 in 请问?"],"o":[["第四声",1],["第三声",0],["第一声",0]],"ok":"Yes — fourth tone, falling.","no":"It's the fourth tone: wèn."}}},"4":{"line":"老板，我[想买]___。","lang":{"chunk":"想买","mean":"xiǎng mǎi (said xiáng mǎi) · I'd like to buy","tip":"想 and 买 are both third tones, so 想 rises: xiáng mǎi. Then just name the food.","learner":["老板，我想买了臭豆腐。","No 了 here — you haven't bought it yet."],"natural":["老板，我想买两个葱油饼。","Number + measure word + food."],"quiz":{"q":["「你好」实际怎么念？","How is 你好 really said?"],"o":[["ní hǎo",1],["nǐ hāo",0],["nì hào",0]],"ok":"Yes — two third tones, the first one rises.","no":"Two third tones: ní hǎo."}}}},"mei_tones2":{"0":{"line":"[少冰]，谢谢。","lang":{"chunk":"少冰","mean":"shǎo bīng · less ice (病 bìng = illness)","tip":"冰 bīng stays high and flat. 病 bìng drops fast. Drink shops: 正常冰 / 少冰 / 去冰.","learner":["少病，谢谢。","bìng is illness — the shop can't help with that lol."],"natural":["少冰，半糖。","Ice and sugar, the two things every drink shop asks."],"quiz":{"q":["「冰」是几声？","Which tone is 冰?"],"o":[["第一声",1],["第四声",0],["第三声",0]],"ok":"Yes — bīng, high and flat.","no":"It's the first tone: bīng. bìng is illness."}}},"1":{"line":"来两个[包子]。","lang":{"chunk":"包子","mean":"bāozi · steamed bun (报纸 bàozhǐ = newspaper)","tip":"包 bāo is high and flat; 子 is light. 报纸 bàozhǐ drops, then dips. Buns count with 个.","learner":["来两张报纸。","That's two newspapers."],"natural":["来两个肉包子。","Say the filling: 肉包、菜包."],"quiz":{"q":["早餐店里，你想吃两个包子。你说：","At the breakfast shop you want two buns:"],"o":[["来两个包子。",1],["来两张报纸。",0],["来两个报纸。",0]],"ok":"Yes — bāozi, high and flat.","no":"Newspaper is bàozhǐ. Buns are bāozi."}}},"2":{"line":"是[四十]块吗？","lang":{"chunk":"四十","mean":"sìshí · forty (十四 shísì = fourteen)","tip":"四十 sìshí: fall, then rise. 十四 shísì: rise, then fall. In Taiwan and the mainland, 块 is the everyday word for a dollar or yuan.","learner":["是十四块吗？","shísì is 14 — a very different price."],"natural":["四十块？好。","Check it back before you pay."],"quiz":{"q":["四十怎么念？","How do you say 40?"],"o":[["sìshí",1],["shísì",0],["sìsì",0]],"ok":"Yes — sìshí, fall then rise.","no":"40 is sìshí. shísì is 14."}}},"3":{"line":"我在前面[下车]。","lang":{"chunk":"下车","mean":"xià chē · get out of the car (瞎扯 xiā chě = talk nonsense)","tip":"下 xià falls; 车 chē stays high. Taxi: 我在前面下车 / 路口下车 / 停这儿就行.","learner":["我在前面瞎扯。","xiā chě means talking nonsense lol."],"natural":["师傅，前面路口下车。","Drivers are often called 师傅 on the mainland."],"quiz":{"q":["你想在下一个路口下车。你跟司机说：","You want to get out at the next corner:"],"o":[["前面路口下车。",1],["下车前面路口在。",0],["路口前面车下。",0]],"ok":"Yes — place first, then 下车.","no":"Say the place, then 下车: 前面路口下车."}}},"4":{"line":"老板，[一杯] ___，少冰。","lang":{"chunk":"一杯","mean":"yì bēi · one cup of","tip":"一 is yī alone, but yì before 杯, 瓶, 碗 (tones 1, 2, 3) and yí before a fourth tone: 一个 yí gè.","learner":["老板，一个奶茶。","Drinks count with 杯, not 个."],"natural":["老板，一杯奶茶，少冰，半糖。","Drink, then ice, then sugar."],"quiz":{"q":["「一杯」的「一」怎么念？","How is 一 said in 一杯?"],"o":[["yì",1],["yí",0],["yī",0]],"ok":"Yes — yì before a first tone.","no":"Before bēi (first tone), 一 becomes yì."}}}},"nadia_5k":{"0":{"line":"我今天[跑完了]五公里，大部分是 ___ 的，感觉 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"跑完了","mean":"pǎo wán le · finished running","tip":"完 = finished. 跑完了五公里 = ran the whole 5K. Walked it? 走完了五公里. 大部分是走的 = I walked most of it.","learner":["我今天做了五公里。","做 doesn't work for distance. Say what you did: 跑 or 走."],"natural":["我今天跑完了五公里，大部分是走的。","Walking most of it is totally fine."],"quiz":{"q":["你走完了全程。","You walked the whole way."],"o":[["我走完了五公里。",1],["我跑完了五公里。",0],["我只走了一公里。",0]],"ok":"Yes — verb + 完了 + the distance.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 我走完了五公里。"}}}},"nadia_label":{"0":{"line":"第一个[配料]是糖。","lang":{"chunk":"配料","mean":"pèiliào · ingredients (on a label)","tip":"On a Chinese pack the list is called 配料表. Chatting with a friend, you'd just say 主要是糖.","learner":["糖是最多的。","Understood! 主要是糖 says 'mostly sugar' even more clearly."],"natural":["主要是糖。","\"It's mostly sugar\" — what you'd say to a friend."],"quiz":{"q":["里面是什么？","Your friend asks: what's in it?"],"o":[["主要是糖。",1],["一份才三块？",0],["没想到这么甜！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 主要是 + the thing: 主要是糖, 主要是油.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 主要是糖。"}}},"1":{"line":"[每 100 克]里有多少糖？","lang":{"chunk":"每 100 克","mean":"měi yìbǎi kè · per 100 grams","tip":"每 = every / per. Chinese labels compare everything 每 100 克 (per 100 g).","learner":["100 克有多少糖？","OK — but without 每 it's one bag, not 'per'."],"natural":["每 100 克里有多少糖？","The way you compare two products."],"quiz":{"q":["你在比两盒酸奶。","You're comparing two yogurts."],"o":[["这个每 100 克糖更少。",1],["一份才三块？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 每 100 克 comes before what you're measuring.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这个每 100 克糖更少。"}}},"2":{"line":"那不就是[换了个名字]的糖嘛。","lang":{"chunk":"换了个名字","mean":"huànle ge míngzi · with another name","tip":"不就是…嘛 = 'isn't that just…' — it sounds like you've caught the label out.","learner":["那是糖的别的名字。","Understood! 不就是…嘛 adds how you feel about it."],"natural":["不就是换了个名字的糖嘛。","Sounds like you see through it."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说：葡萄糖浆？","Your friend reads out: glucose syrup?"],"o":[["不就是糖嘛。",1],["一份才三块？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 不就是 + thing + 嘛.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 不就是糖嘛。"}}},"3":{"line":"等等，[一份]才半袋？","lang":{"chunk":"一份","mean":"yí fèn · one serving","tip":"才 here means 'only', with surprise. 一份 is a serving, a portion.","learner":["一个服务是半袋？","服务 means 'service' — not a serving of food."],"natural":["一份才半袋？","Short and surprised."],"quiz":{"q":["包装上写：一份 = 3 块饼干。","The pack says one serving = 3 biscuits."],"o":[["一份才三块？",1],["主要是糖。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 一份 for a portion, 才 for 'only'.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 一份才三块？"}}},"4":{"line":"[没想到]面包里也有盐。","lang":{"chunk":"没想到","mean":"méi xiǎngdào · didn't expect","tip":"没想到 = I didn't see that coming. Very common when something surprises you.","learner":["我不期待面包有盐。","期待 means 'look forward to' — it sounds like you wanted salt."],"natural":["没想到面包里也有盐。","Just surprised."],"quiz":{"q":["你尝了一口，太甜了。","You take a bite. It's far too sweet."],"o":[["没想到这么甜！",1],["主要是糖。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 没想到 + what surprised you.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 没想到这么甜！"}}},"5":{"line":"[别信]正面，看背面。","lang":{"chunk":"别信","mean":"bié xìn · don't believe","tip":"别 = don't (short, spoken). 正面 / 背面 = the front / the back of a pack.","learner":["不要相信前面。","前面 is 'in front of you' — for a pack say 正面."],"natural":["别信正面，看背面。","Short, like advice to a friend."],"quiz":{"q":["叫朋友看包装背面。","Tell a friend to check the back of the pack."],"o":[["看看背面。",1],["一份才三块？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 背面 is one word.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 看看背面。"}}},"6":{"line":"我把我的 ___ [翻过来]看，第一个配料是 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"翻过来","mean":"fān guòlai · flip it over","tip":"把 + thing + 翻过来: with 把, the thing comes before the action.","learner":["我翻了我的薯片。","Understood — but 翻过来 says you turned it over to look."],"natural":["我把薯片翻过来看了看。","With 把, and a little 看了看."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：你怎么看到配料表的？","A friend asks how you found the ingredients list."],"o":[["我把饼干翻过来了。",1],["一份才三块？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 把 + thing + 翻过来.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我把饼干翻过来了。"}}}},"oliver_money":{"0":{"line":"每次都不多，[加起来]可不少。","lang":{"chunk":"加起来","mean":"jiā qǐlai · all added up","tip":"加起来 = all added up. 可不少 = quite a lot — said with a sigh.","learner":["它都加上来了。","加上来 may confuse people — 加起来 is the clear way to say 'adds up'."],"natural":["一杯咖啡没几块钱，加起来可不少！","Looking at a week of receipts."],"quiz":{"q":["这周咖啡一共花了三百块。","Coffee came to 300 kuai this week."],"o":[["加起来三百块呢！",1],["我要取消自动续费。",0],["我再想想。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 加起来 + the total.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 加起来三百块呢！"}}},"1":{"line":"我都忘了这个还在[扣钱]。","lang":{"chunk":"扣钱","mean":"kòu qián · money being taken (automatically)","tip":"扣 = take off. Apps and banks 扣钱 every month. 自动续费 = auto-renew.","learner":["我忘记我在付钱给它。","Understood! 还在扣钱 — the money's still being taken — says it shorter."],"natural":["我都忘了这个还在扣钱。","都 = 'I'd even forgotten' — a bit shocked."],"quiz":{"q":["你想关掉自动续费。","You want to stop the auto-renew."],"o":[["我要取消自动续费。",1],["加起来三百块呢！",0],["钱都花在吃饭上了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 取消自动续费 is what the button in the app says.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我要取消自动续费。"}}},"2":{"line":"我[再想想]，明天再说。","lang":{"chunk":"再想想","mean":"zài xiǎngxiang · think it over","tip":"Chinese doesn't 'sleep on it' — you 再想想 or say 明天再说. Shop assistants hear it all day.","learner":["我在上面睡觉。","Word-for-word from 'sleep on it' — it means lying on top of the thing!"],"natural":["我再想想，明天再说。","Polite. The shop knows you might not come back."],"quiz":{"q":["店员问你买不买，你还不确定。","The shop assistant asks if you'll buy it. You're not sure."],"o":[["我再想想。",1],["加起来三百块呢！",0],["钱都花在吃饭上了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 再想想 is the polite 'not now'.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我再想想。"}}},"3":{"line":"我大部分的钱都[花在]房租上了。","lang":{"chunk":"花在","mean":"huā zài · spent on","tip":"钱花在 + thing + 上. Don't forget the 上 at the end.","learner":["我的钱大部分去房租。","去 is 'go to a place'. Money is 花在…上."],"natural":["我的钱大部分都花在房租上了。","大部分 and 都 go well together."],"quiz":{"q":["你的钱都花在吃饭上。","All your money goes on food."],"o":[["钱都花在吃饭上了。",1],["加起来三百块呢！",0],["我要取消自动续费。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 花在 + thing + 上.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 钱都花在吃饭上了。"}}},"4":{"line":"我的钱大多花在 ___ 上，我想在 ___ 上[少花点]。","lang":{"chunk":"少花点","mean":"shǎo huā diǎn · spend a bit less","tip":"少 + verb + 点 = do a bit less: 少吃点, 少喝点, 少花点. 在…上 comes before it.","learner":["我想花更少在外卖上。","Hard to follow — put 少 before the verb: 在外卖上少花点."],"natural":["我想在外卖上少花点。","在…上 first, then 少花点."],"quiz":{"q":["你想少喝点咖啡。","You want to drink less coffee."],"o":[["我想少喝点咖啡。",1],["加起来三百块呢！",0],["钱都花在吃饭上了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 少 + verb + 点.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想少喝点咖啡。"}}}},"rosa_tacos":{"0":{"line":"来两个，[什么都加]。","lang":{"chunk":"什么都加","mean":"shénme dōu jiā · with everything","tip":"来 + number = I'll have… (ordering food). 什么都加 = put everything on. Don't want something? 不要香菜.","learner":["两个，和所有东西。","和 only joins nouns — it can't mean 'with everything on it'."],"natural":["来两个，什么都加。","How you order at a street stall."],"quiz":{"q":["你不吃香菜。","You don't eat coriander."],"o":[["不要香菜，谢谢。",1],["多放点香菜，谢谢。",0],["香菜在哪儿买？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 不要 + the thing.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 不要香菜，谢谢。"}}},"1":{"line":"我最喜欢的是 ___ 那个，[里面有] ___。","lang":{"chunk":"里面有","mean":"lǐmiàn yǒu · with… inside","tip":"For fillings Chinese says 里面有 or 有…的: 里面有牛肉和洋葱, 有奶酪的那个.","learner":["我最喜欢的是那个和鸡肉。","和 can't mean 'with' a filling. Say 里面有鸡肉."],"natural":["我最喜欢鸡肉那个，里面有番茄和辣椒。","那个 points back at the one you ate."],"quiz":{"q":["你喜欢有奶酪的那个。","You like the one with cheese."],"o":[["我不喜欢奶酪。",0],["我喜欢有奶酪的那个。",1],["我喜欢有鸡肉的那个。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 有奶酪的 + 那个.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 我喜欢有奶酪的那个。"}}}},"suqing_bankcard":{"0":{"line":"你好，我想[开个户]。","lang":{"chunk":"开个户","mean":"kāi ge hù · to open an account","tip":"At a bank you 开户 (open an account); the card comes with it. 个 makes it casual: 开个户.","learner":["我想开一个银行。","开银行 = start your own bank. You want 开户."],"natural":["你好，开户在哪儿取号？","First question at the door."],"quiz":{"q":["在银行门口，你想问开户去哪儿。你说：","At the bank door, ask where to go to open an account:"],"o":[["请问开户在哪儿办？",1],["我收到你的消息了。",0],["我的钱都花在书上了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 开户在哪儿办？","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 请问开户在哪儿办？"}}},"1":{"line":"只带护照[够吗]？","lang":{"chunk":"够吗","mean":"gòu ma · is it enough?","tip":"够 = enough. 只带…够吗？ asks if one thing is enough. Answers: 够了 / 不够.","learner":["只带护照足够吗？","Correct! 够吗 is shorter for talking."],"natural":["只带护照够吗？还要别的吗？","When you call before you go."],"quiz":{"q":["你只带了一百块，想问够不够。你说：","You only brought 100 kuai and ask if it's enough:"],"o":[["一百块够吗？",1],["我收到你的消息了。",0],["我的钱都花在书上了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — thing + 够吗？","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 一百块够吗？"}}},"2":{"line":"密码是我自己[设]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"设","mean":"shè · to set (a password)","tip":"设密码 = set a PIN or password. Staff may say 请输入密码 (type your PIN) and 再输一遍 (once more).","learner":["密码是我自己做吗？","做 is too general; for a PIN or password say 设."],"natural":["请输入六位数密码，再输一遍。","What the teller will say to you."],"quiz":{"q":["柜员说「请再输一遍密码」，意思是：","The teller says 请再输一遍密码. It means:"],"o":[["Type your PIN again",1],["Tell me your PIN out loud",0],["Your PIN is wrong, go home",0]],"ok":"Yes — 再输一遍 = type it once more, to confirm.","no":"输 = type in, 再…一遍 = once more. You never say your PIN out loud."}}},"3":{"line":"我没[收到]验证码。","lang":{"chunk":"收到","mean":"shōudào · to receive (a text, a message)","tip":"Texts, emails and codes are 收到. 拿到 is for things you pick up with your hands, like a parcel.","learner":["我没拿到验证码。","A code comes to you by text, so it's 收到."],"natural":["验证码一直没收到，能再发一次吗？","When you're waiting and nothing comes."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：我发的消息你看到了吗？","A friend asks: did you get my message?"],"o":[["我收到你的消息了。",1],["请问开户在哪儿办？",0],["一百块够吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 收到 + 你的消息.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我收到你的消息了。"}}},"4":{"line":"卡绑好了，第一笔钱我想[花在]___上。","lang":{"chunk":"花在","mean":"huā zài … shàng · to spend (money) on","tip":"花钱 = spend money. 钱花在…上 says what it goes on: 花在吃上, 花在书上. 笔 counts sums of money: 一笔钱.","learner":["第一个钱我想花为___。","Money takes 笔, and 'spend on' is 花在…上."],"natural":["我的钱都花在吃上了。","A very common joke about yourself."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：你的钱都花哪儿了？你特别爱买书。","A friend asks where your money goes. You buy lots of books."],"o":[["我的钱都花在书上了。",1],["一百块够吗？",0],["请问开户在哪儿办？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 钱花在 + 书 + 上.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我的钱都花在书上了。"}}}},"suqing_praise":{"0":{"line":"谢谢！[还在学呢]。","lang":{"chunk":"还在学呢","mean":"hái zài xué ne · I'm still learning","tip":"The easy, friendly reply to 你中文真好. You'll also hear 哪里哪里 (‘not at all’) or 没有没有 — modest ways to say the same.","learner":["谢谢你的夸奖。","Correct and polite — that works! 还在学呢 adds a friendly line about you."],"natural":["谢谢！还在学呢。","Friendly and true — people will smile."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友笑着说「哪里哪里」。他的意思是：","A friend smiles and says 哪里哪里. He means:"],"o":[["没有没有，我还差得远。",1],["你在哪儿？",0],["我找不到路了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — here 哪里哪里 means ‘not at all’, not ‘where’.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 没有没有，我还差得远。"}}},"1":{"line":"是吗？[才]五十块。","lang":{"chunk":"才","mean":"cái · only (less than you'd think)","tip":"才 + a number = ‘only that much’. It makes the thing sound small and cheap.","learner":["是吗？它是五十块。","No need for 它是 — just say the price with 才."],"natural":["是吗？才五十块。","Casual and modest."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友夸你的包好看。其实它很便宜，才一百块。","A friend likes your bag. It was cheap: only 100 kuai."],"o":[["才一百块。",1],["太地道了！",0],["我还在学呢。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 才 goes right before the number.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 才一百块。"}}},"2":{"line":"都是[大家一起]做的。","lang":{"chunk":"大家一起","mean":"dàjiā yìqǐ · everyone together","tip":"When you're praised at work, give the credit to the team. 都是 … 的 = ‘it was all …’.","learner":["我们一起做的，不是我。","Not wrong — people get it. 都是大家一起做的 sounds a little warmer."],"natural":["都是大家一起做的。","What people say in meetings when the boss says ‘well done’."],"quiz":{"q":["领导夸你做得好，你想说是大家的功劳：","Your boss says you did well. You want to share the credit:"],"o":[["都是大家一起做的。",1],["太地道了！",0],["才一百块。",0]],"ok":"Yes — share the credit.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 都是大家一起做的。"}}},"3":{"line":"这个太[地道]了！","lang":{"chunk":"地道","mean":"dìdao · authentic, the real local taste","tip":"地道 = authentic, the real thing. Most often said about food: 太地道了!","learner":["这个很真的！","真 doesn't mean ‘authentic’ for food."],"natural":["这个太地道了！","Top praise for local food."],"quiz":{"q":["吃到正宗的四川菜，你说：","You eat real Sichuan food. You say:"],"o":[["太地道了！",1],["才一百块。",0],["都是大家一起做的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 地道 is the word.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 太地道了！"}}},"4":{"line":"谢谢！我的___[还在练]呢。","lang":{"chunk":"还在练","mean":"hái zài liàn · still practising","tip":"还在 + verb + 呢 = still doing it. Modest, but it shows you're working on it.","learner":["谢谢，我的中文还练。","It needs 在 … 呢: 还在练呢."],"natural":["谢谢！我的中文还在练呢。","Modest and true."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友夸你中文好，你想说自己还在学。","A friend praises your Chinese. You want to say you're still learning."],"o":[["我还在学呢。",1],["太地道了！",0],["都是大家一起做的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 还在 + verb + 呢.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我还在学呢。"}}},"5":{"line":"在我们那儿，被人夸了，一般[会说]___。"}},"suqing_simcard":{"0":{"line":"我想[办]一张手机卡。","lang":{"chunk":"办","mean":"bàn · to get something done (officially)","tip":"办 is for official errands: 办卡, 办签证, 办手续. 买 is for things you just pay for.","learner":["我想买一张手机卡。","Understood! At the counter you'll hear 办卡 — handy to know."],"natural":["您好，我想办张卡。","At the counter: short and polite."],"quiz":{"q":["你在银行，想要一张银行卡。你说：","At the bank, you want a bank card. You say:"],"o":[["我想办一张银行卡。",1],["有没有小一点的？",0],["今天我要做三件事。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 办卡: bank cards, SIM cards, gym cards.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想办一张银行卡。"}}},"1":{"line":"需要带什么[材料]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"材料","mean":"cáiliào · documents (for an errand)","tip":"材料 = the papers an office asks for. 原件 = the original, 复印件 = a copy.","learner":["我需要带什么纸？","纸 is just paper — the documents are 材料."],"natural":["需要带什么材料？护照可以吗？","What you'd ask before you go."],"quiz":{"q":["工作人员问：护照原件带了吗？你带了。","The staff asks if you brought your original passport. You did."],"o":[["我带了护照原件。",1],["有没有小一点的？",0],["我想把银行卡绑定到微信。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 带了 + 护照原件.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我带了护照原件。"}}},"2":{"line":"有没有[便宜一点的]套餐？","lang":{"chunk":"便宜一点的","mean":"piányi yìdiǎn de · a bit cheaper (one)","tip":"Adjective + 一点 makes a soft comparison: 便宜一点, 小一点, 快一点. Softer than 更便宜.","learner":["有没有很便宜的套餐？","很便宜 = very cheap; you just want cheaper than this one."],"natural":["有没有便宜一点的？","Polite and normal."],"quiz":{"q":["这件衣服太大了。你问店员：","This shirt is too big. You ask the staff:"],"o":[["有没有小一点的？",1],["我带了护照原件。",0],["我想把银行卡绑定到微信。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 小一点的, 便宜一点的.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 有没有小一点的？"}}},"3":{"line":"这个号能[绑定]支付宝吗？","lang":{"chunk":"绑定","mean":"bǎngdìng · to link (to an account)","tip":"绑定 = link a number or card to an app. People also just say 绑: 绑卡, 绑手机.","learner":["这个号能连支付宝吗？","连 is for Wi-Fi or Bluetooth; accounts are 绑定."],"natural":["我想把银行卡绑到微信上。","With 把: 把 + card + 绑到 + app."],"quiz":{"q":["你想把银行卡加到微信里。你说：","You want to add your bank card to WeChat. You say:"],"o":[["我想把银行卡绑定到微信。",1],["有没有小一点的？",0],["今天我要做三件事。",0]],"ok":"Yes — cards and accounts are 绑定.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想把银行卡绑定到微信。"}}},"4":{"line":"我来中国[办的第一件事]是 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"办的第一件事","mean":"bàn de dì-yī jiàn shì · the first thing I got done","tip":"件 is the measure word for 事: 一件事, 第一件事, 三件事.","learner":["我来中国第一个事是 ___。","事 takes 件, not 个."],"natural":["我到中国办的第一件事是办手机卡。","到 or 来 both work."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友约你出去，可你今天有三件事要做。","A friend asks you out, but you have three things to do today."],"o":[["今天我要做三件事。",1],["有没有小一点的？",0],["我想把银行卡绑定到微信。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 三件事.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 今天我要做三件事。"}}}},"suqing_suibian":{"0":{"line":"那吃火锅[还是]吃面？","lang":{"chunk":"还是","mean":"háishi · or (in a question)","tip":"In a question with two choices, use 还是: 茶还是咖啡？ 或者 is for 'either one is fine', not for asking.","learner":["那吃火锅或者吃面？","People understand, but a choice question uses 还是."],"natural":["火锅还是面？你挑一个。","Short, between friends."],"quiz":{"q":["你问朋友想喝茶还是咖啡：","Ask a friend: tea or coffee?"],"o":[["你想喝茶还是咖啡？",1],["看你，你方便就行。",0],["都行，就是别太远。",0]],"ok":"Yes — A 还是 B, no 吗 at the end.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 你想喝茶还是咖啡？"}}},"1":{"line":"我[都行]，你定吧。","lang":{"chunk":"都行","mean":"dōu xíng · either is fine / anything works","tip":"都行 = I'm fine with all of them. Add 你定吧 (you decide) to hand the choice back politely. 都可以 means the same.","learner":["我没关系，你定吧。","没关系 answers 'sorry'; for choices say 都行 or 都可以."],"natural":["几点都行，你定。","When the time doesn't matter to you."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问你坐里面还是外面，你都无所谓。你说：","Your friend asks: inside or outside? You don't mind. You say:"],"o":[["都行，你定吧。",1],["你想喝茶还是咖啡？",0],["看你，你方便就行。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 都行，你定吧.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 都行，你定吧。"}}},"2":{"line":"[看你]，你方便就行。","lang":{"chunk":"看你","mean":"kàn nǐ · up to you","tip":"看你 here doesn't mean 'look at you' — it means 'it depends on you'. 你方便就行 = whatever suits you.","learner":["取决于你。","Understood! 取决于 is more for writing; in a chat, 看你 is quicker."],"natural":["看你吧，周六周日都行。","When you set a time with a friend."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：我们几点见？你哪个时间都可以。你说：","Your friend asks what time to meet. Any time is OK for you. You say:"],"o":[["看你，你方便就行。",1],["你想喝茶还是咖啡？",0],["都行，就是别太远。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 看你, 你方便就行.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 看你，你方便就行。"}}},"3":{"line":"好，那你[有空再说]。","lang":{"chunk":"有空再说","mean":"yǒu kòng zài shuō · let's talk when you're free","tip":"再说 here = 'talk about it later', not 'say it again'. 下次再说吧 is often a soft no. Answer lightly with 那你有空再说.","learner":["为什么？那你哪天有空？","Asking 'why' or pushing for a day after 再说吧 feels pushy."],"natural":["行，那下次吧。","Easy and friendly — no pressure."],"quiz":{"q":["你没听清，想让对方再说一次。你说：","You didn't catch it and want them to repeat. You say:"],"o":[["能再说一遍吗？",1],["下次再说吧。",0],["你有空再说。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 再说一遍 = say it again. 再说吧 alone means 'later'.","no":"再说吧 means 'later'. To ask for a repeat: 能再说一遍吗？"}}},"4":{"line":"都行，[就是别]___。","lang":{"chunk":"就是别","mean":"jiùshì bié · just not…","tip":"都行，就是别… = anything is fine, except one thing. Put what you don't want after 别: 别太辣, 别太远, 别太贵.","learner":["都行，但是不要太辣。","Clear and fine! 就是别 sounds a little more relaxed."],"natural":["吃什么都行，就是别太辣。","The honest answer to 'what do you want to eat?'"],"quiz":{"q":["去哪儿吃都可以，只是不想走太远。你说：","Anywhere is fine, but you don't want to walk far. You say:"],"o":[["都行，就是别太远。",1],["你想喝茶还是咖啡？",0],["看你，你方便就行。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 就是别 + 太远.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 都行，就是别太远。"}}}},"suqing_work":{"0":{"line":"我在___[负责]___。","lang":{"chunk":"负责","mean":"fùzé · be in charge of","tip":"我在 + place + 负责 + thing. Works for almost any job — it sounds like you own your work.","learner":["我的工作是做后端的工作。","工作 twice — the listener may lose the point. Say where you work and what you do."],"natural":["我在一家游戏公司负责后端。","Place + 负责 + thing."],"quiz":{"q":["你在公司管社交媒体：","You run social media at your company:"],"o":[["我在公司负责社交媒体。",1],["加班说白了就是下班了还在干活。",0],["总之，我挺喜欢我的工作的。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 在 + place + 负责 + thing.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我在公司负责社交媒体。"}}},"1":{"line":"我每天[先]___，[然后]___。","lang":{"chunk":"先……，然后……","mean":"xiān …, ránhòu … · first …, then …","tip":"The easiest way to put things in order. Three steps? 先……，然后……，最后……","learner":["我开会，我写代码，我回家。","Clear! 先…然后 links it into one line, easier to follow."],"natural":["我每天先开个短会，然后写代码。","先 + 然后 links it into one line."],"quiz":{"q":["你早上先开会，再回邮件：","In the morning you meet first, then do emails:"],"o":[["我先开会，然后回邮件。",1],["加班说白了就是下班了还在干活。",0],["总之，我挺喜欢我的工作的。",0]],"ok":"Right — 先 A，然后 B.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我先开会，然后回邮件。"}}},"2":{"line":"[首先]___，[接着]___，[最后]___。","lang":{"chunk":"首先……，接着……，最后……","mean":"shǒuxiān …, jiēzhe …, zuìhòu … · first, next, finally","tip":"A bit more formal than 先……然后……, good for explaining how something is done.","learner":["第一，第二，第三。","Sounds like a list in a report."],"natural":["首先看需求，接着写代码，最后测试。","A process you can follow."],"quiz":{"q":["你要说最后一步：","You're giving the last step:"],"o":[["最后，我们测试一下。",1],["加班说白了就是下班了还在干活。",0],["我在公司负责社交媒体。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 最后，+ step.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 最后，我们测试一下。"}}},"3":{"line":"___[说白了就是]___。","lang":{"chunk":"说白了就是","mean":"shuō bái le jiù shì · basically, in plain words","tip":"Turn jargon into plain words. Friendly, a little casual — people use it all the time.","learner":["分诊的意思是 triage。","Explaining with English doesn't help a Chinese friend."],"natural":["分诊说白了就是先看谁最急。","Plain words anyone gets."],"quiz":{"q":["你要用大白话解释「加班」：","Explain 加班 in plain words:"],"o":[["加班说白了就是下班了还在干活。",1],["总之，我挺喜欢我的工作的。",0],["我先开会，然后回邮件。",0]],"ok":"Right — 说白了就是 + plain words.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 加班说白了就是下班了还在干活。"}}},"4":{"line":"……[总之]___。","lang":{"chunk":"总之","mean":"zǒngzhī · all in all","tip":"Wrap it up with how you feel about your work: 总之 + one line.","learner":["就这样。","Ends abruptly."],"natural":["总之，虽然累，但是挺有意思的。","A warm ending."],"quiz":{"q":["你要给这一段收个尾：","Wrap up your paragraph:"],"o":[["总之，我挺喜欢我的工作的。",1],["加班说白了就是下班了还在干活。",0],["我在公司负责社交媒体。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 总之，+ line.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 总之，我挺喜欢我的工作的。"}}}},"suqing_zero":{"0":{"line":"你好，[很高兴认识你]。","lang":{"chunk":"很高兴认识你","mean":"hěn gāoxìng rènshi nǐ · nice to meet you","tip":"Say it when you meet someone new. 你好 is said ní hǎo — the first third tone rises.","learner":["你好，很高兴见到你。","Fine — people get it! For a first meeting, 认识你 fits best."],"natural":["你好，很高兴认识你。","The first line everyone learns — and really uses."],"quiz":{"q":["第一次见面，你说：","Meeting someone for the first time:"],"o":[["很高兴认识你。",1],["这个多少钱？",0],["能再说一遍吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 很高兴认识你.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 很高兴认识你。"}}},"1":{"line":"[来一个]肉夹馍。","lang":{"chunk":"来一个","mean":"lái yí ge · I'll have one","tip":"来 + number + measure word + food = ‘give me…’. At a stall it's normal and polite enough.","learner":["我会要一个肉夹馍。","会 isn't ‘would’ here. Just 来一个."],"natural":["来一个肉夹馍。","Fast and normal at a stall."],"quiz":{"q":["你要两个包子：","You want two steamed buns:"],"o":[["来两个包子。",1],["能再说一遍吗？",0],["能便宜一点吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 两 (not 二) before 个.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 来两个包子。"}}},"2":{"line":"这个[多少钱]？","lang":{"chunk":"多少钱","mean":"duōshao qián · how much (money)","tip":"Point and ask 这个多少钱? The answer sounds like 十块 — people say 块, not 元.","learner":["这个多少钱吗？","No 吗 — 多少 already makes it a question."],"natural":["这个多少钱？","Point and ask."],"quiz":{"q":["问价钱：","Ask the price:"],"o":[["这个多少钱？",1],["很高兴认识你。",0],["太好看了！",0]],"ok":"Yes — no 吗 needed.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这个多少钱？"}}},"3":{"line":"不好意思，能[再说一遍]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"再说一遍","mean":"zài shuō yí biàn · say it again","tip":"再 = again. 一遍 = one time through. Works with anyone — taxi drivers, waiters, teachers.","learner":["不好意思，再一次说？","Word order: 再说一遍."],"natural":["不好意思，能再说一遍吗？","Polite and very common."],"quiz":{"q":["没听清，你说：","You didn't catch it:"],"o":[["能再说一遍吗？",1],["很高兴认识你。",0],["来两个包子。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 再 before the verb.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 能再说一遍吗？"}}},"4":{"line":"能说[慢一点]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"慢一点","mean":"màn yìdiǎn · a bit slower","tip":"Adjective + 一点 = a bit more so: 慢一点, 大一点, 便宜一点.","learner":["能一点慢说吗？","一点 comes after the adjective: 慢一点."],"natural":["能说慢一点吗？","Polite and clear."],"quiz":{"q":["想便宜一点，你说：","You want it a bit cheaper:"],"o":[["能便宜一点吗？",1],["很高兴认识你。",0],["来两个包子。",0]],"ok":"Yes — adjective + 一点.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 能便宜一点吗？"}}},"5":{"line":"[太好吃了]！","lang":{"chunk":"太好吃了","mean":"tài hǎochī le · so delicious","tip":"太 … 了 = so …! 太好吃了, 太好看了, 太好了.","learner":["太好吃！","It needs 了 at the end: 太好吃了！"],"natural":["太好吃了！","Cooks love hearing it."],"quiz":{"q":["这件衣服很好看，你说：","This shirt looks great:"],"o":[["太好看了！",1],["很高兴认识你。",0],["来两个包子。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 太 … 了.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 太好看了！"}}},"6":{"line":"我是___人，我[喜欢]___。","lang":{"chunk":"喜欢","mean":"xǐhuan · to like","tip":"Country + 人 = a person from there: 法国人, 巴西人. 喜欢 + a thing, or + a verb: 喜欢吃辣.","learner":["我是从巴西。","Say 我是巴西人, or 我从巴西来."],"natural":["我是巴西人，我喜欢吃辣。","Where you're from + one thing you like."],"quiz":{"q":["你从日本来：","You're from Japan:"],"o":[["我是日本人。",1],["这个多少钱？",0],["能再说一遍吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — country + 人.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我是日本人。"}}}},"suqing_zero2":{"0":{"line":"来一个肉夹馍，要[纯瘦]的。","lang":{"chunk":"纯瘦","mean":"chún shòu · lean meat only","tip":"At a roujiamo stall: 肥瘦 = fat and lean mixed, 纯瘦 = lean only. For meat, fat is 肥, not 胖.","learner":["我不要胖的肉。","胖 is for people. Fatty meat is 肥."],"natural":["老板，一个纯瘦的。","Short and normal at a stall."],"quiz":{"q":["你想要肥肉和瘦肉都有的那种。你说：","You want the one with fat and lean mixed. You say:"],"o":[["要肥瘦的。",1],["能帮我拍张照吗？",0],["这个怎么用？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 肥瘦的 = mixed.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 要肥瘦的。"}}},"1":{"line":"请问，在哪儿[租]自行车？","lang":{"chunk":"租","mean":"zū · to rent","tip":"租 = rent for a while; 买 = buy to keep. Giving it back is 还车.","learner":["请问，在哪儿买自行车？","That sounds like you want to buy one and take it home."],"natural":["租车在哪儿？还车也在这儿吗？","Two questions you'll really need on the wall."],"quiz":{"q":["你想骑两个小时，然后还回去。你说：","You want a bike for two hours, then give it back. You say:"],"o":[["我想租两个小时。",1],["能帮我拍张照吗？",0],["这个怎么用？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 租 + how long.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想租两个小时。"}}},"2":{"line":"能帮我[拍张照]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"拍张照","mean":"pāi zhāng zhào · take a photo","tip":"拍照 = take photos; 拍张照 = take one photo. 帮我 goes before it. Bonus: 把塔拍进去 = get the tower in.","learner":["能帮我拍照片吗？","Understood! 拍张照 is a bit shorter."],"natural":["能帮我拍张照吗？把钟楼拍进去。","So you don't get just your face."],"quiz":{"q":["你想请人帮你拍照。你说：","Ask someone to take a photo of you:"],"o":[["能帮我拍张照吗？",1],["要肥瘦的。",0],["我想租两个小时。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 帮我 + 拍张照.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 能帮我拍张照吗？"}}},"3":{"line":"不好意思，这个[怎么吃]？","lang":{"chunk":"怎么吃","mean":"zěnme chī · how do you eat (it)?","tip":"怎么 + verb = how to do it: 怎么吃, 怎么走, 怎么用. Great for any new food.","learner":["这个怎么样吃？","怎么样 asks 'what's it like'; 'how to eat' is 怎么吃."],"natural":["这个馍要自己掰吗？","When you've already guessed and want to check."],"quiz":{"q":["你不会用这台机器。你问：","You don't know how to use this machine. You ask:"],"o":[["这个怎么用？",1],["要肥瘦的。",0],["我最想去北京。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 怎么 + 用.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这个怎么用？"}}},"4":{"line":"到了___，我[最想]___。","lang":{"chunk":"最想","mean":"zuì xiǎng · most want to","tip":"最想 + what you want to do: 我最想吃…, 我最想去…. 到了… = once I get to….","learner":["到了西安，我想最骑车。","最 goes before 想: 最想骑车."],"natural":["到了西安，我最想在城墙上骑车。","Lucas's answer."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友问：在中国你最想去哪儿？北京。","A friend asks where in China you most want to go: Beijing."],"o":[["我最想去北京。",1],["这个怎么用？",0],["能帮我拍张照吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 最想 + 去北京.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我最想去北京。"}}}},"tom_veg":{"0":{"line":"就[尝一口]，然后告诉我怎么样。","lang":{"chunk":"尝一口","mean":"cháng yì kǒu · just one taste","tip":"口 = a mouthful. 尝一口 / 吃一口 = one bite. 就 makes it sound small.","learner":["吃一个咬。","咬 is the action 'to bite', not an amount. One bite is 一口."],"natural":["就尝一口嘛。","嘛 makes it gentle — good with kids."],"quiz":{"q":["叫朋友喝一口你的汤。","Ask a friend to try a sip of your soup."],"o":[["喝一口试试。",1],["小朋友给西兰花起了个名字。",0],["我小时候不爱吃胡萝卜。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 一口 works for eating and drinking.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 喝一口试试。"}}},"1":{"line":"我们给它[起个名字]吧，叫什么好？","lang":{"chunk":"起个名字","mean":"qǐ ge míngzi · give it a name","tip":"给 + someone/something + 起名字 = give a name to. 叫什么好？ = what should we call it?","learner":["我们给它一个名字吧。","Understood! For names, the verb is 起: 给它起个名字."],"natural":["给它起个名字吧，叫什么好？","Fun to ask a kid."],"quiz":{"q":["小朋友给西兰花起了名字。","The kid gave the broccoli a name."],"o":[["小朋友给西兰花起了个名字。",1],["帮我搅一下好吗？",0],["喝一口试试。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 给 + thing + 起了个名字.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 小朋友给西兰花起了个名字。"}}},"2":{"line":"能[帮我]洗一下这些菜吗？","lang":{"chunk":"帮我","mean":"bāng wǒ · help me","tip":"帮我 + action + 一下 = could you just… 一下 makes it light.","learner":["你能帮助我洗这些吗？","Understood! 帮我…一下 sounds lighter in the kitchen."],"natural":["帮我洗一下菜好吗？","Light and friendly."],"quiz":{"q":["请小朋友帮你搅一搅。","Ask the kid to give it a stir."],"o":[["帮我搅一下好吗？",1],["小朋友给西兰花起了个名字。",0],["明天再去吧。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 帮我 + action + 一下.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 帮我搅一下好吗？"}}},"3":{"line":"没关系，[下次再试]。","lang":{"chunk":"下次再试","mean":"xià cì zài shì · try again next time","tip":"再 = again, in the future. 下次再… is the kind way to let it go.","learner":["没关系，下次又试。","又 is 'again' for things that already happened. For next time, use 再."],"natural":["没关系，下次再试试。","试试 sounds softer than 试."],"quiz":{"q":["今天太晚了，你想明天去。","It's too late today — you'll go tomorrow."],"o":[["明天再去吧。",1],["帮我搅一下好吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 'again' in the future is 再.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 明天再去吧。"}}},"4":{"line":"我小时候[特别讨厌] ___，现在我 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"特别讨厌","mean":"tèbié tǎoyàn · really couldn't stand","tip":"讨厌 = can't stand. 小时候 = as a kid — no need for 当我是孩子的时候.","learner":["当我是一个孩子的时候，我恨 ___。","Careful: 恨 is real hate, for enemies. For food, say 讨厌 or 不爱吃."],"natural":["我小时候特别讨厌茄子，现在挺爱吃的。","小时候 at the front, then the food."],"quiz":{"q":["你小时候不爱吃胡萝卜。","As a kid you didn't like carrots."],"o":[["我小时候不爱吃胡萝卜。",1],["帮我搅一下好吗？",0],["喝一口试试。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 小时候 + 不爱吃 + the food.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我小时候不爱吃胡萝卜。"}}}},"xiaoyu_ai":{"0":{"line":"我[觉得]___。","lang":{"chunk":"觉得","mean":"juéde · think, feel (about an opinion)","tip":"我觉得 + your view is the softest way to take a side. 我认为 sounds more formal, like in an essay.","learner":["我认为不会。","Fine, people get it! 觉得 is lighter for a chat."],"natural":["我觉得不会。","Light, for chatting over dinner."],"quiz":{"q":["你想轻松地说你的看法：","You want to give your view casually:"],"o":[["我觉得应该给。",1],["就拿翻译来说，它已经很好用了。",0],["主要是因为太贵了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 我觉得 + your view.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我觉得应该给。"}}},"1":{"line":"[主要是因为]___。","lang":{"chunk":"主要是因为","mean":"zhǔyào shì yīnwèi · mainly because","tip":"Give one main reason, not a list. 主要 tells people this is the big one.","learner":["因为……因为……还有因为……","Three 因为 in a row sounds like an excuse."],"natural":["主要是因为我的工作要跟人打交道。","One reason, said clearly."],"quiz":{"q":["你只想说最重要的那个理由：","You only want to give the biggest reason:"],"o":[["主要是因为太贵了。",1],["我觉得应该给。",0],["就拿翻译来说，它已经很好用了。",0]],"ok":"Right — 主要是因为 + reason.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 主要是因为太贵了。"}}},"2":{"line":"[话是这么说，但]___。","lang":{"chunk":"话是这么说，但","mean":"huà shì zhème shuō, dàn · that's true, but","tip":"Admit a point first, then turn. It makes you sound fair, not stubborn. Also: 没错，不过……","learner":["你说得不对。","Too direct — people feel attacked."],"natural":["话是这么说，但我还是觉得不会。","You agree a little, then hold your view."],"quiz":{"q":["朋友说「AI 很快」。你同意一点，但还是不担心：","A friend says AI is fast. You agree a bit, but aren't worried:"],"o":[["话是这么说，但我不担心。",1],["主要是因为太贵了。",0],["我觉得应该给。",0]],"ok":"Yes — the turn needs 但.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 话是这么说，但我不担心。"}}},"3":{"line":"[就拿]___[来说]，___。","lang":{"chunk":"就拿……来说","mean":"jiù ná … lái shuō · take … for example","tip":"Wrap your example: 就拿 + thing + 来说, then what happens. One real example beats three reasons.","learner":["比如说写邮件，比如说翻译，比如说……","A list of 比如 — no example actually lands."],"natural":["就拿写邮件来说，它一秒就写完了。","One example, then what happens."],"quiz":{"q":["你想拿「翻译」举个例子：","You want to use translation as your example:"],"o":[["就拿翻译来说，它已经很好用了。",1],["我觉得应该给。",0],["所以我觉得不用太担心。",0]],"ok":"Right — 就拿……来说.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 就拿翻译来说，它已经很好用了。"}}},"4":{"line":"……[所以]___。","lang":{"chunk":"所以","mean":"suǒyǐ · so (your conclusion)","tip":"End with 所以 + where you land. Then say the whole paragraph — that's your view, in Chinese.","learner":["所以，嗯，就是这样。","A 所以 with nothing after it."],"natural":["所以我会学着用它，而不是怕它。","A clear landing."],"quiz":{"q":["最后一句，你要收尾：","Last line — wrap it up:"],"o":[["所以我觉得不用太担心。",1],["就拿翻译来说，它已经很好用了。",0],["主要是因为太贵了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 所以 lands it.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 所以我觉得不用太担心。"}}}},"xiaoyu_phone":{"0":{"line":"[喂]，您好，哪位？","lang":{"chunk":"喂","mean":"wéi · hello? (on the phone)","tip":"On the phone 喂 usually rises, like a question. Use it for calls — not to greet someone in person.","learner":["喂！（见面打招呼）","Said to someone's face, 喂 sounds like 'Hey, you!'"],"natural":["喂，您好？","Picking up a call."],"quiz":{"q":["你在路上见到老师。你说：","You meet your teacher on the street. You say:"],"o":[["老师好！",1],["我在小区北门。",0],["放快递柜就行。",0]],"ok":"Yes — save 喂 for the phone.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 老师好！"}}},"1":{"line":"我在[小区门口]等你。","lang":{"chunk":"小区门口","mean":"xiǎoqū ménkǒu · at the gate of the housing compound","tip":"小区 = the gated compound you live in. 社区 = the community, or the neighbourhood office.","learner":["我在社区门口等你。","社区 sounds like the local office, not your gate."],"natural":["我在小区东门等你。","Even better — say which gate."],"quiz":{"q":["骑手问你在哪儿。你在小区北门。你说：","The rider asks where you are. You're at the north gate:"],"o":[["我在小区北门。",1],["老师好！",0],["放快递柜就行。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 小区 + 北门.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我在小区北门。"}}},"2":{"line":"[放门口]就行，谢谢。","lang":{"chunk":"放门口","mean":"fàng ménkǒu · leave it at the door","tip":"就行 = 'that'll do'. 放门口就行 is short and friendly.","learner":["请你放它在门前面。","Understood! 放门口就行 says it in five characters."],"natural":["放门口就行。","Short — the courier gets it straight away."],"quiz":{"q":["快递员问：放哪儿？你想放快递柜。你说：","Courier: where shall I leave it? You want the locker:"],"o":[["放快递柜就行。",1],["老师好！",0],["我想问一下，你们几点关门？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 放 + place + 就行.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 放快递柜就行。"}}},"3":{"line":"我想[订个位子]，今晚七点，两个人。","lang":{"chunk":"订个位子","mean":"dìng ge wèizi · book a table","tip":"订位 / 订个位子 for restaurants. On the phone people skip 预订 and 桌子.","learner":["我想预订一张桌子。","Correct — they'll understand. On the phone, people also say 订个位子."],"natural":["我想订个位子，今晚七点，两个人。","Time first, then how many."],"quiz":{"q":["你想订明天中午，四个人。你说：","Book for four, tomorrow lunchtime:"],"o":[["我想订个位子，明天中午，四个人。",1],["老师好！",0],["放快递柜就行。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 订个位子, then the time, then how many.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想订个位子，明天中午，四个人。"}}},"4":{"line":"喂，您好，[我想问一下] ___。","lang":{"chunk":"我想问一下","mean":"wǒ xiǎng wèn yíxià · I'd like to ask…","tip":"一下 makes it light and polite: 问一下, 看一下, 等一下.","learner":["我有一个问题问你。","Understood, but heavy for a quick call."],"natural":["我想问一下，你们几点关门？","Light, polite, straight to the point."],"quiz":{"q":["你想问饭店几点关门。你说：","Ask the restaurant when they close:"],"o":[["我想问一下，你们几点关门？",1],["老师好！",0],["放快递柜就行。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 几点 goes before the verb: 几点关门.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想问一下，你们几点关门？"}}}},"xiaoyu_shopping":{"0":{"line":"你好，我[取快递]，取件码 3218。","lang":{"chunk":"取快递","mean":"qǔ kuàidì · pick up a parcel","tip":"取 = collect something that's waiting for you: 取快递, 取钱, 取票. 拿快递 is fine too in chat.","learner":["你好，我来拿我的包裹。","Understood! 快递 is the everyday word — you'll see it on every pickup sign."],"natural":["取快递，3218。","At a busy station, this is enough."],"quiz":{"q":["你要去驿站拿你的快递。你说：","You're at the pickup station for your parcel:"],"o":[["我取快递。",1],["有小一号的吗？",0],["我昨天在网上买了一本书。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 取 + 快递.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我取快递。"}}},"1":{"line":"这件有[大一号]的吗？","lang":{"chunk":"大一号","mean":"dà yí hào · one size bigger","tip":"大一号 / 小一号 = one size up / down. Add 的 when you mean 'one in that size': 有大一号的吗?","learner":["这件有没有更大的？","Understood, but may sound like 'a much bigger one'."],"natural":["亲，这件有大一号的吗？","You can call them 亲 back lol."],"quiz":{"q":["这双鞋有点大，你想换小一点的。你问：","These shoes are a bit big. Ask for one size down:"],"o":[["有小一号的吗？",1],["我取快递。",0],["我想退款。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 小一号.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 有小一号的吗？"}}},"2":{"line":"不合适，我想[退货]。","lang":{"chunk":"退货","mean":"tuì huò · return (an item you bought)","tip":"退 = send back what you bought: 退货, 退款 (refund). 还 huán is for things you borrowed.","learner":["我想还它。","还 is for borrowed things, like a book."],"natural":["尺码不合适，我想退货。","Give a short reason if you like — you don't have to."],"quiz":{"q":["你想把钱拿回来。你说：","You want your money back:"],"o":[["我想退款。",1],["有小一号的吗？",0],["我昨天在网上买了一本书。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 退款 = refund.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我想退款。"}}},"3":{"line":"东西很好，我给了[好评]。","lang":{"chunk":"好评","mean":"hǎopíng · good review","tip":"好评 = good review, 差评 = bad review, 中评 = so-so. 给个好评 is what shops ask for.","learner":["我给了一个好的评论。","Understood! 好评 is the short word for it."],"natural":["五星好评！","What a happy buyer writes."],"quiz":{"q":["东西坏了，你很不满意，给了：","It arrived broken, you're unhappy. You gave a:"],"o":[["差评",1],["好评",0],["五星",0]],"ok":"Yes — 差评 is a bad review.","no":"Unhappy = 差评."}}},"4":{"line":"我最近[在网上买了] ___。","lang":{"chunk":"在网上买了","mean":"zài wǎngshang mǎi le · bought online","tip":"在网上 goes before the verb: 在网上买, 在网上看. 了 shows it's done.","learner":["我最近买了 ___ 在网上。","Understood! Putting the place first (在网上买了) is easier to follow."],"natural":["我最近在网上买了一双鞋。","Number + measure word + thing."],"quiz":{"q":["你想说昨天在网上买了一本书。","Say you bought a book online yesterday:"],"o":[["我昨天在网上买了一本书。",1],["有小一号的吗？",0],["我取快递。",0]],"ok":"Yes — time, place, then the verb.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 我昨天在网上买了一本书。"}}}},"xiaoyu_zaohui":{"0":{"line":"昨天我[主要]在弄登录页面。","lang":{"chunk":"主要","mean":"zhǔyào · mainly, mostly","tip":"主要在 + verb = what you spent most of the time on. 弄 (nòng) = work on, fiddle with — very common at work.","learner":["昨天我做了很多事情，比如登录页面。","Too long for a morning meeting. Pick the main thing."],"natural":["昨天我主要在弄登录页面。","One line, done."],"quiz":{"q":["你昨天大部分时间在写报告：","You spent most of yesterday on a report:"],"o":[["昨天我主要在写报告。",1],["麻烦你帮我看一下？",0],["明天准备开会。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 主要在 + verb.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 昨天我主要在写报告。"}}},"1":{"line":"今天[打算]把测试做完。","lang":{"chunk":"打算","mean":"dǎsuàn · plan to","tip":"打算 + what you'll do. 把测试做完 = get the testing done.","learner":["今天我会测试。","Understood, but 打算 sounds like a real plan."],"natural":["今天打算把测试做完。","Clear and normal."],"quiz":{"q":["你计划今天把代码写完：","You plan to finish the code today:"],"o":[["今天打算把代码写完。",1],["麻烦你帮我看一下？",0],["我卡住了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 打算 + what you'll do.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 今天打算把代码写完。"}}},"2":{"line":"这块我[卡住了]。","lang":{"chunk":"卡住了","mean":"kǎ zhù le · stuck","tip":"这块 = this part. 卡住了 works for code, homework, even a drawer that won't open.","learner":["我有一个问题在这里。","Your team may not know what the problem is. If you're stuck, say 卡住了."],"natural":["这块我卡住了。","Short and honest."],"quiz":{"q":["你做不下去了，说：","You can't go on. Say:"],"o":[["我卡住了。",1],["今天打算把代码写完。",0],["明天准备开会。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 卡住了.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 我卡住了。"}}},"3":{"line":"[麻烦你]帮我看一下？","lang":{"chunk":"麻烦你","mean":"máfan nǐ · sorry to trouble you, could you…","tip":"麻烦你 + what you need. 看一下 = have a quick look; 一下 makes it small and polite.","learner":["请你帮我看。","Polite, but bare. 麻烦你 … 一下 sounds softer."],"natural":["麻烦你帮我看一下？","Polite and friendly."],"quiz":{"q":["请同事帮你看一下代码：","Ask a colleague to look at your code:"],"o":[["麻烦你帮我看一下？",1],["昨天我主要在写报告。",0],["明天准备开会。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 麻烦你 + 一下.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 麻烦你帮我看一下？"}}},"4":{"line":"昨天我___，今天[准备]___。","lang":{"chunk":"准备","mean":"zhǔnbèi · going to, getting ready to","tip":"准备 + verb = what you're about to do. Close to 打算; both are fine.","learner":["昨天我修 bug 了，今天我将测试。","将 is for news and speeches. In meetings: 准备 or 打算."],"natural":["昨天我把 bug 修好了，今天准备测试。","Two lines, a full update."],"quiz":{"q":["你明天要开会，说：","You're going to have a meeting tomorrow:"],"o":[["明天准备开会。",1],["麻烦你帮我看一下？",0],["我卡住了。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 准备 + verb.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 明天准备开会。"}}}},"xiaoyu_zhoubao":{"0":{"line":"这周[主要做了]两件事：登录页面和测试。","lang":{"chunk":"主要做了","mean":"zhǔyào zuò le · mainly did","tip":"Start a weekly report with 这周主要做了 + how many things, then name them. Two or three is enough.","learner":["这周我做了很多工作。","Too vague. Say what, and how many."],"natural":["这周主要做了两件事：登录页面和测试。","The usual first line of a weekly report."],"quiz":{"q":["你这周大部分时间在做两件事：","You spent most of this week on two things:"],"o":[["这周主要做了两件事。",1],["能不能帮我看一下代码？",0],["下周争取把报告写完。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 这周主要做了 + the things.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这周主要做了两件事。"}}},"1":{"line":"测试这块[进度]有点慢。","lang":{"chunk":"进度","mean":"jìndù · progress (how far along a task is)","tip":"进度怎么样? = how far along are you? Answers: 正常 on track · 有点慢 a bit behind · 百分之八十 80% done.","learner":["测试的进步有点慢。","进步 is about getting better (你的中文进步了). For how far a task has got: 进度."],"natural":["测试这块进度有点慢。","Honest and normal at a weekly meeting."],"quiz":{"q":["经理问你的工作做到哪了：","Your manager asks how far along your work is:"],"o":[["进度正常，周四能做完。",1],["能不能帮我看一下代码？",0],["你吃饭了吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 进度 for tasks.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 进度正常，周四能做完。"}}},"2":{"line":"现在[卡在]支付接口上了。","lang":{"chunk":"卡在","mean":"kǎ zài · stuck on","tip":"卡住了 = stuck. 卡在 + the thing + 上 = stuck on what. Say where, and people can help. 接口 (jiēkǒu) = API.","learner":["我卡住了在支付接口。","Understood! Put the thing right after 卡在 — easier to follow."],"natural":["现在卡在支付接口上了。","Tells everyone where to help."],"quiz":{"q":["一个报错让你做不下去了：","An error is blocking you:"],"o":[["我卡在这个报错上了。",1],["进度正常，周四能做完。",0],["这周主要做了两件事。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 卡在 + the thing + 上.","no":"That one means something else. Here: 我卡在这个报错上了。"}}},"3":{"line":"[能不能]帮我看一下这个报错？","lang":{"chunk":"能不能","mean":"néng bu néng · could you…?","tip":"能不能 + 帮我 + verb + 一下 = a soft request. 报错 (bàocuò) = error message, what programmers say.","learner":["你可以帮我看这个错误吗？","People understand! 能不能……一下 sounds softer, and 报错 is the word your team will use."],"natural":["能不能帮我看一下这个报错？","Soft, quick, normal."],"quiz":{"q":["想请组长看看你的代码：","You want your team lead to look at your code:"],"o":[["能不能帮我看一下代码？",1],["这周主要做了两件事。",0],["进度正常，周四能做完。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 能不能帮我 + verb + 一下.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 能不能帮我看一下代码？"}}},"4":{"line":"这周我主要___，下周[争取]___。","lang":{"chunk":"争取","mean":"zhēngqǔ · aim to, try hard to","tip":"争取 + what you'll get done. Very common in weekly reports — a promise, but a soft one.","learner":["下周我希望完成测试。","希望 sounds like a wish. 争取 sounds like you're working on it."],"natural":["这周我主要在弄登录页面，下周争取把测试做完。","A whole weekly report in two lines."],"quiz":{"q":["你下周要尽量把报告写完：","You'll try hard to finish the report next week:"],"o":[["下周争取把报告写完。",1],["能不能帮我看一下代码？",0],["这周主要做了两件事。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 争取 + what you'll do.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 下周争取把报告写完。"}}}},"zhaolei_food":{"0":{"line":"老板，[来一两]生煎。","lang":{"chunk":"来一两","mean":"lái yì liǎng · one liang, please (one portion — usually four buns)","tip":"来 + amount = I'll have… 两 is an old weight (50 g); for shengjian it usually means four buns. In small shops everyone calls the owner 老板.","learner":["我想要一个生煎的两。","Hard to follow — amount first: 来一两生煎."],"natural":["老板，来一两生煎。","What you hear at every shengjian shop."],"quiz":{"q":["你想要两份生煎：","You want two portions of shengjian:"],"o":[["老板，来二两生煎。",1],["小心烫！",0],["是扫码点餐吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 来 + 二两 + 生煎.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 老板，来二两生煎。"}}},"1":{"line":"先咬个小口，[小心烫]。","lang":{"chunk":"小心烫","mean":"xiǎoxīn tàng · careful, it's hot","tip":"小心 = careful. 烫 = burning hot (food, water). Hot weather is 热, not 烫.","learner":["小心，很热！","热 is for weather or a warm room. Food that can burn you is 烫."],"natural":["先咬个小口，小心烫。","What a Shanghai friend says when the basket comes."],"quiz":{"q":["小笼包刚端上来，提醒朋友：","The xiaolongbao just arrived. Warn your friend:"],"o":[["小心烫！",1],["老板，来二两生煎。",0],["是扫码点餐吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 小心烫.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 小心烫！"}}},"2":{"line":"你们这儿是[扫码点餐]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"扫码点餐","mean":"sǎo mǎ diǎn cān · scan the code to order","tip":"扫码 = scan a QR code. 点餐 = order food. 你们这儿 = here at your place.","learner":["我要扫描这个二维码吗？","People understand! 扫码 is the short word — you'll see it on every table."],"natural":["你们这儿是扫码点餐吗？","Ask once, then just scan."],"quiz":{"q":["桌上只有二维码，没有菜单，你问：","There's only a QR code on the table, no menu. You ask:"],"o":[["是扫码点餐吗？",1],["老板，来二两生煎。",0],["小心烫！",0]],"ok":"Yes — 扫码点餐.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 是扫码点餐吗？"}}},"3":{"line":"服务员，[买单]！剩下的打包。","lang":{"chunk":"买单","mean":"mǎidān · the bill, please","tip":"服务员，买单 = excuse me, the bill. 打包 (dǎbāo) = pack it up to take away. In the north you'll also hear 结账 (jiézhàng).","learner":["服务员，我要付钱的单子。","Too long. Two characters do it: 买单."],"natural":["服务员，买单！剩下的打包。","Pay and take the rest home in one go."],"quiz":{"q":["吃完了想付钱，叫服务员：","You've finished and want to pay. Call the waiter:"],"o":[["服务员，买单！",1],["是扫码点餐吗？",0],["去北京，我一定要吃烤鸭。",0]],"ok":"Yes — 买单.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 服务员，买单！"}}},"4":{"line":"去___，我[一定要]吃___。","lang":{"chunk":"一定要","mean":"yídìng yào · definitely have to","tip":"一定要 + verb = a must. Note the tone: 一 becomes yí before 定.","learner":["去上海，我必须吃生煎。","必须 sounds like a rule. For food you're excited about: 一定要."],"natural":["回上海，我一定要再吃一次生煎。","Sounds excited, not strict."],"quiz":{"q":["你去北京非吃烤鸭不可：","In Beijing you simply must have roast duck:"],"o":[["去北京，我一定要吃烤鸭。",1],["小心烫！",0],["是扫码点餐吗？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 一定要 + 吃.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 去北京，我一定要吃烤鸭。"}}}},"zhaolei_shanghai":{"0":{"line":"请问，去南京东路[怎么走]？","lang":{"chunk":"怎么走","mean":"zěnme zǒu · how do I get there","tip":"去 + place + 怎么走 asks for the route. 在哪里 only asks where it is.","learner":["请问，南京东路怎么去走？","One verb too many — 去 + place + 怎么走 is enough."],"natural":["请问，去外滩怎么走？","Start with 请问 for strangers."],"quiz":{"q":["你想去豫园。问路人：","You want to go to Yuyuan Garden. Ask someone:"],"o":[["请问，去豫园怎么走？",1],["先往左走，再过马路。",0],["这家店贵不贵？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 去 + place + 怎么走.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 请问，去豫园怎么走？"}}},"1":{"line":"我应该从[几号口]出去？","lang":{"chunk":"几号口","mean":"jǐ hào kǒu · which exit (number)","tip":"Metro exits are numbered: 1 号口, 2 号口. People also say 几号出口.","learner":["我应该出哪个门？","门 sounds like a building's door; metro exits are 口."],"natural":["去外滩从几号口出？","Short and normal."],"quiz":{"q":["站务员说：3 号口。你重复一遍确认：","Staff says exit 3. Repeat it to check:"],"o":[["3 号口，对吧？",1],["先往左走，再过马路。",0],["这家店贵不贵？",0]],"ok":"Yes — number + 号口.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 3 号口，对吧？"}}},"2":{"line":"就是[一直往前走]吗？","lang":{"chunk":"一直往前走","mean":"yìzhí wǎng qián zǒu · keep going straight","tip":"一直 = all the way. 走到头 = walk to the end of the road.","learner":["我直走一直吗？","一直 goes before the verb: 一直往前走."],"natural":["一直往前走，对吧？","Checking you got it right."],"quiz":{"q":["对方说：「一直走，走到头就是。」意思是：","They say 一直走，走到头就是. That means:"],"o":[["Keep walking to the end of the road — it's there.",1],["Turn around and go back.",0],["Take the metro two stops.",0]],"ok":"Yes — 走到头 = to the end of the road.","no":"一直走 = straight on; 走到头 = to the end."}}},"3":{"line":"离这儿[远不远]？","lang":{"chunk":"远不远","mean":"yuǎn bu yuǎn · is it far","tip":"A + 不 + A makes a quick yes/no question: 远不远, 好不好, 贵不贵.","learner":["它很远吗？","Not wrong! Just add where from, so it's clear: 离这儿远不远."],"natural":["离这儿远不远？走路能到吗？","Then ask if you can walk."],"quiz":{"q":["你想问这家店贵不贵：","Ask if this shop is expensive:"],"o":[["这家店贵不贵？",1],["先往左走，再过马路。",0],["请问，去豫园怎么走？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 贵不贵, 远不远.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 这家店贵不贵？"}}},"4":{"line":"去 ___，[先] ___，再 ___。","lang":{"chunk":"先","mean":"xiān … zài … · first … then …","tip":"先 … 再 … is how people give steps: 先坐地铁，再走五分钟.","learner":["第一坐地铁，第二走路。","Understood! 先…再… makes it easier to follow as directions."],"natural":["先坐 10 号线，再走五分钟就到了。","就到了 = and you're there."],"quiz":{"q":["有人问你路：要先往左走，然后过马路。","Someone asks you the way: go left first, then cross the road."],"o":[["先往左走，再过马路。",1],["这家店贵不贵？",0],["请问，去豫园怎么走？",0]],"ok":"Yes — 先 + first step, 再 + next step.","no":"That one's for another moment. Here: 先往左走，再过马路。"}}}}};
window.ACTS_I18N = {};

